4.5,"Being a big fan of the original movies, The Infernal Affairs, and hearing a few bad comments about it (upon comparison), I started to become partial when I was about to watch the movie. 

It's true. the story, the plot is one and the same. At first, my opinion of the American remake started to go downhill, The backstory was sorta different, and complicated that I missed the HK version, because they presented it simpler. And since all I heard was cussing (it's like their life depended on saying fuck in every sentence.) 

As it progressed, I saw a lot of similarities, almost a copy even, but with a different treatment. In the end, I really did like it. Martin Scorsese managed to put the exact same story, and fit it into the American culture very well. 

I hate though when the Departed fans bash the original Infernal Affairs for being too simple, when in fact that is what we fans like about it in the first place. Asian simplicity.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2006-09-30","","RT","21897471"
