4.0,"""i'm the guy doing his job, you must be the other guy""
..................................................................
From the opening scenes you know your in for a treat. Scorsese is at the wheel and your in for a hell of a ride. The soundtrack, the editing, that incredible camera work, it's all scorsese showing he's the master of his craft.

Then theres the cast, and it's like the cast of the gods, jack, leo, matt damon all on top form. Jack making it look easy, leo just raising his own bar again and matt has'nt been this good since good will. But it does'nt end there, throw in baldwin, sheen, winstone and a super funny performance from walberg and it makes for one of the finest ensembles in quite some time and no one tries to step on the others toes, it's all played out for the sake of the movie and you just end up wrapped up in it all unfolding.

A great movie that is up there with the best of the year, it's not quite scorsese at his best, even though it's darn close and head and shoulders above most other movies in it's field in recent years and just all the individual ingredients make it a must see for everyone who loves movies.

