3.5,"Being a fan of the Infernal Affairs trilogy, I would have normally been very sceptical about the prospect of a Hollywood remake of the subtle Hong Kong thriller. And though many have raised objection to such a remake, I think we need to remind ourselves that this is Martin Scorsese.
<br/>The god of the urban warzone continues his love/hate affair with the ruthless gangsterism that has almost become synonymous with his New York work.
<br/>In a blow-for-blow account, both films emerge quite evenly, and are both essential viewing. Though the subtlety of the original is more or less taken over by extreme violence (even by Scorsese standards, usually perpetrated by Ray Winstone's hired muscle), it does seem to better fit the grubby aesthetic of Boston.
<br/>Cast-wise, we do suffer from some dodgy Irish accents","3024637d-1dad-471b-8f35-b06f869b06c5",False,True,False,False,3.5,"2006-10-04","","RT","347436027"
