5.0,"This is what I call a movie and I can say I don't give a sh!t if you disagree because this is my opioin and mine alone. That being said this movie is going to rule the oscars and if not I will stop watching them, but honestly an oscar is just a stupid little statue and this movie has an even bigger honor a place in movie history. This is the best put together movie I have ever seen, every scene has meaning and the ending is electrifying. Every character feels human and every actor does their part in the movie. I'm telling you I will go to my deathbed (years from now) swearing that the Departed is not just the best gangster flicks, but the best movie I've ever seen.
 
I could go on about the story line, but you know the basics and revealing anymore would ruin the perfectly mapped out plot. The stand outs of the movie are as follows Leonardo DiCaprio as the undercover cop, Matt Damon as the undercover mobster ratting out the cops, Jack Nicholson as the mobster, Ray Winstone as the muscle for the mob, and Mark Whalberg who has the best scene of the movie (Won't reveal it, but it rocks, I wanted to jump up and clap.). Jack Nicholson is at the top of his game as Frank constello the psychotic mob/porn theater owner. Ray Winstone is quiet and frightining as the guy who does the killings. Mark Whalberg is the cop who spews profanity because he is cool and unpredictable.
 
I could write an essay on this movie, I've only seen it once but it managed to dethrone my favorite movie of all time Pulp Fiction. I've been a fan of the crime/dramas all my life and this is the movie I've been waiting for. This movie combines drama and humor flawlessly one scene you're laughing your ass off the next you're on the verge of tears becuase you care about the characters and a lot of the good ones die.
 
This movie marks the end of looking forward to a new favorite movie, because this one is of course my favorite. The showdown between the two cops will go down in movie history, it is full of surprises. This is one of the best written, directed, and edited movies of all time. At 2 and a half hours it moves at the pace of a good hour and a half movie. Do yourself a favor and see this one, this is the movie you take a day off of work to see.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-06","","RT","900805292"
