5.0,"Wow, thats all i was able to say after seeing the new scorsese film.  It was amazing.  The first 30 min of the movie i was a bit skeptical, cause it was a little boring, but that was just to set up the characters, cause the last 2 hours are amazing, leading up to a finale that i did not see coming (i didnt see internal affairs).
The whole cast is great in their roles, and Leonardo Di caprio has come along way from titanic, and he was really convincing.  Matt Damon was also superb in his role, making him the guy you love to hate, and Marky mark added some style/humor to the film, and he was also very good. However Jack Nickilson steals every scene in which he is in.  He was just superb at being the big crime lord.  He would have you laughing at one moment then the next moment hating him. He deserves an oscar. 
However if anyone deserves an oscar its scorsese for directing the best movie of the year. He is long overdue.  
The basic plot of the movie deals with leo as the good cop who is undercover as one of jacks bad guys, and damon as the crooked cop.  When both sides find out there is a leak on each side, leo and damon must race against each other to find out who the rat is to save themselves. The movie is a thriller/crime-drama. It is very suspensefull, and for the last hour i found that i was at the edge of my seat for most of the time. It was that suspensful.
I Highly recommend this movie if you like either thrillers or crime dramas, cause it suceeds at being both well. It is worth every penny, and is scorsese best picture since goodfellas. GO SEE THIS MOVIE!!!!!","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-06","","RT","900815761"
5.0,"Before the Departed hit the box office today, V for Vendetta was appearing to be taking an easy victory as the best movie for 2006.  Now, it has a really strong contender in Martin Scorsese's newest film.  This is a film that is extremely vulgar and violent, and it's characters are less than respectable citizens.  The film does lighten the mostly serious and intense atmosphere with some of it's dirty humor.  Jack Nicholson is just absolutely great in this, and so is Leonardo Di Caprio.  This film proves to be one of the rare all star cast films that delivers in spades, and that's what I loved about it.
 
I haven't ever had a chance to see Infernal Affairs, which is the film that this movie is trying to remake, but I honestly can't see how that film could have been any better than this one.  The ending to this movie had the audience gasping at times, and there was an extremely surreal feeling to the whole thing.  The final scene with Matt Damon is about as great of a well directed ending as you're going to see, which starts with the dog even sensing something wrong with him.
 
Great! Great Movie that I advise everyone to go out and see, and now I'm going to have a tough time deciding on my movie of the year.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-06","","RT","900840732"
5.0,"[center][img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/the_departed/thedeparted_bigearlyposter.jpg[/img][/center]
 
[center][color=black]For those of you who have not seen this film, trust me, I WILL NOT ruin the movie for you. I will just tell you what I, and my friends thought of this movie.[/color][/center]
 
[center][color=black]I went into the theatre today with alot of expectations for this movie, but I left with more than I expected. The first thing that I have to comment on is the previews before the movie. Every single one of them was great. I'm not gonna tell you which ones they are, but you must be there in time to see the previews. You won't regret it. [/color][/center]
 
[center][color=black][img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/the_departed/_group_photos/mark_wahlberg5.jpg[/img][/color][/center]
 
[center][color=black]Martin Scorsese has made his best film since ""Goodfellas"". The movie really goes on a pace that will keep the viewer pleased the entire 2 hours and 30 minutes. He has an incredible vision for all crime/ganster movies that he makes, and he chose the best actors possible for this film. [/color][/center]
 
[center][color=black]Jack Nicholson has once again proved why he's at his legendary status as an actor. He's still at tip top form, and i'm hoping to see much more of him in films to come. Mark Wahlberg and Matt Damon have proved that they're not just movie stars, but should be well respected as two of the best actors in the film industry.[/color][/center]
 
[center][color=black][img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/the_departed/_group_photos/leonardo_dicaprio8.jpg[/img] [/color][/center]
 
[center][color=black]Leonardo DiCaprio has proved his versatility in this film. I was most impressed by his performance than the rest of the actors in the film. This was the most violent role has taken in his career, and it was a smart decision. He will change alot of peoples minds about rating him as just another movie star/titanic/dicrapio actor. When people say those things, it just freakin irritates me like crazy. [/color][/center]
 
[center][color=black]Martin Scorsese has my vote for best director. Leonardo DiCaprio has my vote for best actor. Matt Damon has my vote for best supporting actor. This is what I think so far for this year, and I highly doubt that it's gonna change. When y'all see it, y'all won't blame me.[/color][/center]
 
