4.0,"...after his Oscar-nominated (and trying too hard to impress) films-- Gangs of New York and The Aviator-- it's good to see him take a break from that and make a mainstream movie in what may be his most star-studded and commercial movie to date and he's having more fun this time!! Jack Nicholson, the consummate actor that he is, owns this movie, and plays the mob boss with gusto!! Matt Damon and Leonardo Di Caprio held their own with stellar performances from a supporting cast consisting of Martin Sheen, Alec Baldwin and Mark Wahlberg. As I've already seen the terrific Hong Kong film, Infernal Affairs, on which this movie is based, there was not much surprise for me and while it lacks the artistic style and dramatic tension of the foreign film, it makes up in grit and raw violence, typical of Scorsese's gangster films, but also injected with humor and wit, making it an enjoyable and satisfying moviegoing experience on a Friday night!!
 
 
