5.0,"The movie is a remake of a movie called Infernal Affairs, I've never seen the original so I can't compare the two. The film follows two cops one good (Leonardo DiCaprio) and one bad (Matt Damon) in Boston. The bad cop infiltrates the cops to let his mob friends know any information, the good cop works to stop the mob by infiltrating them. There is a lot of things that go on in the movie that I don't want to ruin so that's it for plot.
 
Acting the movie is an amazing thing each performance is good and none of the characters are a waste of space. There are a lot of scenes played with raw emotion and lots of anger between the characters. Frank ( Jack Nicholson) is a character with the biggest range of emotions, one minute he is happy and the next he is like TNT. The most surprising performance is from Mark Whalberg, he was always good but not quite to the level he is in this movie. As for the two leads they are awesome.
 
Direction is a key element to any movie and here Martin Scorsesse is at the top of his game, I haven't seen him direct quite like this since Goodfellas. I like how he never lets himself get known as the mob movie director, he works on lots of different genres whether biographical (Aviator), period piece (Gangs of New York) and so on, there is no denying though his two best films are both mob movies this one and Goodfellas are the two.
 
As for violence there is plenty here and it is all brutal. A particularly brutal scene involves a character being thrown off a building the scene is haunting and sad. Then there is a scene where Frank is waving a severed arm around to make a point. You can't talk about this film and not talk about how powerful the ending is, 20 years from now I'll still be surprised by it, it leads you to believe one thing will happen when something else happens all together.
 
Be sure to not miss this haunting and beautifully told story of the toll undercover work takes on the cops involved.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-06","","RT","900913896"
