5.0,"Tonight was the very first time i went to see a Martin Scorsese film, and i am in suttle disbelief as to why this man has yet to win an Academy Award for directing, yet alone for Best Picture itself.  This film is pure Gold, and it looks like we might head into Round 2 of Clint vs. Martin at this year's oscars.  There was no performance that was not outstandingly acted, especially major kudos goes to Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, Mark Wahlberg, and of course, Jack Nicholson (you can never count out the Jack when it comes to movies).  Vera Farmiga went from being a small time actor to not quite an A-List actress, but she had the strength and potential to have a big career in her future.  This may be the year that Scorsese finally gets that 13 1/2'' coveted statue that he is longingly overdue for, as well as nominations from The Jack, DiCaprio and Damon.  This is the year's most phenominal film, and yet manages to be better than GoodFellas.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-06","","RT","900704126"
