[font=Franklin Gothic Medium]Can you say, best movie of the year? For a while there I was getting worried that nothing would pass Akeelah, as much as I love the film I wanted something to rival it. The only movie in sight that looked to do that was The Prestige, but then came along this amazing film called The Departed. I had intrest in seeing it, but not untill this weekend did my intrest grow to such a huge amount. Everyone I know was talking about this movie, the RT rating assured me it was going to be great and I just had to see it OW, not questions asked. We went all the way downtown to see it because my dad and brother had to golf and my friends were all busy so I had to wait, and I hoped it was worth it.[/font]
[font=Franklin Gothic Medium][/font] 
[center][IMG]http://i95.photobucket.com/albums/l154/Jrod_013/mark_wahlberg19.jpg[/IMG][IMG]http://i95.photobucket.com/albums/l154/Jrod_013/matt_damon2.jpg[/IMG][/center]
[font=Franklin Gothic Medium][/font] 
[font=Franklin Gothic Medium]Oh was it ever. First off, theatre was packed to the max. I never go to this theatre, but I went to for this, its the only theatre that I know of so far that will be playing A Nightmare Before Christmas so thank God I went, its advertising it all over so im seeing that. Wrong movie, back to the topic. The Departed belw my expectations out of the water. I already knew this movie was going to be good because, well, look who was at the head of it, but I didnt know it was going to be this good. Being Italian, your acustomed to loving and owning gangster flicks. If you dont have The Godfather 1 in your collections, things may be said. Same with Goodfellas and even Scarface, they are just musts. This I can proudly say, even though its not about Italians, its a must gangster flick for any gangster film lover. It offends you, it thrills you, its grosses you out, it makes you laugh, jump, cheer, everything.[/font]
[font=Franklin Gothic Medium][/font] 
[center][font=Franklin Gothic Medium][IMG]http://i95.photobucket.com/albums/l154/Jrod_013/leonardo_dicaprio3.jpg[/IMG][IMG]http://i95.photobucket.com/albums/l154/Jrod_013/leonardo_dicaprio10.jpg[/IMG][/font][/center]
[font=Franklin Gothic Medium][/font] 
[font=Franklin Gothic Medium]Let me start off with the cast. Can you say amazing? Can you say oscar nominations? If you can, good for you, pat yourself on the back. I didnt know what to expect with the insansely huge cast of all male leads. I was worried with Mark Wahlberg but im not a fan of, but in this movie I was sold. He pretty much gave the 3rd best preformance in the film. His accent, his hand movents, that hair, everything was perfect, he blew my expectations of his acting abilities in this films, OUT OF THE FREAKIN WATER!. And of course, Jack. Oh Mr. Jack. This man is a fucking genious. Best preformance in the movie and maybe of the year so far.Yes im going to swear in this review, becuase if you have seen the film, fuck is basically the tagline. He is insanely good, and insane. Near the end he does this thing with his eyes, holy crap creepy. But his preformance, like all of his preformances stick with you. Damon gives the 2nd best preformance in the movie, he is in one word, amazing. DiCaprio is also very, very good but something about his preformance just wasnt there for me, dont get me wrong it is good, but not my favourite of his.[/font]
[font=Franklin Gothic Medium][/font] 
[font=Franklin Gothic Medium]Everything about this movie is perfect, the pacing is excellent. This could have been really slow but its pretty much a consant and perfect pace. The acting as I mentioned is out of this world insanely good. The story is very hard to follow, and the ending leaves you walking out of the theatre with a whole conversation because that was my car ride home, you have this quesiton when you leave. Who is the rat? Everyone seems the be the rat, and thruthfully I still dont know who the rat is. The last 30 minutes or so where almost everyone dies is gripping and very well shot. Litterally, very well shot. The deaths appear as if they are actually getting shot, dont come off fake. The soundtrack is as always excellent, except for the one song which is probably the most memorable, the one with the man screaming WELL. Oh, a bit overdone there. So to finsih off, best movie of the year so far, one of the Martins best and back to his roots. Let me say this, if he doesnt get nominated for Best Director and doesnt win, im writting a letter.[/font]
[font=Franklin Gothic Medium][/font] 
[center][font=Franklin Gothic Medium][size=4][u]Bottom Line:[/u][/size][/font][/center]
[center][font=Franklin Gothic Medium][i]Best movie of the year so far[/i].[/font][/center]
