4.5,"Martin Scorsese brings us yet another gang movie with the star-studded The Departed. The movie features the talents of Jack Nicholson(Something's Gotta Give), Matt Damon(Ocean's 12), and Leonardo DiCaprio(The Aviator). Big parts are also played by Mark Wahlberg(Invincible) and Martin Sheen(Catch Me If You Can).
 
The movie starts with Billy Costigan(DiCaprio) and Colin Sullivan(Damon) both attempting to gain entrance into the Boston State Police Department. Sullivan goes right through the system, become an investigative officer in no time and earning the praise of all who know of him. Costigan has a harder time, however, Seeing as his family has a history of problems with the law and society, in general, the two in charge of recruiting officers, Officer Dignam and Officer Queenan, tell him he will not be an officer. They offer him an alternative, however. He can go to jail and attempt to gain access into the city mob boss, Frank Costello's(Nicholson) gang and be an informant. While Costigan is going through his jail time, Sullivan is continuing to go through the ranks, but what everyone is unaware of is that he, himself, is an informant for Costello in the Boston Police Department. Once the department figures out there is a leak in the special investigations unit, it is up to Sullivan to find....himself. 
 
So here is the basic plot for the movie: an informant for a mob boss in the police is attempting to discover where the leak to Costello is coming from, but at the same time, Costello knows that there is an informer, and he has asked Sullivan to find him. Costigan and Sullivan have never met, but they are constantly at odds trying to find out who the other is, and they even share the same love interest. Toss all of this in a pot and you get great suspense with plenty of twists and turns that will keep the viewer guessing until the very end.
 
As confusing as the plot summary may be, it is executed almost perfectly, making for a real cinematic treat. DiCaprio, Damon and Wahlberg are the life of the party in the movie, all acting out their parts to perfection. I am not taking anything away from the rest of the cast, however. The performances by the entire cast are all stellar, truly bringing the script to life. The movie also stands alone as a great dark comedy, with plenty of jokes scattered around the movie.
 
The only real fault I believe the movie had was it left a few details unanswered. Maybe that is what the movie was going for, but I walked out and was still asking questions, and getting answers ranging all over the spectrum.
 
In any case, the movie is fantastic, and is definitely one of the must-see movies of 2006. A classic Scorsese and a great movie to usher in the fall movie season. Big thumb up.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2006-10-08","","RT","900914395"
