5.0,"[center][font=Times New Roman][size=3]I finally saw my most anticipated film of 2006, and I'll go ahead and blurt out that it is now my absolute favorite of the year as well. It was kind of like Christmas..:D You know how you get really excited for it..it comes and goes...but the memory lasts forever. I think this will be the case for sure, when it comes to my experience of watching Martin Scorsese's grand film, The Departed.[/size][/font][/center]
 
 
[center][img]http://i17.photobucket.com/albums/b78/actressfemme/thedeparted_bigearlyposter.jpg[/img] [/center]
 
 
 
[center][font=Times New Roman][size=3]First of all, this is the very first film I ever went to see in the theater by myself. Seeing how my Hubs is away, my brother in law declined, and I couldn't take my little boy (of course), I made sure this was the week my mother came to stay with me, so that she could babysit and I could go see it. Going in there by myself allowed me to focus all of my attention on the film completely..I am not sure if I ever looked away from the screen once. However, The Departed is the type that grabs you immediately, and doesn't even think of letting you go for a second. Not one. It is [i]that[/i] entertaining and engrossing. What's brilliant about it though, is that it has the ability to entertain in a way a big blockbuster movie intends to, but remains an incredible, fantastic, moving piece. But what else would you expect from the guy who sat in the director's chair, eh?[/size][/font][/center]
 
 
 
 
[center][img]http://i17.photobucket.com/albums/b78/actressfemme/mark_wahlberg19.jpg[/img][/center]
 
 
[center][font=Times New Roman][size=3]I loved the script, the dialogue, the setting (Boston...Irish...yep.)the direction, the cast, the characters, the performances, the plot, the sub plots, and the ending was satisfying. Perfection all around. There were two parts in the film that made me gasp out loud. (which caused me to laugh inside afterward, because I was kind of loud and sitting next to someone who didn't gasp. I actually uttered the word $h*t after the gasp when something shocking happend. This is rare for me to do in public. haha.) If you're fortunate enough to have seen The Departed, then I am sure you could pretty much put your finger on which scenes I am referring to. It is crafted tightly, with clever ways of dealing with 3 separate important storylines with our 3 main characters. Along the way, the ride took unexpected turns, which knocked me backwards. My heart rate went wild and my palms were sweaty. I even told myself while watching it, to not forget to mention how my palms were sweating buckets.[/size][/font][/center]
 
 
[center][img]http://i17.photobucket.com/albums/b78/actressfemme/jack_nicholson9.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][img]http://i17.photobucket.com/albums/b78/actressfemme/leonardo_dicaprio22.jpg[/img][/center]
 
 
 
[center][font=Times New Roman][size=3]My feelings must be stated on the spectacular performances in this film. Everyone was impressive and I was so proud to see that. They are a huge reason why this was such an entertaining picture. I am not sure how the Academy will decide who to nominate, because someone will be, hopefully a few. I have my hopes set for at least a DiCaprio, Nicholson, and Wahlberg nomination above all else. But if any of the others were to snag one, there couldn't be much of an arguement that they don't deserve it. Leo must have proved himself to those who have constantly kept their eyes closed to his talent, and if not, then I cannot believe it. He is at once vulnerable yet powerful. Terrified yet absolutely brave. He deserves any ounce of praise that may come his way for this layered character he nailed to the floor. I adore him and his performance. (that's an understatement) I cannot say more...he was marvelous!!! Jack Nicholson was perfect, perfect, perfect. A Showstopper. He was Frank Costello, (deliciously evil) and [i]no one[/i] else could've been. Mark Wahlberg may surprise a few, but I always knew he had it in him. Damon was awesome (his accent took me back to Goodwill Hunting) as well as every other person who had lines to deliver. (Alec Baldwin ;)) I had to take the time out to gush over these people, because it's one of the most remarkable casts and performances, in one film, that I have ever seen.[/size][/font][/center]
 
 
[center][img]http://i17.photobucket.com/albums/b78/actressfemme/martin_sheen15.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][font=Times New Roman][size=3][img]http://i17.photobucket.com/albums/b78/actressfemme/leonardo_dicaprio3.jpg[/img][/size][/font][/center]
 
 
[center][font=Times New Roman][size=3]But do I recommend it you ask? :D Drop it all to go see it. It is NOT one to be missed in theaters. One of the greatest experiences at the movies I've ever had, and definately the greatest of the year. [/size][/font][/center]
 
 
[center][img]http://i17.photobucket.com/albums/b78/actressfemme/leonardo_dicaprio21.jpg[/img][/center]
 
 
