5.0,"[img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/the_departed/_group_photos/leonardo_dicaprio3.jpg[/img]
 
[b]THE DEPARTED[/b]
[b]Directed by [/b]Martin Scorsese
[b]Stars [/b]Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, Jack Nicholson, Mark Wahlberg, Martin Sheen, Ray Winstone, Vera Farmiga, Anthony Anderson, Alec Baldwin
[b]R - [/b]strong brutal violence, pervasive language, some strong sexual content and drug material
 
Martin Scorsese returns to the mob genre with this explosive remake of the Hong Kong film [i]Infernal Affairs.[/i] Leonardo DiCaprio is a police informant imbeded in Jack Nicholson's Irish mob, while Matt Damon is a mob informant working for the police. What follows is a tense cat-and-mouse game as each one tries to discover the other's identity.
 
Watching [i]The Departed [/i]is like taking a master class in filmmaking and ensemble acting. All the performances are teriffic, but Nicholson steals the show with demonic glee, tearing into the role with an astonishing ferocity that marks one of the best performances he has ever given. 
 
Quite simply, this is the best film 2006 has given us so far.
 
A masterpiece.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-08","","RT","900764494"
