4.5,"I gotta say it is great, and probably Scorsese's all time most entertaining picture but of course I felt it does have some flaws. Particualrly in the music cues, some of the sound effects and the editing didn't feel as tight as it could, also the preface to the story is put together kind of strange, but none of these take that much away from it. 

Nicholson of course is great, but seriously in roles like these he doesn't even need to try, his voice, demeanor and look just scream villain. I thought the standouts were Dicaprio and Wahlberg, then Damon, Farmiga and Winstone. The one person I felt didn't belong was Alec Baldwin, great actor and all, he just didn't seem to fit. Good bit part by 24 Season Three's James Badge Dale as well. 

The difference between this and Infernal Affairs is the focus, this is focus more on the psychological aspects of the characters, whereas IA was more focused on being a Hong Kong action piece with a great story. 

Writer William Monahan (Kingdom of Heaven) gives the characters great life and dialogue.

My only other comment is that while I loved the movie, it disappoints me that movies only focus on the small part of Boston that is Southie and Charlestown, it;s a gorgeous eclectic city, that in terms of crime rate is one of the safest metropolitan areas around. Also, it's evident that the majority of the movie was filmed elsewhere (Brooklyn to be exact) and some landmark shots were thrown in to give you a sense of place. Either studios are too cheap to film a lot around here or, MA charges too damn much to, you be the judge. 

A-","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2006-10-08","","RT","900714061"
