5.0,"[img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/the_departed/leonardo_dicaprio/thedeparted1.jpg[/img]
 
This movie is just all kinds of awesome.  It's gritty, it's well-acted, it has humor, it has drama...yeah, awesome.  If this thing doesn't win the Oscar, color me disappointed.  Unless there's something coming out later this year that'll top it, but I doubt it.  Leonardo is phenomenal as Billy Costigan, a cop deep undercover.  
 
There are all kinds of rats in the Boston Police Department, and this is basically an ""untouchable"" branch where only two guys know that he's undercover.  As everyone knows, he was a ""Statie.""  So, they need to make it convincing tha the got thrown out.  Yeah, it works.  Matt Damon is quite the opposite, a mole placed in the system by Frank Costello (Nicholson), working his way to the top while reporting to the bad guys.  All of this comes out in the first 15 minutes, so I don't feel like I'm spoiling anything here.  Needless to say, the story winds and unwinds and it's just phenomenal.  I'm guessing that Nicholson will get a nomination for Best Actor or Supporting Actor, as that is what usually happens with this kind of thing.  My vote would be to Leo for lead actor.  I loved him in The Aviator and he was arguably better in this one.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-09","","RT","900670972"
