5.0,"The Departed is set in South Boston where the state police is waging war on organized crime. Young undercover cop, Billy Costigan (DiCaprio) is assigned to infiltrate the mob run by chief Costello (Nicholson). While Billy is quickly gaining Costello's confidence, Colin Sullivan (Damon), a young criminal who has infiltrated the police department as an informer for Costello, is rising quickly to a position of power in the Special Investigation Unit.
  
  Each man becomes deeply consumed by his double life, gathering information about the plans and counter-plans of the operations he has penetrated. But when it becomes clear to both the gangsters and the police that there's a mole in their midst, Billy and Colin are suddenly in danger of being caught and exposed to the enemy - and each must race to uncover the identity of the other man in time to save himself.
 
 At first when I went to see the movie,  I didnt think it was as good as the Chinese version called Internal Affairs which the movie was based on. It was very good movie to go watch to. I like the development of the characters of all three major characters as the story unfolds itself. We got to see more about the two men who go head-to-head to uncover each other identify. The plot itself was a very good original idea with interesting subplot development. I like it at the very near the movie, where Billy and Agent Brown was killed at the evelator very fast and when Colin shot his partner. That very scene was also shown in the Internal Affairs movie as the suprising turn event that no one really expected it to happen. All in all, it was really worth my 10 bucks, and I think everyone should go see at least once and watch the Internal Affairs movie as well.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-10","","RT","900860872"
