3.5,"Based on the entertainment factor alone, this is probably Scorsese's greatest film.  In terms of character and personality, it leaves something to be desired- especially if you expect something like Taxi Driver, Raging Bull, or even Goodfellas.  While there is a lot more going on and the film is easy to get into, it feels paper thin- something that is not a Scorsese trademark.  Of course, with the exception of Bill the Butcher (Daniel Day Lewis) in Gangs of New York, most of Scorsese's more recent efforts have lacked the kind of substance that made this director great.  It's been a while since he's made a true Scorsese-movie, and maybe those days are over- but if he can continue to offer films of this calibre from here on out, I will be more than satisfied.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2006-10-12","","RT","900858129"
