5.0,"A couple of months ago a friend lent me Infernal Affairs. It was alright...a bit confusing but ultimately a very clever plot. The enjoyed it, but I wasn't blown away. The problem I had with it was that I just didn't give a shit about the characters. I found it to be a bit too much like a lot of Asian cinema...very clever but overly epic, lots of silence and zero character development. So when I heard they were remaking it I wasn't that excited, especially when Matt Damon and Leonardo Di Caprio were thrown in the mix. But I thought, hey it's Scorsese it will at least look pretty. The film rocks. Everything about it is right. Every actor owns their role. I thought the leads 'Maatt Daammoon' and Leo were excellent, but Jack Nicholson was even better and on top of that Marky Mark stole the show. Even the lesser supporting actors are great. Overall just an awesome movie.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-12","","RT","338193457"
5.0,"Very rarely do i see a film that can, surprise me, shock me, and keep me totally engrossed through the entire film. Simply put, The Departed is the best film i have seen in nearly 3 years and although, a remake of a Hong Kong film internal affairs this film stands on it's own and is a Scorsese Classic! 

Going into the film i had high hopes, but felt it could easily fall into another case of ""well it's good but nothing sets it apart from Scorsese's other films"" i was worried i'd like it now, and not remember it in a year. Luckily i was not dissapointed.

Amazing use of a cast largely divided into the greats of yesteryear and the supposed greats of today, not a true passing of the torch but we do see them all stand on the same ground and really play off each other. For example, Jack Nicholson can usually be depended on for a memorable performance, but this film made me forget his previous work which is a good thing to say the least, it showed his acting ability and not simply ""Jaaack Nichoolsooon!"". the same could be said for the younger guys including an actor who is showing he is much better than a giant cruiseship, Leonardo DiCaprio has broken his ""boytoy"" image with some challenging roles and that's right earned my respect :P And without giving anything away, look for awesome performances from Mark Wahlberg and the stunning Vera Farmiga.

This film, like all GREAT Scorsese films has interesting characters, strong story (this one is one of the strongest in years), dialogue that sticks with you and performances to be remembered. i rarely give a film a perfect review, but this film despite it's length merits a 5 star review.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-12","","RT","357260777"
