4.5,"For some reason I went into the theater not hoping for much. I love Jack (and really, off of pure acting talent, who wouldn't), but the other members of the cast didn't thrill me. 

I was pleasantly surprised.

DiCaprio can claim to have put Titanic behind him at last. He pulled out a depth to his character that was unlooked for and very pleasant to see. I actually - if I can say this - liked him in the lead. He held it, and seemed to do so very well. Wahlberg as well, playing the tough, trash-talking leader of the undercover unit, left behind previous (and not so great) roles for this film.
Jack, however, steals the show. His performance seemed effortless; a persona, brought out as Costello, that I never doubted for an instant. Could I just admit here that I would NEVER want to meet Nicholson in a dark alley, ever? The prize for the weakest link in our story must unfortunately go to Damon, who was never more then annoying. 
The bones of the film impressed as well. The writing - which was at times loaded with so many expletives I had to laugh - was fantastic. Costello's one liners and odd/awkward conversation tendencies were great. It also - for the most part - wasn't overly dramatic. The editing and cutting of the movie was new to me and refreshing, bringing out thing's I'd never seen before.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2006-10-13","","RT","75672627"
