4.5,"[font=Arial]Scorsese and his stupendous cast achieve a fantastic, incredibly tricky balance in placing as much importance with the conflicts within characters as with the conflicts between them.  The liars themselves start to unravel long before their lies do.  And no one's dishonesty goes unpunished, regardless of justified means or ends.  The story moves along at an energetic, I would say breakneck pace.  It's gritty.  It's gripping.  It is the best of both worlds: psychologically engrossing and wildly entertaining.  Along with [i]Taxi Driver[/i] and [i]Goodfellas[/i], I think you can add this one to the list of movies Scorsese will be remembered for.[/font][font='Times New Roman']       [/font]","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2006-10-13","","RT","900904251"
