5.0,"There wasn't a chance in hell I was going to see this film and not thoroughly enjoy it. Departed is as expected, another fabulous piece of film from now legendary Scorsese, who  goes back to his roots of suspenseful ganster films with great characters(and played by brilliant actors). Scorsese being a man who likes to work over and over again with the same actors(eg. all his earlier works with the likes of Deniro and Pesci), appears to have his sights on DiCaprio, after this, The Aviator and Gangs of New York. And why not? Leonardo has proved his acting talent on nearly every occasion(and does have a lot of traits of young Robert Deniro). Once again his strength, presence and emotion are fully shown with the character of Billy Costigan. In fact all the actors in this film were amazing, with one of the best casts seen in awhile. The other amazing performances to note are Mark Wahlberg and of course, as usual, Jack Nicholson; all playing individual and memorable performances. But there wasn't a performance in this film that did not stand out and hold its own, and everyone should be recommended.
Such a fabulous story too(that I know find out is take from Hong Kong's Infernal Affairs, though obviously re-adapted) with a different perspective from Italian and Sicilian style mafias of later America, to highlight like other films such as Mystic River the scale and magnitude of Irish organized crime in upper eastern America. 
I cannot talk enough about the reasons I loved this film, so the only thing I can say is if you haven't seen it, see it. If you have seen it, see it again.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-14","","RT","136274994"
