4.5,"[img]http://i50.photobucket.com/albums/f320/dehlz/thedeparted.jpg[/img]
 
Since I'm going to start reviewing movies I've seen, I had to include this Scorcese masterpiece that I watched last week with my girlfriend. My thoughts leaving out of the theater were ""I have to watch the original film Internal Affairs now"".
 
The Departed is a remake (even though some execs and even Scorcese himeself deny this) of the 2002 Hong Kong film - Infernal Affairs, which I hadn't seen before. 
 
Overall, the film kept me at the edge of my seat throughout. Costello played by Jack Nicholson played especially well and stood out to me the most. Jack was hilarious, especially at the way you weren't sure when he was just about to crazy and all ""The Shining"" on us. Well, he didn't actually, but came close to it when he started literally sniffing around like a rat at Costigan, played by Leonardo DeCaprio. Sullivan, played by Matt Damon was his usual calm, always level-headed character. Dignam, played by Mark Wahlberg played a smaller role in this movie than I had initially thought, but I think overall he played the asshole role well. Last but not least, Alec Baldwin played the role exactly like I remember him from the last movie I saw him in, ""Along Came Polly"" (just go to the bathroom scene with him and Ben Stiller for a good laugh). 
 
Without going too much into detail, the movie never once had me thinking it was going in one direction or another, it simply kept me second guessing on how it would end or how each character would be involved in the developing storyline. The plot was detailed and believable throughout and lets just say we get a pretty non-hollywood-standard ending and I loved it.
 
But like I said, great movie, great plot, great acting - I hope it does well at the Oscars. I had seen rave reviews from RT before heading to the theater so I had high expectations coming in. It never dissapointed like some other movies where the Tomato-meter was just wrong. I'll definately be purchasing this film when it hits DVD.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2006-10-14","","RT","900916181"
