5.0,"In ""The Departed,"" we are treated to what is one of the most intense and genuinely enjoyable films of the year. Not only that, it's fantastic (we're talking serious Oscar-contender here).
 
Scorcese (if that's correctly spelled) has a wonderful vision for the film that comes through in every aspect, from the pace to the soundtrack to the acting. Just when you think you can't take any more bloodshed or sexual banter, a humorous scene (often involving Jack Nicholson who is brilliant...as usual) kicks in and gives you a much-appreciated break.
 
The story of two moles (basically foils of each other) infiltrating a gang and the state police is fascinating, especially as they discover the other's existence and try to find the identity of their counterpart. Matt Damon and (especially) Leonardo Dicaprio are in top form, filling out their parts believably and passionately, lending the film an incredible set of legs to stand on.
 
Also of note is Mark Wahlberg, who steals the scenes he appears in by being an arrogant jerk... it's truly hilarious.
 
Overall, ""The Departed"" is one of the best films of the year. This is not one to miss.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-16","","RT","900916705"
