It is such a great remake of the Chinese film, Internal Affairs. It has unbelievable writing that keeps the film rolling up and down a fast-paced roller coaster ride that's full of twists and surprises. DiCaprio is sublime, along with pretty much the rest of the cast, but Nicholson is also in top shape, along with Mark Wahlberg. Martin Scorsese was long overdue for an Oscar and this might be the film to give him that Honorary Oscar-- don't get me wrong! I liked The Departed, but Scorsese did deserve it for other of his older classics like Taxi Driver, and Raging Bull. Even so, Scorsese antes up his game along with Monahan's sharp adapted screenplay that gives the characters some damn good excuses to cuss the hell out of each other. 
