5.0,"[size=3]""The Departed"" a classic crime drama and/or cop movie that's really shows why Martin Scorsese is so talented. I knew this was going to be good but i was totally shocked on how good it was and how much i liked it. Martin Scorsese's directing is fantasic that damn well should earn him a nod come oscars time. This may well be his best directing and movie considering ive only seen parts of ""Goodfellas"".One thing though is this far superior than his last film ""Gangs of New York"" that wasnt all that great.[/size]
 
[size=3]The acting is nearly perfect with everyone and i mean everyone giving a good proformance. No actor or actress is bad in here. Some proformances are better than others but still very good but all means. Leonardo Dicaprio is fabulous giving one of best proformances of his career tha's award worthy. When is Jack Nicholson ever bad?...the answer is never as he also gives a award caliber proformance is a role that he at times seemed ""joker"" from ""Batman"". Matt Damon is very impressive but i liked his proformances in ""Good Will Hunting"" and the Jason Bourne movies more. One that steals some of thunder from Damon as a lead is Mark Whalberg in the best proformance of his career to date giving a supberb proformance even though his roles is small compared to the ones of Nicholson, Dicaprio, and Damon. Other good proformances come from Martin Sheen, Alec Baldwin, Ray Winstone, and Vera Farmiga.[/size]
 
 
 
[size=3]The writting is excellent that at times has powerful, crisp, and sly dialouge and at other times...has rather funny lines. The editing and cinematography are great espically in a movie like this. Biggest suprize of all is how entertaining the movie thanks to highly intriguing story. There is a lot violence on a level that was suprizing but it had meaning to the whole movie and make the movie have a really good gritty and realistic feel to it. Also, i loved the soundtrack in this movie with classic rock songs such as ""Comfartably Numb"" and ""Gimmie Shelter"" and part of the score of that had irish head banging type of music that made the movie feel even more tense and entertaining.[/size]
 
 
[size=3]I liked how it dealt with a different type of gang (irish) and not the mob like every other gangster movie thats been made.This movie is an adaptation of foreign movie ""Inferrnal Affairs"" which i saw and was very good. The price i payed for seeing that before this movie is kind of seeing what was going to happen next but Scorsese made in a way and changes enough that i was still shocked. I did get confused with the story for a few moments but got back on track and i wasnt confused anymore.Aside from being overally entertaing the movie is rather tense and builds and builds keeping you on the edge of your seat. Now that i think about it ""The Departed"" has no actually flaws so sit back and enjoy the ride to classic movie thats masterpeice of filmmaking thats very oscar worthy and probably the best movie of the year so far.[/size]
 
[size=3]4,A-[/size]","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-17","","RT","900783080"
