3.5,"Directed by Martin Scorsese
Starring Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, Jack Nicholson, Mark Wahlberg, Martin Sheen, Alec Baldwin

Im curious to how The Departed will fare in the next Academy Awards. Heres Scorsese with perhaps his best cast ever, an incendiary script (based on Hong Kongs Infernal Affairs) and his desire to win after Gangs and Aviator, but somehow I feel that this movie wont do it. This is one of those I feel strongly could have been better with the ifs. This is without a doubt Scorseses genre but how Id like to argue that it would have felt different and somehow better (with the making of a classic) had Curtis Hanson or Soderbergh helmed it. Still, it was taut, provocative, engaging and very entertaining. Damon was the best among its stellar line-up along with the actress Vera Farmiga, whos a cross between Jennifer Love Hewitt and Anne Archer. I dont think Wahlberg was right for the part though. As the belligerent officer whose lines were almost always shouted, he comes as irritating not because of his character but because it was irritating how he tries to be irritating (not to mention a bad hairdo). But with a crew like this one, this is not to be missed.
Best Scene: The elevator scene.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2006-10-18","","RT","900887761"
