4.0,"This is a very good movie but while I was watching it, I kept on comparing it to Infernal Affairs.  Infernal Affairs is slick and tense the whole way through.  While this one is well paced, in that it didn't feel long at all, I never felt they were getting any closer to getting anything actually done.  Also, I had a problem with the building they used in this one.  In the original movie, it was a skyscrapper that looked over the city so the characters could look over the city they were protecting.  In this one, it's an abandoned building that's six floors off the ground.  Oh, and in this one, people  get beaten every ten minutes.  Good thing there are no unions in the police force.  And while the dialogue is clever most of the time, sometimes it's just swearing for the sake of swearing.  Also, the editing feels sloppy, like they did a rush job in some instances at the beginning.
Still, all the acting is top notch and if you haven't seen the original, you'll probably enjoy this more than I did.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2006-10-19","","RT","23992688"
