4.0,"Loved it! All my family saw this before me and they all rated it very highly, their only real criticism being its length. This IS a long movie and you feel like you're there in front of the screen for a good few days rather than hours. But it's the best week of your life! The action, the violence (my friend hated the gore/blood), the acting, the script, the storyline, the casting - everything was perfect. This, for me, was Leo's best film since his 'glory years' with Romeo and Juliet and Titanic. He was utterly believable as the good guy turned bad, and Matt Damon too was perfectly cast as a sly guy, a self-obsessed twat - much the same view as I have of him in real life. Jack Nicholson has charisma that could charm the pants of any woman still breathing (and that is an alarming and disturbing thought indeed) and Alec Baldwin may never recover from being labelled a F.A.G. But this movie was fantastic. An utterly enjoyable, perfectly understandable and easy to follow character driven piece of gangster violence. I would recommend this.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2006-10-19","","RT","324846921"
