[b]SYNOPSIS:[/b]
Director Martin Scorsese's movie, set in Boston, is about a policeman going undercover as a mob member and a mob member infiltrating the police force. Leonardo Di Caprio is undercover cop William Costigan and Matt Damon is undercover mobster Colin Sullivan. Costigan and Sullivan get into a lot of situations that almost reveal their true identities. The supporting cast includes Jack Nicholson as Sullivan's mob boss, Frank Costello; Ray Winstone as Costello's body guard; Mark Wahlberg as a hot-headed police sergeant; and Vera Farmiga as a love interest for both Damon and Di Caprio's characters. Alec Baldwin was also in it.
 
[b]My Review:[/b] We loved this movie! It had all the elements that makes a movie good, but above all, it had great actors in Leonardo de Caprio, Matt Damon and Mark Wahlberg - all my favorites! The language was a bit off-putting at first, but once you heard it over and over again, you were desensitized. Great ending - super surprises! This movie was action-packed and never had a lull or dull moment. I was on the edge of my seat for the whole thing. Might have to see it again just to get all the details straight.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2006-10-21","","RT","900874875"
