5.0,"Will someone please give Martin Scorcese an Oscar already?  This guy has been overlooked so many times that it is not funny.  He's deserving and everything he touches practically turns to gold.  If he does not win for [u]The Departed[/u] I'll be convinced of one of two things, either the Academy of Motion Pictures is corrupt, or there is no G-d.
 
[u]The Departed[/u] gets its' name from people who have died, and let me tell you this movie is full of death.  If there is one premise of this film it's who's the rat? Both cops and mob each have their own snitch in play and it is up to the other guy to discover the identity of their competition.  With a lot at stake and their lives on the line it is only a matter of time before the truth is revealed.
 
Filled with an all-star cast this movie is the must see film of the year.  Everyone is Oscar worthy and no one falls short in their roles. To be honest I expect some of the no names to potentially be nominated for the golden statue.  Love him or hate him DiCaprio will more then likely get some recognition for his portrayal of the cop working deep undercover in the mob. Anthing Nicholson touches is magic, and portraying a mob boss certainly isn't a strect for him, but he still manages to pull it off nicely.  Damon's cop working for the mob was perhaps an excellent choice as he looks like the boy next door and not a villain.  I would like to note I sware I saw Affleck doing a cameo as a cop folding the flag at the funeral.  Finally, Wahlberg although I am not a huge fan of his is definetly brilliant in his portrayal of the no nonsense says what he thinks staff sergeant. 
 
The story is well done and well explained there are no signs of plot-holes.  If there is one movie you need to see this year, see [u]The Departed[/u]. If you don't or you hate it then you obviously suck.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-22","","RT","900716260"
