4.5,"[b][size=5]Marie Antoinette[/size][/b]
 Directed by: Sophia Coppola
 [img]http://media.monstersandcritics.com/articles/1210219/article_images/image2_1160574916.jpg[/img]
 
 Well, this is certainly...something.
 
 Coppola isn't a flash in the pan.  This is a uniquely styled film where Coppola knows what she wants to do and does it.
 
 It's also very funny, it's got some of the most hilariously awkward scenes ever put to film, it's very well acted, and very pretty to look at.
 
 Yet...I felt as if there was just not enough 'umph' to the characters.  Like I was only getting 9/10ths of the story.  
 
 Still, that just kept it from being great.  It is a very unique, well constructed and enjoyable film that has more then it's share of style and humor.  Worthwhile.
 
 [size=4][i]8.0[/i][/size]
 
 
 
 
 
 [size=5][b]The Departed[/b][/size]
 By: Martin Scorsese
 [img]http://x4e.xanga.com/3ec831e7d1c3848426612/b24032223.jpg[/img]
 
 Ends up this is as good as most people say it is.  It's definately a throwback to films like Goodfellas and Mean Streets.
 
 I'm amazed at how much good dialog the movie had.  Great plot too.  It was complex and detailed, yet not convoluted.  You know they are doing this sort of thing right when you can say that honestly.  
 
 DiCaprio's performance is Oscar worthy.  It's the best he's done since The Basketball Diaries, and I'm a big fan of his work in the last two Scorsese pictures he's been a part of.  
 
 I love how things keep twisting back on each other, yet it all still makes sense.  The entire supporting cast is good.  Scorsese's direction is flawless.  Nobody else could have directed the violence as beautifully or the plot as gracefully as he did.
 
 Best of the year.
 [size=4][b]
 9.5[/b][/size]
 
 
 
 [size=5][b]Graduation Day[/b][/size]
 Directed by: Herb Freed
 [img]http://www.jasonpaulcollum.com/reviews/graduationday/grad_box.jpg[/img]
 
 This is a one of those movies that just isn't enough.  It's got the slasher formula down well, but every aspect of it just doesn't have enough of an edge to it to really work.  You wind up with a film that, while not a horrible example of it's genre, just has too many other similar films that's better than it.  See 'Prom Night' instead.
 
 [size=4][i]5.5[/i][/size]","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2006-10-22","","RT","900589254"
