3.5,"I am still alive..Yes, I am and I have to force myself NOT to work tonight after dinner. So, I thought I'd share my thoughts with you about this movie I saw last night. I went to this movie with my dragonman ONLY because I love him and I have been told that healthy and adult relationships are about compromise..:o 
[img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/the_departed/thedeparted_bigearlyposter.jpg[/img]
 
So, there I am, totally openminded about the movie, not having a clue about the story, very happy that it was shot against the beautiful scenery of my beloved Boston. In the beginning totally bewildered about what the storyplot was..Why are they yelling at my adored Leonardo Di Caprio? And I never understood what Mat Damon was doing saying ""Dad"" to archetypal Bad guy Jack Nicholson..
But after over 2 and a half hours of bloody shots and thinking: DAMNED, I am actually caring about the characters in a REAL GUY movie..:confused: 
 
I didn't have real time to digest the whole movie yet, but after some flashlight insights (meaning they came without me actually really thinking it over) I made this depth psychology analysis of this movie.
 
The movie is about a world where the feminine is sorely missing. The world of cops and robbers is ruled by negative animus figures who are paranoid about power Over others and certainly not about the more socalled anima traits of 
relatedness. In a world where one doesn't have the luxury of cultivating the art of compassion because it will lead to your physical death, to betrayal and to capital punishment, one can only be ruled by the archetype of the cold distrustful warrior.
 [img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/the_departed/_group_photos/jack_nicholson13.jpg[/img]
 
And so, this movie shows us the archetypal conflict between the good guys and the bad guys. The fight between socalled good and bad is merely a reflection of the conflict between archetypes. The bad guys are serving a one-sided and narrow goal of self-serving goals of self enrichment and profit, thereby uncaring about the effects of it's behaviour as a bad ruler would, whereas the good guys serve the public, as a good ruler would. 
[img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/the_departed/_group_photos/leonardo_dicaprio1.jpg[/img]
 
The rats in the movie are invisible to one another but well aware of the threat to each other's lives, just as it would be in a real life between two shadow figures. The rat who infiltrated the good guys, is the necessary shadow of an oganisation that believes it's devoid of darkness while the informant who infiltrated the bad guys is the necessary shadow of an organisation that wants to be devoid of light.
 
It's no wonder however that both shadow figures (Mat Damon and Leonardo di Caprio) are in an affair with an important feminine figure. 
[img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/the_departed/_group_photos/leonardo_dicaprio21.jpg[/img]
 
She is a psychiatrist who councils cops, thereby representing the psychic conduit to heal the deep inner split between the fake good guy (Mat Damon) and the fake bad guy (Leonardo di Caprio). She lives with a fake good guy who is cold and not in touch with his feelings and then falls for this shadow figure who is a cop gone astray, but who is much more human and vulnerable than her live-in boyfriend.
 
When she finds out she is pregnant of a new baby (and we are uncertain who the father is), there is a necessary showdown and climax of the movie where the shadow figures meet and battle each other over life and death.
However, as in all universal truths, when the balance shifts, everything shifts. So, at a time that seems the fake good guy has shifted the power in his own benefit, his fate is in the hands of yet another unknown and unforeseen shadowfigure; a good guy who takes the law into his own hands, thereby rectifying the balance between the eternal dance between good and bad, darkness and light.
[img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/the_departed/_group_photos/matt_damon20.jpg[/img]","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2006-10-23","","RT","900767850"
