3.0,"I really didn't want to see the Departed after I found out it was a remake of Infernal Affairs. I couldn't really see myself wasting two hours and a half of my life watching a Scorsese film. But my boyfriend had come up from Los Angeles to visit me and we didn't have anything better to do so we went to see it.
 
 The two biggest reasons why I disliked the film were the length and having to sit through Boston accents for that long. Kind of ridiculous reasons but I'm pretty simple. Mark Wahlberg got all the good lines which I thought was dumb. I was taught that when crafting a story, you should distribute your good lines equally among your characters. Acting was good all around which would be a ""duh"" looking at the cast.
 
 I really don't know why the movie had to be so long. Really around the two hour point I stopped caring and wanted to leave.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2006-10-25","","RT","900883931"
