4.0,"I never have been a fan of gangstar films. I've only seen one Scorsese film (""The Aviator""). So I can say (although I have little to compare with) that this is the best gangstar and best Scorsese film I've ever seen! Violent yes; offensive hell yeah! But the violence isn't gory, its fast and quick. And yeah they swear ALOT! But its almost comical. And thats how its written: very clevar, very smart, very well done. Abit slow and it is long and confussing but only for the first hour really and then its just quallity film making. Which shows alot; very few loose ends or troubles it shows good direction. So yeah Scorsese was very deserving of the Oscar...why he hadn't won it 30 years ago I don't know. Best Picture of the year? No while very well done I am not jumping up and down raving about it unlike others I've seen this year (Little Miss Sunshine (which should have won), Stranger Than Fiction, Little Children or Notes on a Scandal). What I am raving about is the music choice and in partiqular the cast. First I liked the choice to go for a modern-italian-irish sounding soundtrack. But moreover the cast! Now I am jumping! Wow so good not a single bad performance! They all break out of the box and do wonderful performances! Loved DiCaprio who I usually dislike. And liked Wahlberg who I've never really noticed. And Jack...Ahhhhhh Jack, when is he not lovable? Like never! From the first line which is clearly him he draws you in! Alot of missed nominations and awards here; in partiqular the SAG for Best Ensemble. So overall: A fine piece of film...but not best picture of the year...in my opinion; but best director for sure!","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2006-10-27","","RT","201123538"
