5.0,"My Apologies for a long disapperance. I have moved and I was all ready backed up before hand in reviews. So to grace you with the movies I have viewed with mini reviews.
 
Little Miss Sunshine
-WOW, This is an awesome comedy. Real dark humor mixed in with a messed up family which may seem far-fetched but probablly isn't far from todays modern life at all. This film is one of the best of the year.
 
The Wicker Man
-A remake gone wrong. However the origional wasn't much better. This beetastic flick with dominant twisted females hording an Island was never a good story with just ""ok"" performances.
 
The Covenant
-Nice film with a nice concept and awesome FX. It lacked in explaining itself and never quite got into the entire concept it was bringing to the table. However some good performances for this High School teen drama version of Underworld with Witches.
 
The Black Dahlia
-A good film indeed, good performances all around. However it was real lengthy in its pacing and has too many drop off scene switches which makes you think the film is ending, But isn't really ending.
 
The Departed
-Like Tony the Tiger says ""It's Great"". This film delivers a medocre paced cop and robber drama in a cat and mouse game. The Departed helped Director Martin Scorsese return to the spot light. Once again working with Leonardo Di Caprio. Martin and Leo both worked together in the Aviator which was an excellant film. Along with this Leonardo Di Caprio brings out his acting abilities and amazes an audience. He is by far one of the best actors on todays market. Along for the ride in this film are Jack Nicholson, Matt Damon, Alec Balwin, Martin Sheen, and Mark Whalberg. The only draw back is the mulitple twists played into the ending with some parts left to assumption and not explaining.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-27","","RT","900729238"
