5.0,"Martin Scorsese seems to always direct great films with a all star cast. Great story and character's. Great performances all around. It's hard for me to pick someone out of this film who stood out as the best. This film may not be for everyone. But the story and characters are so good that I can't think why anyone would not like it.  Plus a ending I didn't see 's coming. Great film for a cop or mob film lover. Another classic film brought to us by Martin Scorsese.","",False,True,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-28","","RT","377976632"
4.0,"[b][img]http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/msnbc/Components/Photos/061004/061004_departed_hmed_3p.hmedium.jpg[/img][/b]
 
[b]The Departed is no doubt a quality film. The acting is FANTASTIC, and I loved the choice of music throughout. It starts out quickly with a lot of characters and a lot happening at once. The film becomes more engaging as we become more aware of what is happening and who is really who. The final five or ten minutes are truly outstanding. [/b]
 
[b]Overall, it's a step up for Scorcese from The Aviator (in my opinion), but isn't even in the same stratosphere as Taxi Driver (again, my opinion). It's one of the year's strongest films, but as a personal favorite doesn't necessarily rank among some others for me. [/b]","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2006-10-28","","RT","900757738"
