4.0,"Colin Sullivan is a rat in the Massachusetts State Police for an organized crime sydicate run by Frank Costello.  Billy Costigan is a rat *for* the Massachusetts State Police *in* Frank Costello's organized crime syndicate.  With this convoluted story, there are killings, there are violent encounters of every color, including an all-out shootout that could give the ever-famous shootout from ""Heat"" a run for it's money (not as big, but nearly as intense).  After his roles as a good guy in almost every single film he's ever made, I didn't believe at first that Matt Damon could pull off playing a crooked cop... but he does it, with flying colors.  Wahlberg is a bit over the top as the loose-cannon undercover ops director, and Sheen is almost too even-keeled to play the chief of police.  (There are more than a few scenes between Wahlberg and Sheen where I almosted laughed as the ""good-cop-bad-cop"" scenario came to life right before my eyes.)  Without spoiling the plot, I can say that a major loophole failed to distract me from the ending.  I found myself after the movie going ""Wait a minute..."" and recalling an omission that nullifies a lot of the last 15 minutes of the film.  Message me to ask what the omission is if you are confused.  Anyway, that's why this one only gets 4 out of 5:","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2006-10-29","","RT","307352198"
