5.0,"I know recently all the blogs on rottentomatoes have all been up about The Departed.  But I feel compelled to add to the accolades that it has been receving.  The Departed was a great movie.  Never once in the movie did I feel bored.  The only times I wanted it to end was that so I could talk about it to my friends.  Leonardo DiCaprio did a good job.  He did, however, have such a whiny voice at times.  I realize that this is just his natural voice but in pivotal scenes it seems like sometimes his voice would get higher pitched and it ended up taking away a bit from the movie.  I've never thought that DiCaprio has been a bad actor.  I think sometimes he gets a bum rap from some people because of his earlier work (Titanic, Romeo and Juliet).  Truthfully I don't think he did that bad in either of those movies. But I think he gets labeled a pretty boy more than he should.  Matt Damon was great also.  I heard that DiCaprio and Damon flipped a coin to see who would play which mole.  I'm not a hundred percent sure if this is true or not, but if it is than it makes an excellent story.  Once again Jack Nicholson was on top of his game.  I heard the part was offered to DeNiro, but I'm glad he turned it down.  He wouldn't have worked as well as Nicholson.  Overall, top notch Scorsese pick.  I don't know if I'd say it was as good as Goodfellas yet.  If it stands up to multiple views like Goodfellas, then it might be.  But only time will tell","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-31","","RT","900883756"
5.0,"Awesome movie. A must see","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-10-31","","RT","346707164"
4.5,"To be honest i wasn't expecting this movie to be good and was thinking that critics and people will take it as Scorsese's worst movie but i guess i was prooven wrong. This the best Scorsese i have seen yet. I'll start with the strongest and best thing in this show which is the very very very smart screenplay which took us back to movies such as Chinatown and Taxi driver. Althouhg it is very simple and not complicated but the way everything is told was very genius. But unfortunately Scorsese will get another nomination at the oscars but wont win. Despite his amazing job here he wont win the oscar coz he comes in second place after United 93's Paul Greengrass. But still i can't deny that he prooved once again what a great genius he is putting this intelligent movie all together. watching all the actors together, i felt that they were all racing for the top spot which is the best performence of the movie. But without any doubt the winner was Jach Nicholson who although we're used to watch him play such psycho characters, but he still knew how to give it the sense of originality. Between the young leads, i found that the real charmer was Leonardo Dicaprio who's [erformence was more confident and solid then Matt Damon's. But still Matt did a very good job. And for once Mark Wahlberg managed to give a decent performence which is by far the best in his career","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2006-10-31","","RT","223895340"
