4.5,"The Departed was a great movie.  It starts out in the past with Jack Nicholson's character taking under his wing a kid whose parents had been killed.  The kid grow up and enrolls in the police academy.  He quickly advances in through the force to become a detective; however his ulterior motive is to keep Jack Nicholson's character in the know.  At the same time, a kid from the wrong side has also entered the police academy.  He becomes and ""under"" undercover cop trying to infiltrate Jack Nicholson's group.  The two world's collide and eventually everyone associated with Jack Nicholson is killed.  
 
This was a great movie, I really enjoyed it.  Everyone was cast really well and everyone did a superb job.  It was a little over 2 hours long but it didn't seem like it at all.  There was constant action and the plot kept going on and on.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2006-11-05","","RT","900879239"
3.0,"Good story and violence!!","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2006-11-05","","RT","151172074"
4.5,"[u][url=""http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a4/The_Departed_poster.jpg""][img]http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a4/The_Departed_poster.jpg/405px-The_Departed_poster.jpg[/img][/url][/u]
 
[u]The Departed[/u] - When I first heard about this, I had my doubts. I'm not really a big fan of remakes...why remake something that's already great. Anway, after seeing the cast & the director...I was in for the ride. Even though, the film keeps the basic structure of the original, it's very much it's own film. It's very hard to believe that William Monahan didn't even watch the original while adapting the screenplay for this, he did a fine job. Leo, who's always been an actor, I either like or hate when I watch him in his films. But after seeing him in this, he's becomed one of my favorite actors right now in Hollywood. Clearly, the best performance in the entire film, great job Leo. Jack Nicholson, the best of the best. I knew what I was getting from him but wow! He hammed it up all the way, he took to it to another level. Terrific performance, this man has to win the Oscar for best supporting. Mark Wahlberg, I thought was abit over the top but overall he was very solid in the role. Alec Baldwin, Martin Sheen, Ray Winstone are good in their supporting roles. I think Vera Farmiga as the therapist & girlfriend is wonderful, clearly the most underrated performance in the film. I'm surprised not many people mention her. I hope she gets a nom. As much as I love Marty, I thought he was losing it...his last couple of films, haven't really been that great. They haven't had that great touch of his but after seeing this I was wrong, dead wrong...he's back baby!! and his directing is as great as is ever been. Noticed, how I didn't mention Matt, well, he's really the biggest flaw in the film & my least favorite from the cast. Don't get me wrong, he's not bad, he's just... OK, in other words, he's forgettable. I really think Marty could of gone with someone better, for instance, I don't know. Christian Bale, who would of been perfect. The Departed manages to be as good as it's counterpart, if not better. Clearly, the best film of 06. Just give Marty his Oscar, already.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2006-11-05","","RT","900683602"
