5.0,"In a nutshell this film is ace.
Undercover & corrupt cops, drugs, violence, the usual Scorsese package, though I didn't think it was as violent as some of his earlier work.
Leonard DiCaprio gives a brilliant performance in this film, and Jack Nicholson, typically great as always. My only gripe was why the hell is Ray Winston in this film? He can't act to save his life!
I found the ending to be a bit of a surprise, not what you would expect from the way it is panning out, don't worry though it all comes right in the end :) 
 
I did read one review on here, someone complaining about this film being too violent or whatever and asking when are people going to say 'enough is enough' to this in films. It's like this; you don't have to watch this film. Walking into a Scorsese film can normally guarantee certain elements which he likes to use e.g. the language and violence. Who is anyone to say that society should help stop these types of films? If you don't like it don't go and watch them. Everyone is different hence why people like different types of genres. If we all took this attitude there would be no such thing as artistic freedom of speech..... and the studios wouldn't earn half as much money as they do now :p 
 
Can't wait for it to come out on DVD!
Watch it.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-11-12","","RT","900905524"
