3.5,"[font=Georgia][size=1]What a disappointment. When Martin Scorsese brings together such an amazingly talented cast, I expect dynamite. What I received was a completely unoriginal crime drama that survives on its star power alone.
 
  With so many critics singing their praises for this and RT users calling for awards from the mountaintops, you would think it's a can't-miss classic. Don't buy into the bullshit. See this for what it is. 
  
  Movie of the Year? No. 

Also, I'd love to write a long-winded diatribe nitpicking the atrocious ending and preposterous events throughout the flick, but I won't spoil anything.
