3.5,"The Departed is an engrossing movie to see, with outstanding performances of all actors. Both an compliment to the actors and to the director. A good thing that Scorsese did was to keep the natural dominant presence that Nicholson usually has on screen, in tone with the other characters.

Compared to the original (Infernal Affairs), I'd say that The Departed comes off much more as a dramatised opera. It misses the subtlety and the tragedy of the characters as portrayed in Infernal Affairs. What did suprise me, was that much of the screenplay remained almost an exact copy to the original as well. One would say that they'd give their own twist to it, but no.

