4.0,"Another excellent example of why Scorsese is one of the best directors working today, although I have doubts whether it is the one to finally grant him his oscar (long overdue). I haven't seen Infernal Affairs which is a shame because I am going to end up comparing it to this instead of the otherway round but ah well. The acting is excellent, Di Caprio is the next De Niro and he gave my favourite performance out of the bunch even if Mark Wahlberg and Alex Baldwin threatened to steal the scene everytime they appeared (loved how they channelled their characters in I Heart Huckabees and The Cooler respectively) The violence is up there with all Goodfellas, Taxi Driver, Mean Streets etc, particularly the brutal last 20minutes that took me really by surprise. I didn't give it 5 stars because I felt there was something missing, some scenes were taut thrillers at their best but other parts felt like Scorsese was struggling to do too many things at once. Excellent movie though, definately the best crime thriller I have seen this year, even if it doesn't ultimately bust its way into the top 5 of 06'.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2006-11-21","","RT","8214698"
