5.0,"[b][i][u][size=5]The Departed[/size][/u][/i][/b]
[b][size=3]Starring - Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, Jack Nicholson, Mark Wahlberg, Martin Sheen and Alec Baldwin[/size][/b]
[b][size=3][/size][/b] 
Let me just start off by saying that [b]The Departed [/b]is a perfect film. Period. Now, let´s move on. Martin Scorsese´s latest film is about two men from opposite sides of the law who are undercover within the Massachusetts State Police and the Irish mafia. For start, the plot seems interesting, but you can´t think of a way of how it´s going to develop for two and a half hours without going down to boredom or predictability, but Scorsese manages to develop it in the most magnificient way, never letting down the audience.
 
[img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/movie/gallery/1159016/photo_01.jpg[/img]
 
The script is fantastic, [b]The Departed [/b]has an excellent dialogue, very clever and most of the time very very funny, which combined with the fantastic music that the film has, makes a perfect combination. But the whole movie wouldn´t be anything without the amazing performances from the cast, they were all outstanding, but the two guys that I can highlight the most are Jack Nicholson, who plays the perfect maffia boss, and Mark Wahlberg, who surprised me with his excellent acting in the role of a sarcastic and violent cop. Also, DiCaprio, was great as he always is, and Damon and Sheen were incredible as well.
 
[img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/movie/gallery/1159016/photo_14.jpg[/img]
 
I loved every single one of the scenes of the movie, of course liking some more than others, and I LOVED the ending, which I thought was the most perfect way to end a perfect film. [b]The Departed [/b]is exciting, violent, bloody, funny, clever and thrilling, it´s not only Scorsese´s best film in my opinion, but also one of the best movies of our time. If you have to watch a film of this year, watch [b]The Departed[/b], believe me, you won´t be dissappointed. 
 
[img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/movie/gallery/1159016/photo_26.jpg[/img]
 
