5.0,"Since its been a long time since I've done a review I figured I would throw up some reviews of recent films I've seen on both the TV and in theater

[u][b]The Departed[/b]
[/u]
Definately my favorite film so far this year with tons of depth and powerful acting giving Scorcese a possible academy award run this year.

[u][b]The Dukes of Hazzard[/b][/u]

This is what you get when you take a cult classic TV show, try to modernize it, and do everything humanly wrong in the process.

[u][b]Saw III[/b][/u]

Don't listen to all the hype about this being a great ""gore flick"" because all the gore is set off by painfully slow backstory and flash-cut directing that'll make your eyes scream. Also as a side note: for being next to dead jigsaw sure seems to be fine on keeping involved in a conversation.

[u][b]A Sound of Thunder[/b][/u]

What should have been an ingrossing time-travel film is turned into an annoyingly unfullfilling film. The director turns and twists a good concept into a sadly bad film with poor acting and a main monster that looks like godzilla and king kong's child.

[u][b]Lucker Number Slevin[/b][/u]

Though overly predictable its a fun film for what its worth and good acting helps to carry the film.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-12-01","","RT","900667747"
