4.0,"[b]""The Departed"" starring Leo DiCrappio, Matt Damon and Jack.[/b]

 [b]What It's About: [/b]Leo is a cop, posing as a mobster. Matt is a mobster, posing as a cop. Hilarity ensues. Ok, not really.

 [b]What I Was Expecting:[/b] Well, c'mon. It's Scorsese doing a mafia movie. It's not like there's a low bar here.

 [b]What I Got: [/b]A violent bloodbath of a film. If it wasn't Scorsese, it would be exploitation. But that part aside, it's a really good film that goes on about 45 minutes too long with a few too many points where it seems like it's ending (imagine ""The Usual Suspects"" with Chazz going after Keyser Sose. Not necessary.) And what's worse? The one really sympathetic character? You never know what happens to them. The acting, the technicals and the music are great and this one is worth seeing in the theatres. I don't think it will hold up nearly as well on video.

 [b]Rating: B+[/b]

 [b]Random Thoughts:[/b]
1. Okay, I know I gave it a B+, but how good could it be if I'm watching scenes and trying to pick out where the PA's had to be standing to cue the actors.
2. If one more person gets shot in the head...and there it is. 
3. Funny. Instead of using make-up or effects to show Nicholson when he's younger, they hid him in shadows. Not very effective.
4. The biggest female role was the love interest played by one Vera Farmiga. She's going to win an Oscar someday.
5. Speaking of Oscars, Leo, who I normally don't like, especially in Scorsese films, deserves one here. If they nominate Jack, I'm going to riot. Not too good in this.

 [b]The Trailers:[/b]

 [b]1. Catch a Fire - [/b]What is this title even supposed to mean? It's an apartheid movie, I think. I don't know if you knew this, but I guess apartheid is bad. So grateful to Hollywood for pointing these things out.

 [b]2. Deja Vu -[/b] Okay, if you are going to do a movie called Deja Vu, you CANNOT do a film that looks like every other Tony Scott/Jerry Bruckheimer P.O.S. Props to any critic who can review this film and NOT turn the title into a description of the film itself.

 [b]3. Stranger than Fiction -[/b] I cannot wait for this film. Will Farrell, Emma Thompson and Dustin Hoffman? Looks hilarious.

 [b]4. The Good Shepherd[/b] - Bob De Niro pretends he's Martin Scorsese and even casts Matt Damon in the ""real history"" of the CIA's beginnnings. Ummm...if it were ""real"", it'd be a documentary, folks.

 [b]5. 300[/b] - What the hell is this garbage? I thought it was a joke at first, like I was going to hear a cell phone ringing at any point. Nope, this is serious. 300 is also the number of reasons this film should never have been made. I could only stop and think all the starving people the $60 million spent to make this garbage could've fed. This movie will NOT crack $10 million at the box office. I guarantee.

 [b]6. The Blood Diamond -[/b] This one could go either way. I kind of got the impression that they're going for an Indiana Jones meets Black Hawk Down. Takes guts to even try. The controversy from the diamond industry over their potrayal in the film kinda makes me laugh.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2006-12-01","","RT","900634358"
