5.0,"Starring: Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, Jack Nicholson, Mark Wahlberg, Martin Sheen, Ray Winstone, Vera Farmiga, and Alec Baldwin.
Directed by Martin Scorsese.
Written by William Monahan.
Rated [b]R[/b] (for strong brutal violence, pervasive language, some strong sexual content and drug material).
Running time approximately 2 hours 32 minutes.
 
Martin Scorsese's [i]The Departed[/i] is his best film since 1990's [i]GoodFellas[/i], and I stand by that. Sure, he has directed some truly wonderful films since then ([i]Casino[/i], [i]The Aviator[/i], etc.), but this one's just magnificent. The cast is superb, especially DiCaprio, Damon and Nicholson, who's truly a wonder to behold. Nicholson has never frightened me so very much. His performance is most certainly deserving of an Oscar nomination, if not a win. Scorsese has yet to receive a Best Director Oscar, and I'm unsure as to whether this film will be the one to finally get him one or not. This is, so far, the second-best film of 2006 (were it not for the tremendous success of [i]The Fountain[/i], my newly appointed favorite film, it would be at #1). [b]**** (out of ****) A+[/b]","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-12-03","","RT","900731877"
