5.0,"[font=Times New Roman][color=black][b]The Departed[/b][/color][/font]
 
[img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/the_departed/_group_photos/matt_damon2.jpg[/img]
 
[b][color=#000000][font=Times New Roman]When I was your age they used to say you could become cops or criminals. What I'm saying to you is this... When you're facing a loaded gun, what's the difference?[/font][/color][/b]

 
[font=Times New Roman][color=#000000]The Departed is a superb film. Martin Scorsese makes an intense violent energy packed film. You wont find a movie better acted, better directed or as fun as this one all year; thats for sure. Leonardo DiCaprio and Matt Damon are probably the best two actors working today and no one plays off of each other better than these two. I couldnt have been more excited about a film than this.[/color][/font]

 
[font=Times New Roman][color=#000000]Im a big fan of Scorsese but he out does himself with The Departed. Some of his other films drag at certain points. While he always get a good performance and hes one of the best filmmakers of our time, The Departed is a film for anyone to get their mind blown. I cant think of a better film that had me more interested than this one. The Departed is a story of good cop/bad cop. We see DiCaprio and Damon play each others opposites in this cat and mouse film. DiCaprios the good cop playing bad guy in the mob with Jack Nicholson and Damon is bad cop playing good guy with fellow officers Mark Wahlberg and Martin Sheen. I honestly think that each of these actors gives one of their best performances. While Im sure that Nicholson will be getting a best supporting actor; for most of the movie he just hams it up  not that there isnt anything wrong with that. Who wouldnt want to see Jack Nicholson play an insane mob boss? The true standout is the short-fuse Dignam played by Mark Wahlberg. I never considered Wahlberg that good of an actor since I thought he was one of the worst parts in the dreadful Planet of the Apes, but your attention goes to him in everyone of these scenes. Expect great things from everyone in this cast, but really Wahlberg out does himself.[/color][/font]

 
[font=Times New Roman][color=#000000]Based off of the Hong Kong film Infernal Affairs, which I havent seen; I couldnt love The Departed more. While Ive seen it so long ago, I just enjoyed myself. Its the most entertaining films of the year and I believe its going to go down as one of the best crime dramas of the decade. There are some powerful scenes as the ending or when Oliver (Sheen) the only truly good character of this film, gets caught in a bad situation. DiCaprios reaction is heartbreaking. [/color][/font]

 
[font=Times New Roman][color=#000000]The Departed is not without its flaws. The final act, which has an INSANE amount of plot twists to get your heartbreaking out of your chest. While, I dont consider that a flaw and its a great scene, there are a few plot holes moments before that. Its shameful that Madolyn (Vera Farmiga) doesnt get more closure at the end considering she did a wonderful job holding up against all these tough cops. Regardless of flaws though, its a thrilling one hell of a movie and Scorsese proves hes a storytelling mastermind.[/color][/font]
[font=Times New Roman][color=#000000][b]Grade: ****/****[/b][/color][/font]
 
[b][font=Times New Roman][color=black]Jackass: Number Two[/color][/font][/b]

