[b][color=#000000][font=Times New Roman]Hi, I'm Johnny Knoxville, and I'm going to the moon![/font][/color][/b]

 
[font=Times New Roman][color=#000000]I dont even know what to say about Jackass 2. Its exactly what you expect. Ill note that I didnt necessary choose to see this film, but ended up going and laughing  a lot. There isnt a lot to it as regards to an actual film, but damn its entertaining. Its not something Id ever want to re-watch or ever get use to seeing, but it was worth checking out in a packed theater with everyone else there not believing how far these guys will go for a laugh. Sure, its filmed exactly like the television show and its pretty much the same as far as the show goes, but it makes money  a lot of money for not having any convinced plot in it. Its pretty much a movie for any college kids to laugh at and thats what its aimed at. Call it what you will, it delivers for those who are willing and knowing what theyre getting into. [/color][/font]
[font=Times New Roman][color=#000000][b]Grade: **1/2 / ****[/b][/color][/font]

[b][font=Times New Roman][color=#000000]Interview with the Vampire[/color][/font][/b]

[img]http://lestat.de.lioncourt1.free.fr/vamp5.JPG[/img]
 
[b][color=#000000][font=Times New Roman]For 30 years I had avoided that place. Yet I found my way back there with hardly an upward glance.[/font][/color][/b]
 
[font=Times New Roman][color=#000000]With a cast like Tom Cruise, Brad Pitt, Kristen Dunst, Christian Slater and Antonio Banderas, Id expect a really impressive film. While Interview with the Vampire is pretty decent effort, its not anything to call home about or praise any of these actors with the exception of Kristen Dunst who gives one of her, if not her best performance as a young girl who gets turned into a Vampire and is forced to live an immortal life in the body of a 10 year old. She takes her cute face and breathes terror into it as she becomes spoiled with blood and obsessed with her new life. Shes the only one who probably actually shows range. Its great to see Tom Cruise and Brad Pitt, two power houses today, act with one another and its even more fun to see Cruise as a evil, I couldnt even help to be bored that neither didnt give more than they had to, to make a good movie.[/color][/font]

 
[font=Times New Roman][color=#000000]Interview with the Vampire is probably one of the better vampire films and a very creepy film it falls short for a number of reasons. Part of which is the impressive cast that never delivers more than passable performances. Since it takes place well over a few centuries, the film has a large number of time jumps and traveling that just doesnt feel very smooth for the film. I understand that it takes place well over time, but it just suffers from the adaptation of book to film with those jumps. Same goes for Brad Pitts narration. Its still extremely creepy and something fun to breakout for Halloween, its not memorable. [/color][/font]
[font=Times New Roman][color=#000000][b]Grade: ** 1/2 / ****[/b][/color][/font]","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2006-12-10","","RT","900641968"
