4.5,"[img]http://i132.photobucket.com/albums/q19/jennidax/thedeparted_bigearlyposter.jpg[/img]
 
 
 
Wow, making up for lost time is what I am trying to accomplish with my movie marathon Saturdays. If it wasn't for my friend again, I would have stayed at work on Saturday until god knows when. That is part of the reason that I am depressed---because I have to work a 6th day tomorrow(Monday) All so I can take off from work from Dec 24 to Jan 2nd. A vacation!!! I haven't taken one of those since I flew to Boston a year and a half ago to see god(I mean Bono) in concert.
 
Well, here goes...My choices this week are again, as far apart in genre as I could possibly get.
 
We saw ""Borat"" first. I have heard soooooo much about how incredibly funny this film was. I guess my expectations were too far up there because all said--I was NOT impressed. I am not saying that the movie wasn't funny, or that I didn't laugh--I did, a lot. It was actually so funny for the first 15 minutes or so. After that, it got really old. It was the same thing for 90 minutes. I give Mr. Cohen credit, he pulled off a good character, and stayed well in character for the entire film. It was a bit over the top and in general, will appeal more to the male audience than the female. I would have enjoyed this more if I had waited to rent it in a few months.
 
Now, on to the film that was further up in my expectations than I thought. I have always been a Scorsese fan and have seen every one of his films. Although not set in his normal New York(I love New York) It was very typical Scorsese with his brilliant fades and gritty realism. The cast in this film was fantastic, everyone played well off of each other. They even got the accents pretty well down. My Leo again impressed. I like him more with each new film he does. And his accent was better in this film than the South African accent he had in ""Blood Diamond"" Even though my friend who speaks with South African people frequently and says Leo's accent was spot-on. We agreed on another subject, even though the buzz is all about Jack Nicholson---He better watch out because I think Leo out-shone him by a mile. Even though I liked the ending and was happy that Scorsese didn't hand everything on a silver platter to you---I want to know what was in the envelope. I can guess--obviously--but I still want to know.
 
Hopefully there will be another double feature next Saturday too.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2006-12-17","","RT","900730646"
