4.5,"[center][font=Century Gothic][img]http://us.movies1.yimg.com/movies.yahoo.com/images/hv/photo/movie_pix/warner_brothers/the_departed/thedeparted_bigearlyposter.jpg[/img][/font][/center]
[font=Century Gothic]Sometimes I worry that hype can ruin someone's opinion of a movie, but I saw the Departed several months after hearing everyone orgasm over it, and it didn't keep me from being insanely impressed. This is just a great cops and robbers movie, maybe the best I can think of. I never really got the whole Leonardo DiCaprio fascination before now, but he's just a bucket of gold in this movie, as are Mark Wahlberg, Martin Sheen, and the Nickels. I can't believe Scorsese directed something like this so late in his career; it was a lot like watching Munich last year and having to fork back over a lot of points to someone you thought was on the way out. The only thing keeping it from a perfect 10 for me personally is what I consider a merely decent performance by Matt Damon, and a fairly meaningless, inapplicable message about the ethics and consequences of snitching on your friends.[/font]","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2006-12-17","","RT","900909790"
