4.5,"Hi there to my film readers...
 
 I'm standing there on a line ...! wright ?
 
And I'm wondering if  Scorsese's new film [url=""http://best-movie-critique.blogspot.com/""]The Departed[/url] is gonna be that boring than his last 2 (Aviator and The Gangs Of  New York).
 The first thing came to my mind when I decided to go and see [url=""http://best-movie-critique.blogspot.com/""]The departed[/url] was ""how long is his new movie ?'. The answer came write away ... 2h and 45 min.
 Come on... I thought, I bored already ! All Scorsese last movies had good cast but their length made them so boring somewhere in the middle...
 I kind lost my faith in Scorsese abilities since Goodfellas and Casino, although before the movie I had fully believe in Damon's and of course in Nicholson's acting.
 
 And so the movie starts !
 
 With nice plot in the beggining and once again Nicholson in grate shape, fast dialogs with nothing extraordinary for a gangster film of course but makes you get anxious see if any of [url=""http://best-movie-critique.blogspot.com/""]the departers[/url] gets caught...
 
 You know not once in the film I get bored and that was by it's own one of the best things hapened to me in the whole movie. The thing I afraid the most in this movie makes me feel so comfortable that I didn't want The Departed to end.
 
 So for conclusion I finnaly think  it's time for Scorsese to get an Oscar (if Inarritu doesn't make the surpise !) even for direction or best film and the fact is I think he worth it and in his battle helps him the excellent actings from [b]Nicholson, [/b][b]Wahlberg and [/b][b]Damon.
 
 [b][b]U[/b][/b][/b]ntil my next post have a nice day and night ...

