4.5,"Some ratings of the last movies I watched in cinema in December.

- Will not talk too much about [I]Black Christmas[/i]. I don't like horror movies in general but this one was especially stupid and didn't have any kind of atmosphere. Garbage.

- I liked Breaking and Entering in the theatre but don't think about it afterwards, because the story is just not working, especially in the last half hour or so. It is overwritten and features some very poor dialogue. Still there are great performances by all the actors - especially Juliette Binoche and Robin Wright Penn - and the directing by Minghella is top-notch. 

- Did like Hollywoodland a bit more, even though I couldn't make anything of it a long time. It is not the neo-noir it wants to be, but it is a smart and highly entertaining film. Ben Afflack proves that he can act (even if I don't find his performance award-worthy) and Brody is great as always. The movie really picks up in the second hour.

- The Departed is not my movie of the year, but the best genre piece of the last years and the best Scorsese since a long time. Loved the story, loved the performances and directing - it should get some awards.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-01-02","","RT","900939403"
