4.0,"VERY GOOD. BUT...I prefer the hong kong original (infernal affairs).  I agree with infamous hugo when he says there is more character development than the original, but I found that infernal affairs 2 compensated for that.  I couldn't get used to the accents either they were a bit weak.  Ray Winston did the worst accent (he's english, trying to be american/irish) O.M.G! I loved Di Caprio's performance (accent was wobbley), Jack Nicholsons performance was inspired and Matt Damon was okay.  I just felt certain scenes were inferior to their originals, especially the bit with the police chief meeting up with the mole on top of the roof, that was an awesome scene in the original and it seemed like they blew it in the remake. certain jokes (that were taken from infernal affairs) didn't seem so funny in the remake either, but thats not to say it lacks wit or is badly written, it's not.  I laughed quite a few times, Alec Baldwin was hilarious as was Mark Whalberg.  The endings a bit ""hollywood"" too. To cut a long story short it's a great film and I would of scored it higher if it was original and better than Infernal Affairs, thats just my opinion.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-01-14","","RT","504204934"
