1.5,"The hype circling this film will peak the interest of many. That's what this piece attempts to overcome, it's hype. A high hope that when you throw talented actors, hot tail, and New England accents that it sorts everything out on its own. What this film suffers from is what it shoots to be: tough and unforgiving. It is not tough. It's hotshot mobster can't even hold his stance as ruthless. Further issues include why all the power players got to be in such positions when they played such idiots throughout the duration of this bloodfest. Who's the rat? Maybe the guy who used to be a cop! Why do the accents come and go every few scenes? I found they came out of hiding on lines that Scorcese wanted emphasized. Incredible. This film, for its appeal to the public masses, will receive high marks from most. I, however, will take no part in it.","",False,False,False,False,1.5,"2007-01-25","","RT","345944370"
