4.0,"The original is pretty solid overall, whereas Scorsese's film is grittier, has far more moments of suspense and tension, stronger characterization, a phenomenal visual prowess in storytelling, and an outstanding Jack Nicholson stealing the show amongst a number of near perfect performances -- Leo, Damon, Wahlberg, etc. the only weak link is a very bland Vera Farmiga. This isn't an emotionally resonant movie in the same vein as some of Scorsese's previous efforts (say, Raging Bull and The Aviator), and thankfully it doesn't set out to be. Scorsese isn't here to nab Oscars, he's here to have fun and make an accomplished action/crime thriller, and on that level he succeeds more than admirably, you can really see the director's energy and passion fused in every frame of this picture.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-01-28","","RT","209509975"
