5.0,"The Departed is not only one of (if not the best) film of 2006, it is also one of the best films in Scorsese's career. Truth be told he deserves the oscar more than anyone else does that night. But if Chicago's win for best picture in 2002 proves anything, it proves the best film doesn't always win.
  
 A grittier, more stylistic and entertaining take on Infernal Affairs, we see the world of modern day Boston through the eyes of a cop pretending to be a mobster and a mobster pretending to be a cop. Scorsese has a way of making us believe the story is inches away from outing one of these characters. I would call it suspension of disbelief, but he achieves something even greater, unpredictability.
 
 I would reccommend this movie simply for the dialogue and performances alone.  The most worthy examples of both of those come from Mark Whalberg and Jack Nicholson who admittedly steal the show.  Granted, they are given more to work with.  Ever wonder why the most extreme characters are usually not the main characters (a la Will and Grace?)  This is a career best for Mark Wahlberg who I never imagined being capable of such talent.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-02-04","","RT","900692720"
