2.0,"What a disappointment.  ""The Departed"" was all kinds of ""fucked up"", as they might say.  Everything about the movie was bad.  From the editing to the dialouge to the music selection...everything was horrible.

First...editing.  What the crud?  There were some editing decisions that just really didn't make sence.  For example, there was one part where the shot cut to a black screen with a hole in it circleing Matt Damon crossing a street.  Then the circle widened to the entire shot, and I'm sittin there thinking...why!?  What was the point?  We're in the middle of a scene, and they have an effect like that.  WHY?!?!  You really have to see it to get a good idea of how dumb that part was.  Other editing decisions I had a problem with was the quick cutting between shots, especially at the beginning becasue it gave the effect like it was just a collection of instead of a flowing sequence.  The constant cutting made the pace of the movie go really fast, which could disorient and confuse the audience.

Then, the music.  This was a serious movie, but the music was of an irish rock style...IRISH ROCK!!!  It was horrible.  And not only was the music horrible, but placement of the music was very untimely.  At times, you'd be sitting there trying to get into the movie, then all of the Irish rock starts playing.  Then, once you get use to it, the music just stops without warning.  Very untimely.  I hated it.

I really didn't like the dialouge, which had the word ""fuck"" or ""fickin'"" after every other word, but I can't complain too much about it because it's just how the language is in Boston.  And besides that, I've seen movies that had language 3x worst (like...""Running Scared""...eh ehm).

*SPOILER*

And what really ticked me off was everyone died!!!  How do you kill an all star cast?!?!  Martin Scorsese, the director, is an idiot.  ""The Departed"" should have never been made.

*End of Spoiler*

But after all of ""The Departed""s horribleness, what makes me hate this movie even more is how overrated by people.  How on earth can the Academy Awards give this film Best Picture?  How could they even NOMINATE it?

I think the only possitive thing I got out of this movie was that it wasn't called something like ""The Rat"" or ""The Mole"" or something stupid like that.  ""The Departed"" fit the movie perfectly becasue, litterally, everyone departed.

Like I said...Scorsese is and idiot and deserved nothing at the recent Academy Awards.","",False,False,False,False,2.0,"2007-02-12","","RT","462672823"
