3.0,":fresh: 3/4. Ill start by saying this is my second best film of 2006.Ive been waiting for a good Scorcese flick after a string of poor,and average ones.He finally breaks free by directing this hard nose film about corruption and betrayal in the mass. police unit. It is leaked that Frank Costello,(played to perfection by Jack Nicholson),has a guy working undercover in the unit. That character Colin Sullivan is played by Matt Damon. As they say fight fire with fire , the police without telling anyone, hire a man Billy Costigan(DiCaprio) to go undercover and find information on Costello. This film is filled with surprises. I really like the beginning when Costello says so brilliantly,""I don't want to be a product of my environment. I want my environment to be a product of me. Years ago we had the church. That was only a way of saying - we had each other. The Knights of Columbus were real head-breakers; true guineas. They took over their piece of the city. Twenty years after an Irishman couldn't get a fucking job, we had the presidency. May rest in peace. That's what the niggers don't realize. If I got one thing against the black chappies, it's this - no one gives it to you. You have to take it"".I think this really epitomizes what an asshole Costello is.
 
[center][img]http://www.smh.com.au/ffximage/2006/10/06/Departed_061006113718780_wideweb__300x375.jpg[/img][/center]
 
 
The acting in this film is top notch.Mark Walberg was great as the tough cop Dingam,Martin Sheen was also great as Queenen.I think come academy award time that Martin Scorcese should win best director,and I think Walhberg has a good chance at best supporting actor.I still am dumfounded how DiCaprio wasnt nominated for best actor. This was by far his best role to date. He was very believable in his role. Also,if you let it,this film really can get you.Im not gonna say what ,but some of the scenes really caught me off gaurd.Wonderful music also helped in the film. Overall just a fascinating good cop bad cop film.Though it aint no Taxi Driver or Goodfellas it is a very well done film. Also the rewatch factor of it isnt great.Definatley worth renting.One of the 10 best of 2006. 
 
[center][img]http://www.post-gazette.com/images4/20070222ho_scorsese_450.jpg[/img][/center]
 
 

[size=3][size=2]3-1-07 / I really dont think this way about the film anymore. I rewatched and It really isnt all that good. No way in hell should it have won best picture. The academy is just all politics. Glad for Scorcese yes but where was the academy in 1990 or 1976. Not a bad film but overrated.[/size] 
 
 
 
[/size]","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-02-14","","RT","900932265"
