5.0,"I've seen this film three times now, and each time it ends I can't wait to watch it again, which now I can(thank God for DVD.)  Scorsese is obviously a master director and this film shows why.  Many have compared this to GoodFellas, one of my favorite films, and said that Scorsese is returning to his roots, also bringing up Mean Streets.  But what makes this so good is that it's actually nothing like those other classics.  The story is taken from Infernal Affairs, and, while many will disagree, it is far superior.  I've heard it said that this film is very fast paced, but compared to Infernal Affairs it's practically slow.  What takes 5 minutes in Infernal Affairs takes 2o minutes in the Departed.  It sinks us into the world and by the time you come to the climax, which gets more suspensful with each viewing, you almost forget this is a movie.  I don't think it will win Best Picture but it deserves to.","",False,True,False,False,5.0,"2007-02-14","","RT","452231375"
