5.0,"My God. 
 
 It seems like there has rarely been a director that has turned out such consistantly great material, nominated that many times, and still has not won.
 
 Seriously, If the Oscars were truely the barometer of Hollywood that they pretend they are, Marty would have won countless times before. (And Chicago would not have beaten The Pianist (2002), and Shakespeare in Love sure as hell wouldn't have beaten Saving Private Ryan(1999). But I digress.)
 
 This time, Scorsese's remake of a Chinese film, Infernal Affairs, does not tread the same water that the majority of the asian remakes have done. Sure this doesn't fail like Pulse or The Grudge (or God forbid the Battle Royale remake thats in the works.), but most people can chalk that up to Infernal being of a completely different genre. Or that this remake has some actual talent behind and infront of the lens. But the fact is that Scorsese took a great film and elevated it to the status of being a masterpiece. 
 
 Scorsese has recieved noms several times in the past, and each time lost, even when nominated for some of his best work (Goodfellas, I'm looking at you.) I just have a feeling that he's going to follow in the Footsteps of Robert Altman. (5 Nominations, never won. Ended up getting the Honorary Lifetime achievement Oscar)
 
 I hope this year's Academy Awards prove me wrong.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-02-17","","RT","900953830"
