5.0,"[center][img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/movie/gallery/1159016/photo_18.jpg[/img]

[left][font=Courier New]There arent many moments when I say something like this, but here it is. [i]The Departed[/i] is one of those rare films that is actually superior than the original film. I loved [i]Infernal Affairs[/i], and was a little iffy about seeing [i]The Departed[/i] because I was upset that America felt the need to remake it. But after seeing [i]The Departed[/i], I can safely say that there is enough room in this world for the both of them.

Martin Scorsese is a shoe in for Best Director at this years Academy Awards. Though he isnt my personal pick, he is still pretty damn close to that title in in my eye. [i]The Departed[/i] is excellently filmed. But then again is that any surprise? Scorsese is one of the worlds best directors, and [i]The Departed[/i] shows he still has what it takes to make a superb film.

I loved watching Leonardo DiCaprio and Matt Damon as the films two moles. Im very surprised that neither were nominated for their roles, though DiCaprio is up for [i]Blood Diamond[/i]. But in [i]The Departed[/i] these two offer some of their best performances ever. And both generate the sort of onscreen appeal that keeps your eyes glued to the screen.

Jack Nicholson is probably my favorite actor of all time. So it makes me happy to see him playing a role like Frank Costello, rather than some weirdo in a dramatic comedy not that there is anything wrong with that. Jack was a blast to watch in this film. And is easily the best villain of 2006. Martin Sheen, Mark Wahlberg  and Alec Baldwin all deserve praise for their amazing performances as well.

[i]The Departed[/i] is just one of those films that works 100% perfectly. The pacing is perfect, as is the editing. And the story and its characters draw you in. With its two and a half hour run, I figured there would be a couple moments where my attention would drift off. But that never happened. [i]The Departed[/i] is just that damn good of a movie.[/font]
[/left]
[/center]","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-02-19","","RT","900669856"
