4.5,"Holy shit this was an amazing movie. I had been wanting to see this film for so long and couldn't see it in the cinema (damn age restrictions) but I finally got to see The Departed. And what a film it is.

First of all the cast is just superb. I mean Damon, Nicholson, DiCaprio, Wahlberg, Baldwin AND Sheen. All in the one movie! This is part of the reason I loved this film so much; the casting. Each character has their own style and way of dealing with things something that was just fun as hell to watch.

The twists and turns of the movie just keep you guessing the whole way through, right until the ending (which I will get too very soon). The random acts of killing and all round violence is shocking no matter how or when it happens.

Scorse has done a fine job at directing. I can safely say this is his best film in years, certainly since Goodfellas. But is it better than that? No. I can't believe someone could say that this is better than Goodfellas, it's not in my eyes anyway. But there is no need for downgrading this film by comparing it to something else.
The justified way to downgrade this film is, yes that's right; the ending!

I was totally confused with the ending, Didn't get it at all but once I found out what it actually meant then I ws kind of pissed off. I felt cheated. Why oh why did you have to include that last 10 seconds, Scorsese? It's hard to believe that a short amount of screen time can waste the last two and half hours but I think this ending did. It is the ending that has held me back from giving this the full stars. It's a shame.

Scorsese has made an excellent film. Great casting, amazingly written and with some twists and turns that you never see coming. It's a shame about the ending though.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-02-20","","RT","174105927"
