I wanted to like this film and thought this might finally be a Martin Scorcese film I can enjoy. I was 50/50 right. While not terrible like [i]Gangs of New York[/i], this film didn't blow me away either. I thought it was too long and Scorcese's style is just not my cup of tea as well as the gangster/mafia subject matter.
 
[i]The Departed[/i], adapted from a Hong Kong film that I haven't seen, is a spy vs. spy movie where the police have planted an undercover agent in Frank Costello's Irish mafia, and he himself has groomed a young man since childhood to be his eyes and ears in the police department. The two spies soon get wind of each other and it becomes a race on who can get to the other before they themselves are caught.
 
