4.0,"[color=yellow]Alright. Yet another brief rundown of the films I saw this past month:[/color]

[color=#ffff00][i]The Covenant[/i] was so stupid. I watched it twice because I thought I missed something, but then I realized that it was just a bad movie. And a bad script. It's like [i]The Craft[/i] meets [i]Mean Girls[/i] except with hormonal teenage boys in Ipswich. Confusing and craptastic. Renny Harlin. What's up with that?[/color]

[color=#ffff00][/color] 
[color=#ffff00]I love John Cena. Its weird, but I do. I find him adorable. I am sure that it would damage his wrestling champ persona to hear that I think of him as a big cuddly bear. However, cute does not a good actor make. [i]The Marine[/i] reminded me of [i]The Punisher[/i] with Robert Patrick in the crazed John Travolta role.[/color]

[color=#ffff00][/color] 
[color=#ffff00]I also love Helen Mirren. I am obsessed with her portrayal as Elizabeth I in HBO's mini-series [i]Elizabeth I.[/i] So, I had to see her as Elizabeth II in the Oscar nominated film [i]The Queen[/i]. She was note perfect. She doesn't even look like herself. Michael Sheen was also fantastic fledgling British Prime Minister Tony Blair. The film brought up interesting thoughts about generations and the cold, isolated lives of Britain's Royals. A real conflict between duty and popularity...appeasing the masses. However fictionalized about the death of Princess Diana and its aftermath, it certainly reverberated with a sort of sympathy for QEII. When she saw the stag on the Balmoral property and comments about the price at which it was caught and the hunters stalked it for miles--was she commenting on her own position or Diana's?[/color]

[color=#ffff00][/color] 
[color=#ffff00]Another person I love is Michel Gondry. [i]The Science of Sleep[/i] was visually great, trippy and innovative. It looked a lot like [i]Eternal Sunshine of the Spotless Mind[/i], but it did not have the strong story. The story in this one was all wonky. Oh, and it doesn't have the strong acting like the latter's either. Stephane (Gael Garcia Bernal) a head case, and I found no sympathy for him. The English/Spanish/French was confusing, too.[/color]

[color=#ffff00][/color] 
[color=#ffff00]I absolutely loved [i]The Departed[/i]. I bought it on DVD without seeing it and I made the right choice. Leonardo DiCaprio was fantastic Billy Costigan a cop working for the Irish Mafia and Matt Damon is a jerk (and I love him) and skeezy as a longtime Mafia soldier working for the cops. Mark Whalberg stole the movie for what little time he had in it. He was effing hilarious. And Jack Nicholson grossed me out--AGAIN. [/color]

[color=#ffff00][/color] 
[color=#ffff00]GIVE THE DIRECTING OSCAR TO MARTY SCORSESE! [/color]

[color=#ffff00][/color] 
[color=#ffff00]Laters. [/color]
[color=#ffff00]Courtney[/color]","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-02-23","","RT","900725718"
