[i]Domino (2005)[/i]: 
The Good: The only thing that's keeping me from giving this a 4 is that it's loosely based on a real story. That alone made it interesting to watch. The action scenes were well-done, and the acting was decent enough to carry the film along.

The Bad: About half-way through the film the editing drove me nuts. Similar to [i]Man on Fire[/i] in the way that it feels like you're on crystal meth while you watch it. That's not exactly appealing to me.

The Ugly: Color schemes.

