2.5,"Sigh... Infernal Affairs was SO much better, and without the amazing cast used in the original, this movie falls apart. It's almost a complete rip-off of Infernal Affairs, copying almost the entire second half and leaving out the cool parts (like the morse code, man!) Some of the character-building scenes work, I guess, but Leonardo is absolutely detestable and horribly twitchy and nowhere NEAR as brilliant and suave and convincing as Tony Leung. I mean, how did this guy become the most trusted dude in the gang?? I also hated how they separated Anthony Wong's character into like four different people, and watered down his coolness. Gah. It's OK if you've never seen the original, but it's really not that good of a movie.

