3.5,"[center][img]http://www.popmatters.com/images/film_art/d/departed-poster.jpg[/img]
 [/center]
 [size=4]
 Not a bad choice for best picture, but if it really was the best movie from 2006 than it was certainly an underwhelming year. The Departed was a solid, well written, well directed film. The pacing is quite good and the acting is very good considering how many people are in the cast. The accent work was some of the best I have ever seen in film. I will always be impressed by what a good director can do with actors I generally don't like.
 
 [/size][center][img]http://www.moviezine.se/filmbilder/026/departed.jpg[/img]
 [/center]
 [size=4]
 The biggest issue with the film was the editing. Which is an embarssment considering it won the award for best editing. It was riddled with continuity errors and jumpy cuts. Although The Departed is a solid flick, it just didn't blow me away. As with any best picture winner, you should definatly see it, but don't expect  perfection. [img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/user/smilies/fresh.gif[/img][img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/user/smilies/fresh.gif[/img][img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/user/smilies/fresh.gif[/img][/size]","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-02-28","","RT","900789434"
