4.0,"So I was expecting a package today.  A package worth over $50.  I wake up at 12 and go downstairs to look outside.  There's nothing here yet, so I figure it will come later today.  I go online to check the status and hm, it says it has been delivered.  I call my dad to see if he happened to pick it up this morning.  He says no.  I see it was delivered at 10:30 so I figure they must have made a mistake.  I call them up and they say it should have been delivered.  I start to get angry because I really wanted the package today.  They tell me they will send a message to the driver to call me.  He hasn't yet called.  No package has ever been stolen from my house, and that includes things such as guitars, subwoofers, amps, very expensive equipment.  Yet this small box somehow is the first thing to get stolen.  Blasphemy!  That driver has stolen my package and is hiding from the truth!  F'ing FedEx doesn't even ring your doorbell; you know why?  So their drivers can act like they came to your house but keep your package instead!  There is a conspiracy with this dirty company and I will never trust them again.

So I bought an old album by the Microphones.  It's very nice; spacial, atmospheric, and captivating.  I wish I could lose myself in it and stay there for at least a week.

Bloc Party's new album is ok.  Lyrically they've grown and they are going for a deeper and more emotional feel.  Sometimes it works and sometimes I just don't care.  I don't care about cocaine really.  But when they talk about something with substantial emotive effect and the music glistens and ascends into something special, they succeed.    But that's sometimes.

Arcade Fire.  Quite speechless about it.  There are a few songs that reach a lyrical content and style that I've been longing for.  The storytelling is wrapped in darkness and uncertainty.  And it absolutely mirrors my feelings on life.  This is a special album and one of the best I've heard.

Man did I love Little Miss Sunshine.  It's the type of movie that can make you believe in love again.  And I'm not talking about just companionship; I'm talking about loving life.  Simply awesome.

The Departed was pretty damn good but best picture?  Ehh, Pan's Labyrinth deserved that and didn't even win best foreign film.  Fuck the oscars.

I'm so bored.  I should write a song or something.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-03-01","","RT","900918679"
4.5,"It was about fricking time Scorcese won a Best Director Oscar. Though I really felt this was not his strongest work, it was still light years ahead of what most is churned out of Hollywood these days. There's also a reason why this won the Best Picture Oscar. Scorcese's story telling is at an all-time best in this one. I especially liked the use of The Rolling Stones songs in different scenes and plot movements of the film. A mind-blowingly good cast with Nicholson, Leonardo, Matt Damon and a stunning performance from Marky Mark Wahlberg, who somehow learned how to act. Bravo for you dude. Also one of Matt Damon's best performances. A great ending. Bloody. But a signature climax to a Scorcese film. He just doesn't do warm and fuzzy endings. An all-time classic.","df5ea73c-55ee-4d8a-b011-b6cb41aca734",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-03-01","","RT","435223952"
4.5,"nice and full of turns- i especially like that mark walberg is the hero","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-03-01","","RT","448770389"
5.0,"This is Martin Scorsese at his most confident, reinterpreting the Hong Kong based movie Internal Affairs and turning it into a Irish Boston based revenge driven mob movie with twists aplenty. And what a remake!! Yes, the plot is hard to keep up to track with with so much 2 take in and so many double crossings during the movie, but Scorsese deals with the multi layered plot like the top professional he is. He gets feisty but marvellous performances by Dicaprio and Damon, also great support from Mark Wahlberg, his most polished turn in years. But the show stealer in this movie is the formidable presence that is Jack Nicholson. He delivers his lines with such venomous wit, its infectious. Saying that all the actors are done by a favour by a very articulate script. The volence is brutal in places but what you expect in a mob movie?? So this is not for the faint heartest of people. But if you miss out on this classic, you should be ashamed. Deserved winner of Best Film at The Oscars and finally the academy has recognised Scorseses work for Best Director, this is a bonafide modern classic and if this is Scorseses swansong to the genre of gangster movies, then he can leave it with his head held high. A CINEMATIC EXPERIENCE TO REMEMBER!!","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-03-01","","RT","21119024"
