4.0,"I think my expectations were a little too lofty. Not to say that the movie wasn't great - it certainly was - but to me it was really just a fantastically-executed thriller rather than the new messiah of cinema that most have hailed it to be.

Of course, it's not The Departed's fault that my own personal bar was raised by hype, so it's fortunate that the movie has so many merits of its own. Everyone gives the performance of their careers. Jack Nicholson is evil, Matt Damon is gut-wrenchingly slimy and Leonardo DiCaprio has come a hell of a long way from Titanic.

The plot is intriguing, the dialogue is frantic and powerful, and the movie never lets up. There's always something on screen for the viewer to take in. The Departed uses its two and a half hour running time perfectly.

About time poor old Martin Scorsese picked up that Best Director Oscar.","",False,True,False,False,4.0,"2007-03-02","","RT","494497759"
