4.0,"[b]Zelig [/b]>> Very well made mockumentary. Not completely laugh out loud hilarious, but kept my attention for the most part.

[b]The Departed[/b] >> This was hard to decide on a rating. It was suspenseful with engaging characters. Shows the futilily of the efforts the characters endure to get in control. I am not quite sure why it was nominated for Best Picture though. Some of the jump cuts and score cuts seems too stylish and could come off as either sloppy or pretentious. Martin Sheen was not needed in the full roster, as well as the love triangle. Mark Walberg shines in a small yet deviant role. Leo and Matt are excellent as usual.

[b]Sympathy for Mr. Vengeance[/b] >> Ever since I saw the amazing [i]Oldboy[/i], I want to see this film by the same director. Offbeat, violent, and, oh yeah, vengeful.

[b]Stranger than Fiction[/b] >> Maggie Gyllenhaal is my girlfriend... I wish! Anyway, this film was witty and charming. However, it had some chiched elements of romantic comedies.

[b]Babel [/b]>> Expansive. Ambitious. Takes us around the world with characters struggling with personal crisis or the cause and effect of public crisis. These people are all linked in a chain reaction of events even before the film starts. I particularly enjoyed the Japanese segment. My least favorite was the trip to Mexico.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-03-03","","RT","900616225"
