4.0,"I have a lot of multi-part entries right now, jesus.  I don't know, I'm just being lazy in not making these their own entries, I guess.  Miller's Crossing was entertaining, but probably not rewatchable.  Not a favorite Coen brothers work.  American Beauty was fucking outstanding.  Three Kings was great as well, a military movie I could watch again (and probably again after that).  George Clooney, tell me when and where.
  
  And The Departed?  Fucking, that ending... fuck.  It was perfect for me.  For what I wanted out of the movie, it did it.  It really fucking did it.  [i]Outstanding[/i] ending to a great film.  Call me what you will, but I like revenge.  I don't need a fluffy ""everyone can turn out to be good, all is forgiven"" ending...

Good Night and Good Luck is a film I should have watched much sooner than today.  The McCarthy hearings are something I've always had an interest in, and this look at them through the Murrow angle was fantastic.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-03-04","","RT","900707909"
