4.5,"It wasn't the best film of the year (that honour would definately reside with The Fountain, and Children of Men would follow), but The Departed definately deserved it's Oscar wins.  People said this is Scorsese's return to form, to which I say - where'd he go that warranted a return?  His last GREAT film was Casino, and that was only 10 years ago.  Hell, The Aviator from a couple years ago was also excellent.  At any rate, this is Marty's 5th best flick.  Exciting, intense, wickedly funny, graphically violent - everything a great Scorsese film should be.  It has perfect music, fantastically choppy editing, a performance from Nicholson that is in my top 10 fav performances of all time, and of course, there's Marty's directing, that once again proves there comes a time in a filmmaker's life where he's so good, he can break whatever rules he wants.  I love him, and I love this film.","",False,True,False,False,4.5,"2007-03-06","","RT","168016709"
