4.5,"Damn good movie.  We have two problems.  One -  Hollywood has run out of ideas for good movies.  More and more is starting to turn to remakes of foreign films, particularly asian films without properly crediting them.  The first credit on screen should have been a reference to INTERNAL AFFAIRS.  Without that movie this would have been nothing.  So they make this movie and don't reference Internal affairs properly, which is probably a better movie.  They should make a rule for remakes of asian films.  Underneath every title of a asian remake, it should say  A REMAKE OF AN ASIAN FILM.  Therefore the title should say  THE DEPARTED - A REMAKE OF AN ASIAN FILM  It's just that the american public can't stand a movie without americans in it, so Internal Affairs will never recieve its proper due.

