1.5,"[img]http://www.popmatters.com/images/film_art/d/departed-poster.jpg[/img]
[size=1]Why was the film met with so much praise? Because of the casting and direction. Believe me, if Scorsese hadn't directed this and/or if this film didn't have an all-star cast but still had the same look it would have been seen as a b-movie that would go nowhere. And that is what it is. A completely over rated film. [/size]
 
[size=1]The story and the ending were ridiculous. How hard could it be to figure out who the mole was? Costello works with the same five guys on EVERY job. Four of them have worked with him for some time. One hasn't and after he joined the leaks start. How hard is that? Seriously? [/size]
 
[size=1]I don't understand how anyone can applaud any of the acting. Matt Damon doesn't emote at all. Leonardi DiCaprio has never impressed me as an actor. This is no exception. Mark Wahlberg's detective has to be one of the most annoying characters ever. Always pissed off and sarcastic as hell, for what? It's a wonder that he is even there, he has no role to play at all. An omission of his character wouldn't have made the movie any less. Vera Farmiga by default gives the most adequate performance, but even she doesn't display the same amount of depth she did in Down to the Bone (a far, far superior movie). And although I generally like him, Jack Nicholson is so over the top it was painful to watch.[/size]
 
[size=1]I question all of the Oscar wins. Not one aspect was award worthy. I'm left to wonder if the film wasn't just awarded as a pity prize for Scorcese's multiple loses over the past thirty years. He should have been passed over again.[/size]","",False,False,False,False,1.5,"2007-03-12","","RT","900909117"
