2.5,"Let me make this crystal clear. Crime movies are SO not my thing. Especially brutal, swear-ridden bloodbaths such as this. This,  however, was the gangster movie example for my pop culture class, so watch it I did. It was... bearable. Totally not my cup of tea, but bearable. Basically one guy's a cop pretending to be a gangster, and the other guy's a gangster pretending to be a cop. They both know there are rats afoot, so they run around in circles chasing each other and playing both sides. Then basically everyone - and I mean everyone - croaks. Whee. I watched this insanely early in the morning, so I found all that a little hard to follow. I also found the decisive lack of strong female characters a big turn-off. The women in this movie are only around to screw with and make derogatory comments about. I REALLY didn't like that. I will say that the many death scenes were quite memorable, dramatic, and - one in particular - quite shocking. I jumped. But in all honesty, there really wasn't anything I found overwhelmingly amazing about this movie. It's just more crime stuff, and I've had enough of that already on TV. Meh.","",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2007-03-14","","RT","216046805"
