4.5,"Thank God this won Best Picture!
 
    [img]http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v253/Rizik/Departed.jpg[/img]
 
   The Departed is some of the best storytelling Ive seen for a while. It tells a story of duel protagonists acting as undercover rats as Jack Nicholsons character says it. With these dual protagonists, come duel antagonists, played by Nicholson and Martin Sheen (along with Alec Baldwin and Mark Wahlberg), you get an amazing sense of tension being pushed onto the protagonists, as they also act as the driving force against each other. Ah, its so nice to get a good drama.
 
    [img]http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v253/Rizik/departed1.jpg[/img]
 
   Scorsese does an absolutely awesome job at giving the audience the right amount of information at the right times, that just multiplies the plot threads into a twisting and exciting climax. Every scene felt seamless in its execution, the pacing dictated this. With two venues to go down, this movie jumps around a LOT. Every scene kept a great beat, and had an overall purpose towards the climax (unlike a certain Babel). Oh, it makes me giddy, because the ending is just how I like them too.
 
    [img]http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v253/Rizik/departed2.jpg[/img]
 
   For me, Mark Wahlberg stole the show for me. He just cracked me up with his over the top lines that fit really well. Its ashamed that he didnt get the Oscar for it, Alan Arkin dies in his movie. :P
 
     This is top notch entertainment right here. Along with the Prestige and Pans Labyrinth, this is one of the most solid pieces of film of 2006. 
 
     A 9.5 for this one. Just spectacular.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-03-15","","RT","900845766"
