5.0,"Seeing the two kids from the Basketballs Diaries sparring verbally again was a bit of a highlight for me though I'm not sure why. Perhaps it was the moment when it finally dawned on me that Mark Wahlberg was actually quite a diverse actor rather than a one note pony. (I probably should have realised that when, as Tommy Corn in I Heart Huckabees he had me in stitches but apparently I'm too stupid.)

Anyway, an excellent film with a complex plot that is done SO well that it never SEEMS complex. DiCaprio is probably at his peak here. At least so far. He was REAL as Costigan and impressed me no end. Scorsese has such a good handle on violence that it must come naturally to him to make it look so damn nice and yet mesmerisingly realistic. An awesome script accompanied by a brilliant director, fantastic cinematography and incredible acting make this a damn fine film. Oh and let's not forget the insanely powerful Irish band, the dropkick murphys', musical input that really underscored certain parts of the movie with more emotional resonance.

