4.0,"A fiendishly, well-executed gangster film and a breath of fresh air from Scorsese who hasn't made anything this good since Goodfellas.  The casting is terrific.  Damon, DiCaprio, Walbergh, and Baldwin are surprisingly good under Scorsese's lean direction.  It's especially great to see Nicholson pull off the mob boss without falling into the trap of what could have easily become self-parody.  It's no Goodfellas or Taxi Driver but it's miles above the tepid Gangs of New York or the overly-ambitious The Aviator.  The Departed is remarkable for how well-paced it is and for how effortlessly it pulls off what it sets out to do--which is to entertain the hell out of us.  The Departed is a modern crime classic in pulp cinema.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-03-17","","RT","157150836"
