4.0,"[center][img]http://www.iwatchstuff.com/images/2006/08/departed_poster_utilizes_ba.jpg[/img]

[left]
    [i]The Departed[/i] may not have what I loved so much about [i]Goodfellas[/i] but there's something about Scorsese's work here that captures my attention fully. Mostly, I think it's the amazing work of actors like Nicholson, Damon, and DiCaprio (also not too mention Whalberg) that makes the movie what it is.
    The story itself isnt entirely new or different from past mobster flicks but the actos tend to keep your mind up to pace and hanging in there despite the fact that one can become totally lost in what's actually going on in the film.
    There are two negative points I give this film.

    1) Length - let's face it...today's majority of people cannot sit there and watch a film reaching the 3 hour mark without any sort of boredom or inner voice yelling ""when will this be over?!"" despite how much they enjoy the movie. There was enough substance to justify the length but some parts feel unnecessary and too drawn out.

    2) Like I mentioned...the plot and story becomes mumbled at times and doesnt really keep attentions too well.

Also, if you're not a fan of the F-word dont see this movie...this has more F-word drops than you could imagine and even got me (a constant swearer) to the point where I thought most if not all of time was unnecessary.
[/left]
[/center]","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-03-18","","RT","900825890"
