4.5,"Occasionally, new DVDs will find themselves joining my family of films. They may command special viewing (ie NOT in alphabetical order) especially if the movie is new to DVD, which is the case for these four DVDs I've watched recently.
 
[b]Casino Royale[/b] was good...I suffer from reading too many reviews of the film, though, and I expected to be blown away. I, to put it simply, was not. I felt it was real and gritty enough, but the cheesiness of past Bond flicks made them Bond flicks. [b]GoldenEye[/b] will always be a favorite of mine as will [b]Tomorrow Never Dies[/b]. That's not to say the movie wasn't good...it was (8 out of 10, hello) but it definitely wasn't as great as many claimed it to be.
 
Now, [b]The Departed[/b], was every bit as good as people said it was - though I don't think it's Best Picture good. But, then again, what do I know? [b]Crash [/b]was and [b]Brokeback Mountain[/b] was not. Oh, well. Talk about blurring the lines between good and bad!
 
When you mix Cameron Diaz, Jack Black, Jude Law and the incomparable Kate Winslet, you absolutely cannot go wrong. [b]The Holiday[/b] was easily one of the most watchable films of 2006. As romantic comedies go, it's bound to be a classic in the mold of [b]You've Got Mail[/b], [b]Something's Gotta Give[/b] and [b]Love Actually[/b]. Winslet truly elevates every movie she's in, making better a film that could have been tired and cliche.
 
While watching [b]Hollywoodland[/b], I kept thinking back to [b]L.A. Confidential[/b] and how great that film was. Though [b]Hollywoodland[/b] never quite attains [b]Confidential's[/b] level of virtuosity, the film highlights Ben Affleck's surprisingly spot-on performance of George Reeves, the original Superman. His untimely death led to much speculation in early Hollywood and this forms the basis of the plot. The film definitely intrigues, and as a self-proclaimed lover of history, I had to read up on the mystery around George Reeves.
 
And that, my friends, gets you all caught up on my current DVD watching status. I've got a long way to go to watch all of my movies before December 31st this year, but the year is still somewhat young. I can still do it! Check out my lists to see a ranking of my DVDs as I watch them. I will likely update that more frequently than my journal, but one never knows! Tootle-oo!","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-03-19","","RT","900749700"
