4.5,"[size=3][font=Times New Roman][color=white]Here are a few REALLY stupid things I have [u]accidentally[/u] done in the past couple of days. [/color][/font][/size]
 

 
[size=3][font=Times New Roman][color=white]1.  Stopped at a green light. I should probably not daydream while Im driving [/color][/font][/size]
 
[font=Times New Roman][size=3][color=white]2.  Tripped down the stairs. Im always doing this. Im going to break something one day.[/color][/size][/font]
 
[font=Times New Roman][size=3][color=white]3.  Inhaled a grape slushy too fast. Brain freeze hurts![/color][/size][/font]
 
[font=Times New Roman][size=3]4.  Dumped Marinara all over everything in my truck.   [/size][/font]
[font=Times New Roman][size=3][/size][/font] 
[size=3][font=Times New Roman][color=white]5.  Punched myself in the face. Trust me, it can be done. People will laugh at you. I would have laughed at me. [/color][/font][/size]
 

 
[font=Times New Roman][size=3][color=white]Here are the reviews I promised. Im not that much of an in depth movie reviewer. Sorry! Next week we will have Little Miss Sunshine, Pans Labyrinth, and Ghost Rider. [/color][/size][/font]


 
[font=Times New Roman][size=3][color=white]Cars[/color][/size][/font]
 

 
[size=3][font=Times New Roman][color=white]Yes, Im just NOW seeing this. It was a good movie. I just have a sinking feeling that I will compare every pixar film to The Incredibles from now on. Even Pixars worst stuff is better than 75% of the other crap out there. [/color][/font][/size]
[size=3][/size]

 
[font=Times New Roman][size=3][color=white]My Super Ex-Girlfriend[/color][/size][/font]
 

 
[size=3][font=Times New Roman][color=white]I had heard such horrible things about this movie that I didnt expect much going in. I didnt think it was that bad. It was fun and cute and good enough for the type of movie it was supposed to be. Plus I would probably watch an Everybody Loves Hypnotoad marathon if it was starring Rainn Wilson. [/color][/font][/size]
[size=3][/size]

 
[font=Times New Roman][size=3][color=white]The Departed[/color][/size][/font]
 

 
[font=Times New Roman][size=3][color=white]I was making necklaces while I was watching so I had to ask Charles what happened! a lot. Pay back! He always asks me what someone said even if he is staring at the screen and is paying full attention. The plot was good without being too pretentious or overcomplicated. The actors were great and there was lots of violence. What more do you need for a good movie?[/color][/size][/font]","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-03-20","","RT","900771907"
4.0,"A much better film than I was expecting it to be.  As an Oscar winner, I was skeptical of its worth, but was pleasantly surprised.  Martin Scorsese has really pulled out alll the stops in this film, which is full of decent actors and gripping suspense.  Leo has fiinally proven that he can actually act, so that we can forget about those 'King of The World' days! Unexpected twists and turns-will have you glued to your seat.  The best gangster movie since Goodfellas.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-03-20","","RT","15853376"
