4.5,"omg, this film is amazing. one of the best perspective movies around. martin scorsese did a wonderful job directing this film; tasteful in art yet not distracting. the performances are terrific from all sides of the film. the plot revolves around the boston police department and the mafia; both sides are searching for a rat in their organization that is actually working for the other side. the only criticism of the film i have is that it is a bit hard to follow, and if the audience isn't on the same page as the story, then the filmmakers haven't done their job in keeping our interest. but if you do realize what is going on, the enjoyment of the film ensues. although it is a crime/drama, there is definitely an apparent hilarity to the film that only matches the works of william shakespeare. the title of the film, the departed, is so appropriately named that you can't help but be amused when the movie is finished. the big picture and moral of the film hovers around the concept that when one gets involved w/ crime, EVERYBODY gets screwed, so much to the point where no one, not even the audience, knows whom to trust, or for whom they are working. i wasn't sure i was going to like this film, but in the end i definitely think it was worth it!","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-03-26","","RT","489544420"
