3.5,"I am not what you would call a Scorsese fan, so I was surprised by how much I liked this movie. The cast was fantastic - I've always liked DiCaprio and Damon and it's always good to see them flex their acting muscles and prove they're more than just pretty boys. Nicholson does scary evil very well - and Martin Sheen makes an unlikely but brilliant good cop to Wahlberg's bad. The plot is about as original as you are going to get in this genre of movie - and the tension is superbly built as Costigan and Sullivan race to uncover each other's identities. However... [SPOILER ALERT] I did feel like the script kinda faltered towards the end - as though they weren't sure how to end it so the storyboard just read ""...and then everyone shot each other."" I also think that Scorsese tries too hard as a director - in every scene he tried a new fancy camera angle or effect, as though trying to prove he deserves that Oscar that he's yet to win. In the end I felt it made the overall production feel a little visually jarring - and not in a good way.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-03-26","","RT","122574735"
