5.0,"What is the deal with people complaining about the fact that ""The Departed"" was a copy of ""Infernal Affairs""? You guys do realize it's a remake, and it's bound to have a few things in common with the original, right? it is of the opinion of this movie fan that ""Infernal Affairs"" is a very good movie...that said, ""The Departed"" is the best American film since ""Saving Private Ryan""! First off, the acting. Pitch perfect, you will not see better ensemble acting anywhere. The cast is incredible starting with Leonardo DiCaprio and Matt Damon, who often get dissed because of the fact that they were once ""pretty boys"". Let me set the record straight, these guys can act, they know what they're doing, and this film is exibit A! Then you have the supporting players...Alec Baldwin, Martin Sheen, Ray Winstone, Mark Wahlberg...all absolutely amazing! Then you have the king of them all...Jack. Some people say Jack was doing little, but chewing up scenery in this film. To which I reply...you will not see a more truthful portrait of evil anytime soon. Jack is not over the top, Frank Costello is over the top! And Jack knocks it out of the park! But the biggest surprise for me was the seldom mentioned Vera Farmiga as Madolyn. I had know idea who she was before this movie, now I'm going to be first in line for her next movie. In a part that could've been fluff in the hands of another (weaker) actress, she adds a life and a subtlety to a woman who is every bit as unsure of her life as the two lead roles. That's the big difference in Martin Scorsese's ""The Departed"". While the same plot elements are here, the human truthfulness, that can only be given by actors and a good script. But does that make Scorsese worthy of an Oscar? You bet it does! The best directors in the game know when to step back and let their actors do the work, and with a cast like this, Marty made the right choice. Plus, no one picks a soundtrack like Scorsese, The Rolling Stones, Pink Floyd, The Beach Boys, Nas, Dropkick Murphys, Patsy Cline, should I go on? While ""IA"" is a terrific film, ""The Departed"" is made that much better because of a deft script, and most importantly, the actors. The best film of the decade thus far!","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-03-29","","RT","900735102"
4.5,"Martin Scorsese created one of his more interesting masterpieces.  This isn't your average movie especially by Scorsese standards.  The acting is perfect and the tone shifts so dramatically but still feels natural to perfection.  This is one of the few times there is a remake of a movie that is on par and even surpasses the original at times.  It was almost a carbon copy of the original but still maintains it's own identity.  Leonardo is showing more potential than I would have ever expected.  I think he has learned more from Scorsese than I felt he deserved but they proved my wrong.  I just hope he is able to carry what he has learned into other jobs because I am looking forward to seeing where his career goes.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-03-29","","RT","700009207"
