5.0,"[center][font=Century Gothic][size=3]Well again here is a movie that my husband wanted to watch and I didnt yet I ended up liking it. I really need to wake up and smell the coffee and just start watching what he wants to watch. I end up liking it every time. What movie might I be talking about? The Departed. I know you probably wondering why the heck would I not want to watch it? Ehhh not sure. But I didnt. [/size][/font][/center]
[center][font=Century Gothic][size=3][/size][/font] [/center]
[center][img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/movie/gallery/1159016/photo_04.jpg[/img][/center]
[center] [/center]
[center][font=Century Gothic][size=3]The state police force in South Boston is waging an all out war on Americas organized crime. Billy Costigan (Leonardo DiCaprio) is basically forced into an assignment to infiltrate the mob run by Frank Costello. (Jack Nicholson) Billy quickly blends right in and gains Costellos confidence. While all this is going on Colin Sullivan (Matt Damon) is quickly rising in the state police. What people dont know is that he is an informer for Costello. Each of the men is consumed in their double lives. When it becomes crystal clear to the police that there is a mole among them, Billy and Colin are suddenly in great danger of being exposed for the rat that they are. Each races to uncover the identity of the other to save themselves. But are they willing to turn on everything they have known to save their own lives?[/size][/font][/center]
[center][font=Century Gothic][size=3][/size][/font] [/center]
[center][QUOTE] You accuse me once, I put up with it. You accuse me twice... I quit. You pressure me to fear for my life and I will put a fucking bullet in your head as if you were anybody else. Okay? [/QUOTE] [/center]
[center] [/center]
[center][font=Century Gothic][size=3]What can I say about this movie other than it deserved every single award it got. The story is instantly compelling and a bit unbalanced but it is quite appropriate. The editing of the movie was a bit jagged and jumpy but it works well. It helps give that constantly looking over your shoulder feeling that all the characters had. [/size][/font][/center]
[center][font=Century Gothic][size=3][/size][/font] [/center]
[center][img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/movie/gallery/1159016/photo_34.jpg[/img][/center]
[center] [/center]
[center][QUOTE]  Police Tech: Who the fuck are you? 
Dignam: I'm the guy who does his job. You must be the other guy. [/QUOTE] [/center]
[center] [/center]
[center][font=Century Gothic][size=3]As far as the acting goes it was pretty solid. Jack Nicholson who normally steals a movie was outshined by DiCaprio, in my eyes. While he plays a good role DiCaprio just stole the whole movie. DiCaprio was solid, and I normally detest him but loved him as Costigan. Damon as always was Damon. While Im not a fan at all of him he did well. Other notables were Alex Baldwin, Martin Sheen, Mark Wahlberg and more. Every role in this film was really done well. I cant really say anything bad about the acting. [/size][/font][/center]
[center][font=Century Gothic][size=3][/size][/font] [/center]
[center][img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/movie/gallery/1159016/photo_01.jpg[/img][/center]
[center]Oddly enough for some reason at this point of the movie I was rooting for DiCaprio to hit Damon and make him scream like a girl. [/center]
[center] [/center]
[center][font=Century Gothic][size=3]In a time where there is a crap load of well crap coming out on DVD and into the theatres this movie shins. If you havent watched this yet then give it a chance. [/size][/font]
