4.5,"After three times, I think I can finally talk about this movie. The first thing I'll note is that only for Scorsese is this not a five-star movie: Raging Bull and Taxi Driver are miles ahead of this one. And yet, it's still a great movie... 

The second thing I feel that I should say is that Blood Diamond was almost as good... what makes a ""Best Picture"" is always hard to define. Both really different, and both really good, either movie would have been deserving most years. I think it was just Scorsese's ""turn,"" in the Academy's eyes - I mean, you can only screw a guy over so many times.

To only talk about this movie, though, I guess I'm still pretty much speechless. The ending is what does it for me... I want to know what happens next... to give us 2.5 hours and still leave the viewer wanting more, I guess that's why it won. DiCaprio, again, in a great performance in which he outshone Matt Damon and ol' Jack alike - the tension in DiCaprio's character is just outstanding, and the whole movie turns around it. One to watch again and again, no question.","",False,True,False,False,4.5,"2007-04-07","","RT","463897201"
