4.5,"A Scorcese Masterpiece.....Need i say more?? The film may be adapted from an award-winning Hong Kong blockbuster titled ""Infernal Affairs"", yet for those of us who don't understand Chinese, this is as much an original! The plot is fantastic. Leonardo DiCaprio,Matt Damon and Jack Nicholson share the spotlight, each delivering powerful performances in their respectful roles that are more than praiseworthy! Mark Wahlberg performs his relatively shorter role to its optimum, raising hopes of a Scorcese classic to unfold! The story is incredible, a mafia man infiltrated the Boston P.D., while at the same time, a police officer infiltrates the same Irish mafia, headed by the incomparable Jack Nicholson. For years, they relay information and tip-offs to their secret employers, before a series of mistakes alerts them to each other's presence and compromises their safety in their surroundings! The race now begins for each to uncover the other mole before his own cover is blown! The action in the movie is fantastic, and in true Italian style, Scorcese spares no amount of gore to make the film seem as true-to-life as possible! Swears and curses fly around everywhere, as families who've come to watch the family cover their children's ears! The action is thick and fast, the music at the background is excellent, and the movie keeps moving along at a good pace without ever slowing down! It's an excellent film, one of the best I've seen in a long time! Miss it if you dare!","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-04-16","","RT","698604899"
