4.5,"Another Scorsese Masterpiece! ""Good Fella's"" is one of my fave. and yet I hated all of ""The Godfather's"" (I know, I know, lol..) so I was interested to see how I was going to like this movie. I think that this had such young fresh actors and the movie took on such complex perspectives automatically drew me in even though the ending which I won't reveal left me reeling a la classic Scorsese style. Di Caprio who is turing out to be one of the most versatile and classic actors has grown in such huge leaps and bounds from his petulant and narcissistic days of ""The Titanic"". He mesmerized me and I absolutely forgot every movie role he's undertaken while watching  him here, which shows what a classic actor he's done instead of being a character actor. Jack Nicholson was great as the charismatic and dark boss, yet you either like Jack or not, I teeter between the two, yet he will always be Jack, not a classical actor like some of the young bucks in this movie. For this movie he worked. Matt Damon is another chameleon who charms in one movie as a real likeable character and then in another like this movie oozes with a deadly charm. I just saw ""The Good Shepherd"" and he couldn't have been more different. Kudos to him. I also always love watching Mark Walhlberg, who leapt off the screen like a cougar with his intensity. He's another character actor, but he's so full of passion and intelligence that he always manages to win me over. Martin Sheen is a classic actor and even though he didn't have a lot of screen time, his presence was felt all through the movie, esp. touching Di Caprio's character the most in some of the most raw and vulnerable scenes. A character and actor I've never seen before playing a therapist, Vera Famiga, was wonderful too. Her honesty and authenticity was believable in an amazingly difficult job esp. when forced between being a professional ""counselor"" and girl-friend between Damon's twisted character and Di Caprio's tortured character. I don't know if I could sit down and watch this movie over and over again, but I do know that I will watch it again and feel all the intensity, admire the brilliance of the movie and still feel relieved when it's over...","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-04-21","","RT","537660834"
