3.5,"ok... finally seen it...

it isn't a bad film but.....
it doesn't do or add anything that the HK original doesn't do better. In fact if I were to do a back to back comparison, Id say that this version isn't as good in many areas.

i) the translation into the west has meant that the buddhist themes, something that ties the charcters together so strongly in the HK film is missing. While the HK film ends up being a character study, this is more about the plot and as such is a simpler film. To me, the result is that this film loses a lot of what makes the HK one that little bit more special than the rest and what makes this film not so special.

ii) the characters aren't fleshed out enough or have the same depth as their HK equivilants. THe very little we see of them is more or less superficial and we don't get the internal struggle of the characters. Again, this lacking element means that you lose a bit of what makes the HK film that cut above the rest.

iii) the Hk film takes the traditional HK version of gangster and undercover plot and in a way pays serious homage to them and as such is crafter around the usual HK tv/cinema imagery but each with a twist and a little tongue in cheek. Again, with this missing, some things just don't seem to make sense in this version of the screenplay.

Remember, I'm not saying that this is a bad film because it isn't, far from it. The film is very well made and very polished and very controlled. It just loses something in the translation. They've done a good job in taking what works and losing what doesn't as I imagine it takes a brave soul to cut bits of the screenplay of a film that has such a huge reputation. 

Go see this.....


...but make sure you see the HK version first.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-04-26","","RT","153708116"
