2.5,"When ""The Departed"", a bloated, overlong remake of a recent Chinese movie, ""Infernal Affairs"", won the Best Picture Oscar this year, I said that we'd see even less creativity out of Hollywood and we'd have foreign films remade with increasing frequency.

Well, it'st starting. And it's starting with some really lame excuses to hide the creative bankruptcy and quests for Oscars the lazy way.

[quote]
The Oscar-winning Best Foreign Film is to be remade as a Hollywood movie. German espionage drama ""The Lives Of Others"" will be revamped as an English-language film with moviemakers Sydney Pollack and Anthony Minghella coming together for the project. 

Pollack tells trade paper Daily Variety, ""We would just desperately love for that film to be something that reaches more people. We haven't gotten locked into making it yet, but we're working hard at trying to get it going."" 

The film's writer/director Florian Henckel Von Donnersmarck claimed Oscar gold for the film in February.
[/quote]

So, now they can't even wait a year before starting their remakes. Pathetic is too mild a word for this. 

Hey, Pollack! If you ""just desperately love for that film to be something that reaches more people"" how about licensing it for various markets and getting some great translators and casts of really good voice actors together and do an English dub, a French dub, and a Cantonese dub? 

Of course, if you do that, you wouldn't be able to pretend you're not trying to slack your way to an Oscar nomination by redoing an already great movie.

(By the way, ""Das Leben der Anderern"" is a GREAT movie that you should see--it's one of the best political dramas every put on film. The same goes for ""Infernal Affairs""--it's a must-see if you like clever police dramas. I think you should stay away from the remakes, whether it's ""The Departed"" or the planned ""The Lives of Others"" remake. There's no reason for these remakes to exist, other than lazy filmmakers and timid financial backers looking to sponge off someone else's creativity.","",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2007-05-04","","RT","900810146"
