5.0,"<i>""THE DEPARTED CELEBRATES THE RETURN OF MARTIN SCORSESE ! ""</i>
<br></br>
To watch a story that built with high-complexity and so deceiving from the very beginning to the jaw-dropping ending where everybody's dead,including Billy Costigan who deserves his happy ending,and foolishly dead in the very last second,  is like riding a gigantic <b>nerve-twisting rollercoaster</b> with big loops along the way.The Departed is a modern-day Scorsese's masterpiece.After gained triumphant with all-time-best-movies like Goodfellas,Raging Bull,and Taxi Driver,Martin Scorsese cameback in the<b> BIG</b> way,also shows the world that he's still Martin Scorsese he used to be,a grand architect to a movie like Taxi Driver,but apparantly from now on,the new-generation of  audience will know him as Martin <i>""The Departed""</i> Scorsese,as the legacy of this movie continue with the Oscar's <b>""The Best Picture""</b> in his hands. 
The acting is no less breathtaking,<u>Leonardo DiCaprio</u>,who plays <i>Billy Costigan</i>,is in his best performance in a long while,<u>Matt Damon</u>,who plays <i>Colin Sullivan</i> also balanced Leonardo's strong performance as the bad guy,meanwhile,is it really appropriate to question <u>Jack Nicholson</u> himself in this movie?Again,a role to prove the world that he's a <u>master-class</u> acting machine,this time as,<i>Frank Costello</i>,an unpredictable mafia-boss,even in his brightest smile.<u>Wahlberg</u>,in his Oscar-nominated role,always be the <b>SCENESTEALER</b> everytime he appears in the screen,and the other one that barely took my attention is <u>Vera Farmiga</u>,who nailed her performance as both Sullivan's and Costigan's love interest.
Beside the breathtaking acting ensemble,<b>The Departed also has enough tension to rock your nerves,grandly twisted and definitely a modern-day crime classic.</b>
Martin Scorsese <u>re-declared</u> his place in the tight-race of world's greatest film-maker,and we,the audience,have a blast after leaving the cinema!<br><font size=""3""><b>A crime-classic.</b></font></br>","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-05-06","","RT","402973285"
