Leonardo was also a joy to watch.

How they keep the accents going is beyond me.
Great movie","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-05-08","","RT","417142846"
5.0,"The Departed is the exact confirmation of Martin Scorsese's title as the single greatest director of modern times. The film crosses familiar territory for Scorsese, and fortunately, he knows the crime genre extremely well. Fortunately, with an all star cast, no member is left out or excluded in any manner. Scorsese found just enough screen time for each character to be recognized. 

Leonardo DiCaprio officially received his title as one of the greatest actors of modern times with his role in <i>The Aviator</i>, and he returns in another Scorsese picture that proves him as much more than a pretty face. Jack Nicholson, in the role of Frank Costello is unforgettable, and will hopefully be recognized in yet another Oscar worthy role. Matt Damon is perfectly cast as a very likeable man, yet extremely evil in terms of the character's morals. 

There aren't enough words to properly describe <i>The Departed</i>'s sheer genius. Watching this film's theatrical trailer does not instill the excitement and suspense that the film itself delivers to the audience. Though not quite Oscar material, I strongly wish that voters will discover that Scorsese is a director with a long overdue award. <i>The Departed</i> is a masterpiece that works more than just another crime thriller. One reason for its genius is the fact of how each and every event is played through. Its lack of cliche makes it an instant classic, as most of the final scenes will leave viewers breathless. Extremely powerful material mixed with breathtaking cinematography, and outstanding performances makes <i>The Departed</i> one of the best pictures of 2006.

UPDATE: Upon 3 to 4  repeat viewings, this film loses quite a bit of its ""shock"" factor. Part of the reason for this film's success was relied upon its ability to surprise audiences. When the outcome is evident, the film loses a lot of my original excitement. It is a great film, no question. However, I don't hold it in the same regards as I once did.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-05-08","","RT","127520289"
