3.5,"Infernal Affairs is just so much better. There is no question. Scorsese took a brilliant, slick thriller and turned it into a rather bloated, tired old gangster movie. Scorsese threw fat on the lean bones.

Jack Nicholson is in his element, almost too much so, we know this character, we know these faces, we feel a certain sense of predictability in a character which should really be off the walls. I hate Matt Damon and wish anyone but him had been cast in his role. Leonardo gives an excellent performance.

The plot is good, the direction comendable, and the development is well placed, if a little hollywoodesque (did we need the girlfriend character to show the good rat??- This BTW is given a much better angle in IA) I got annoyed with the script at points, because that much swearing is unecessary even in a gangster film.

Ending was interesting, but it just doesnt at all compare to the sense of regret that resonates through the ending of Infernal Affairs.

Congratulations Mr Scorsese- you've bent over the american film industry and injected it with your tired old juice. Its quite an achievement considering how tired you are at this game....","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-05-08","","RT","46291776"
