4.5,"What a great flick! This was the one that brought Martin Scorcese his long-denied Oscar. While I'm not sure it was Oscar-worthy, it was one of the best films I've seen in a long time. A great cast just helped things along. Matt Damon and Leo DiCaprio were excellent as the cops who were both playing both sides against the middle. Jack Nicholas was basically playing himself. Martin Sheen and Alec Baldwin did a pretty good job (Baldwin's done well in a number of films lately. When did he learn to act?) Mark Wahlberg was the standout though, in the part of a totally hard-ass foul-mouthed cop in charge of the undercover officers. It was good all the way through, but the last 30 minutes had me riveted to the screen. I can't give it 5 stars though, for a couple of continuity and editing problems, and a couple of unfilled holes in the story line. But it's worth every bit of 4 and a half. I only wish I had seen this in the theatre instead of on my home screen.","",False,True,False,False,4.5,"2007-05-09","","RT","754264657"
