4.0,"First things first - this is really not Marty's best film. Nor is it as good as Infernal Affairs. Whereas Affairs was sleek lean, and posed its questions in a spiritual way, Marty's effort, is rather excessive and at times completely bloated. the thing that saves it is that the reason for this excessiveness is to fill out Jaaaack's mob-boss, who while being typically Jack, is easily the most interesting thing in the film. 
Other than that, Marty lets the brilliant premise play itself out mostly, while coaxing a great performance from Di Caprio. Matt Damon struggles a little in comparison (particuarly accent wise) but still is solid, and Marky Mark somehow got an oscar nomination for shouting alot and having a go at everybody. The premise is entertaing anyway though and though a surprising amount is lifted directly from Infernal Affairs (considering Marty's protestation that this really wasn't a remake - who was he kidding?) but still remains one of the most entertaing films from 2006. Check out he original first though.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-05-09","","RT","242414265"
