3.5,"Man, movies these days suck!
 
Fantastic Four was one of the worst movies I've ever seen. Its about a bunch of really lame superheroes with really lame powers. The acting was so terrible I found myself wishing horrible things would happen to the actors in real life. The only redeeming qualities were some explosions that kept me from falling asleep. Only a day or two after watching this I found I couldn't even remember what the movie was about, and I caught myself straining to recall it. Then I figured, haven't I already wasted enough of my life on this movie? I can't believe there is a sequel this summer.
 
The Interpreter, another really bad movie. Its about some political something or other and some assassination at the United Nations. This gets better than Fantastic Four because the acting was better, but it was so boring I had to use all the self control I could muster to not hit fast forward. The entire plot was awful and not interesting or satisfying in any way.
 
The Departed was really well done, and the acting was great, great directing, and all of that. But, it just wasn't really that captivating. I guess this is not my sort of movie - mob bosses, undercover cops, guns, etc. But I liked it while I was watching it. I didn't really think any of the characters were that likable though. The character development was pretty slim. Pretty good overall, but deserving of best picture? Definitely not.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-05-12","","RT","900849563"
