4.0,"I have to grit my teeth when I talk about this film because it brings out an unholy rage within me.

It receives 4 stars because it's a good film and I enjoyed the film.  I like the cast and I think the performances are wonderful; Jack is particularly brilliant.

That's where it ends though because this is a blatant rip off of a superior film.  An my problem with this film is that everyone is touting Scorsese as some sort of genius for taking one film, changing the names and the location of it and then releasing it under the title of - The Departed.

This is Infernal Affairs and make no mistake about it.  Even the director of Infernal Affairs came out after The Departed received oscar recognition and spoke of his disappointment at the fact that Scorsese gave the film nothing new what so ever.

So why didn't Infernal Affairs receive an oscar?

Too many people have only watched this particular movie and ignore the original because it involves the reading of subtitles.  

It's a good film.  It's very enjoyable and i've not heard a bad thing uttered about The Departed.  Still, take the time to compare it to the original.

At the end of the day I can't call it a bad film though...it's not.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-05-26","","RT","780883171"
