5.0,"Michael Mann!

if Michael Mann directed The Departed this would have been the new Heat for the Y2k kids.

Director Martin Scorsese's ""The Departed"", a gangster flick based from the Hong Kong thriller ""Internal Affairs"", goes without saying as perhaps his best work since ""Goodfellas."" Working on a genre that's right up his territory, Scorsese is back on top of his game and recreates a new dimension to the genre. This crime thriller treads the same theme as much of its director's previous films does. It's about two young men, the people around them, and the complications brought about by their characters' ambiguity.

To begin, Scosese probably went a little over the top with casting. I realize that big names bring big bucks, but having dominating talents like Alec Baldwin (if you don't agree, see Glengarry Glen Ross or any one of his stints in SNL) or Martin Sheen in supporting roles is distracting. Such recognizable faces removed any sense of anonymity or realism from those roles -- they felt more like cameos than real characters. Not that Scorsese is the first to make this mistake; The Thin Red Line suffered from this same fatal flaw.

The music, whilst not as eclectic as Goodfellas, is still good. There are only a few songs here, mostly in the background. But it works, and that's all that counts. The score used was tense, and never did this film seem like a conventional thriller. The music held it together.

As directing goes, this film was a more than solid thriller. The whole film felt tight and polished. Maybe this is a bad point in some ways. It lacks some of the energy of Scorsese's earlier films, and probably could have benefited from some more of it.

The Departed is a masterpiece of style, the sleekest and most seasoned film-making setting the accent on cool on this exemplary, quintessential, unpredictable, ridiculously perfect orgasm of a film. If you're reading this waiting for me to say something even slightly negative about what is inarguably the greatest film of 2006, which I sate with the knowledge that in these last three months of the year, there is not one film that can surpass this one, then you can keep waiting, because there is nothing negative at all to say of this movie. You couldn't even make something up.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-05-27","","RT","349144635"
