5.0,"Ever imagined what it would be like to have Leonardo DiCaprio, Jack Nicholson, Matt Damon, Alec Baldwin, Mark Wahlberg & Martin Sheen all in the same movie. Well, Martin Scorsese was able to pull off this cast with his own American version of the Hong Kong thriller Internal Affairs called The Departed. Definately one of the best casts ever put together on-screen. The acting here is excellent & mostly all of the main roles here are Oscar® worthy. The lead characters here are played by DiCaprio, Damon & Nicholson. The rest of the supporting cast including Baldwin, Wahlberg, Sheen & Vera Farmiga (from Running Scared) is nearly perfect.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-05-28","","RT","781736284"
5.0,"Very few movie would I dare call PERFECT.  But The Departed (correctly pronounced as Tha Depahted)is one of those movies.  Everyone's acting was superb and being that I'm from fairly close to Boston and love the city it was even more essential to me that they get the accent right.  AND THEY ALL DID!
Leo has never been anywhere close to being on my list of favorite actors but his performance here was compelling and real (something I thought he was incapable of).
Jack describe Frank Costello as the most evil charcter he's ever played and I'd have to agree.  Slimy and ruthless and a perfect role for him inspired by Whitey Bulger.  
Damon finally gets to use his real accent and preforms beautifully here as well but the 2 guys who suprised me the most were Alec Baldwin and Mark Whalberg.  Not only were great actors but they were freakin hilarious!  Any time they were on screen they just brought a ruthless and hysterical quality to it that I fell in love with.
Scorsese... you are a freakin genius!","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-05-29","","RT","781948652"
