4.0,"Simply put, The Departed is amazing.

The movie can generally by summarized by one of its opening lines of "" we learned as kids that in life you can either be a cop or a criminal"". 

Billy Costigan (Leonardo DiCaprio) is an young cop in Boston assigned an undercover job of infiltrating a mob syndicate run by Costello (played by Jack Nicholson). Meanwhile, a young criminal, Colin (Matt Damon), has embedded himself in the police department's Special Investigation Unit. Both their lives become endangered when the two organizations realize they have moles in their presence. How the former police academy classmates seek each other out is what The Departed is all about. 



DiCaprio and Nicolson

Besides Leonardo, Jack, and Matt, the all-star cast includes Martin Sheen, Mark Wallberg, and Alec Baldwin and everyone is obviously fantastic.

Leo, though his Boston accent is sometimes off, gives a really convincing and sincere performance and is definitely a contender for the Best Actor Oscar. ( I have to say, Leo's winning me over again... I love this guy!)

Jack is a great villain and Matt pulls off his both good guy and bad guy role really well.

Like Scorceses' last movie, The Aviator, The Departed drags a bit, but unlike its predecesor this one picks up quickly in the 2nd hour and keeps you on the edge of your seat. 

Overall, the movie is really entertaining and unique, but be warned it does have its share of bloodshed... so if you're squirmish, be prepared. 

ANYWAY, This definitely should win the BEST PICTURE Oscar!



Damon and DiCaprio duke it out in The Departed.

Alec Baldwin and Marc Walberg play good cop, bad cop.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-05-29","","RT","781823824"
