3.5,"It's all about the performances.  And the direction.  Oh, and the script.  Well worth watching, though it certainly is overrated.  If I can make one recommendation to Scorcese, it is that he is well past the point where he should retire his obsession with having Rolling Stones songs in every movie he makes.

The film runs a little long with both characters and scenes that were not completely necessary to move the story forward.  As well, certain aspects of the cat-and-mouse game between the rats tend to become repetitive after a while.  And while the complex structure of lies in the film certainly keeps one guessing, ultimately the last ten minutes is a bit cheap in its deus ex machina level of surprise turn arounds.

That being said, no one can deny that the performances, direction and cinematography is all top notch.  The caliber of acting talent is without a doubt one of the finest assembly of actors I have seen in decades, and each actor put it all up on the screen.  All in all, I would have to say that Matt Damon easily outshines DiCaprio at every turn with a character and a performance that is captivating and complex.  DiCaprio's character is much simpler and less interesting to watch, which makes one question exactly what the studios were thinking in advertising this as a DiCaprio vehicle.

Oh, yeah. Panty twisting.

They could have used with a better editor, but then again studios seemed to be obsessed with epic length movies with less than epic length stories, so who really knows what they were thinking?","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-05-29","","RT","781870637"
