4.0,"Focusing on the Boston police force and the city's underground mob, director Martin Scorsese creates one of the more intriguing thrillers in recent memory.  A remake of Japanese crime thriller Infernal Affairs, and an A-list set of actors including Jack Nicholson, Leonardo DiCaprio, Alec Baldwin, and Matt Damon, the movie runs at a breakneck pace, taking the viewer through the affairs of corrupt cops and undercover cops, and their involvement with the violent Boston mob, led by the apparently insane Frank Costello (Nicholson).  Plot twists and betrayals abound, and whatever initial notion you may have concerning ""good guys"" and ""bad guys,"" that idea will certainly be turned on its head before the movie's close.  However, compared with the ultra-intelligent script, the movie's rather anticlimactic ending felt like a cop-out.  While certainly not Scorsese's best effort, as some would claim (nor the best movie of 2006), The Departed, with its suspenseful drama and back-stabbing plot twists, certainly deserves a rental.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-05-30","","RT","782032585"
