5.0,"A gritty and brutal morality tale about loyalty and betrayal among cops and criminals set against the backdrop of Boston. Martin Scorcese is very well deserving of his Oscar for Best Director. Under his control, the all-star cast makes a very violent and bloody film emotionally engaging. The plot is complex, and the film deserves multiple viewings so one can fully grasp the depth of the multiple betrayals. Leonardo DiCaprio's performance more than makes up for his god-awful part as the romantic lead in 'Titanic', fully embodying the role of William Costigan, a man struggling with sacrificing his morals in order to bring down Boston's biggest mob boss. Great directing, great acting, and a great screenplay make for what I thought to be the best film of 2006.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-05-30","","RT","781970277"
