4.0,"The latest Scorsesse picture is unlike his past outings in many ways. This time we see both sides of organized crime in the sense of 'good guys' and 'bad guys' and the loyalties among them. Yet, the further these lines are drawn, the more difficult it is to distinguish between the two. Thiis uncertainty adds a layer of depth to the story and changes the conflict so that the victor will need plenty of endurance and stamina to cope with paranoia and ill placed trust just as much as the need for bullets and brawn.
Scorcesse chooses his plot to tell his story rather that the style he has become known for which is probably best as it may have confused the story otherwise. The only gripe I have is that it's ending perhaps ties things up too tightly. Nonetheless, another great film from one of our greatest directors.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-06-01","","RT","629783094"
