3.0,"Well, The Departed certainly wasn't boring. There were enough plot lines and well cast characters to keep even the most ADHD viewer (like me, for example) in their seat. Leonardo DiCaprio was extremely believable and sympathetic as Billy Costigan, a cop too smart to be a cop and enlisted to go under cover in the Irish gang that is running organized crime in Boston. Matt Damon is thoroughly unlikable due to his behavior as Colin Sullivan the gang's spy within the police force. Jack Nicholson didn't really impress me much as Frank Costello the boss of the crime ring; he has done bad and crazy so many times that I really didn't see this as a stretch for him at all. Mark Wahlberg played a small but vital role as Dignam, who is Costigan's contact within the police force and the one character who is in a position to figure out what's really going on. The film was a bit of a nail biter as you wait for one side or the other to catch a spy and the danger increases as more characters interact with them. However, I felt that there were too many characters and plot points conveniently thrown in at times and some of the plot points were not satisfactorily followed through on. I don't mind some questions being left unanswered if I feel that it was done on purpose but in this case I just felt that they ran out of time and there is no excuse for that in a 2 1/2 hour long movie! Anyway, it was very good and well worth watching, but not the best I have ever seen.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-06-01","","RT","782136115"
