2.5,"Alright let me say a couple things about The Departed.  First, it was a fun film. It wasn't the best film of 2006 by anyone's drunken imagination.  Scorcese deserved an Oscar for countless other films like Taxi Driver, Raging Bull and the Goodfellas, but not this.  The best way I can describe this film is as a 2 hour long music video.  The camera work is too much-- it takes away from the film rather than add to it.  When a viewer is watching a movie, notices camera work and then asks, ""Was that necessary?"" is not a sign of successful camera work.  This might have been Scorcese trying to prove a point-- he's still dynamic enough to be a good filmmaker.  Scorecese of all people shouldn't fall into such a trap.  The dynamite cast also took away from the film.  I couldn't buy into Jack Nicholson as a character, nor Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon and Mark Wahlberg.  It was a fine film, just not the best last year, not even a part of the best 5 films last year.  Definitely not Scorecese's best at all.","",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2007-06-01","","RT","781821824"
