5.0,"5 STARS. This movie is a remake but the execution by master director Martin Scorsese makes it all the more enjoyable. I saw this movie with my dad and he said to me before the movie started ""If I dont like it well go see a different movie."" Then the movie starts and Jack Nicholson's voice starts talking and then my dad says ""Ok I like the movie."" Its instantly captivating. There is a lot of cursing but me and my dad didnt mind that because the story and the acting was so good that the cursing seeemed nessesary for the story to continue. Not that im oppossed to cursing because I do it all the time but if you do it in a movie and have no story namly Smokin Aces which could be the piss pour piece of shit rip off of this masterpiece then it really makes no sense to see the movie. I mean if I wanted to do that I would just piss of my mom and save my self $8.45. But The Departed is honestly a piece of art rivaling movies such as Scareface and The Godfather. Go see this movie. If you dont you will truley miss out on and intellegent movie that is rarley seen now. The music is great. Howard Shore score is a change from his usually epic sound. I like the fact that it has a spanish flavor to it. And the theme is absoulutly great. pick up the soundtrack by Howard Shore. You wont regret it. 5 STARS","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-02","","RT","782252068"
