5.0,"After six repeat viewings and some harsh grading, I still can't find anything wrong with this film. The screenplay is tough, complex, threatening, potent. The plot is executed at breakneck speed. The actors, all-star that they are, do the near impossible in making the audience believe they aren't playing a character, but they ARE that character. The cinematography by the Scorsese/Schoonmaker team is seamless and has the ability to make you understand what has happened only after the image is gone from the screen.

