3.0,"A disappointment in many ways. Scorsese always worked best when doing original, personal movies. Copying Asian cinema is certainly not one of his strengths. ""The Departed"" borrows most elements from the much fresher and more believable Hong Kong ""Infernal Affairs"", but stretches it almost unbearably and concentrates on the players instead of on the plot. The adaptation to the Boston scene doesn't work in my opinion, the acting is a letdown and the constant swearing kills the atmosphere for me. Why Scorses got his very first Oscar for this weak assembly is beyond my knowledge.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-06-03","","RT","782036699"
