1.0,"I hated this movie. It wasn't much better than a campy Mission Impossible-type movie. The pretense that this garbage is Oscar-worthy is unbelievable. I mean, it wasn't without entertainment value, but I can't imagine anyone who knows anything about movies believing that this should even be considered for best movie of the year. I'm sorry Marty, but you'll have to do better than this puerile, misogynistic, cell-phone centric, bad guy v. good guy nonsense. Scorcese has made some good and great movies, e.g. Raging Bull, but also Mean Streets, The Last Temptation of Christ, Taxi Driver, the Last Waltz; but just because he didn't win for his more deserving films shouldn't entitle him to consideration for this movie. If you're a woman and you like this movie, you probably also like being objectified and marganilised by the men in your life. Crappy accents abound. Chest-thumping male stereotypes rule the day. Leo and Matt Damon are like two goofy Tarzans competing for their useless Ivory Tower-dwelling Jane. Jack Nicholson......I've had enough of him. It isn't that he was bad in this, but it seems as if his inclusion was some Academy-kowtowing. I mean, we know that the Academy loves Hack, I mean Jack. So why not throw him in the mix. If you like good movies, you deserve better than this. I give it a D.","",False,False,False,False,1.0,"2007-06-04","","RT","782654402"
