4.5,"My introduction to Martin Scorcese was made at the age of 7 when I slyly decided to watch the film Casino behind the backs of my parents. Scorcese made as much of an impression then, as he as made now upon my second viewing of this instant classic. His use of panning shots and quick character development is only fitting with the setting and plot of the film. Though the emphasis is thrown upon our three main characters in the film played by Jack Nicholson, Leonardo DiCaprio and Matt Damon, we cannot help but remark upon how life-life and, sometimes, humorous the other characters can be.

In the film, Sorcese, once again, demonstrates the power in his film making by giving us violence that actually puts us in the situation resulting in a very dramatic and shocking viewing.

The Departed, however successful it may be as one of Scorcese's films, is not a film of originality; it is a re-make of a Hong Kong film called ""Infernal Affairs"". Nevertheless, he did not fail in giving the North American public a film worth viewing.

The Departed is a great watch and, in my case, an excellent investment.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-06-04","","RT","782637030"
