4.0,"So I'm one of those guys who thinks that Marty Scorsese never really deserved an Oscar. I'm still not completely sure he deserved one for The Departed; if I could surround myself with the likes of Jack Nicholson, Leo DiCaprio, Mark Wahlberg, Martin Sheen, Matt Damon, Alec Baldwin, and (hah) Anthony Anderson, I could probably win an Oscar for best director too. That being said, it was a bad ass re-make. Its length was perhaps one of its major setbacks. Not that I can't enjoy a good 3-hour movie from time to time, but I felt like it could have been wrapped up a bit quicker. My other main complaint was the ending; though I haven't seen the original film that Departed was based on, so if it stayed true to the story I can't fault it for that. I'll agree with the gent below me that this film is a bit overrated, but you know how the Hollywood men behind the curtain plug the movies that just have to make it big. I probably won't watch it again for a long time, but it's a must-see if you like crime action dramas with interwoven comedy directed by Marty. Like, uh, Goodfellas.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-06-05","","RT","783007000"
