5.0,"The Academy of Motion Pictures have been on the run from Martin Scorsese, having stolen so many Oscars from him.  Despite 2006's list of excellent nominees, Scorsese finally cornered them in a dark ally, put a gun to their head, and stole the whole show: best director, best picture and a couple other Oscars.

Everyone knew that Scorsese was out for that Oscar, so when I walked into the theater my expectations for this movie were through the roof.  Every one of them was met.

This is the third Scorsese picture starring Leonardo DiCaprio, and I hope that they continue working together as each film is better than the last.

All the actors and their performances were top notch in this flick, Mark Wahlberg is becoming a new favorite of mine, Leo has merely reaffirmed my faith in his abilities, and Jack Nicholson honestly could have played the part of a demented crime baron in his sleep.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-05","","RT","783191092"
