5.0,"Martin Scorsese always has to make movies about tough, over-masculine, patriarchal, homophobic, womanizing, brute Italian mobsters: Mean Streets, Raging Bull, Goodfellas, Casino, etc etc.  So I think it's good for him to diversify his directoral horizons and make a different kind of movie: one about tough, over-masculine, patriarchal, homophobic, womanizing, brute Irish mobsters.  And what a movie it was.  All the coincidental paradoxes, ironies, and twists make one hell of an entertaining movie.  The complex story unravels itself out perfectly, so you're confused only in the little amount of time you need to be before all the serious action takes place.  Of course, amazing performances by Jack Nicholson, Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, and Mark Walhberg.  DiCaprio stole the show; it's hard to believe such a pretty boy can embody a sneaky creep so well.  Probably the best movie of 2006, out of the ones I've seen at least.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-05","","RT","782566620"
