4.5,"This movie was incredible from start to finish.  The attention to detail and the realism brought forth by Scorsese and the cast made this movie great for me.  The screenplay by Bill Monohan was among the best of 2006, and the cinematography and editing were spectacular.  I also loved the soundtrack, with two  acoustic guitar laden tracks by Howard Shore, composer of such films as 'The Silence of The Lambs'.  While the movie is long, not a second is wasted as the character development and plot move along briskly.  Damon, DiCaprio, Wahlberg, and Nicholson all delivered great performances as well.  Even though this was a remake, and I still haven't seen the original, I highly reccommend it.  This film deserved all four Academy Awards that it got! (Best Picture, Best Director, Best Editing, and Best Supporting Actor)","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-06-05","","RT","782468680"
