4.0,"ironically, not scorsese's best (i guess the guilt finally caught up to the academy), but still, better than a lot of what is out there--even when scorsese misses, it's not by much, and there's always some redeeming quality present.  gangster films are his 'sweetspot', and when your antagonist is handled by jack nicholson, well, you've already got two marks in favour.  as the anglicized version of 'infernal affairs', this a nice, tight remake which focuses instead on the irish mob around boston, and scorsese favours us with an a-list cast including dicaprio, damon, and mark wahlberg who, frankly, proves almost as adept as nicholson in stealing every scene he's in--as dignam, wahlberg gives arguably his best performance ever, despite the minor role.  was it the best film of 2006?  actually, no (pan's labyrinth, united 93, or letters from iwo jima, easily), but still decent.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-06-05","","RT","783056370"
