4.0,"Very well done remake of Infernal Affairs (which anyone who liked this movie should watch).  
DiCaprio and Damon give more notable and intense performances than I've seen them before.  Their rooftop confrontation at the end definitely gets your heart pumping no matter how many times you see it.
Wahlberg does well with his role, but really, the Best Supporting Actor nomination was undeserving.
Has some great memorable sequences, especially the ones taking place at 344 Wash.
It also has a great soundtrack.  Dropkick Murphys, Rolling Stones, Human Beinz...and Howard Shore provides the usual excellent score.  Listen for a beautiful guitar accompaniment when Leo visits the psychiatrist.

Still, I prefer the original.  This one doesn't have the same emotional effect that worked in Infernal Affairs.  The beginning felt too long (just about the first hour covers what Infernal Affairs had done in only ten minutes and this one felt more distant for the audience than the original did) and some of the scenes and dialogue seemed to have some unnecessary adult ""comedic relief"" that slowed down the pacing (basically anything out of Wahlberg's mouth, the setting in the porno theater, etc.).
And I prefer the original's treatment of Matt Damon's character as a morally confused man in a bad situation rather than this film's take on him as a selfish bastard with a talent in lying and betraying others.  
This film certainly does a good job in changing the story to fit with the new take on the character, though, right down to changing the ending from the original.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-06-06","","RT","782711127"
