1.0,"I've never liked Scorsese, and the fact that him and his crew received Oscars for this piece of trash will forever be a haunting mystery to me. Some may argue the characters are better defined here than in the original Hong-Kong blockbuster, but that is why there are two films following the original ""Infernal Affairs"". The acting here is terrible and Scorsese can't keep his cinematography and plot coherent (nor has he ever). I have seen Raging Bull, Taxi Driver, Cape Fear (another of his remake hopefuls), and other trash films. Scorsese is overrated and should not be worshipped by millions of Americans who think he defines their gangster culture. The uneducated as well as those drowning in the mainstream will find this film ""brilliant"" and ""deep"". I don't care what you say, I will never like this film. I am partial to originals.","",False,False,False,False,1.0,"2007-06-06","","RT","783267121"
