4.0,"Big film. However, Scorcese should have won his first Oscar 30 years ago, back in 1977, for Taxi Driver, but lost to Rocky. A pathetic result if you ask me. Back to the Departed. Great cast, not always the best acting performances. The standouts for me were Mark Wahlberg and Alec Baldwin and the way they interact in some scenes was amazing. However, as good and big as this film was cinematically, Infernal Affairs was arguably better. Personally, I beleieve that Scorcese should have a few best picture and best director Oscars on his mantlepiece for Taxi Driver and Goodfellas and perhaps one or two others, however, I also believe that Alejandro Gonzalez Innaritu as a director, did a much better job as a director on Babel. As for best picture, I think that the right film won.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-06-06","","RT","783223579"
