4.0,"Scorsese returns to familiar territory with this gritty and unpredictable crime thriller. The direction is surehanded and deft, and the screenplay realistically captures the course, abrasive world of South Boston. The cast is uniformly excellent, especially DiCaprio and Damon, although Nicholson seems merely to be playing a role we've seen numerous times before. That being said, he does a good job playing an insane criminal, with exceptional influence and power. Wahlberg's character is severely underdeveloped, as is Farmiga as the female lead. The violence is startlingly brutal and uncompromising, and the suspenseful climax defies expectation. Perhaps not Scorsese's best, but at least won him his much-deserved Oscar. A bold and fast-paced film that maintains audience interest throughout.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-06-06","","RT","783343764"
