1.0,"Alright, some people may call me crazy for not holding this supposedly good movie in such high esteem, but I must confess that this was absolutely without a doubt Martin Scorcese's WORST film ever. Period.

And it's not because of the actors in it either. Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, Martin Sheen & Jack Nicholson are among the Hollywood elite when it comes performances. What kills this movie ultimately is the storyline. 

It in my opinion lacks the complexity and uniqueness that made earlier Scorcese classics masterpieces. Goodfellas, Gangs Of New York, Raging Bull, Cape Fear & The Aviator are some examples. In this case, there is a very weak plot and story about two rats (one on the side of crime and one on the side of justice) who spend the film playing both sides. The excessive and pointless violence and vulgar language didn't help either...and yes, you can have too much of both in a film.

In classic Scorcese fashion, the film was extraordinarily long. But perhaps the WORST part of the film is at the very end when ""unexpected"" bullets fly in the warehouse. I had to put my head down and just anticipate the credits.

I'm a fan of Scorcese's work, and I always enjoy his films. But everybody always has to have that one movie that is their WORST. For Scorcese, The Departed is it.","",False,False,False,False,1.0,"2007-06-06","","RT","782103973"
