5.0,"Scorsese's best film since ""GoodFellas""; an exceptional examination of competing moles pledging allegiance to both sides of the law, while trying to be invisible.  The mood, as in every Scorsese film, is restless and wonderfully alive; its inclusion of both ""Comfortably Numb"" and ""Gimme Shelter"" deserve incredible praise on its own.  But the meat of the movie -- the story, its characters, and the fundamental questions of identity it raises -- are most praiseworthy, and the performances are excellent all around (with DiCaprio beginning to prove that, under Scorsese, he may indeed be a great actor, much to the chagrin of ""Titanic"" bashers worldwide).  Great fun.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-07","","RT","783355065"
