4.5,"What an excellent movie. I will always give an ""A"" to a movie that I watch late at night on a work night and when the movie's over, I can't sleep because the story was stimulatingly mind boggling. 

I will not give away details, but in general, the movie is about two cops: one, DiCaprio has been hired, but is deliberately not on the payroll so that he can spy on and get inside the notorius Irish mob led by none other than Jack Nicholson.

the other, played by Matt Damon, is a crooked cop that is on Nicholson's payroll who alerts the Irish mob when the cops are making moves to arrest or undermine the mob's organized crime.

Damon is a stunning bad guy but I was more impressed and surprised by DiCaprio's amazing acting. I felt his paranoia and pain in his character and felt that this was by far, his best role in a movie.

The cast was outstanding. Mark Wahlberg as an obnoxious undercover cop deputy and the other roles play by various cast members was spot on.

I had a small issue with the ""Reservoir Doggish"" ending. I also noted an interesting plagiarism taken from the famous woman walking away from the man in the cemetary scene made famous in The Third Man.

This is the best movie I've seen in some time though the ending is a little disappointing.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-06-07","","RT","783660030"
