3.0,"[img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/movie/coverv/14/966414.jpg[/img]""The Departed"" is set in South Boston where the State Police Department is waging an all-out war to take down the city's top organized crime ring. The key is to end the reign of powerful mob boss Frank Costello from the inside. A young rookie, Billy Costigan, who grew up in South Boston, is assigned to infiltrate the mob run by Costello. While Billy is working to gain Costello's trust, another young cop who came up from the streets of ""Southie,"" Colin Sullivan, is quickly rising through the ranks of the state police. Earning a spot in the Special Investigations Unit, Colin is among a handful of elite officers whose mission is to bring Costello down. But what his superiors don't know is that Colin is working for Costello, keeping the crime boss one step ahead of the police.
[size=3][b]Not a bad movie, but I don't think it deserved the Academy Award for best picture. Rehashed storyline about a mole in the mob & a mole in the police department. Didn't find enough tension or much interest in the story. Big name director, stars, lots of blood & cussin', so it gets an oscar? [/b]:confused: [/size]","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-06-08","","RT","900808355"
5.0,"One of Scorsese's best","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-08","","RT","784098284"
5.0,"Fantastic.  I can't stop watching.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-08","","RT","783542760"
5.0,"Leo adds another tour-de-force to his ouevre.  He plays a painkiller-addict undercover cop trying to stay alive within Frank Costello's brutal Boston Irish-American mob.  He puts himself in the lion's den as he gets along only with the help of oxycontin and percocet and a gun; the cellphone that connects him to Mark Whalberg is his only lifeline.  Based on Infernal Affairs, a classic Hong Kong cinema masterpiece, The Departed overtakes the original and surpasses it, making it quite possibly Scorcese's best film.  Has one of the most shocking and best endings in all of modern film.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-08","","RT","783788528"
5.0,"maybe the greatest movie I have seen in five years besides children of me","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-08","","RT","783131074"
