2.5,"Scorsese is great, The Departed isn't. I don't get what all the fuss is about. Many say it's his ""best since Goodfellas."" A ridiculous claim since Age of Innocence and Casino came out after Goodfellas, and are way more thoughtful. The Departed certainly had the potential to be great, but misses its chance when an important character is overshadowed towards the end, and not given room to have any emotional weight. Also, the dialogue frequently sounds like it's written. Characters somehow manage to have endless amounts of witty remarks at their disposal to the point where they could easily be professional comedians instead of Boston cops. These annoyances can be overlooked for the most part, but when the jarringly unsubtle final shot fades to black, it's hard not to feel disappointed by it all. That said, The Departed is probably still worth seeing, even if it's one of the more conventional movies Scorsese has ever made.","dc7ca44c-1ae5-4015-b9de-9d8f71a9134b",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2007-06-08","","RT","783984892"
