4.5,"Since the Infernal Affairs trilogy is one of my favorites, I was either going to love or hate The Departed. Fortunately, it's the former for me. Despite having the same premise and even some identical sequences, IA and TD are very different in feel. The Departed is more sprawling and epic, whereas the original film is taut and slick. The best thing about The Departed is definitely Leonardo DiCaprio, whose role here finally gains him entrance on my List (you know what I'm talking about). Matt Damon is good as the baddie, and Jack Nicholson is freaky (as usual) in an over-the-top turn as the mob boss. Despite all the tension in the story, Alec Baldwin and especially Mark Wahlberg bring tremendous comic relief as true-to-life foulmouthed law enforcement officials. I was okay with the contrived condensing of IA's female roles into one character. The only thing that's a shame about this movie is the cheesy closing shot. Marty, you're better than that!","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-06-08","","RT","783971279"
