4.5,"Now that I've seen it more than once, I feel I'm able to express a few thoughts. It seems with this movie Scorsese set out to include realistic depictions of people being shot in the head, and boy did he succeed in that department! DiCaprio gives his all and is convincing, but he lays the intensity on a little thick at times (I also found Billy's relationship with Madolyn came pretty much out of nowhere, and could have been developed a little better). Nicholson, while very good and over-the-top as usual, is slightly miscast. The manufactured Down East accents of Sheen, Damon and Wahlberg get to be a bit much after awhile (particularly in their repeated use of the word ""microprocessors"" midway through). All of these are minor gripes however; the entire cast explodes and the film is awesome. I can't decide whether I want Marty to use The Rolling Stones' ""Gimme Shelter"" in every film he makes from now on, or never again! And finally, the ending creeps me out as much as it did the first time, no matter how many times I see it. Ranks as my third favorite Scorsese picture, after GoodFellas and Raging Bull (which in my opinion are virtually untoppable).","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-06-09","","RT","784265546"
