5.0,"I'm usually not a big fan of mob movies. The Godfather series has never really attracted my attention, even though I do have great respect for Francis Ford Coppola for other movies he's made. However, this movie is just what I want to see, a plot that is actually interesting, characters that I actually give a crap about, events that I can actually react to when they happen on screen. I hated Damon's character in this movie, he did a great job acting out the role but in my opinion Colin Sullivan was a jerk, here's a guy that has a great job but uses it to his advantage lies are coming out of nostrils throughout the whole movie and he's so good at it. In the end he gets what he deserves, Leonardo gets with his girl and his girl leaves him and you get a hint at the end in the funeral ceremony that while she's pregnant, the kid may be Costigan's. That's what I love about this movie, I cared about the plot and I even hated some of the characters. Very few movies inspire me to even blink nowadays but this one is really a keeper. I don't care that the plot was based on Infernal Affairs for those of you who can't get over that.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-09","","RT","784237367"
