4.5,"One of Scorsese's best films, I think. Definitely has its problems. Jack Nicholson is way too over-the-top. The scene where they hound Jack in the empty warehouse has huge holes (it's like one of those bad horror scenarios where a squad of cops arrives and yet only one cop is inexplicably left to face the bad guy). Also the sex scene between Leo and the psychiatrist was cheesy to-the-extreme and all-but killed the momentum of the movie (the use of ""comfortably numb"" on the soundtrack during that scene was very lame as well). That all said, the characters, acting, screenplay, camerawork, and overall narrative fluidity show that Scorsese is on top of his game. This is a complex story with a complex message and it works on both a superficial level as well as something deeper.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-06-09","","RT","782299354"
