4.0,"The Departed is a remake of an Asian film. But it is also not the first time that Martin Scorsese has done a remake (E.g. Cape Fear). That aside, Scorsese has made a standout film yet again in The Departed that shows why he is among the best directors in the business, if not the best. 

In watching this movie, one should understand, it is a guy movie, period. It is laden with sex, violence, and more profanity than most people would expect to hear in an ""R"" rated movie. Given he does explain why most of his movie are so violent, thereby justifying the language and violence. The one downside to this movie would be the camera work. There seems to be almost an overabundance of shots where the cameras zoom in and pan around characters at the same time. It is enough to make any audience dizzy. Despite this, the story is very well written and executed. Writer William Monahan lets audiences know that Matt Damon's character is a mole, working in the Boston Police Department, but he does not simply go and make it blatant, which sadly, so many writers do. Monahan's adaptation of this movie makes audiences guess about the intentions of Damon's character, and even those of Jack Nicholson's character.

The bonus features on the second disc are what really make this 2-disc edition so worth the money. It is not just some extra features. Collectively, the hour-plus TCM special ""Scorsese on Scorsese"", ""Crossing Criminal Cultures"" and ""Story of The Boston Mob"" are equal to a film studies class/seminar. Students and fans of the film arts will thoroughly enjoy these features. They are proof positive (as if he needs to prove himself) that Scorsese is among the very few elite directors in the movie industry. Even the deleted scenes feature are worth watching. Each scene includes an introduction by Scorsese, explaining them, although without saying directly why they were cut. All he says before the scenes is that they didn't get cut because they were bad, etc. He is very ambiguous about this epxlanation. 

That aside, Scorsese has presented a movie to his fans that, unlike so many double, triple, etc. disc DVD's that is more than worth the money paid. It is yet another excellent mark on an already excellent career of one of the film industry's best.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-06-09","philip s","RT","ffcf3604-dd3f-41d2-aaa3-6d03a497d5ba"
