3.5,"Scorsese's final, long overdue Oscar is what i'd call the 'sympathy award' - the yes-you-can-finally-have-one-because-everyone-else-loves-you tribute. Well, that was the impression i got from the Academy anyway. This is by no means the film Scorsese should have the won the Oscar for - ideally Raging Bull or Goodfellas. However its Scorsese all the way - sweeping camera angles, quick edits, graphic violence and some great sizzling screen performances. Nicholson and DiCaprio are the stronghold of the movie, i didn't think much of Damon. DiCaprio certainly has some talent on him. It's taken him a while though. Overall, a very well acted, character-driven film with a great script. Alec Baldwin's character gets me in stitches all the time, he has some excellent lines. Not as good as Goodfellas though, but a crackin' attempt anyhow.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-06-10","","RT","783899391"
