5.0,"Oh yes.  How can I sum this up without using too many superlatives?  It's one of the best crime films ever made; a meditation on megalomaniacality anchored by the two best performances of 2006 from never-better Leo DiCaprio and Jack Nicholson, as well as brilliant turns by Vera Farmiga, Matt Damon, and Marky Mark.  Tight editing by the master Thelma Schoonmaker and sharp direction from on-his-game Martin Scorsese make this 150-minute hum, and the script by William Monahan is at turns dark, brooding, hilarious, poignant, and genuinely thrilling.  The best stand-alone film since Fight Club, and it holds a place in my all-time top ten.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-11","","RT","784256329"
