4.5,"I went to see this film having no real knowledge of it. I'd just heard it was good from one or two people. When I came out of the cinema, I felt I had just witenessed something beautiful. Being 21, I hadn't seen films like Goodfellas and Scarface at the cinema. Now I know what the people who did felt like. This is simply genius. Incredible performances from Damon and DiCaprio (who finally shows just how great he can be), and Jack Nicholson....oh Jack, how I long to bathe in your glory. His portrayal of grittiness is only beaten by his coldhearted ruthlessness. Mark Wahlberg, who i had long written off as a ""meh"" actor, is great, and shows that he can be a good supporting actor. Not Goodfellas, but way up there with Scorcese's finest works.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-06-11","","RT","784424699"
