4.5,"Wow! I should start by saying that movies like this are rare, and I personally await anxiously for the arrival of such well-scripted, brilliantly-cast and intellectually engaging movies. The last such gem was Inside Man, and similarly this movie is anything but dull and keeps the noodle at work. The script is profoundly spoofy as it mocks the Bostonian-Irish police and gang culture of the near past. All members of the all-star cast perform well to deliver the dialogues and although we?ve all seen Nicholson do better, this isn?t in anyway is claim to shame. DiCaprio is surprisingly brutish as he plays an uncanny undercover rat, and Damon does a decent job of playing the unjust antagonist of the flick. Ah, and then there?s Whalberg ? there simply isn?t enough of him and his cocky, bullish and satirically fueled character. All-in-all, I was thoroughly entertained and will invest the 20 bucks in buying a DVD when it?s out. Despite that it?s a two and a half hour long run, the audience will never be given a breather as you?re constantly occupied with suspense and edge-of-seat excitement. So why didn?t I give this an A? haha, well, let?s just say some will disagree with how they chose to end it, and I feel my personal sentiments on it aren?t too positive, hence that?s where it lost the full rack of points. Regardless, Scorsese has certainly done a very good job at directing this movie, and I strongly recommend everyone, regardless of your personal preferences on movie genre, to go and watch this!","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-06-11","","RT","784614496"
