4.0,"Great film-making is truly achieved when a director is able to sustain drama in an unpredictable way all the way until the last second of film. The Departed was so that in all the brilliance a film can be and more. The writing of Monohan is utter insanity with loud truthfulness pounding on the drums of the audience. Matt Damon as always performs magic. But the biggest surprise in this film is truly Leonardo's performance. I was very impressed by his artistic growth. Jack never disappoints as usual and I must say I have never seen Alec in bad performance. The magic in this film is that you really don't think about how good this film is or how appropriate the casting and costumes and art because you are completely lost within the pages of the story. Though, in my opinion Children of Men was a better film, i'm happy with the Academy's decision to give it Best Film, Best Adapted Screenplay, and a well deserved Best Director.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-06-12","","RT","784844119"
