1.5,"Best film? Hahahahaha. No, really. Does swearing and bloody violence a good film make? Nope. Jack Nicholson - you may be the man and all, but dude, can you overact! Best adapted screenplay? Are you kidding me? The screeenplay took a brilliantly taut script and added Hollywood formula (i.e. the bad-guy gets his come-upance at the end, the ambiguity of the original characters is polarised into ""good"" and ""evil"", and people must use profanity to be taken seriously). Ideas that work in Chinese were taken wholesale into English. Result? The film looks contrived (example: the writing of the Chinese character on the envelope vs. the spelling of citizen). What a shocker. Infernal Affairs - the original - is a brilliant, brilliant film. Even though its an hour shorter than the remake it builds characters better, and is much better plotted.","",False,False,False,False,1.5,"2007-06-12","","RT","784181027"
