3.5,"I think Martin Scorcese really wanted an Oscar badly.  Instead of stepping out on a limb like he has done in recent years, he went back to the style of Goodfellas, for better or for worse.  While this is truly a fantastic film with a great cast, I just get the feeling that this is Goodfellas in Boston.  Leonardo Dicaprio is the star of the film, he certainly has come a long way since Titanic.  The stress his character goes through really shows up on the screen.  Matt Damon is also excellent, although he doesn't show the depth of character that Dicaprio does.  Unfortunately, Jack Nicholson really doesn't play anything new.  This is a role he has played before, and doesn't really offer anything new.  While I appreciated Scorcese finally getting the Oscar, this film really didn't break as many barriers as most of the other Best Picture nominees.  Still, this film does not cease to entertain, if only in a manner that Scorcese has done many times.  Please put the crime drama to rest Marty.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-06-12","","RT","784105502"
