2.5,"What a shame marty won an oscar for this.  It violates the single most important rule of a story- you must feel empathetic for a character.  The ending with a rat going across the balcony was maybe the worst metaphorical reference in the history of film.  While the acting was great - they ALL play the same voice/persona.  Oh wow, some have a Boston accent!  Their characterizations have no originality, and is more or less a hodgepodge of Donnie Brasco and Pulp Fiction.  Let's not forget that this is an adaptation and far from original.  Lastly, I cannot ruin the ending, but that was the worst and least impressive cop out of a conclusion that a screenwriter could ever commit. I can give 10 other films that were more worthy of an Oscar nomination in 2006.  Once again a movie proves that society/critics buy more into hype than substance.","",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2007-06-13","","RT","782438427"
