1.0,"Completely aware that I have pissed off the majority of my friends in numerous arguments regarding this horribly overrated movie I finally have a venue where I can rant and blog and do all the things that nerds who think their opinions matter do on a daily basis.  I will list the top ten reasons this movie was good and then the top ten reasons it was horrible.
  TOP TEN REASONS IT WAS GOOD:
1.  Acting - Top caliber performaces from pretty much the best in the business.  Leo is almost untouchable as an actor (but then some guy named Gosling came around)
2.  No number 2.  There is nothing else good about the movie other than the acting.
TOP TEN REASONS THE MOVIE WAS ABSOLUTELY MEDIOCRE AT BEST.
1.  Acting - everyone says Mark Wahlberg was so great...was he?  I've watched it a couple times now and it still seems as if he is overacting and completely cliche.
2.  Waste of time and space love triangle.  Did this movie really need a lame love triangle that went absolutely nowhere and did nothing for any of the characters involved except prove that the woman was a scandalous slut?
3.  The Cops are retarded.  Matt Damon is standing in front of his decorated veteran police captain telling his father over the phone that he's not coming home for dinner but his friends are?  What?  That wouldn't be suspicous to anyone else, let alone a police captain??  He's a grown man, why would his friends be going to eat dinner with his father?  Apparently these cops know nothing about ""secret codes"".
4.  Retarded Criminals.  There is no excuse for Jack Nicholson to fail to see that DiCaprio was a cop, I mean, Leo's sweating bullets every time he's questioned.
5.  More shotty writing.  Leo knows at the end that Damon is the bad guy.  He finds out while he's sitting in the POLICE STATION.  Instead of standing up in the POLICE STATION and making an announcement, while the evidence is right in front of him, he runs away and decides to meet the guy alone on a fucking roof.  Genius, absolutely genius.  It's not that hard to stand up and say, ""Hey, all you cops, this guy is an informant, here's the proof right here, lets do something about it.""  Boom, no unnecessary death.  Which leads us to...
7.  Ridiculous ending death scene.  Ooh ooh I know what will make the movie great. Lets kill as many characters as we cand in the last scene of the movie!  No one will expect that.  Therefor it must be good!
8.  I'm tired of typing, plus reliving this piece of shit movie is kind of upsetting me, so I'm gonna go.  If you haven't seen it, sorry for spoiling it but at least you won't waste your money.","",False,False,False,False,1.0,"2007-06-15","","RT","785058991"
