5.0,"""If you had lied, you'd a had an easier time getting what you wanted."" This quote is at the core of ""The Departed"". Sometimes we must lie in order to get what we want. We must lie in order to survive. And much of the time, we are lying to ourselves. The Departed is a character-driven story that relates deep and hard-to-stomach themes. It banks on a great deal of Western psychological research, exploring the depths of the psychodynamic unconscious, or ""the central locus of the lie"", as it is known. The unconscious is the basement where we hide all the stuff in us that we cant accept: good or bad, nasty or great. And those ""too nasty"" and ""too great"" truths are heavily guarded by a lie. William Costegan lied to himself. He didn't know how great he was. He hid is own good potential from himself. ""You got a 1400 on your SAT's kid you're an astronaught , not a statie."" ""With all do respect, school is out"" He had great potential but he locked it away in the basement. This movie reminds with masterfully entertaining plot, dialogue, acting, and symbolism: if we want to get to where we want to go -if we want to climb up high- then we have to sometimes lie, and when the time is right, pentrate the lie to get at that source of truthfulness within. And with that truthfulness, you and I will already be at where we wanted to go.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-15","","RT","785371228"
