5.0,"This movie kicked my ass in the theater. I had such high hopes for Scorsese's return to the crime world and it met every single, last one of them. Leonardo should have been nominated for this instead of the overrated Blood Diamond. He played ""tortured past"" to perfection here. Matt Damon continues his great hitting streak (what ever the hell happened to his buddy Ben is anyone's guess) and turns in a great performance. Mark Wahlberg's Dignam is off-the-wall hilarious. Everything he says is a stitch. Martin Sheen, Vera Farmiga, and Alec Baldwin, and even Anthony Anderson round out a great, great cast. Oh wait, there was some guy named Jack Nicholson in this too. I think he has a future in Hollywood. Seriously, he chews up every fucking scene he's in (he's pure evil) and only turns in one shitty line (""This isn't reality TV!!!). Even that line, while inexcusable, can't ruin this movie's rating - and neither can the guy at the end who talks like he's straight out of the roarin' 1920's (""We gotta stick together, see?).
Watch this movie at all cost - then ship yourself up to Boston.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-15","","RT","785314234"
