5.0,"The film that finally did what should have happened long ago, and many times since. Yes, this is the film that won Martin Scorsese his first and so far only oscar. Such an original approach to the sometimes formulaic mob film, a twisting plot that is expertly told by the more than capable Scorsese. Following the parallel lives of a cop infiltrating the mob, and a mobster infiltrating and climbing the career ladder in the Boston police department, and how their lives filled in deciet effect every aspect of them. DiCaprio plays Billy Costigan the cop infiltrating the South Boston mob. However, Frank Costello, played by Nicholson, who does a superb job only capable of Nicholson himself, has a man on the inside as well SIU officer Colin Sullivan (Damon). Both men know there are leaks from both sides. Costello and Sullivan are both trying to discover the rat in Costello's crew, while Costigan tries to keep his identity hidden, while building a case against Costello and trying to find the leak in SIU. Not to mention both men's relationship with a police shrink. The film is expertly acted and out of all the twist, the best happens last. Leaving a suspense filled dramatic ending. This is a movie at its best.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-15","","RT","785264915"
