4.5,"Of course Martin Scorsese wanted people to watch this movie and three or four times be completely shocked and think it was so original, because with a mob story you're going against ""The Godfather"", ""The Soprano's"", etc. and people have seen it already. Maybe that was the point though, the mob story in general is going to be the same because yes it did(does?) happen but not to the extent that there will be hundred's of people wanting to tell about their life in the mob. Was ""The Departed"" better than ""The Godfather""? Impossible to answer because they shouldn't even be compared. ""The Departed"" is a different, modern(modern to me since watching ""The Godfather"" is obvious it took place in the early 1970's), almost reasonable view from the inside and from the outside. Of course Leonardo was the main character, the ""good"" guy, and that's obvious, however it speaks volumes that Jack Nicholson(of course), Mark Wahlberg, and Matt Damon were the ones that really made this movie what it was. Really phenomenal cast that know precisely what their character is supposed to be feeling. And of course, great last scenes for Leo and Matt.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-06-15","","RT","785239119"
