5.0,"As a man of Irish decent, I've been waiting to see a good movie about my brothers to the north. This is a depiction of Irish organized crime that wanted to portray realism to the core. The idea for the double lives came from the Chinese film Infernal Affairs. I unfortunately have not gotten to see it to know how much of The Departed comes from it, but it has to be amazing to considering how this turned out. Stellar performances are littered throughout and that goes almost without saying because these actors never let you down. With Marty Scorsese behind the camera there was never any doubt this movie would turn out amazing. If you want a gangster flick and you're tired of the Italian mafia and your copy of Boyz 'N the Hood can't be found, then check out a little Bostonian action and prepare to find a whole new niche of street action.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-16","","RT","785429664"
