4.5,"From July 9, 2007:

The Departed was extremely well directed.  The pacing was brilliant, the soundtrack with some recurring theme music was strategically interesting, and the direction was appropriately rewarded.  Marty did not disappoint.

The story is based on an ultimately interesting but semi-unlikely cat-and-mouse setup.  Not only is it a sort of adaptation from an earlier movie, but the sensibility of this picture hearkened back to Heat, a film that Scorsese did not direct, but that two of his particular friends and possible muses starred in.  Like The Departed, it plays very heavily on the celebrity status of the two leads and finds the fictional characters' lives--diametrical opposites and yet not completely, sharing small but significant similarities--as dramatically interwoven as that of Collin (""Collie"") and Billy.

The plot was brilliant.  Especially brilliant was Leo and, regardless of what people may say of him, the guy can really act.  The nuances of the tortured Billy character, his ticks, his temper, his nervousness, his emotional baggage and turmoil, all were conveyed effortlessly by DiCaprio.  King of the World aside, he really was mesmerizing.

Mark Wahlberg gave a hilarious turn as the loose cannon cop in charge of undercover detectives in the field.  Also funny was Alec Baldwin as another cop in charge of coordinating raids.  In fact, the acting was brilliant all around.  Jack Nicholson used his natural quirkiness in an effective way playing eccentric mob boss Costello.  All in all, this film was truly one of Scorsese's best and more than deserved its accolades.","515cc4af-e9b9-4e95-b53e-7e2f8921b0b5",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-06-16","","RT","782505241"
4.0,"Finally, a film that would give Marty Scorsese the Oscar that should have been his in March of 1991. The Departed is the 79th film to be awarded the Best Picture of The Year Oscar and it was and still is liked about many who watch this film. The acting is professional and not slap-stick. The plot is enjoyable and thrilling. The music in this film is different because Scorsese usually never uses a score of any kind with his films because of the particular style he goes by directing. However, he wanted to try something different and it worked with this film. EVERY SINGLE PERSON IS NEVER LEFT WITHOUT DOING A PERFORMANCE THAT SHOULD HAVE BEEN AWARDED FOR BEST ENSEMBLE. However, Little Miss Sunshine is a film that had the best ensemble for its reasons (Go rent that film on spare time, good 2 hours for you to feel good). It's a film that you can enjoy with a nice beer and laugh and also have a thrill, and a laugh.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-06-16","","RT","784548208"
