3.5,"This movie was outstanding.  The acting and portrayals of each character were perfection, the directing by Martin Scorsese was the best that it gets in movies, the tension created on camera between the different characters was so untouchable.  The phone scenes were beautifully done, and I respected the movie for not using ""555"" numbers on the caller ID.  I also thought the crafting of the movie was so brilliant, it almost had me screaming.  Some of the shots and sequences are breathtaking (one of my favorite being when a main character is in an airport, and we see a mother and daughter walk past him, highlighting two completely separate walks of life.  It was bloody, it was rough, it was vulgar, and at times it was discusting (I didn't need to see that much of Jack Nickelson.)  WHen the movie started, and within 15 minutes I heard like 4 minority slurs, I nearly turned it off, but I'm glad I stuck with it.  At the time, I just wasn't grasping that that is just the nature of the characters.  Now, I do feel as if the screenplay was a bit weak at certain points, and it wasn't too difficult to get bored during the denounment, but the ending pulled it all together.  So, was it worth the oscar NOMINATION--heck yes.  Did it deserve the win, in my opinion?  Against Little Miss Sunshine?  No.  I think Little Miss Sunshine was the best film of last year, but this is probably a close second.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-06-16","","RT","781732773"
