4.5,"From the moment the intro music faded to the moment the credits were rolling, I was shocked. The screenplay was perfect. Every single character was calculated, intelligent, and real; everyone made their best moves, and it boiled down to who had been dealt the best hand. Colin Sullivan [Matt Damen] has been brought up from childhood by mob boss Frank Costello [Jack Nicholson], and is taught to confidence his way into the Boston Police Department; there, he works his way amongst the top ranks in order to inform his mob boss of police activity and methods of avoiding surveillance. Meanwhile Billy Costigan [Leonardo DiCaprio] is a Police Academy graduate who faked a dropout to join the mob undercover, planning to reveal the whereabouts of organized crime ringleaders and illegal activity. Colin and Billy each inform their respective recipients, each group becomes more and more uneasy by the large number of untimely, ""coincidental"" detections of criminal activity, and equally coincidental evasion. The police and the mob alike begin to suspecting a rat amongst them, and each group simultaneously attempts to sniff their rats out; this film witnesses the chaos that ensues.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-06-16","","RT","785379768"
