5.0,"I loved everything about this movie. Some accuse Scorsese of making a genre film. But my question is what's wrong with making a genre film? Weren't films like the original Scarface and Angels with Dirty Faces genre films? The difference between this film and so many other contemporary crime films is that Scorsese gives us real characters that we care about. The cast is simply terrific. DiCaprio should never have to hear another 'Titanic' joke, Damon is an underrated actor who gives us a different character in each film (compare this to his performance in 'The Good Shepherd'), Nicholson is at his Faustian best, and Mark Wahlberg steals the show. I'm so happy that his film won four Academy Awards including Best Direction for Marty.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-16","","RT","784021379"
