5.0,"Was I blind the first time I saw this? My first viewing of this movie had me mixed, I found the story line to jumbly and the content a little explicit. But on a second viewing, nearly a year later, I found this movie to have more structure than any movie I have seen and the explicitness of it to have real adaptability to real life. This is by far one of my favorite movies of all time. Looking beyond the clever storyline, you will find the depth of it to grow through the characters. Never has a movie gone so far into character motives like this movie has. Scorese brilliantly contsructs the story not only through the script, but in the articulate film making style. A fresh style that captured some of the best camera work combimed with excellent editing. Jack Nicholson brings so much to the table, producing one of the most memorable characters in film history and doing it with intense originality. He serves the one liners like no other. Aside from Jack, the rest of the cast pulls the wait including Leo, Damon, Wahlberg, Vera Farmiga, and even Alec Baldwin. Never did I expect a crime movie to be so smart, jabbing away at concepts such as religion, racism, and responsibility. Who doesn't love the Shakespeare ending? Watch closely, it will jack your mind.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-17","","RT","785516403"
