2.5,"With everything set up for me to like this film (Scorsese,an ""Irish"" connection, soundtrack by a band I've been drinking with) it is a fairly amazing achievement that I'm so dissapointed in it. Jack Nicholson is always going to aspire to no greater character acting than to play himself yet again, but to see Scorsese's directing talents crumble to such populist garbage was heart-breaking. The lowest point was the deliberate inclusion of a rat as a backdrop to one of the unrealistic monologues of Matt Damon's informer character. Middle school standard symbolism at best. Direction that could have achieved an oscar purely on the basis of a past career was saved partially by (and I am equally suprised by this as the poverty of Scorsese's direction) Leonardo DiCaprio, who was really fairly good and believable. Oh, and Matt Damon and Mark Wahlberg sucked ass.","",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2007-06-19","","RT","783722432"
