3.0,"My Aviator review mentions how I missed that movie in the theaters and its a mistake I will always regret. Well, between the kids (kids! in here!) screaming, the guy next to me saying oh boy every 5 seconds, the cellphones and the total uncomfortable seats for a 2 and a half hour movie missing a movie in a theater might not be so bad.

I liked the movie, a lot but it loses a few points mainly for being a remake, from a 2002 movie non the less (thats like....yesterday). The relationship between Dicaprio and Sheen was not worked at all so once his death comes by, does Dicaprio care? Do we? Hey, you don't agree with your new boss Wahlberg, so lets just leave your undercover agents in the dust with paid leave, awesome. No cameras in the back? Ingenious, sigh. Great performances by all but the movie has these few little annoyances all around it that wont elevate it into a really great movie. From the reviews Ive read about Infernal Affairs makes me feel I would like the original much much more.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-06-22","","RT","230795453"
3.5,"A competent and stylish remake of the 2002 Chinese original 'Infernal Affairs'.  Scorsese directs the action in his own unique style, both gritty and slick, and manages to draw some exceptional performances from the likes of DiCaprio and Nicholson, although Damon struggles to find his feet and Wahlberg is poorly cast.  Though at times gripping and highly enjoyable the film lacks the pace and energy of the original and ends up being a glossier but inferior imitation.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-06-22","","RT","786065065"
