4.0,"A very good film which, while not quite scaling the dizzying heights of Scorcese's ""classic"" work, this is still a thoroughly entertaining way to spend a couple of hours.
Some magnificent performances, especially from Nicholson, Wahlberg and Sheen, back up Damon and DiCaprio, both of whom are on top form. 
It's Damon who steals the show, using his natural charm and good looks in a devious and troubling new way.
The script is sharp and fizzes with brilliantly Bostonian hostility.
If anything, slightly to long (there is the potential to make this a tighter, more intense thriller wth a shorter running time), and featuring the sort of brutal violence that the world in which it is set engenders, this is a well made and brilliantly acted cop thriller.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-06-25","","RT","782095814"
