5.0,"This is one of those films that has everything going for it before it even gets made.  A top notch director, writer, cast, and it's even based on a successful movie franchise already.  For the most part, it lives up to those expectations, with enough great individual scenes and dialogue to make this a must see.  My one beef is that there are some pretty diluted plot elements that just make no sense no matter how many times I see the movie (what is with that scene where Matt Damon pretends to be the guy's lawyer?  I have no idea what is going on in that scene).  There is also some surprisingly bad acting, but it is so dominated by great acting in the rest of the movie that it's hard to fault it too much.  All in all, this is a pretty great crime flick that I wouldn't give any awards to but is still fun to watch, even multiple times.  This is Scorsese's most epic crime film, which also deserves commendation.","d354e8b5-8ced-4c43-bd1a-7d679f8d5289",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-26","","RT","783714667"
