5.0,"An amazingly on-target portrayal of life in Boston. Nicholson does not surprise at all with his brilliant performance, but Dicaprio does. I was very impressed with him, as I went in not expecting him to pull off the Boston attitude. The cinemtography is well done, the movie action is high and moves fast, and it was very well written.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-06-29","","RT","785888390"
3.5,"A huge disappointment, but that's my own fault for buying into the hype. Some great performances (the finest you'll see from DiCaprio & Marky by a long margin) marred by muddled (at times I'd even go so far as to say random) cinematography, a story that's never quite as clever as it thinks it is and a generally saggy, shambling feel to the proceedings- easily could have been 30 minutes shorter, and would have been all the better for it. Never quite an action film, never a true character study, it tries (and, let's face it, fails) to be all things to all people. While above average, nothing special at all, and didn't even nearly deserve the Oscar, but if we pretend Marty was given it for Goodfellas a few years late then all is well with the world.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-06-29","","RT","786445384"
