4.0,"Very good thriller from director Martin Scorsese. Re-imaging Chinese crime film Internal Affairs as an American epic, Scorsese returns to familiar territory and produces another fine look at the underworld. But whereas GoodFellas gave us a nostalgic look at gangsters, The Departed is distinctly contemporary in its style, and has a much grittier, cynical feel because of that. You can see that while Scorsese once influenced the Sopranos, the show is now influencing him. Heading The Departed's all-star cast are Leonardo DiCaprio & Matt Damon, whose characters both start out on the streets of Boston's Irish American community, an area which is ruled by crime boss Frank Costello (Jack Nicholson). Both share the ambition of joining the Police force, but for very different reasons. As they pursue their goals we see the characters' lives become tangled without them even realising it. DiCaprio & Damon's performances are amongst their best, & Nicholson thrives as the gangster who has evil running through his veins. A strong script, Scorsese's flair with violent screenplays, & an amazing supporting cast that includes the likes of Mark Wahlberg, Ray Winstone, Martin Sheen & Alec Baldwin make this one of the best mob movie's in recent years.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-06-30","","RT","786441296"
