5.0,"What is so great about good cop and gangster movies?? No sense of morality, no decency and certainly no scruples. 

This is a movie with a stellar cast and crew, probably the best Ive seen in differrint roles. It does rank as one of my favourite movies, and deserves its 5 stars.

Leo di Caprio and Matt Damon are polar opposite persons, though they both attended the police academy, Matt Damon getting the plushy, high ranking authroative job, while Leo, not quite high ranking material, accepts an undercover job, in working for Boston's criminal Kingpin, Costello (Nicholson) What they dont know is that they are both the most despised persons from both sides of the law: they are both rats. Damon is a corrupt police officer planted by Costello himself, and Leo is an UC from a well known criminal background, both are being targeted by both sides, while each has to deal with their personal issues and very volatile lives as double agents. 

Gripping and hard hitting! I love the Irish themes, the music, the accents, the locales and the attitude, first and foremost. Of course, take out ever single swear word int he dialouge and you would only have 25% of PG rated script left. ^_^ The music and tension is dramatic, this movie kept my interest and I enjoyed it, and Ill treat this as a modern classic.

Well, the big stars and crew is what made this movie superb. Ive never been a Leo fan, his boyish thingy always pissed me the hell off, but after seeing this, and knwoing about Blood Diamond, I can now say what a talented and effective actor he is. He's matured, and pretty much a big gun now, not a kid, and thats how I would like him to be, and if he keeps on getting good roles and movies such as The Departed, we might be looking at a screen legend in the making. Matt Damn was good, not his best, but did well. Jack Nicholson..... Im an awesome fan of his, one of my favourite actors, and its good to see age hasnt impacted on his talent and screen power, he is superb, actors like him dont exist anymore. He is wild, coarse, and looked liked he loved doing this movie, as did the rest of the cast, it shows in the final product, their postive energy and drive shows in their near flawless performances. But my two thumbs up goes to Mark Wahlberg, and even as a supporting cast, he had the best lines, the best shots and the some of the best attitude, I cracked up every time he spoke, he was the perfect asshole on screen, but you gotta love him, he dishes out some of the worst abuse from his script, and he delivers like he was born to do it. ^_^ 

Martin Scorsese is a superb director, he made some of my favourite movies, and this has got to be one of them. Im a big fan of crime thrillers, and in comparison to Infernal Affairs, I liked this much better.

The interwoven personal storylines, mainly attributed to Leo's near mental breakdowns, is excellent, all due to Leo's great acting. (I cant believe im saying that!) - But the real focus is the two infromants facing off in a hunt to find the other out before the other find them, and there is a pretty good ending which most wont see coming. Dramatic, abrupt, and some would say very unfair, but it is an good ending neverthless, and it is what I would expect from a top notch crime thriller!

One of the best in my book. Happy to say it has a special place in my very large DVD collection, and rightly deserves it.","",False,True,False,False,5.0,"2007-07-03","","RT","238100606"
