5.0,"Scorsese's best film since Goodfellas.  The best performances come from DiCaprio and Jack Nicholson with Ray Winstone and Mark Wahlberg also giving good performances.  The movie is definitely deserving of its Oscar for best film; it's just unfortunate that Scorsese had to wait this long to get the credit he was due.  The movie's set in South Boston where Leo becomes a mole for the cops in the Irish mob, and Matt Damon becomes  a mole for the mob in the State police.  The film becomes a great cat and mouse game with a lot of drama and paranoia thrown in.  The soundtrack is great too, as it features among others, Van Morrison & Roger Waters' live version of Comfortably Numb, and John Lennon's screamer, ""Well, Well, Well.""  Alongside Goodfellas and Raging Bull, this is one of Scorsese's best.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-07-04","","RT","785819015"
