3.0,"I hated this the first time I watched it. It was far from the original that it was based on, even if it did copy shot for shot a fair amount of scenes. Infernal Affairs was far superior even if it didn't have the epic proportions of Scorsese's remake. Solid but god awful editing and greatly lacking in the heart and motives of the characters of the original. I did not really feel a sense of Costigan's despair from being undercover for 1 year verses Yan's 10 years of being undercover, Nor did I feel Sullivan's desire to be a good guy like Ming's in the original. Basically it was a good film but no one got the characters right, the editing was crap, the good parts were direct rip offs, and it all ends wrong. But you wouldn't know that if you didn't watch the far superior original Hong Kong version of this film, made only 4 years prior.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-07-04","","RT","787065940"
4.0,"Acclaimed Eastern thriller ""Internal Affairs"" is re-imagined as a Marty Scorsese tour de force starring Jack Nicholson, Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, Alec Baldwin and a scene-stealing, (extremely foul-mouthed) Mark Walhberg. Telling the story of two double agents, one working for the police force, the other infiltrating a dangerous Boston crime syndicate, this is easily Scorsese's best film since ""Goodfellas"" being gritty, violent, well-acted, funny, and extremely memorable. Sublime stuff from a master cinematographer.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-07-04","","RT","784151151"
