5.0,"I have never been a fan of Scorsese, but this film is one of the best I have seen in recent years.  It is definitely plot-driven and escapist, but the characters and events create an engrossing, downward spiral of deception and bloodshed.  Leonard DiCaprio has come a long way since Titanic (as The Aviator also attests), and Matt Damon possesses a screen presence I would have thought impossible for him to attain.  Jack Nicholson is gloriously hammy in a role obviously written for him, and brilliant supporting performances from Ray Winstone (ominous as the hitman Mr. French), Martin Sheen, Alec Baldwin, and Mark Wahlberg (foul but hilarious) astound throughout.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-07-05","","RT","787058090"
