5.0,"Scorsese's best work. This film truly brings to you the emotional distress and madness of being undercover. The all star cast conveys their feelings almost better than their words. Each emotion is throughly felt and there is a true sense of danger and care for Leonardo DiCaprio's character. Jack Nicholson is superb in his depiction of a mob boss. The inter play between Matt Damon and DiCaprio's cat and mouse game adds complexity but is not too overbearing for the overall plot. The setting of South Boston allows for play that had not yet been seen in mob films. Scorsese has always deserved and Oscar, but this film sealed his fate and showed all of Hollywood how long over due his recognition was. This movie is second only to the original mob movie: The Godfather. This movie is my modern day favorite.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-07-07","","RT","787342558"
