3.0,"ok ... I've taken some time to breathe and get over the things I didn't like about this film as I was watching it that made me say that ""it sucked, end of story"" when I first reviewed it. So, here is a slightly less biased review.
First of all, I'd just like to preface this by stating up front that I have yet to see a Scorsese film that I thought was a masterpiece. Now, that being said ... I cannot in all honesty say that Scorsese is a bad filmmaker, on the contrary he is an excellent filmmaker. The problem with Scorsese, for me, is that he always comes close to genious and never quite gets there. And, I suppose, if I'm being perfectly honest, that there is nothing really wrong with this film per say ... it just failed to live up to the hype that seems to swirl incessantly around Scorsese. I just don't see it people. What I see, are a bunch of basically fine films, that nevertheless never really say anything important. This film made me angry, and I suppose I have to give credit to Scorsese in that one respect ... he is very good at pushing my buttons. I would recommend this film to anyone that likes the typical Scorsese film, and anyone that would like to see a hollywood film that nonetheless pushes the acceptable boundries of Hollywood films. DiCaprio is excellent as usual, Damon is his usual boring self, and well ... who could not want to see a film with Jack Nicholson in a lead role. So, I guess, I would have to say that yes, this is a fine film, but no ... I do not, nor will I ever like Scorsese as a direcor, but I give him credit where credit is due. Oh ... did I mention this is a Hollywood remake of an Asian film??? Come on Hollywood, find your own material.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-07-07","","RT","782253549"
