4.5,"Pretty damn great on many levels it has to be said. He should have got the Oscar for Goodfellas, but Scorsese deserves it here for directing a magnetic story with one of the best casts you could imagine. Damon & Nicholson are ace but Wahlberg steals the pic in one of the most hard-boiled roles ever, Alec Baldwin shows surprisingly terrific comic timing in his support role while DiCaprio is almost as good - a career best, the first time I've ever truly seen him as a great actor. The script, too, shines and while I feel there's perhaps one twist too many at the end, it wins points for being tightly strung, uncompromising and truly brilliantly acted by pretty much everyone involved. One of the crime genre's best, no question.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-07-07","","RT","785635908"
