3.0,"ok movie. It had an ok story and usual classic directing by Scorcese. Wahlberg deserved the best supporting actor award but was nominated. He plays the typical Irish cop, mean and cursing every second. What a performance!! My usual complaints would be Dicaprio. He does his best but he's just doesn't fit in the role. Especially the scene of him in prison. A guy that looks like him would be raped and killed in prison. He is seen beating people like twice his size. He is just not Joe Pesci as an actor. See Pesci is small too but makes you believe he is dangerous. Dicaprio can't do that. Damon is also pretty bad but fits the role being from Boston I guess. Nicholson also was pretty bad as he is one of my favorite actors. He is getting old and it's showing. Very good story and gets better every time you watch it. Has an interesting ending.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-07-08","","RT","787369775"
5.0,"The best film of 2006. Martin Scorsese's best work since 1990's Goodfellas. DiCaprio, Damon, and Wahlberg turn in the performances of their careers. Jack Nicholson, in his first pairing with Scorsese, adds yet another stunning performance to his already impressive career. The best choice for Best Picture from the last decade.

OSCAR WINS (MY OPINION)
Best Picture
Best Director (Scorsese)
Best Actor (DiCaprio)
Best S. Actor (Nicholson)
Best Adapted Screenplay","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-07-08","","RT","236157403"
