4.5,"You know a movie is great when, just when you think you've figured it out, it makes you stand up, yell ""WHAT THE FUCK?!?!"", and throw a shoe at your tv. The Departed is one of those movies. 

Now, I'm not one for senseless violence/vulgarity in a movie, but The Departed turns it into an art. It has the perfect blend of action, plot & character depth, comic relief, and twists to keep you from turning away from the screen for a second. 

Martin Scorsese is one hell of a director for taking all of these independent stars and molding them into a seamless storytelling machine. Leonardo Dicaprio, Matt Damon, Alec Baldwin, the utterly hilarious Mark Wahlberg, and Jack ""I scare small children with my facial expressions"" Nicholson were all fantastic, creating their own characters and adding to the story without stealing the limelight from anyone else. This was truly an ensemble drama. 

All in all, The Departed was great. Was it the best picture of 2006? Debatable. Was it a fantastic piece of film? Oh yes. 

p.s. Boston accents are hilarious. Yes, Jarvis, I said it. Fack.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-07-12","","RT","783804649"
