3.5,"Well crafted movie with a truly remarkable premise.  Also this is the best acting performance I've ever seen from DiCaprio, he was nomianted for an Oscar for a reason.  Nicholson and Damon are also solid.

The movie is certainly over the top in the gratuitous violence department though, and that costs it some points, which is a shame.  Also, there's that little business about the ending that doesn't sit well with everyone (myself included).

a 4 star rating would mean that I recommend this movie to just about anyone, so this falls just short of that.  It may also be significant that I saw this film twice, and enjoyed it much more the 2nd time.  I think it's because i wasn't thinking about what MIGHT happen next and was focused on what the characters were actually doing to each other.

