2.5,"I can understand the hype behind this movie, all star cast, incredible director. But in the end The Departed just isn't a great movie.

Creating a movie about the Boston mob does not in of itself make a movie interesting. Yes, Matt Damon and Mark Wahlberg's accents and character portrayal were fantastic, but what about everybody else? Jack Nicholson was himself with a lot more profanity. Leonardo DiCaprio did a subpar job, as an undercover agent, his nervous and suspicious demeanor throughout the film was more reminiscint of a drug addict than an undercover agent. And Martin Sheen was the blandest I have seen in a long time.

The film itself is filled with holes and annoyingly simple character roles and development. A cookie cutter gangster flick should be called what it is. Scorsese has done some incredible work, but with a script that was poorly adapted off the Hong Kong original, this absolutely should not have won him an award.","",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2007-07-14","","RT","787867214"
