0.5,"This film actually deserves no stars at all - apalling expositional dialogue, over-the top blood spurts and terrible direction. All the subtlety and perfection of the far superior Infernal Affairs is blown away in favour of a stright-to-TV standard cops-and-robbers fest. This film highlights the arrogance of Western filmmakers who presume that they can make better versions of Asian originals. Proof positive, also, that Scorsese is the biggest example of Emperor's New Clothes this side of Kubrick. Terrible. Don't bother - I couldn't stand to sit through the whole thing, but beleive me, I saw more than enough.","",False,False,False,False,0.5,"2007-07-14","","RT","786215362"
