4.0,"Very good movie. I would have given it an extra half star if it wasn't for the weaker movie making towards the end of the movie when there is a huge plot hole (elevator scene) that cheapens the movies outcome. I'm not complaining about what happens but just that something materializes out of nowhere (the plot hole) to dramatically change the story line. Scorsese should have been more careful to hint or allude to the eventual outcome or at least the character that causes it.
Otherwise this is a very strong film, great acting by all. DiCaprio is impressive, Mark Wahlberg is intense and so is Nicholson. Matt Damon gives his best performance to date but still has some maturing to do as an actor as he is not believable at all times, in other words you can tell he's acting.
