1.5,"Too much hype, not enough substance","",False,False,False,False,1.5,"2007-07-18","","RT","788165426"
5.0,"Typically, a movie gets by via the main talent of one major character that helps drive the movie, and typically that performance is considered Oscar worthy (such as in ""Ray"" or ""Capote""). But seldom does a movie come along that arguably features career defining performances from nearly the entire cast. If the performances of Jack Nicholson, Matt Damon, and especially Leonardo DiCaprio aren't the best performances of their career, they are at least top 3 roles. The same can be said for many of the supporting actors as well, from Martin Sheen, Alec Baldwin, Vera Farmiga, small roles for Anthony Anderson and Ray Winstone, but Mark Wahlberg steals the show amongst this group as the foul mouthed and fiercely loyal Staff Sergeant Bryce Dignam. Coming from a person that has processed a massive disdain for Wahlberg, it is arguably his most entertaining role to date. Meanwhile, DiCaprio and Damon prove that they are  two of the best male leads of our generation, Nicholson notches another impressionistic performance, and Scorsese reaffirms his place as one of our greatest filmmakers. 

Outside of the characters, the plot, action, editing, dialog, and even the occasional humorous asides are amazing, intertwining double and even triple turns seamlessly without getting convoluted. Examining each detail is fascinating, and the film is, simply pu, an absolute joy to watch as a smart and engaging action film, crime drama, and thriller.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-07-18","","RT","783374002"
1.5,"Jack Nicholson hijacks Scorsese's film and renders it unwatchable by doing his heavy-handed ""Jack"" thing.  DiCaprio and Damon's fine performances belong in a different and altogether better film to Nicholson's panto-worthy turn. Even the usually-peerless Scorsese drops the ball, his stylish camerawork failing to redeem uninspired set-pieces that lack drama. Not a patch on 'Infernal Affairs', the original and the best.","",False,False,False,False,1.5,"2007-07-18","","RT","788163239"
