4.5,"I wonder if Jack Nicholson's buddies ever get tired of long conversations with him, because he TALKS with this weird SYN-co-PATION and chews out EVERY, SINGLE word to make SURE that it HITS like a BULLET. And bullets are the name of the game in ""The Departed,"" with each one of the dozens making a genuine impact on plot and audience alike. 
So, yeah, that's Jack Nicholson - at his best, you've seen it before. The rest of the actors aren't wasted here - just as good as the all-star line-up suggests. The star of the movie is really Scorsese though, who may have made his magnum opus with ""The Departed."" It induces chuckles and grimaces, often at the same time, throughout most of the film - an odd-ball sort of gangster flick in which you root for nobody, are nervous for everybody's well-being, and are likely, as the credits roll, to exclaim ""Now THAT was a movie!"" A cold-blooded nailbiter of an experience, well worth it's Oscar.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-07-18","","RT","786350463"
