4.0,"An excellent mafia-style conspiracy thriller. This combination of a prodigious plotline with the added bonus of a cast of some of the best names in Hollywood, this movie is sure to put a feather in the cap of viewers wanting a good police-gangster war. A compelling tale of the Irish mob located in Boston, and a twisting tale of the paradox of never knowing exactly who to trust. In the world of in-between, whether you're a cop or a criminal, in the words of Jack Nicholson's character ""when you're facing a loaded gun, what's the difference?"" Quite the paradoxical piece of work, good ol' Leo DiCaprio plays a cop pretending to be one of the mob to expose and bring them down, while Matt Damon plays a gangster conveniently placed in the heart of the cops, and both their actions serve to cancel each other out as one fights to take down the other. Definetely higly recommended, but if you're not a fan of blood and gore and flying f*bombs, not for you.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-07-22","","RT","781864583"
