3.0,"Entertaining, sure. Oscar worthy? Not so much. This was clearly a pity-party for Scorsese at the Academy Awards this year, as ""The Departed"" contains many flaws. Apparently losing his flare and ability to tie contemporary realities into his movies, Scorsese presents this elborate mob-plot arrogantly and haphazardly, but there is nothing denying the entertaining factor of the film. DiCaprio, Nicolson, Damon, and especially Wahlberg form an excellent cast, each giving tour-de-force performances worthy of recognition. The title of the film gives away the reocurring motif throughout the picture, but it nevertheless is a tense, and enthralling mob saga. A lack of substance and annoyingly distracting side-plots hinder this self-proclaimed ""masterpiece,"" but there's no denying this is the work of a masterful filmmaker, even if he obtained his dues in false recognition.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-07-24","","RT","782266061"
