DiCaprio delivers one of his best performances and Wahlberg delivers his best (cameo). Nicholson is an awesome coice as mob boss, and I'm glad he got such a role in such a late stage of his career.

The direction and celtic music are both top notch in the movie. Though many people feel Goodfellas is Scorsese's best film, I feel Departed takes the crown (despite its chaotic ending). I feel this movie treats all the stars involved more fairly and is overall a more intense tale.

