3.0,"An extremely over-rated crime flick with some of the worst dialogue I've heard since Alone in the Dark. I really wanted to like this movie more, but in the end it just turned out to be Goodfellas Lite. Sure, the story was a little different, but you can't tell me there aren't any similarites between the two. 

Mark Wahlberg and Matt Damon prove to me once again that they are in movies just for their looks and not acting ability, while Leo DiCaprio and Jack Nicholson deserved better dialogue. The plot twists and revelations are yawn inducing as well.

I'd like to point out that I didn't exactly hate The Departed, I just can't seem to fathom why everyone gives it such high ratings. When compared to Scorsese's other films like Goodfellas and The Last Temptation of Christ, The Departed looks like a lame firecracker in a room full of Hellfire missiles.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-07-25","","RT","782155104"
