5.0,"There will always be a sort of generational differing over whether Goodfellas or The Departed is Scorsese's masterpiece. The Departed is obviously the most heavily awarded, but its praise does not come without recognizing the director's previous work that has backed-up over three decades. Nonetheless, it's one of the most well-made crime dramas in film. Martin Scorsese masterminds the film's flawless movement. Ballhaus' photography is physical and aggressive. With an almost constant soundtrack and Thelma Schoonmaker's speedy intertwining of scenes, it's relentless, exhilerating, consistently hyperactive. The story is textured and pefectly plotted with entrances, exits, and deaths that are Shakespearian in grandeur. The script offers searing dialogue propelled by an immaculate cast. DiCaprio is raw and eruptive, complementing Nicholson's off-putting marraige of perversion and grace. Ray Winstone, Vera Farmiga, all of them fantastic, but my favorite is Damon's intimidating antagonist, the puppet master behind the bloodshed. The film is perfect, well-rounded, a visceral experience.","0b304beb-9a50-41d2-ac66-2bf90a150a35",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-07-26","","RT","782310949"
