4.0,"There are no ""OMG SCORSESE~!"" moments. The script wavers from razor-sharp to frankly shit (with a strange obsession with Sigmund Freud). DiCaprio is half-decent, until you realise that's actually meant to be his character and not his character playing an undercover role. And yet this film COMPLETELY RULES IT. Damon is classy beyond even his growing reputation; Marky Mark is hilarious, backable as Seabiscuit and generally awesome; Ray Winstone is so there; and Nicholson is the Joker again, only better. The plot is thick and delicious as plum pudding, improved further with lashings of hot violence, and in general it's Scorsese's best film since the early 90s. 

Unfortunately marred by an Oscar, but you can't have everything.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-07-29","","RT","782854655"
