5.0,"What can I say -- Scorsese does it again.  What a surprise.  He has done several films about the mob/organized crime over the years, but never repeats himself.  The characters are all interesting, and I found that some of the parts were very different for the actors involved.  Mark Wahlberg's was my favorite; even with all the complicated (and scene-stealing) characters of Nicholson, Damon & DiCaprio.  Wahlberg kept me wanting more of Wahlberg.  His and Martin Sheen's characters played so well off each other.  And let's not forget Alec Baldwin; he was good too!  Lots of Scorsese violence, some real surprises and a great ending.   It's a disgrace to think that it has taken this long for Scorsese to get his Oscar, and I'm very happy that he was finally recognized for the artist that he is.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-07-29","","RT","782215468"
