2.0,"Well, basically it's about a gangster who becomes a snitch for the police department (Matt Damon), and a police officer who becomes a snitch for organized crime (Leonardo DiCaprio). The story had a lot of potential (specially being ripped off from one of the best Hong Kong Gangster films ever), yet does not come through in the end with any drama or emotion. As characters die through the course of the film, I could frankly care less. Also, the two main characters being in love with the same women seemed so implausible that it just came off as ridiculous and lazy on part of the writers. Moreover, maybe it's just my sense of language, but most of these characters did not come off too me as tough. Constantly cursing, and acting the whole time like your ready to start a fight does not come off as tough to me, and I could give a damn about their southie accents. I will admit, that even though Leonardo DiCaprio is not one of my favorite actors, I think he did a great job in this film. Yet, overall I was not that impressed with the acting, which is such a shame having such a great cast. The only one who really stands out is Mark Wahlberg, and unfortunately he got the least screen time of all. Even Jack Nicholson acted as well as ever, but could not really take it home with the weak dialogue he was given. The end of the film is the weakest of all, leaving me with a feeling of 'Oh, its over, whatever...' Please watch INFERNAL AFFAIRS instead!","",False,False,False,False,2.0,"2007-07-30","","RT","787788698"
5.0,"Only Scorcesse has the clever brilliance to weave such a masterpiece as this. One of the best films of the decade.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-07-30","","RT","787290365"
