3.0,"Overrated Scorsese film.  I've heard everyone claim this to be as good as his masterpiece ""Goodfellas,"" but I don't see it.  It's the least straightforward mob film I've ever seen, the convoluted plot concerns two insiders, one a Irish-American gangster (Matt Damon) posing at a Boston police detective and a cop (Leo DiCaprio) posing as mobster working for a crime boss (Jack Nicholson).  While well acted, the story is so complicated that its very confusing unless you've watched the film a few times.  Some of the plot elements which seem important (like the tan envelope...you know the one) are never mentioned again and basically leave the audience to deduce what happened.  It's almost like a few scenes that should have been in the movie were accidentally left on the cutting room floor.  However, its still an interesting film...if you want to put in the effort of taking notes to sort out all the details for it to make sense on the first viewing.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-07-30","","RT","782100490"
