4.5,"Scorsese is brave, Nicholson, DiCaprio, Wahlberg, Sheen, Damon and Farmiga are brilliant in this modern day Shakespearian Tragedy.

Undoubtedly people are discomfortable in the illustration of gangs and violence, but Scorsese has the ability to bring out the reality behind this lifestyle.

In this honest and bold feature, Scorsese reminds his audience that he is in control, and all things expected might as well be thrown out the window.

Plot twists are fun, but emotional twists and coping is at the forefront in this feature.  

DiCaprio, as usual, is one of the most under-rated actors of our time.  Nicholson made a brilliant decision in taking up this part and Wahlberg, Damon, Sheen and Farmiga can definitely hold their own.  Expect them in future roles beyond this one.

Any fan of crime and mob movies should see this movie.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-07-30","","RT","789104068"
