1.5,"The Departed is, along with his more recent efforts, notably such as the appallingly turgid ?Gangs of New York?, another depressing sign of the slide in to severe mediocrity on the part of the previously exemplary Scorsese. The Departed is a poor imitation of the Chinese 'Infernal Affairs' trilogy, which are all without a doubt handled with far more subtlety, intelligence and style in every respect. Di Caprio is reasonable, if not entirely convincing. Damon is however truly appalling, and conveys about as much menace and cunning as a lobotomised pet gerbil, a great shame given the genuinely brilliant performance by his Chinese counterpart in the same role. Add to this very poor cinematography, with everything seeming all too slapdash and sloppily executed for my tastes, and you are left with quite a mess of a film. Well worth avoiding at well over 2 hours long as well!","",False,False,False,False,1.5,"2007-08-01","","RT","782889262"
