4.0,"The actors gave not only convincing and edgy performances in The Departed, but their chameleonic adaptation to their characters' own role dissonance became a mingling of realistic portrayal of their roles and the dramatic surrealism of their personalities. This movie was so well paced that the audience has enough time to digest its gritty innards but is served their next tantalizing exposé into the minds of the characters before they can puke it back up. Scorsese is back in his element doing what he does best - directing gangster dramas. The script is adapted from the HK crime thriller Infernal Affairs. Even though I felt the script and strong performances were partially responsible for Scorsese's Oscar, it is long overdue looking at his body of work and does not come undeserved. However in the end, I am left with the feeling of having wanted more from The Departed, simply for it to have been more than an extremely well crafted adaptation, and to have been able to identify a sense of ingenuity which sets it apart from its predecessor.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-08-01","","RT","785154076"
