4.0,"A great movie that hooks you in from the get-go and has you hanging on until the end.  The acting is superb, especially that of Jack Nicholson. (Mark Wahlberg's acting is overrated in my opinion.)

Having now watched Infernal Affairs, I have to say that Departed is better in that it's more entertaining and provides a much deeper portrayal of the setting, the characters and the situation they're in, but it's worse in that it drags along and lacks the Hong Kong original's darker and more serious portrayal of the story.  I'd rate them about the same overall.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-08-02","","RT","787790316"
4.0,"To call this a return to form for Scorcese would imply that The Aviator and Gangs of New York weren't very good, which is not true, but it is a return to what Scorcese does best,  
Violent sweary and compelling Mafia gangster flicks.
The ever dependable Mr DiCaprio delivers a sterling portrayal of angst, terror and desparation, Jack Nicholson is... Jack Nicholson.  Matt Damon is deliciously deceitful as a corrupt FBI agent but the star of the show has to be Mark Wahlberg's foul mouthed and volatile covert ops agent.

Great Stuff.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-08-02","","RT","788620385"
