3.5,"A thrilling crime film with a great cast, and great performances from Damon, Di Caprio and Nicholson. After the interesting beginning, the main story is dramatic and full of suspense.

However, having already seen the Internal Affairs trilogy, this movie was not that great for me. It stayed fairly faithful to the original, but with everything done the American way. Compared to the original, this film used more humour, and to good effect. The HK film had more logical plot though.

The actors in the Hong Kong version had more (developed) character (or identity even).  A few important scenes were also simplified (police chiefs and crime boss confrontation) or removed (initial meeting between the two moles in audio shop). The ending is somewhat poor and anti-climatic. Instead of making you wanting more, it makes you feel confused.","40fb72c2-7b2f-4d01-aa80-beabb6c716dc",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-08-03","","RT","171151226"
