3.5,"I still couldnt believe that this had won the best picture title... having watched The Infernal Affairs first, I think this one is just some slightly better film of its kind. Infernal Affairs is a masterpiece, and i thought no one is going to top that, and till now, no one have topped it yet, not even this one. Okay, so i do admit that TD wasnt that bad as a remake, but it seems to me that scorsese only changed the 1st half of it, then the 2nd half of it is just a cardboard-cut-out of IA. I can tell you, the first half of it was quite boring, it wasnt till the 2nd half of it, it was getting interesting, that you all started to love it, admit it people. IA is a better psychological thriller, i love those emotional scenes where you see the actors ACT, without saying any lines, and the HK actors really did a great job. I personally think that they are even better than dicaprio and damon in some way. TD is just a movie which you can hear a hundred of swear words and shoutings, and that is what ppl complaining about this movie.

