5.0,"Anyone who thinks The Departed is a Hollywood ripoff/remake of a ""superior"" Chinese film called Infernal Affairs has obviously never seen both of them, or, if they have, haven't realistically compared the two. Lau and Mak, like many other Chinese filmmakers, copied the techniques of American action movies when making the Infernal Affairs trilogy, resulting in some cool action films with good plots and religious subtexts. Scorsese, while American, draws stylistic inspiration from Italian, French, Swedish and Japanese filmmakers from the late 1950s and 60s, and his films have consistently shown this by being different and better than other ""Hollywood movies"". In my opinion, this is Scorsese's best: all the themes and messages of the last three decades of his career, but actually woven through an intricate plot. It's an amazing movie, whereas it's Chinese source material is simply a very good action drama, and, in pure style, far more ""Hollywood"" than The Departed. If you prefer Infernal Affairs, that's fine, but to say that The Departed doesn't stand on its own merit is ridiculous. It's one of about only three movies in the past ten years to win Best Picture and deserve it.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-08-08","","RT","783010383"
