5.0,"Scorsese's back and he's scored again. This time his gangster flick takes place on the ""mean streets"" of South Boston, with an all star cast of topnotch toughs. You'll be blown away by Leonardo DiCaprio's caustic yet vulnerable undercover cop giving one of his best performances to date. As the screws tighten, you feel the pressure and the fear that almost give him a heart attack at being discovered as the mole trying to find the rat and not get caught by macabre mob boss, Jack Nicholson. Jack's wiseguy is witty, and wickedly monstrous, Matt Damon is disarmingly charming and sly, and Alec Baldwin is a kick as a know-it-all FBI head, who gives every dark line humor and a twist. Mark Wahlberg performance is like a pit bull going for the throat. I still say Scorsese should have won the Oscar for ""Goodfellas"", his classic masterpiece of the gangster genre, but this one is also a frightening study in the extremes of violence to which humans will go and he won the DGA award for best director for this movie. It will keep you in suspense to the end, as to who will get whacked by whom and when. Don't miss out on it.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-08-09","","RT","784690637"
