2.0,"I firmly believe that this is probably one of the most overrated films to come along within the past few years.  Perhaps my view is a bit biased, being that I saw Infernal Affairs (for those of you that don't know, ""The Departed"" is a remake of the Hong Kong film, ""Infernal Affairs"")first before this, but it really does not live up to the standard that Infernal Affairs set.  The plot is essentially the same as Infernal Affairs, yet The Departed contains some glaring flaws that were nonexistent in its Hong Kong counterpart.  My biggest problem with the film is the ending, which is pretty much the epitome of the Hollywood cliche that ""in the end, everyone gets what's coming to them"".  Part of what made Infernal Affairs a good movie is that it did not make of this overused plot device.  Secondly, Jack Nicholson's character        does not seem very consistent when compared to the same character present in Infernal Affairs.  Mark Wahlberg's character was unnecessary and obnoxious, and overall, it seems that almost all of the primary characters have no believable motives behind their actions, so it doesn't seem real.  Scorsese did not deserve all the praise he received for this movie (it really is an obvious and bad rip-off if Infernal Affairs), and it was absolutely not worthy of the Best Picture Oscar.","",False,False,False,False,2.0,"2007-08-11","","RT","782877296"
