0.5,"This movie promised a taut, exciting cat-and-mouse game between two intelligent, equally-matched antagonists, and it completely failed to deliver.

(spoiler alert!)

I was very patient with this movie.  The first hint something was wrong was the death of Martin Sheen's character.  The filmmakers had taken a potentially interesting character played by a great actor and killed him off by having him act in a stupid and out-of-character way.

Then came the death of Jack Nicholson.  So this super-intimidating crime boss is killed ... cowering in a back alley, not even putting up a struggle?  Okay, that's not particularly satisfying ...

But wait, there's more!  The mole in the police department is uncovered because ... well, he isn't uncovered at all, he just abruptly decides to go straight.  Yes, that's how the movie's main conflict is resolved -- the dude just changes his mind.  And this won an Oscar for Best Screenplay??

I haven't even mentioned what happens next.  The last 20 minutes of this movie are so spectacularly incompetent that I felt like I was watching an Ed Wood movie.  No, worse than that -- a USC student film.

(Okay, that was a cheap shot.  But seriously, this movie sucked.)

Scorsese has made interesting films before, and he will quite possibly make interesting films again.  But this one was an out-and-out failure on every level.","",False,False,False,False,0.5,"2007-08-11","","RT","790019461"
