4.0,"Beautifully made movie.  One of Scorcese's ""masterpieces"" definitely.  I have to say I think the film is great until about the last 10 minutes.  Everything happens in the last 10 minutes.  It's almost hard to follow (and that's hard for ME to say that)...I also think that there is footage that should be put into the ending so it ties up the holes.  Those that have seen the movie might get what I'm saying.
Other than that...the acting is incredible Leo, Matt, Mark are all fantastic.  I think Matt Damon was very underappreciated for his role.  I also think there are amazing supporting performances by Martin Sheen and Alec Baldwin.  But believe it or not...the performance I was most impressed by was Jack Nicholson.  He's just so amazing.  HAHA.
