2.5,"Firstly i'd like to say that this isn't the disaster that many have claimed and yet it is nowhere near the level that deserves an Oscar; although it probably was about time Scorsese was recognised by the academy just not for a play by numbers retelling of a superior film. That said he still delivers a good set piece, and Damon and Dicaprio are reliable, Nicholson camps it up to unbearable levels whilst Sheen phones it in and Wahlberg is far too abstract for a role in the state police. At times the movie feels as though Scorsese is forcing some kind of filmmaking that is almost perversely influenced by himself. Ignore the quotes this is nowhere near as slick as Goodfellas or indeed Casino, you get the impression Marti wishes it was. Schoonmaker does a disasterous job of the edit and the soundtrack is skewered horribly but somehow it just manages to hang in there, holding your attention. Laughable sequences aside (cartoon wipe and rat on the balcony) Scorsese produces an entertaining gangster movie that only really stands up as a popcorn munching infernal affairs.","",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2007-08-19","","RT","782214747"
