5.0,"An intricately crafted plot, engaging characters and flawless set-pieces keep you blissfully unaware of the fact that you're not watching a crime-drama, but rather an exploration of the themes of identity and nihilism. The characters are morally ambiguous; violent and selfish with warped senses of loyalty, they are only painted as heroic or villainous by the circumstances of their environment. The film perfectly captures the strangling, claustrophobic modern Irish culture that pervades the Boston setting. The Departed has a hefty running time, but there is no redundancy or long-windedness, as every crafty shot is essential. I haven't seen the Hong Kong original, so before you tell me how much better it is, kindly shut the fuck up. This is easily Scorsese's best flick since Goodfellas, if not his best ever.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-08-19","","RT","783915378"
