4.0,"This film will always be tainted for me because director Martin Scorsese stole the 2006 Best Director Academy Award from Clint Eastwood. That said, this movie was strong. Though it draws on strong parallels from The Godfather, it tackles many deep and common themes found not only in criminals, but in law-abiding, upstanding citizens. The casting really helped this film as well. Mark Wahlberg got a well-deserved Oscar nod for Supporting Actor and Leo DiCaprio's performance was actually believable, which was a welcome ""departure"" from his convoluted roles in The Aviator and Blood Diamond.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-08-21","","RT","787012587"
