1.0,"Scorsese may have won the oscar for this one, but always keep in mind that the Oscars are far from perfect, and the academy felt they owed him one for passing him over for the far superior ""Raging Bull"". This film features spotty accents (having lived in Boston, I was not convinced of the authenticity of perhaps half the cast, including leads), a meandering and unfulfilling story line, a decidedly lukewarm love interest, stereotypical characters, and direction that I hesitate to describe as anything better than just about par. This is latest in a line of films of poor quality from this once formidible artist (starting with ""Casino,"" a poor companion piece for ""Goodfellas,"" and then moving on to such forgettable epics as ""Gangs of New York"" (Daniel Day-Lewis was the exception to that testament to poor acting) and ""The Aviator"".) This film somehow won editing awards, despite the fact that at a whopping 2 h 30 min, I know pack rats that would have discarded a full half of the film. Save your time, money, and some fond memories of a once good director. Don't bother.","",False,False,False,False,1.0,"2007-08-21","","RT","790533614"
