3.0,"Relied far too much on gangster movie cliches. The opera, the good Cop/bad cop team, the stereotypes and the terrible accents all work towards undermining a really excellent story.
The performances were, on the whole very good, DiCaprio especially (I don't think I've ever said that before in my life) and Nicholson and Wahlberg made the best out of the ridiculous characatures they were given. Matt Damon and Vera Farmiga however were giant acting black holes. 
The dialogue was corny, the cinematography had moments of obtuse weirdness, there was just very little originality or depth to it.
That's not to say the film was terrible, it was actually very watchable, but almost all of it's value came from the story, convincing me that I probably should have sat and watched Infernal Affairs instead.
I can't believe it won the oscar for best adapted script, that was the worst thing about it, and I certainly can't believe it won best picture.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-08-23","","RT","786220984"
