4.5,"Scorsese adapts 2002âs Infernal Affairs for the American audience with his trademark blunt violence and gliding camera.  Matt Damon and Leonardo Dicaprio go head to head, each under cover for different sides of the law and each trying to sniff out the other.  Jack Nicholson, Alec Baldwin, Ray Winstone, Martin Sheen, and Mark Wahlberg round out an astounding cast of hard-hitting guys from both sides.  The pinnacle of this well scripted film happens when not a word is uttered, Damon and Dicaprio breathing into the phone, waiting for the other to speak.  With a now in-joke, surprise ending, the film delivers a rounded view of the inner workings of opposing sides of the law.  Scorseseâs continued use of a varied soundtrack, his insistence on jump cuts, and his attention to straight-out violence are right at home in this film.","49f7eda4-4f5b-4d86-b021-752970c638fd",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-08-24","","RT","790981423"
