3.0,"Best Picture? Really? I enjoyed this movie for the most part but sadly it's overrated. Scorsese's directing is great and the script is really good but there's so many things lacking. DiCaprio is really good, Damon is good and Nicholson plays Nicholson. Everyone in the film tries so hard to do the Boston accent and most pull it off but Nicholson doesn't even bother trying to even act Irish let alone speak like he's Boston-Irish. Am I supposed to buy that he's the head of the Irish mob? It's an obvious standout and, well, I don't buy it and it's disappointing. This film is littered with great actors and they all do a great job but Damon is not a great bad guy. These performances just can't compare to the performances of Andy Lau, Tony Leung and Eric Tsang from ""Infernal Affairs."" Not to mention the ridiculous and almost laughable ending. ""Infernal Affairs"" knew it wanted to be an entertaining cop drama and it succeeded but this seems to have more ambition, complete with a much longer runtime, and it fails to do anything more. Perhaps if this was an original idea I would give it higher marks but it's a remake that doesn't surpass the original. It's enjoyable and was good, it's just underwhelming and overrated. There's far better crime dramas out there that deserve your time more than this.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-08-25","","RT","790171783"
