4.0,"Leonardo DiCaprio does nothing for me. Usually. MAYBE his performance in The Man in the Iron Mask but it wasn't really noteable. Most movies I've seen him in(haven't seen Blood Diamond or Gangs of New York yet) he seems to play the same character, in my view. So after some Shakesperian ambitions are continued with equally passionate yelling of a girl named Rose , he would suddenly escape Tom Hanks a couple of times, then go insane along Hawkeye from MASH (to make a funny parallel :P ) and anyway we get to this one.
Well, so yes, ok, I really enjoyed his performance in this movie as I genuinely enjoyed the movie in itself. Hasn't happened for some time to me, to actually react to action scenes, if that has ever happened. 
It's great, what can I say, I think I could be a bit annoyed I liked i so much because of its blockbustery touch but I did and that's the end of it.
DiCaprio really can act or at least in this movie he does, showing a deep struggle that reaches the viewer. And if we've seen that before, the anxiety of an insider in close relationship with enemies, we haven't really seen what's coming up next and I'm talking about two such moles, with two different attitudes on what they are doing, simultaneously.
I find it terrific, the way their plans interract through the psychiatrist they're both interested in, through Frank, through scenes such as the phone call one. It's just great, judge al you want. :)
Well done, Mr. Scorsese, you've entertained me through suspense and action.
Last but not least, all hail Jack of course. (though I must give the credit to DiCaprio..reluctantly but necessarily)

I've heard the original surpasses this one. That may be, but as far as entertainment goes, this production succeeds.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-08-25","","RT","788887145"
