0.5,"Oh for goodness' sake - this was such a good, stylish, understated HK film; how could it have gone so horribly, horribly wrong?  I mean, even setting aside the fact that no human alive can tell DiCaprio, Wahlberg and Matt Damon apart (in all their squinty-eyed glory), the problems of this film can be summed up in the final shot: why did he have to die (because Hollywood wouldn't let you have a bad guy who lived?), and WHY did there have to be a RAT outside on the railing?

I was almost prepared to give it three stars for a just-sorta-middling effort; then they had to put in the rat.  Who WROTE this?  It's like David Mamet puked, and that puke wrote the picture.  Duh.  Guh.  Buh.  Avoid.  Rent Infernal Affairs instead.

Wait wait wait - Best PICTURE?  Best DIRECTOR?  What the hell film did THEY watch?  That's insane, and I'm deducting half a star for each of those, and another half for Best Editing...Best SCREENPLAY?!?  Am I on another PLANET, here?  What did I just say about David Mamet's puke?  Oh, lord...I don't know if I can take away that last half a star and go into negative numbers, but I would if I could at this stage.","",False,False,False,False,0.5,"2007-08-28","","RT","783404545"
