4.0,"This movie would have been perfect. If only they hadn't ended it the way they did.

And no, my criticism of the ending has nothing to do with me wanting a formulaic ""Hollywood"" ending (and anyone who thinks this isn't a Hollywood film is kidding themselves). It's because it was just bad writing, plain and simple. A weak, cop-out of an ending that felt forced and pretentious.

You see, the biggest problem with Hollywood endings is that they usually don't fit with their stories. They're endings where the writer has gone out of their way to twist and contort the the conclusion into a positive outcome. Well, ""The Departed"" does the same thing, only on the other extreme. Instead of thinking about who the characters truly are and having the balls to see them through to their logical conclusions, the movie flakes out and pulls a cliche ""Anti-Hollywood"" ending.

Cliche Hollywood endings = Bad writing
Cliche, Anti-Hollywood endings = Bad writing

It's a shame, because the rest of the movie was so fantastic.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-08-29","","RT","790044434"
