1.0,"What a disappointment. To me, this movie just seemed like an exact copy of ""Gangs of New York."" This movie went absolutely nowhere for me. Sure there were some moderately suspenseful moments, but nothing in this movie merited it's popularity. Maybe society is just to stupid to realize that this movie had been done before, but for some reason it took home a best picture as well as countless other oscars. The thing I found most disturbing about this film is that there were no relatable characters, or anyone with any redeeming features whatsoever. The cast showed so much potential, but in the end none of them did anything worth while. Leonardo DiCaprio was good. His acting was the only reason I kept watching. But Matt Damon and Mark Wahlberg (who look identical) were both horrible. It wasn't just that their character's had no humanity in them at all, it was just bad acting. And Jack...well, he played the same character he's always played. People criticize this film for the ending, which did seem like an easy way to wrap up the story, but there are so many other fundamental flaws with this film that it's hard to even get to the finish line with this overrated flop.","",False,False,False,False,1.0,"2007-08-29","","RT","786564435"
