5.0,"Most accessible Scorsese I have seen, and probably Hollywood agrees, which is why he finally got the Oscar he deserves.  He's tough -  impressionistic, psychological and -heck - I don't always get what his stuff is all about. Departed however, makes clear and politically relevant comments. Argued with my father over which was best film of the year - this or ""The Last King of Scotland"" - I will stick with The Departed. As always the texture of his films is so thick you want to scoop it off the screen with a butter knife and smear it all over your lips and face. In this respect, prefer Scorsese to David Lynch - more control, less pretense, never looks like he's working hard ... brilliant, brilliant film ... so careful in every respect - definitely one of his masterpieces.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-08-31","","RT","789965302"
