4.0,"If there is a more complex movie than this, it is beyond human comprehension. The Departed is one of those movies that when you think about how incredibly detailed it is you wonder how and why anyone would even try to attempt to film it in a cohesive way. Scorsese out did himself, The Departed is an instant legend. Not to mention the acting is so real it's unbeatable. And Leo is the man. The only thing to dislike in this movie...is that there is hardly anything to take from it. I didn't learn anything, however, it is one perfectly told story. Amazing, a crime-movie-MUST-SEE.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-09-02","","RT","784884625"
4.5,"A truly excellent crime thriller directed as only Martin Scorsese knows how. In this remake of the Chinese film ""Infernal Affairs"" two men, one a criminal who has infiltrated the Police, and the other an undercover cop working as a mole in a crime syndicate, find themselves in a race against time to discover the identity of the other, all under the watchful gaze of Mob Boss Jack Nicholson (who as always is brilliant). The stellar cast also features Matt Damon, Leonardo DiCaprio, Mark Wahlberg and Martin Sheen, who all put in fantastic performances. I'm not a DiCaprio fan, but I must say that he is quite convinving in this role, which is probably his best. This is edge of your seat stuff, and the last ten minutes build to an unforgettable ending.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-09-02","","RT","790441289"
