5.0,"This remake of the classic Hong Kong film ""INFERNAL AFFAIRS"" (which this movie was inspired by Micheal Mann's HEAT) was a perfect remake of the film.  Martin Scorcese tied up some of the loose ends and characters from The HK version real nice.  The Departed is a great film from start to finish with a cast that's unbeatable. As always, Scorcese adds his flare and touch to un-romanticize the ""gangster"" image that's instilled in our youth of today.  But Scorcese poses serious question in the differences between the criminal element and the law. What's most important is the point that on both sides, they are just cogs in the machine of justice. As always, the glamorous life of a gangster begins as it ends-an ambiguous future in crime that always ends in death.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-09-03","","RT","791654293"
