2.0,"For 90 mins it feels like a better than average Scorsese film. Nicholson's hillarious, Damon is solid, Leo okay, Ray Win not good, Wahlberg holy shit. The problem with the film-making becomes clear in the last 30 mins when the director suddenly has to tie up all the loose ends of the story, and we're in a different film where characters are killed in a shooting gallery. This may seem realistic but the kills are glib and upset the pacing of the previous part of the film. Its a serious fracture and it ruins the film's pace as well as our investment of the story. A shame.","",False,False,False,False,2.0,"2007-09-12","","RT","782336096"
