2.0,"the reason why i dont like this movie, aside from the fact that i was highly insulted by helen mirren saying it was a japanese movie, is that it cant live up to the expectations of the original.
infernal affairs had a clear distinguished plotline and performances. this remake had endless swearing, and way too many graphic blood scenes
i like martin scorsese, i really liked his previous films and the fact that he won his first oscar for this movie is great. but i believe that he should have won for any of his previous outings rather then this sluggish remake, as it ponders on for way too long, while the original Infernal Affairs was only a slim 90 minutes, aind its fast pace and unique confrontations between Andy Lau and Tony Leung Ka Wai are fantastic.
