4.0,"having seen the hong kong version, infernal affairs, i had my doubts about this film deserving its oscar win.  the plot of infernal affairs did well enough for moving past the action movie genre into something more thought-provoking, but it didn't seem enough for an oscar.  now having seen the hollywood version, i understand.  unfortunately for tony leung and andy lau, i think the actors overall were able to bring much more dimension to the characters.  leo was brilliant as costigan...he tends to play the same tough-guy-hiding-his-vulnerability roles, but he does well in them.  his portrayal of a man falling apart was palpable and real.  nicholson was genius as well, and i enjoyed his expanded role in this version.  damon does well for himself and he fits his character, but i liked andy lau better in that role.  overall this screenplay did much better at allowing the characters to explore their descents into neurosis and insanity as deception and obsession cause their controlled lives to fall apart.

the last scene disappointed me, however.  i enjoyed the ending of infernal affairs more.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-09-15","","RT","784228406"
