2.0,"Well obviously this movie had a lot to live up to.  People seemed to catch onto this movie quite early, due to its star power and such.  But I think the Best Picture Oscar is rarely given to the film that actually is worthy of it, although I can't speak for that year's nominees.  And the ceremony that year seemed like a Scorsese pity party, which is always pathetic and undeserved no matter who it's happening to.  But anyway, back to the movie.  I didn't think there was anything that outstanding about it, first of all, and Scorsese's influence on the soundtrack is at its worst here.  If I ever make a movie of my own, ""Gimme Shelter"" will be playing in the background of every scene, because it's such a powerful tune that people haven't heard nearly enough of.  And the shitty faux-Pogues, these-go-to-11 music didn't help either.  I'll also be sure to show at least a dozen people being shot point-blank in the head, because that's edgy and cool and what real life is about.  But mostly I want to cast only the biggest and brightest Hollywood stars of the era, because there's no such thing as too much star power, and why pay any attention to actors who try to keep a low profile anyway?  And I want my actors to have unbelievably bad Boston accents.  Especially DiCaprio, because his magnificent acting abilities will surely balance it out.  

This movie was a remake.  Scorsese is irrelevant and should stop making movies.  Let's maybe watch the originals instead of wasting millions of dollars trying to make these films more palatable to an American audience.","",False,False,False,False,2.0,"2007-09-19","","RT","781796945"
