4.0,"American versions of Asian movies have been pretty terrible of late (see The Ring, Pulse, Dark Water and i could go on but you get the point!) and i feared the worst when i heard that Mou gaan dou (Infernal Affairs) was to get the same treatment. When i first saw Infernal Affairs i believed it to be as good as Hollywood crime blockbusters like Heat so didn't see the point in it being remade. However with Scorsese at the helm, a quality cast (Wahlberg almost manages to upstage Nicholson!) and with William Monahan following Sui Fai Mak's original screenplay fairly closely, i can see why this movie has done so well. For those put off by sitting through movie with subtitles (you know who you are!) this is perfect","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-09-19","","RT","788969178"
