2.5,"What a stinker.  Makes me appreciate the sheer greatness of Infernal Affairs even more.  So much wrong with this movie, may have liked it if I'd hadn't seen the film it was a remake of first, but still I see it for being a pile of poo.  Poor in the same way Vanilla Sky is, but not quite that bad.  The cast, considering their pedigree, is  piss poor when comparing the main four characters.  Lau, Leung, Tsang and Wong dick all over Damon, Di Caprio, Nicholson and Sheen.  Didn't like how they merged the two female characters into one, ESPECIALLY hated the fact that Di Caprio was shagging her.  Di Caprio seemed completely unlikeable and I had no sympathy for him, unlike Tony Leung in the original.  Lau is charming and slightly sympathetic whereas Damon is just RUBBISH.  WHAT THE FUCK WAS THE POINT OF MARK WAHLBERG'S CHARACTER?  Did they just have him in it to show up like a hoodie at the end.  Would've been stronger to not have him at all, or let Damon kill him off.  Poor show, poor show.  Best Picture my arse.","",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2007-09-25","","RT","785226909"
