3.0,"This is not a terrible movie.  It's a fundamentally sound piece of American cinema for which the Academy decide to finally reward Scorsese for his lifetime of achievements.  Discounting the fact that this was almost a direct remake (even more direct than say Vanilla Sky to Open Your Eyes) of a film that came out only 4 years earlier, this is an interesting film well directed and acted by seasoned Hollywood professionals.  The original screenplay from which this movie's screenplay was based on is so sound that even upon losing all cultural and anecdotal references so poorly translated, the plot still grips and fascinates the simplistic mind sets of Oscars voters.  I would strongly disagree with those who claim that this film butchered the original.  What they did was make the film understandable and relatable for a larger audience.  For what it's worth, I think they did a great job with the material they've got, it just wasn't a particularly laborious amount of work.  For those of you who like your movies a little less ""b & w"" with many different shades of gray, see the original.  For those who enjoy stylized high drama in classic Scorsese fashion, you'll dig this.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-10-05","","RT","781972587"
