1.5,"Although I don't think of the original INFERNAL AFFAIRS as a masterpiece in HK cinema, watching THE DEPARTED actually made me appreciate the original that much more... all the additions, as well as omissions Scorsese and his cohorts went about with the remake not only didn't improve on the problems with the original, it made things far worse... with THE DEPARTED winning best picture at the Academy Awards, it only removes further credibility to what's fast becoming a depreciated ceremony marred by Hollywood inbreeding and studio interests... while Hollywood continues to ruin potentiallly great work by banking on Michael Bay-type story treatments just to ensure even 12 year olds could understand their films, they seem to forget many of the films they make aren't supposed to be watched by children to begin with. Scorsese should have won Best Picture for at least a couple of his films in the past, yet he is given an Oscar for the worst film in his body of works... it's a sad day in cinema, and one viewing of this garbage is enough evidence to show our civilization is defintely on the slide....","",False,False,False,False,1.5,"2007-10-08","","RT","796615864"
