5.0,"Expertly filmed, with a top-notch plot.  Not sure it should have won Best Picture though, because that rat at the end right in front of the State House was just too over the top -- and it was incongruous too, given that I didn't see one State Senator take a bribe in the film, or anything like that.  But Leo . . . I tell you, I wasn't all that impressed with him in Titanic, but his performance in this film -- you could literally see him losing his mind -- is the stuff that Oscars are made of.  Forest Whitaker should watch his back (and he may well be able to do so, on account of that lazy eye . . . okay, that was mean.  But he's rich, so it's okay).  Oh yeah, spoiler alert.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-10-13","","RT","793084390"
