0.5,"it sad to think that martin scorsese, once america's greatest living director, was forced to shoot a film like this to win his first best film's cademy award.  in fact, this is by far his worst film.  it is a typical serialized hollywood thriller blockbusters, with all the devices of that genre: nice chicks, artificial plot, big loads of guns, ridicolous dialogues, and two genetically modified actors like di caprio and damon who simply have not the right faces for a scorsese's film.  the director's usual traits - baroque camera movements and positions, ""vintage"" soundtrack, effective visualisation - result out of place. the same for ballhaus cinematography, whose best moment is at the beginning (keeping the face of nicholson in shadow is a clear tribute to gordon willis' work in ""the godfather"").  it is a pity that scorsese's name is associated with a film like this.","",False,False,False,False,0.5,"2007-10-16","","RT","782953269"
