4.5,"Scorsese strikes again! And this time, he got the recognition he has deserved for so long in the form of an Oscar. Funnily enough, this isn't his best film - not by a long way - but it's still really, really good. 

It's a remake of <i>Infernal Affairs</i>, which in 2002 put Hong Kong well and truly on the map for 21st century Cinema. And guess what? It's better than the original. No, really, it is. And that's coming from someone who is almost always disappointed by remakes of great films. I really feel that the story flows a lot better here, and the trio of Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon and Jack Nicholson is pretty damn formidable.

Two and a half hours from start to finish, it's an entire hour longer than the original, but one thing you can be sure of with Scorsese is that every minute of his film is necessary. Every scene, every line spoken...it all plays a part in making the film as good as it is.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-10-16","","RT","782914005"
