4.0,"This movie is very enjoyable, paced almost impeccably, and for Matt Damon, gives him a character against type. Where as I've seen Leornado Dicaprio do characters similar to this before (and by the way he does it very well) I just thought Matt Damon was the better character of the two -  ruthless, evil and conniving. In fact every actor in this movie puts in a good performance bar Mark Wahlberg who really tested my nerves with his bullshit good cop/bad cop (well he seems he wants to be a bad cop just he's more annoying than anything else, although truthfully in the end he gets his wish). 

The slightly unhinged cop undercover and the ruthless and conniving gangster infiltrating the police works extremely well and each group playing off one another through them is a very clever plot device. Also, Jack Nicolson's charisma as gangland chief Costello gives the film a slightly lighter edge (which is no bad thing, especially for people who don't usually watch gangster movies. It eases them in better).

The end is death heavy and slightly disappointing, one scene in particular (which if I remember was in 'Infernal Affairs' the original Hong Kong movie this is based off as well) had me going 'eh, why!? Why do that!'.

Despite some of these niggles I have to admit I really enjoyed this movie and only ever was bored for a little bit in the first hour (although truthfully that's cos everyone was coming in and out of the room while I was watching it, and at one point I had to put the rubbish out cos it was bin day the next day) when I missed a few things and had to catch up. Even if you don't like gangster movies this is still a good watch.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-10-17","","RT","786157135"
