4.5,"I love Martin Scorses and this film is an example of his incredible skill as a filmmaker.  I have not seen the original film (Infernal Affairs) but the film is excellent from start to finish with a gripping plot, excellent acting, and beautiful cinematography.  Although its characters are somewhat larger than life (especially Jack Nicholson's) the film never loses its down to earth feeling.  Keeping it real is something Scorses has always been excellent at doing (Raging Bull, Taxi Driver, etc.).  Mostly this is a film about deceit and how who you are, what you want to be, and what you are supposed to be can create such havoc on the 'soul.'","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-10-17","","RT","796862460"
