2.0,"I knew a man who lived down by the lake who made his living bartering and trading and kicking the bellies of pregnant women seeking to terminate their pregnancy at discount prices (at 5.00 a pop during the depression, it was welcomed with open arms).  We went golfing every couple of weeks together, on one such outing he set up a proposition for me, ""Get me 30 pairs of cotton panties smeared with strawberry pudding and I'll make you my running-mate.""  I did as he said, looting mem-mem's undergarment drawer.  Once they were collected and delivered to him he decided, ""Ehh... I don't really want to do that any more.  Seems like it's more trouble than it's worth; I'd rather just play Sega Saturn -- have you seen the graphics on this thing?  Out of this world!""  --  It was one of the most infuriatingly tedious and disappointing six months of my life at the time, that was until ""The Departed"" came out 13 years later.","bb1289d1-31b2-4080-a82c-44c6c3f660b5",False,False,False,False,2.0,"2007-10-21","","RT","788979954"
