4.0,"There's not much wrong with 'The Departed' other than it's a Martin Scorsese movie. DiCaprio and Wahlberg are both superb and there are moments of visual brilliance - but the film has none of the depth of character and attention to detail of Goodfellas, Taxi Driver, Raging Bull etc.

Also, the soundtrack, although superb is poorly used - and the 'wham bam' pacing of the first hour actually comes across quite forced and  suggests a film made for those with zero attention spans.

Still, it's a highly entertaining watch and an action thriller of exceptional quality. And any movie which features the cover of 'Exile on Main St.' in a key scene deserves 4 stars right off the bat.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-10-22","","RT","562313598"
