4.0,"Pretty good film. I don't understand the love everyone has for it; while ""pretty good"" is not low praise, I don't think I would have given it Best Picture. The plot is interesting, if a bit convoluted, the cinematography is good and most of the supporting cast (Mark Wahlberg, Alec Baldwin, Martin Sheen) as well as Matt Damon are spectacular. I thought however that the female lead and Leonardo DiCaprio fell pretty short, and Jack Nicholson's turn as the mob boss Frank Costello, interesting at the film's start, only becomes very strange by its end. The high point is the script, which falls short sometimes in the dramatic movements but which possess some of the best movie jokes I've seen in years. Rent it, rave about it, but no need to keep it on the shelf at home.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-10-27","","RT","784276371"
