5.0,"Great film.

I won't talk about it at great length because it's just a brilliant film, and that's about all you can say.

The only thing I can see wrong with this film is Matt Damon's death which has to be the most unconvincing screen death ever in the history of cinema. If I can get a video of it then I'll put it up on this page. 

Here's the scene: Matt Damon's character has just gone shopping, he returns home, tries stroking a dog but the owner of the dog pulls the dog away (because Matt Damon is a ""fuckin' rat motherfucker rargh!"" or something), Matt Damon then opens the door to his flat and finds Mark Wahlberg in it. Mark Wahlberg is wearing plastic bags on his feet so that he leaves no trace of evidence, points a gun at Matt Damon, Matt Damon says 'ok' nonchalantly and just after he says that, Mark Wahlberg shoots Matt Damon in the face leaving blood splattered all over his door and the wall behind him. Then, in all of about 2 seconds, Matt Damon then winces a little bit, does a weird little dance, pulls a face that looks similiar to early video recordings of Paul McCartney in The Beatles playing on Ed Sullivan, and then falls to the floor still holding his shopping.

Cue the Team America impression... ""MAAATTT DAAAAAAMON!!!""","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-10-29","","RT","799330977"
