4.5,"Awesome.  Scorsese definitely deserved his oscar for this film which was surprisingly realistic in a wave of downright silly undercover cop flicks.  For a little while, I doubted this, but the film redeemed itself as time went off and had a great ending.  To the lady in the store who ruined this ending, may ye swab the decks in hades.  I went all this time without seeing the film (been out over a year) and not having anyone ruin anything, and as I pluck the video from the bin at the store yesterday, this lady ruins the ending.

Back to the film, it was great.  Probably the best role I've seen Matt Damon in ever.  The entire cast, with the likes of Di Caprio,   Nicholson, Whalberg, and Sheen, was spectacular of course.

There were a few loose ends, of course, but that was mostly attributed to a very complex screenplay.  Direction and execution of said screenplay was monumental, and a great film success.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2007-11-07","","RT","783808837"
