5.0,"Perfect. Perfect. Perfect. Movies of this magnitude can be hard to review because the plot scope is so big and entailed, it makes you feel almost vein trying. Though mostly derived from Siu Fai Mak's Infernal Affairs, this is Scorcese back at the top of his game. There is not one even marginal performance in the picture. Stepping away from the obvious praising of Nicholson, Damon, DiCaprio, etc., it is the character roles that really loft the movie to the heights it reaches. Mark Wahlbergh, Martin Sheen, and Alec Baldwin make for a hilarious, yet smart and realistic trio of Boston Police, and who the hell will ever forget Mr. French!! With Van Morrison and the Dropkick Murphys in the soundtrack, this film literally has it all. I wish that I could name better films (I'm sure I could with enough time), but I can't think of any off hand.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-11-08","","RT","901023772"
