3.5,"Really gripping film that kept twisting but I found that by the end I was just empty. I felt some sympathy for Costigan and a lot for the hapless love interest but beyond that they were a sorry bunch of thugs and criminals using and double-crossing each other. I almost cheered when Costello got killed. Overall it really left me with a dim view of humankind.

That said, it was beautifully done (though possibly the rat at the end was a misjudgment), well acted and I genuinely couldn't guess what was going to happen next. I also liked that no-one really got away with anything and that they were all consumed by the mess they got themselves into. It was interesting to watch how people behave in such situations.","cd6cab5f-b238-4876-85f8-753c00d1b7f1",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-11-10","","RT","797555521"
