3.5,"Ok movie, great ending. It seems to teeter on the edge of having a message or theme or social commentary, but it doesn't quite make it. I'm not sure why this won Best Picture. Out of the others, I've only seen the Queen, and frankly, that was more deserving. 

Since we've already seen Damon do the Southie thing, it wasn't remarkable. But DiCaprio did a great job as the reluctant mole, and Wahlberg was impressive. 

But on the flip side, I'm just starting to dislike Nicholson more and more. As one reviewer put it, he's just ""play-acting."" Here's what another reviewer said:

""Sporting a devilish ""The Witches of Eastwick"" goatee, his eyebrows working at hyper-speed, the legendary actor cavorts through the picture, having so much fun that, at times, he teeters on doing, well, a Jack Nicholson impersonation.""","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-11-11","","RT","785822003"
