5.0,"I finally saw this film on HBO a couple days ago and it's just as fantastic as everyone says it is.  This is a phenomenal movie that easily ranks with Casino, Goodfellas, Raging Bull and Taxi Driver among  Martin Scorsese's finest movies.  It's a tour-de-force with a brilliant plot of duality. One of the greatest duality tales of all-time, you never really know who's who or what's what throughout the film.  I believe it's Leonardo DiCaprio's best acting yet and yet another spectacular performance by Matt Damon, who has to rank among the cream of the acting crop in Hollywood with his portrayal of Colin Sullivan.   I haven't even mentioned the great supporting roles of Mark Wahlberg, Jack Nicholson (let's face it, the movie's about Costigan and Sullivan, not Costello), Martin Sheen, Alec Baldwin and Vera Farmiga, who adds to the incredible atmosphere of double-crossing and deception.   A wonderful movie.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-11-14","","RT","781782307"
