4.0,"A typical Scorsese in many ways, which is a good thing. There's a lot of violence and swearing, and in the middle of it are two men who are looking for themselves, but in quite different ways. While DiCaprio's character's quest is for salvation as much as the truth, the corrupt cop played by Matt Damon is on a less metaphorical search for the mole inside the police, which makes for a good story twist, but does not necessarily give the character as much depth as it might have deserved. Only in few moments the two of them seem to be equally lost.
Nicholson is playing his part in the brilliant but somewhat familiar manner he has cultivated over the last few years. This part was probably written with him in mind and he plays it well, but doesn't really add anything new.
Anyway, solid performances from all three headliners, aided by a great cast of supporting actors make this an enjoyable movie (of course only if the violence and swearing don't turn you off).
Plus great pictures by Michael Ballhaus, as usual.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-11-16","","RT","802954294"
