2.0,"Amongst the worst of Martin Scorcesse pictures and not a necessity in HD. The movie feels very uninspired and rarely has the charm and spontaneity that have marked his many classics. Despite the much superior 'Infernal Affairs' and the director's talent in handling remakes (e.g. 'Cape Fear'), the cast looks bored and the writing and soundtrack choices are very poor. I always wonder if De Niro would've made a difference to this one had he been available... Good story but some of the scenes were literally pulled off the original Hong-Kong 'Infernal Affairs' storyline. The overall production budget seemed wasted and more suited towards one of the rarely weak episodes of a 'Sopranos' tv show. The whole Irish mob angle was also poorly played, watched 'State of Grace' instead. Jack Nicholson seemed to be playing a very low-budget criminal, who seems more like a retiree spending his free time within the confines of the local bar. He really looked embarassing picking up a shoe with all his strength and being tough... The whole New England and Bostonian accent thing too was a bit gimmicky, sometimes heavily pronounced and at other times, barely heard. Overall, a disgrace that this was voted by the Academy as Best Picture/Director in 2006.","",False,False,False,False,2.0,"2007-11-21","","RT","804681958"
