3.5,"This movie was a LOT better than I thought it would be . . . Leonardo DiCRAPIO - but decently unannoying and convincingly gritty, Matt Damon - a little to hunkish and likeable but is easily forgiven in his Bostonian attitude he lays down, Mark Wahlberg - who would have thought that there should have been more of him.  But what REALLY anchored the movie down was Jack Nicholson.  The story was half decent and the music definitely was good - without Jacko, the movie would have been lost in boring mediocrity.
