2.5,"I am so disappointed. I thought it felt tacky. No real style. We didn't get involved with the characters real inner troubles. They took the Idea of Infernal affairs and striped it bare to produce this, what I would call, failed attempt. They even tried to make references to the original. Dicaprio with his arm cast was one but the arm cast means more in the original because he has it on when we first see the character and we relise why when watching the 3 film. Matt Damon's large stereo that his girlfriend put the CD in was another but that stereo is how the original pair meet not just something on the shelf. All these things are characters in there own way but this film had no characters. The biggest example I can make is the scenes on the roof. It looked like they had just built that with wood. No glass, no reflection, no looking at yourself. you probably think I'm one of those hate remakes people but I'm not. I thought the original Ring film was pants but I love the American remake. I think the best thing about this film was that they put an american ending to it so they hopefully can not make or mess up the third original film.","",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2007-11-26","","RT","471953934"
