5.0,"Very rarely does a film like this have such impact, but at the same time have such a sense of realism and superb acting. Scorsese is at his best, and not since Taxi Driver has he mustered such gusto in his stylish and profound body of work. It's not just the directing either, it's the cast that simply mows down any other movie in it's class. The Departed which is loosely based off of Infernal Affairs isn't even close to a remake, it's a whole new concept of idenity and perception. There s nothing but a complete and total treatise of identity from the film's brilliant script, along with Dicaprio and his painful portrayl of the loss of idenity. It's one of the oldest concepts in any medium, but he plays it to the extreme. This is easily one of the most grittiest, yet stylized films I have ever had the honor of seeing and is easily one of my favorite films. The Departed not only rounds itself out with class from it's crew and stars, but because of it's nihlistic and morose ending. Yet still, there's something left at the end when you look upon the golden chapel that feels complete, no matter the outcome of a tense, terse, and overtly shocking film. A pure piece of cinema that everyone should own.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-11-27","","RT","804354336"
