3.0,"High-polish, well-produced, great in just about everything--acting, writing, directing, plot, characterization, etc.--but while entertained I wasn't particularly moved by the experience. The big thing I kept wondering is, why are we so fascinated by mobsters and their activities? It seems so many of the greatest movies have been about mobsters (and the greatest directors, like Scorsese, are obsessed with them)... is it simply because they represent a perversion of society, where all the traditional ideals of family, loyalty, ambition, etc. are twisted  to their breaking point and thus reflect on how those values apply to traditional society? What does ""The Departed"" and its ilk--the Godfathers, Scarface, Goodfellas, and what not--have to say about us, ordinary people who don't get involved in complicated double-crosses and mass shoot-outs? I'm honestly not sure. (Also: Wahlberg is awesome.)","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2007-12-08","","RT","789547447"
5.0,"In South Boston, where the state police force is waging war on organized crime, young undercover cop Billy Costigan is assigned to infiltrate the mob syndicate run by gangland chief Costello. While Billy is quickly gaining Costello's confidence, Colin Sullivan, a hardened young criminal who has infiltrated the police department as an informer for the syndicate, is rising to a position of power in the Special Investigation Unit. Each man becomes deeply consumed by his double life, gathering information about the plans and counter-plans of the operations he has penetrated. But when it becomes clear to both the gangsters and the police that there's a mole in their midst, Billy and Colin are suddenly in danger of being caught and exposed to the enemy--and each must race to uncover the identity of the other man in time to save himself.*



The Departed Follows Rookie Cop Billy Costigan Who Becomes A Mole On The Inside of The Mob Run By Boss Frank Costello. Its His Job To Win Costello's Trust And Help His Detective Handlers Bring Costello Down. Meanwhile, Officer Colin Sullivan Has Everyone's Trust. No One Suspects He's Costello's Mole. The Departed Is A Classic Crime Thriller From Legendary FilmMaker Martin Scorsese. Leonardo DiCaprio And Matt Damon Give Extraordinary Performances, Theyre The Show-Stealers Here. Jack Nicholson, Mark Wahlberg, Martin Sheen, And Alec Baldwin Give Award Worthy Supporting Performances, And Vera Farmiga Makes A Very Memorable Appearance Here As Well. The Departed Is A Film So Damn Good, Its Almost Unbelievable. Few Films Are As Well Made And Suspenseful As This One. A Superb Work of Pure Genius. The Greatest Crime Thriller I Have Ever Seen. Brilliantly Made And Superbly Crafted.*



""Frank, how many of these guys have been with you long enough to be disgruntled, huh? Think about it. You don't pay much, you know. It's almost a fuckin' feudal enterprise. The question is, and this is the only question, who thinks that they can do what you do better than you?""*



""When you decide to be something, you can be it. That's what they don't tell you in the church. When I was your age they would say we can become cops, or criminals. Today, what I'm saying to you is this: when you're facing a loaded gun, what's the difference?""*



 ""I don't want to be a product of my environment. I want my environment to be a product of me.""*



Martin Scorsese Is A Cinematic Genius And One of The Greatest FilmMakers Around. The Departed Is A Film That Will Stay With You Long After Its Over. Exceptional And Extraordinary In Every Way Imaginable. A Compelling, Mesmerizing, And Spellbinding Experience. No Words of Mine Can Describe How Amazing This Film Really Is. Leonardo DiCaprio Has Really Become One of The Most Gifted And Thrilling Actors Around, And Matt Damon Is Brilliant. The Entire Cast Is Award Worthy, Every Single Performance Is Phenomenal. Martin Scorsese Can Literally Do No Wrong. The Departed Is A Masterwork. A Perfect Example of Truly Flawless FilmMaking. A Wildly Compelling And Intensely Powerful Thriller. A Phenomenal, Incredible Achievement. I Love It. A Flawless Film...","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-12-08","","RT","804829469"
