5.0,"This film just goes to show you that Martin Scorsese still has it. Recently he has brought us a mixed bag of sweet and sour (The Aviator, No Direction Home are sweet and the rest remain sour). This film seems like a remake but screenwriter Monahan based Nicholsonâs character on wanted Boston mobster Whitey Bulger, which makes for a much more original realistic feel. Scorsese paired Nicholson with DiCaprio & Damon to do variations of the Scorsese shuffle to the tune of Gimme Shelter & I'm Shipping Up To Boston. Not to mention the best supporting cast imaginable (Alec Baldwin, Mark Wahlberg, Ray Winstone, Martin Sheen & a mention to Vera Farmiga) this film conveys a very established but young at heart Boston mob film.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2007-12-17","","RT","803994757"
