1.0,"""When I was your age, they would say, we become cops or criminals.  Today, what I'm saying to you is this: When you are facing a loaded gun...""

Costello says these words near the beginning of the movie and they sum up the voice of the entire film. There is no difference really between the cops and the criminals. They're both violent, vulgar brutes. There's no good and no evil, not even order and chaos. In the end all things come to destruction, all things face the end of the loaded gun. 

Scorsese's film is an ode to nihilism and one of the few in quite a while that I couldn't even bring myself to finish.

Also, my criticisms of this movie are not simply ethical. I know I'm in the minority on this but I thought that the narrative was disjointed, the editing poor and the cinematography uninspiring. All that aside, however, the quality of the acting can't be denied.","",False,False,False,False,1.0,"2007-12-19","","RT","806746881"
