3.5,"compared to all his movies,
this i find the less 'surprising'.
maybe because i've watch the
original and knew how the fate
of this characters will turn out.

what's the fun in it, when you
already knew their fate?

bad luck for me, but still i find
it entertaining, by studying the
development of the plot;
this is the benefit of watching
a master at work of knowing
already where he is heading.

no doubt, it was very well directed when you see how all the scenes are pasted together very firmly, you could almost taste a point where Mr Scorsese saying 'this is EXACTLY how i wanted it to turn out.'

i've learned from watching this, that from 'stealing' a story, you still can make it a masterpiece of your own, by maintaining the key-points of the scene and localizing it to a different environment.

this movie also won an Oscar for it's editing. no argument to that;
when the first intro-15 minutes-scenes was cut rapidly short, and was feed with
so much interesting information and the non-consistency of raise/low volume of the score, cutting through scenes; feels like an editor experimenting/taking risk with his playful-artist's touch, that works
perfectly.
(especially love the sudden-raise-volume-cut to the prison scene, and the titling 'Departed' just snap in yr face with a big-flat-black and white-clean-sharp fonts, snapping back to Leonardo and the ambiance of his inmates. this is the kind of stuff Mr Scorsese do, 'IN YR FACE!' effect.)

nothing much more to say, except
i wish Mr Scorsese had won his first directorial-Oscar for his older-classic works rather

than this.

and it's too bad that i still prefer
Infernal Affairs eventhough this
is an entire different kind of movie
to be compared to.

this is a hate/love movie.

hate the last scene and the quick-kill
ending, but still it feed the premise
of the movie;

""nothing is given to you, you have to take.""

and i'm sure there's no persuading is needed for anyone
to watch this Oscar-Best Picture.

sigh.. and yeah.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2007-12-20","","RT","801607421"
