2.5,"I was fairly disappointed by this film. Not that I was itching to see it, but I was expecting more. I was trying to figure out how to recognize this as a âMartin Scorseseâs movieâ by the direction of it. Could have been any high profile Hollywood filmmaker!
The familiar gangster plot and themes are explored here, as they have been through Scorseseâs previous films but this time itâs with different accents. But I kind of felt, I had seen it all before. It had some decent dialogue, here and there. It was helpful having someone from Boston, watch it with me and explain some of the references. Scorsese didnât seem to use the city as a decent back drop, as he has before or as a gritty city to play out this violent narrative.
 Some of the acting was pretty ropey and not very convincing. Mark Wahlberg was practically awful and seems to want to be like his co star Alec Baldwin (in his cameo in GlenGarry Glen Ross) and be all aggressive as the bullish detective. The love triangle seems to be very loosely put into the narrative. I donât understand why Madolyn (Vera Farmiga) falls for Billy Costigan (Leonardo DiCaprio) and is with Colin (Matt Damon), maybe i missed that part of the film or it wasnât really explored. Actually, Leonardo DiCaprio is the only thing that is worth watching in this film, I thought his role was excellent. As for Jack Nicholson as Costello, well, I kept thinking of him as the Joker. He was just being him and not putting any effort into it.","",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2007-12-29","","RT","787650778"
