4.0,"Return to semi-form this, if not really scaling any significant heights for Scorsese. Holds it own to the original Infernal Affairs really more through the pace and feel of the film. I enjoyed the setting of the film in Boston, I think that worked. The acting was good, although I'm stilled not convinced about DiCaprio in a macho type of role. He delivered a good performance when dealing with the characters emotions, however I still couldn't buy into him being a tough guy. At one point it looked like he was trying to mimic De Niro with the downturned mouth and that was ill-advised at best. Overall though, the voilence was appropriately brutal, the direction strong and less flamboyant than recent outings. It's not classic Scorsese and there are still those signs there that he isn't what he used to be but it's still better than most, but certainly not award worthy even if this hadn't been a remake.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2007-12-31","","RT","803482211"
