3.0,"Don't get me wrong I love Scorsese, but this film seemed kind of generic and a little lame. I liked the film as a whole but it didn't feel as personal as other films he has done recently. He was in love with Gangs of New York and it shows in his work. Even in The Aviator, which I felt was unbalanced, he seemed to care for Howard Hughes quite a bit. Now I don't want to say that Scorsese phoned this film in, but it didn't seem to have the passion that most of his films have. He has now won a best director Oscar, and lord knows that he has deserved it in the past, but I don't feel that this film would even be in his top 10 best films. I can see how people are excited that he has returned to gangster pictures, but I was just left wanting more.

