#5 Movie of 2006

Director: Martin Scorsese
Starring: Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, Mark Whalberg, Jack Nicholson

I had unheardof expectations for this movie, mostly because Martin Scorsese is probably my favorite director of all-time. Ultimately, my expectations were not entirely met, but The Departed is still a great film, and one of the best of the year.

Scorsese's direction here is sharper than in any film he's made since Goodfellas. His mastery of editing and precise use of popular music is again confirmed here, and the entire film feels fresh and invigorating. The performances are excellent, especially supporting roles played by Alec Baldwin and Martin Sheen.

The film doesnt have much lasting appeal afterwards, and in terms of stretching the cinematic scope it doesnt really go too much off the board. A solid film with great performances, but I still feel like it could have been even better.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2008-01-05","","RT","901002675"
