4.5,"The Departed comes across as a film desperately trying to win an Academy Award.  The first problem is when the (what appears to be) stock footage intro doesn't jive with what is to come after.  So right of the bat, things are a bit jarring.  Second problem is the all star cast.  They all perform excellent and fit their rolls well.  However the ""branding"" they bring with them overpowers their actual rolls.  I can't help myself thing Jack Nicholson (rather than Francis ""Frank"" Costello) is the Boss of the Boston Irish Mob, and is running around with Jack Dawson from the Titanic (rather than Billy Costigan) , while Jason Bourne is meeting with Marky Mark and the President of the United States at police HQ (rather than Sgt. Colin Sullivan, Staff Sgt. Sean Dignam and Capt. Oliver ""Charlie"" Queenan).  Third problem is the token love story that has to be jammed in the middle of all this to keep the female audience interested.  Isn't that just like a woman to be getting in the way of things while the men are trying to get their job done?
Anyway, that is why The Departed loses half a star.  It really was an excellent movie.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2008-01-05","","RT","790145971"
