2.0,"Terribly over-rated film that won only because the Academy forgot to award Scorsese for his far better films of the past. Overly long with no less than 30-minutes of unnecessary scenes. A weak ending that happens all too fast. Completely over-the-top acting as well as far too many plot holes. But the great production and acting of Nicholson and Farmiga save this from being a waste.

Scorsese needs to learn how to edit again and stop with overly long films with endings that require just seconds. Poor editing and filming. Also, this has got to be the most leftist cast ever assembled.

