5.0,"In a vicious world, a land of no-trust and fear, this is what you will get (See Fukuyama on Trust).

This is a cartoon-version of the future if we let the half-witted pseudo-intellectuals create our future for us. This is just a preview.

The economic-man is Wimpy (I'll pay you Tuesday for a hamburger today), and he is said to be ""rational"". She is driven to buy things that she does not need with the money she does not have.

And the ""rational"" man? He knows no loyalty and no trust and no sentiment, unless he can calculate what other humans mean for him; he is out for himself; after all Darwinism says so ""survival of the fittest"".

This is the bungle in the jungle, and the Thrilla in Manila. In the future, it will be all about who can cheat who, as long as manna keeps raining from the sky; but it won't. Manna does not rain; people make it rain.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-01-12","","RT","805109228"
