4.5,"This ensemble movie is a sure fire indicator that the legend, Martin Scorsese is over the losing streak he's been hit with these last few years. Whilst Scorsese has been churning out the movies consistently it's been ten years since he gave us something really worth talking about (1995's Casino) and 'The Departed' is it. The premise is as such: Two cadets, Billy Costigan & Colin Sullivan (Leo DiCaprio & Matt Damon) commence training to become much respected Boston State Troopers. It becomes clear early on that the their lives are to take polarising paths but that the fates of both men are intertwined. Whilst Costigan is covertly removed from the program to work undercover in the world of organised crime and infiltrate the gang controlled by the elusive and merciless Frank Costello (cinematic godfather Jack Nicholson). Sullivan schemes his way into detective ranks and carries out the tasks he's been groomed all his life for by leaking information to his secret sponsor Costello- who's under intense scrutiny from the police. Though this is a long film it doesn't drag at any point. It twists and turns without confusing the viewer and the plot keeps the momentum throughout, gaining speed towards the end, but don't be fooled into thinking it's over at the climax. The highlight of 'The Departed' is most definitely DiCaprio who was robbed of the Oscar nod this time around. He steals attention and not necessarily screen time from the other huge names here- a world away from the pin up roles of his early career. One person who did shine at the nominations lunch was Mark Wahlberg as Dignam, a cop and one of Costigan's two connections to his pre-criminal life. Dignam is a brash, vulgar, runaway train of a character whom Wahlberg manages to bring a doomed weakness to. No performance could be faulted here, save Alec Baldwin who delivers what's asked but it seems he's allowed himself to become typecast as an oblivious, loud and obnoxious man. For those who aren't fans of the crime/thriller epic genre I?d recommend you put your doubts aside and check this out, if only for the chance to see so many amazing actors sharing the screen and directed by the man who perfected the genre. Overall this is a gem of a film and not one to miss. What better accolade than the title of the movie that finally garnered Scorsese?s overdue Oscar statuette?","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2008-01-18","","RT","811484467"
4.5,"A very dark ""mob"" movie about moles and rats. Very stressful to watch, with some suprising and shocking twists. A super cast complement each other in their stellar performances. I thought DiCaprio was particularily convincing as a deep mole in a crime organization that begins to realistically crack under the strain.The last frame was lame. I get it; rats.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2008-01-18","","RT","793800919"
