4.5,"[size=2][font=Century Gothic]Without a doubt, ""The Departed"" is one of the best films I've seen in the past 5 years.  Thoroughly gripping, mesmerizing and engrossing with outstanding performances by Leonardo Dicaprio, Matt Damon, Jack Nicholson and Mark Wahlberg.[/font]
 [/size] 
  [size=2][font=Century Gothic]This is a nearly perfect film, and the Blu-ray version of this release is just amazing with the way it is able to render fine shadow detail from dark scenes.[/font]
  
  [font=Century Gothic]My only criticism of this film is the somewhat incomprensible relationship between Matt Damon and the psychiatrist, played by Vera Farmiga. There's very little development of the genesis of their relationship, and it seems somewhat inexplicable as to why they're together.  This flaw takes away some of the power of the film, since her relationship with the Leonardo Dicaprio characters could have provided a more highly charged layer to the drama that unfolds before us.[/font]
  
  [font=Century Gothic]However, this small flaw shouldn't overshadow the incredible gritty power of this film.  I'm going to watch this film again in the near future, and if I continue to be blown away by it, ""The Departed"" might crack my Top 10 Films of All Time list...[/font][/size]","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2008-01-21","","RT","900863649"
