2.0,"They did rewrote quite a few of the story lines & characters and maybe for someone who's never seen the original, it would've been worth their penny.
Unfortunately, I find that it's been rushed over & they failed to build up the tension slowly so it does loses its effects in the audience's reaction they would rather be aiming for.
Doesn't do much justice to the original Hong Kong version.
Too much focus on the wrong things, like recruiting too many hot shots instead of getting in more talented raw faces.
People anticipate more, especially when there's a number of big names from Hollywood contributing to the credits.
It just totally spoiled the whole thing.
Look at ""Perfume"", it only has Dustin Hoffman and the rather well known Alan Rickman to boot their credit but it was presented stunningly because they made us ""wait for it"".","",False,False,False,False,2.0,"2008-01-31","","RT","807459653"
