3.0,"For me Scorsese has always been one of the most overrated directors with only few great ones under his name. The Departed was once again disappointing, but still decent entertainment.
The beginning of the film feels awfully dragging, and it takes over an hour before the story really gets a hold of you. The events, the dialogue and the characters don't feel real or believable (the same problem was much worse in Gangs of New York) and poor editing ruins the tension.
Nicholson is what he is these days, but Matt Damon is again top notch. Leo is starting to acquire some charisma, but there is still something in his acting that bothers me... Vera Farmiga was a positive surprise and the chemistry between the guys and her character is the best thing this film has to offer. Of course the tension regarding the main story provides great moments too, and the finale reminds me of Hitchcock's complex plot twists.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2008-02-11","","RT","796515071"
