5.0,"Who knew that a movie about a cop-mob war (without any gimmicks and such) would be so much fun?  This movie is a thought-provoking look into a world with no rules (basically; the cops only sometimes follow them).  Not only is it an occassionaly funny action movie, it's incredibly smart.  The characters Costigan (a very good DiCaprio) and Sullivan (a better Damon, possibly his best role), the two protagonists (though on different sides), share  some similarities in character.  However, Sullivan is used to explore how well a web of lies can stay hidden, and Costigan is used to explore how one can stay sane in a web of lies.  And this may come as a surprise, but Jack Nicholson steals the show as the charismatic but terrible mob leader.  Add Scorsese's sharp direction, and you've got a winner.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-02-14","","RT","797962720"
