3.5,"There was a day when Alfred Hitchcock added his name to the title of his films, ie, ""Alfred Hitchcock's Psycho.""  The Departed felt a little bit like that, as Scorsese uses many devices that he perfected in previous films (ie, Casino, Taxi Driver, Goodfellas), but here that all seems matter of fact and a given.  It is entertaining and a good film, but it does not carry the same force that his earlier mob sagas did and it is weird that he got the Oscar for this given that this film is not in his top 5.  Oh well, maybe the Academy was trying to make up for previous mistakes.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2008-02-24","","RT","782615306"
