3.5,"Godard would be pleased, the jump cuts were well present, and the tale is about the intimate shots, ones that place the characters close together without the world around them mattering. What is curious, is that often these intimate shots are of characters alone, creating an interesting way of proving that no matter how similar the paths are of each person, they are isolated by their distrust and paranoia. The title (The Departed) refers to God holding the faithful, and yet none of the characters are faithful, and sadly, it seems that neither is Scorsese: to himself. The film lacked some of the punch his earlier works, and he felt distracted, leaving something to be desired from an otherwise riveting tale.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2008-02-27","","RT","789697510"
