3.0,"It was okay.  My family loved this movie, especially since the characters were Irish, and I could see some of that.  But the acting and script just didn't work for me the way it did for others.  I  didn't care about any of the characters, so I didn't care how it ended.  All of the actors are so big that I think I had a hard time seeing them as the characters instead of the actors.  And honestly, I had a hard time seeing Matt Damon as a bad guy.  Plus, I have a real problem with all the graphic violence and language in Scorcese's films in general, and this one was no exception.   I mean, I love the Sopranos and can deal with the language and violence on that show better than this.  I heard the original foreign version is better so maybe I will rent that.  

That said, be sure to watch the link of Matt Damon on Letterman about the movie.  He was an unbelievable Matthew McConaughey impression.  I could not stop laughing!","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2008-02-28","","RT","796359099"
