5.0,"The cynics that say this movie is basically a one-man whorehouse (the man being Marty), with his clientele lining up outside, each one (after violently screwing him for a good two hours) giving him a small piece of gold that he can eventually melt into an Oscar, are right. If this movie was made for actual artistic reasons, those reasons were quickly turned into ""Treasure of the Sierra Madre"" style longings for gold. But I don't care! Marty, Leo, Damon, Jack, Marky-Mark, Sheen, Winstone, Anthony Anderson and ""The Baldwin"" are going to take me on a wild, fucked up tour through the cops and criminals of South Boston, and I am going to eat up every second of it. Fast-paced, filled with beautiful, pestilent curse words and delicate, bloody headshots, this film is the greatest of my teenage years, not because it's got any stupendous acting, or brilliant cinematography, or any real message that applies to most people, but because, to quote Matt Damon, its ""Feckin' fun"".","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-03-01","","RT","790579536"
