5.0,"I am a big fan of the partnership between Scorsese and DiCaprio, as well as that, the trailer really caught my eye and I had tipped it for Oscar success way before it got there.  I think that the storyline is original and the cast is superb.  Nicholson is always a joy to watch and with actors such as Mark Wahlberg (In his best performance to date), Alec Baldwin, Martin Sheen and the lovely Vera Farmiga, not to mention DiCaprio in yet another exceptional (and oddly unrecognised by the Academy) performance and Matt Damon playing a dirtier character than we have become accustomed too with the ""Bourne"" and ""Oceans"" films but a great portrayal nonetheless.  Scorsese for me, is at his best when dealing with the ""mob"" genre and he proves that here.  I actually prefer this film to ""Goodfellas"" (although I agree that his 1990 masterpiece is also an exceptional piece of work) and I look forward to future collaborations between Leonardo DiCaprio and his Director here.  Scorsese is easily one of the top two film-makers alive today and should have won the Oscar for ""Best Director"" years and years ago for films such as ""Taxi Driver"", ""Raging Bull"" and/or ""Goodfellas"" but I feel that ""The Departed"" is one of his very best achievements in film-making and certainly worthy of a much deserved award for a genius behind the camera.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-03-04","","RT","808440282"
