4.0,"Alright. If you're a born Bostonian, if you know where Savin Hill is, if you've ever been needled into a bar brawl with a guy called Fitzy, chances are you'll like this movie a lot. I'm one of those people, and while this is definitely not a masterpiece by Scorsese's terms, it's still an incredibly exciting police thriller, that works largely because it has a great sense of humor that most films of the genre tend to lack (just look at last year's awful ""We Own the Night""). It's a shame that Scorsese  and Monahan didn't really delve into some of the interesting the ideas that the film presents. It mostly skims the surface. However, it makes up for its lack of depth in its more literal plot, which is very captivating, to say the least. What really makes it work, though, are the actors. Why DiCaprio was nominated for ""Blood Diamond"" and not this...I don't think even God will ever know. He's great, as is Matt Damon in a rather different role. Nicholson, of course, is masterful, but so are Martin Sheen and Ray Winstone, whose less showy supporting performances are integral to the feel and flow of the movie. Without them, the movie probably wouldn't work as well. Alec Baldwin shows up too, and he's a hoot. In short, the movie is simple in ambitiions, but it's extremely worthwhile, and quite rewatchable. I saw it three times with different people, while it was in theaters. Odd as it may found, this was the ""Raiders of the Lost Ark"" of 2006 - entertainment filmmaking of the highest aesthetic quality. Is that enough for you? Fuckin' cocksuckah...","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2008-03-09","","RT","782891517"
