4.5,"[font=Arial]I can't believe I racked up so many reviews lately. I always get on here and spaz out, spending most of the time answering comments and replies, and never actually posting. Of course I slap myself when I get offline. I should really write a note.
[/font][center][u][size=7][font=Arial]The Departed[/font]
[/size][/u][size=7][b][font=Courier New]***+
[/font][/b][/size][url=""http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Image:Departed234.jpg""][img]http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/50/Departed234.jpg/200px-Departed234.jpg[/img][/url][size=7][b][font=Courier New]
[/font][/b][/size][center][font=Garamond][font=Arial]""What are you waiting for? You want them to chop me up and me to the poor?"" I'm going to come right out and say that I feel most RT members are perhaps a little too harsh on this film. I understand that it didn't deserve the Oscar, and I know it is my least favorite nominee, but The Departed is, put simply, a masterpiece. It's sort of like Million Dollar Baby; not my first choice, but I have to recognize how well-made it is. So there. The Departed flows with a beautiful sort of pacing, and I was never not entertained or not fascinated by what was happening on screen. Mark Whalberg, Jack Nicholson and Leonardo Dicaprio were all Oscar worthy in this.
[/font][size=7][font=Arial][u][font=Arial]The Office-Season One[/font]
[/u][/font][/size][/font][center][b][font=Courier New][size=7]***
[/size][/font][/b][url=""http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Image:The_Office_%28USA%29-titlecard.png""][img]http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ad/The_Office_%28USA%29-titlecard.png/250px-The_Office_%28USA%29-titlecard.png[/img][/url][b][font=Courier New][size=7]
[/size][/font][/b][center][font=Arial]""Oh, man, am I a woman?""
[size=7]PILOT [i]5/10[img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/user/statusicon/forum_old.gif[/img]
[/i][/size][/font][center][font=Arial]I didn't exactly enjoy the pilot episode. In fact it was downright irritating. It never got ""in the groove"" or even became that comedic. And the ending just annoyed me.
[/font][font=Arial][size=7]DIVERSITY DAY [i]8/10[img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/user/statusicon/forum_new.gif[/img]
[/i][/size][/font][center][font=Arial]This is my favorite episode by far. It is absolutely hilarious, and I enjoyed this wholeheartedly.
[size=7]HEALTH CARE [i]7/10[img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/user/statusicon/forum_new.gif[/img]
[/i][/size][/font][center][font=Arial]This was pretty good. Rainn Wilson did very well in this, and the writing was pretty witty.
[/font][font=Arial][size=7]THE ALLIANCE [i]8/10[img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/user/statusicon/forum_new.gif[/img]
[/i][/size][/font][center][font=Arial]You know what? This might actually be my favorite. In fact it is. Okay, strike that earlier comment.
[/font][/center]
[font=Arial][size=7]BASKETBALL [i]7/10[img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/user/statusicon/forum_new.gif[/img]
[/i][/size][/font][center][font=Arial]There could have been a lot of comedic situations coming from this, but it settled for just average verging on good.
[/font][/center]
[font=Arial][size=7]HOT GIRL [i]8/10[img]http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/user/statusicon/forum_new.gif[/img]
[/i][/size][/font][center][font=Arial]Third favorite. Amy Adams was great as a guest actress.[/font]
[u][size=7][font=Arial]Martian Child[/font]
[/size][/u][size=7][b][font=Courier New]**+
[/font][/b][/size][url=""http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Image:Martian_child_post.jpg""][img]http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bb/Martian_child_post.jpg/200px-Martian_child_post.jpg[/img][/url][size=7][b][font=Courier New]
[/font][/b][/size][center][font=Arial]""The astronauts drink Tang."" I think I could have really enjoyed this movie, but it settled for just average. It banks way too much on emotion, and thus it fails a little. Still, it's good natured, sweet, and that little boy is adorable. I don't expect any of you to see this, though. Oh, and it was nice to see Sophie Okonedo in this, who was ROBBED for Best Supporting Actress in 2004.[/font]
[u][size=7]Volver
[/size][/u][size=7][b][font=Courier New]**+
[/font][/b][/size][center](The website I go to didn't have a picture. Don't really care, actually).


[/center]
