3.0,"Very watchable.  It's got a great energy like a classic Scorsese film in that scenes don't drag at all.
Jack Nicholson is terrible though.  It seems like dream casting with him as the Whity Bulger like crime boss, but Jack goes way too far over the top in the role, veering into the ridiculous in almost every scene.
Boston local guys Matt Damon (as usual) and Mark Wahlberg are great, flourishing in the salty dialogue.
DiCaprio is game, if somewhat miscast, as the rougher looking guy who goes undercover for the cops.
I've heard it said that it too often feels like a bunch of moments from Scorsese's better, earlier work mashed together and reheated in the microwave.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2008-03-27","","RT","809185202"
