5.0,"Absolutely brilliant movie.  I haven't seen a lot of Scorsese's work but now I'm wanting more!  The movie's sharp dialogue and barrel full of twists and turns keep you intrigued throughout the whole thing and doesn't let up through out the whole picture, even after the very Shakespearian ending (I won't spoil it for you beyond that if you haven't seen it) which resolves the movie without giving you a lot of closure but at the same time you think ""justice is served...I think"".  This movie is also proof that Leo is one of the most underrated actors in Hollywood!  It was also good to see Matt Damon return to his roots in a picture that takes place in Boston...probably the first time he's really been able to use his natural Southie accent since Good Will Hunting.
Bottom line: Brilliant acting, excellent editing and cinematography...Scorsese has scored another winner and a well-deserved Best Picture Oscar!","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-03-31","","RT","788225768"
