5.0,"When I was your age they say ""we could become cops or criminals what I'm saying to you today is whats the difference? That quote from the old veteran actor Jack Nicholson is all I needed to hear to see this movie and most importantly see the return of a legendary filmaker back to his old roots again. This time Scorsese actually gives us plenty more that we can chew on. First of he gives us an extrodinary A List cast that ranges from the youngest and talented actors (Leonardo Dicaprio, Matt Damon, Mark Whalberg) to the more old legendary excellent actors (Jack Nicholson, Martin Sheen, Alec Baldwin) Hell even Anthony Anderson shows up in da picture and thats not a problem because we all know that Martin Scorsese has led some of the finest actors to stardom in there career take ROBERT DE NIRO AND NOW LEONARDO DICAPRIO AS SCORSESE PROTEGES SORT OF SPEAK. The Departed is exactly what I expected from Filmake Martin Scorsese but it delivered 10x more the anticipation I was expecting. First of he dresses this movie first into another gangster epic then completley flips it around throught the middle then we end up with a brilliant cat and mouse or should say ""RAT & RAT"" Action thriller. The location shot in Boston Stands out so much in this movie its perfect you actually feel like you just steped into an irish gangland. Dont even get me started on the performances in this movie one word to put it ""FLAWLESS"" Its nearly damn perfect but the female love intrest here played by (Vera Farmiga) I feel was miscast and couldve done a better job. Everyone else played there part right on cue. The most stand out performance and breakthrough I must say is by a Ferocious yet sarcastic Seargeant Dignam played mean street bad cop, good cop style by a brilliant (Mark Whalberg) also Leo & Damon did outstanding jobs playing Rats after one another but to me the spotlight goes to the supporting cast Including another nut case performance if one may say by none other than Jack Nicholson who here plays the notorious crime boss Frank Costello. He also manages to somewhat find a strange sick kind of humour within this character which I thought wasnt over the top but was just great to see Nicholson adapting back to his old acting roots. The story hear is a fireball of entertainment that never drags youll be intrigued from the jumpstart begining dialouge to the SURPRISING and yet SATISFYING ENDING. Oh WOW What a way to end u a movie I must say it left me speechlees with a smile on my face. This truly is Scorsese most enjoyable movie and his passion in making this film here shines. I'm so pleased this movie won BEST PICTURE AND MORE RIGHTFULY WON THE GREAT MARTIN SCORSESE HIS CHERISHED BEST DIRECTOR OSCAR. The best and most fun movie of 2006. Its simply just flat out BLOODY GOOD. That great SCORSESE VIOLENCE never ceases to amaze. If you havnt seen do so Immediatley YOU CANT MISS THIS ONE.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-04-09","","RT","819561473"
