5.0,"The Departed is about two just-graduated officers from Massachusetts State Police Academy follow opposite sides of the law: Billy Costigan is assigned to work undercover with the Irish mobster Frank Costello to get evidences to arrest him. His true identity is only known by his superiors Dignam and Oliver Queenan. The protÃÂ©gÃÂ©e of Costello, Colin Sullivan, is promoted in the Massachusetts State Police and is the informer of Costello. Each police officer gives his best effort trying to disclose the identity of the other ""rat"".
The screenplay and the direction of Martin Scorsese was excellent. I liked all the twisted plots that this film had.
The cast was perfect, I think Leonardo DiCaprio's performance was awesome, and he should have been nominated for this role to Best Actor, instead of his role on Blood Diamond. Matt Damon also surprised me, because is not usual that he plays the bad guy, and he did great as always. Jack Nicholson is perfect as the head of the irish mafia, combined in his role sarcasm and evilness.
It's great that the Academy recognized this film with 4 Academy Awards, including Best Picture and Best Director. If you like movies with action and twisted plots, The Departed is the movie that fit in this description.","cfbd3bbc-cb5b-441e-8acc-83275818da32",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-04-20","","RT","821168357"
