4.0,"A very smart film, possibly Scorsese's cleverest, and certainly my favourite of his film (as controversial as that statement is).

The plot is fast, superbly told, and complex.

Jack Nicholsen is very good here, giving as per usual, an astounding performance. It could be argued that he is given a tad too much free reign, but I really liked what he did with the part.

DiCaprio is also really, really good. I think he is a very underrated actor, and here certainly shows his true potential as an excellent performer. I think his main problem is he gets cast in bad films, and this is definitely not one of them.

Mark Wahlberg is really very good too, he makes his character such a prick, and I was pleasantly surprised by Matt Damon too.

The cinematography is really very nice, and I think took that gritty Scorsese feel and made it very 21st century. It still looks like his other films, but has a really nice modern twist.

The music is also really good, I immediately had to get the Dropkick Murpheys' song as soon as the film finished. There is of course a large Rolling Stones presence, it wouldn't be Scorsese without it.

The ending is mind blowing, literally mind blowing and so unexpected.

The only criticism that I can raise against it is that I found the accents a little annoying, they're not wrong or badly done at all, just that accent itself grates on me.

Unlike other Scorsese movies, I didn't come out feeling like I needed to take a minute just to reacclimatise, which I normally do as they are so heavy, I just wanted to watch it again! Definitely one to see, and one to buy so you can see it again and again.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2008-05-17","","RT","788248203"
