5.0,"""When you decide to be something, you can be it. That's what they don't tell you in the church. When I was your age they would say we can become cops, or criminals. Today, what I'm saying to you is this: when you're facing a loaded gun, what's the difference?""
Martin Scorsese's remake of 2002 Hong Kong film Internal Affairs, was  destined to be a star studded event. In that sense it didn't fail as all involved worked off each other and  put on a hell of a show.Nicholson,DiCaprio,Wahlberg,Damon,and Sheen were wonderful.
Billy Costigan (Leonardo DiCaprio)  volunteers to go undercover(for the state police) in the  Irish-American mob while Colin Sullivan (Matt Damon) a member of the mob climbs the ranks of the state police. What ensues is lies,betrayal,and violence.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-06-07","","RT","825126763"
