3.0,"So this is really good. The acting, anyway. People rave about Scorsese as a director and maybe it's his ability to get the hell out of these guys way, or perhaps to coach them into doing their jobs, that is worthy of praise here, but otherwise, I wasn't entirely impressed. It's a great movie but I find my attention wandering a bit with the police procedural stuff as opposed to the film's more human moments. On some level this movie's the exact opposite of films like 'Babel' or 'Crash,' which are all about the sometimes-fanciful ways in which people are connected. Here DiCaprio and Damon play two guys linked more strongly than either of them suspect, and they keep missing each other. And that's the core of the film for me. Good stuff.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2008-06-08","","RT","800992409"
