4.0,"While not Scorsese's best film, it was certainly the best film of 2006...and, arguably, the best film of this decade. The characters are interesting, but remain too dark for the audience to come to love or even like. That is what makes this film. The heart of this movie is the question of who, if anyone, is good. Even ""the rat"" planted within the underworld (Costigan), for the authorities, is morally challeneged. A brilliant job by the legendary director.
The actors give strong performances. Sheen is quietly powerful as the voice of truth and justice. Damon is impressively dispicable - a change of pace for him. DiCaprio shows he can act...and Wahlberg (who garnered a Oscar nomination) is superb as Sheen's #2. Even Alec Baldwin reminds why he is still recieving scripts. But a great deal of the applause must go to the lion of the show - Jack. He brings a new kind of evil to the public, from the moment we first hear his voice, to his last scene. A prime example of the Academy ""missing the mark"" comes in the fact that they completely snubbed Nicholson, who was the best supporting actor of the year.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2008-06-20","","RT","827349914"
