4.5,"Well, this is one of the hardest movies to review, <b>first of all, it is a remake. Second of all, surprisingly, the end result is <u><font size=""3"">BETTER</font></u> than the original <i>Infernal Affairs</i>,</b> and what makes it harder, <b>it carried home the greatest honor of the year, <i>2007 Academy Award's Best Picture.</i></b><br>
The most shoking truth yet painful is, that <b>THIS IS THE FIRST TIME ACADEMY AWARD RESPECT SCORSESE FOR HIS CONTRIBUTION IN MAKING MOVIES.</b> Yes, they've given the old man 5 nomination. <B><U><font size=""3"">NOMINATION!</font></u></b> Yes, that's where the painful part is. If I was one of them who would pick the winner for the <i>Academy Award</i>, maybe I'll be fired already for shouting Scorsese's name against of what they've picked everytime he got the nomination. Honestly, <i>The Departed</i> is not a perfect movie where he should get his oscar is. He should get it 28 years ago when he directed <i>Raging Bull.</i> But, better late than never.<br>
Scorsese gave his own way of directing, it's <b>original</b> way of directing. <br>
<b>This is a <b><u><font size=""3"">DECLARATION</font></u></b> for DiCaprio that annouce that he's now an actor we can all count of.</b> Throw away Jack Dawson's image, this is the new him. He made a great chemistry between Billy Costigan and Colin Sullivan, played by Matt Damon. Jack Nicholson again, gave a charisma no one can replace, he's the soul of the movie. And in my opininon, <b>this movie's scene stealer is not Vera Farmiga</b>, that's Mark Wahlberg, he played as powerful as the other three, with the less scene to take.
The script was terrific, not to mention plenty of dishonorable remake. Now we know that maybe remake will only works in this genre, or maybe it only works in the hands of Scorsese, because we've seen the battlefield and they all brought down by the original and they all have failed and seems like they all just want to make money by making something that we will only remember for the next 5 minutes after we left the cinema. <b>That's ironic, how Hollywood have to steal the other countries' story but still calling theirself the biggest movie headquarter.</b><br>
It's not forgiven, but if they can make it something different and better, than we can take a deep breath, and be relieved. William Monahan changed my point of view of remake, <b><u><font size=""3"">INSTEAD OF JUST COPYING, THEY MAKE SOMETHING BETTER.</font></u></b><p>
<div align=""center""><a href=""http://imageshack.us""><img src=""http://img78.imageshack.us/img78/10/departedaie4.jpg"" border=""0"" alt=""Image Hosted by ImageShack.us""/></a><p><i>When you decide to be something, you can be it. That's what they don't tell you in the church. When I was your age they would say we can become cops, or criminals. Today, what I'm saying to you is this: when you're facing a loaded gun, what's the difference?</i><br>
<b>-Frank Costello-</b></div><p>","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2008-06-29","","RT","405148126"
