5.0,"<font face=""courier new""><I>Lies. Betrayal. Sacrifice. How far will you take it?</I><BR><BR><BR><font size=""2""><div align=center><B>Director: Martin Scorsese<BR><BR>Writers (WGA): William Monahan (screenplay)<BR>Genre:Crime | Drama<BR><BR>Starring: Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, Jack Nicholson, and Mark Wahlberg</B><BR><BR><BR><a href=""http://photobucket.com/images/the%20departed%20poster"" target=""_blank""><img src=""http://i31.photobucket.com/albums/c395/1MajorPimp123/departed_poster_dicaprio.jpg"" border=""0"" alt=""The Departed 2 Pictures, Images and Photos""/></a><BR><BR><I>""When you decide to be something, you can be it. That's what they don't tell you in the church. When I was your age they would say we can become cops, or criminals. Today, what I'm saying to you is this: when you're facing a loaded gun, what's the difference?""</I><BR><BR><BR><font face=""courier new""><font size=""3""><B><U>THE MOVIE OUTLINE</U></B></div><BR><BR><font face=""courier new""><font size=""4""><B><I>""T</B></I><font size=""2""><I>wo just-graduated officers from Massachusetts State Police Academy follow opposite sides of the law: William Costigan is assigned to work undercover with the Irish mobster Frank Costello to get evidences to arrest him. His true identity is only known by his superiors Dignam and Oliver Queenan. The protégée of Costello, Colin Sullivan, is promoted in the Massachusetts State Police and is the informer of Costello. Each police officer gives his best effort trying to disclose the identity of the other ""rat"".   <font size=""4""><B>""</B></I><BR><BR><BR><div align=center><a href=""http://photobucket.com/images/the%20departed"" target=""_blank""><img src=""http://i193.photobucket.com/albums/z85/snshffld/departed.jpg"" border=""0"" alt=""departed Pictures, Images and Photos""/></a></div><BR><BR><BR><div align=center><font face=""courier new""><font size=""3""><B><U>MY APPRAISAL</U></B><BR><BR><font size=""4""><B>PIECE OF EXPLOSIVE CINEMA!</B><BR><BR><font size=""2"">Outstanding and sensational, The Departed is the most enjoyable crime movie of 2006. I shamelessly in love with this Martin Scorsese's dazzling work. The entire crew and storyline <font size=""3""><B><I><U>SWEPT ME OFF MY FEET!</U></I></B>. <font size=""2""><I>The Departed</I> has everything needed to make one movie enjoyable but also intelligent at the same time. This is how a crime movie should be made. It has masterclass acting on top of brilliant storytelling. A bit disappointing to find out that this is only a remake of Hong Kong's <I>Infernal Affairs</I>.<BR><BR>Daammn. Mark Wahlberg was brilliant!! It's without doubt his very best performance I've ever seen. He was my hero before he's f*cked as seen in <I>The Happening</I> and <I>Max Payne</I>. He's fierce, exasperating, and also very very stylish. I love his character most of all! I wanna see more him at top of his game.<BR><BR>The excellent cast made it possible to handle such complex story. Leonardo DiCaprio at his best and so is Matt Damon. Jack Nicholson was OK but not at his finest. DiCaprio, all eyes on him! I totally adore the matured DiCaprio as also seen in <I>Blood Diamond, Body of Lies</I>. It was a goodbye to our slashy ""I'm the king of the world!"" boy to Leonardo DiCaprio, a serious actor.<BR><BR>I rewatched The Departed again on 2.5 inch iPod screen but the compelling and tense story made it possible to increase my heart rate. No kidding. I was stunned and very thrilled. This might not be everyone's favourite of Martin Scorsese's but whoever miss this classy flick of his, consider yourself at a HUGE LOSS. <BR><BR>Stylistically directed and beautifully cut. <font size=""4""><B><I>The Departed</I>, this year's most mesmerizing motion picture.</B><BR><BR><BR><a href=""http://photobucket.com/images/the%20departed"" target=""_blank""><img src=""http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v206/pommeapplepie/departed.jpg"" border=""0"" alt=""departed Pictures, Images and Photos""/></a></div><BR><BR><B>Billy Costigan: </b><I>[to the bartender]</I> ""Cranberry juice.""<BR><BR><B>Man Glassed in Bar: </B>""It's a natural diuretic. My girlfriend drinks it when she's got her period. What, do you got your period?<BR> <BR><I>[Billy grabs an empty glass and smashes it onto the man's head.]</I>","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-07-05","","RT","821839408"
5.0,"Who am I? I'm the guy that does his job, u must b the other guy!""","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-07-05","","RT","830205834"
