5.0,"Wow! One word, WOW! Martin Scorsese is a wonder! I really applaud him for his film career and the achievements he's made. It is really hard to believe he had not recieved an oscar for achievements in directing until this film. And his oscar was greatly deserved because The Departed, in my opinion, was close to perfect.

A great cast! Jack Nicholson delivers as the criminal. He's had experience the Joker, Jack Torrence, and soo many more. He shines in each role he plays. To see a classic doing what he does best was really entertaining to watch. For Mark Wahlberg I usually tend to veer away from his work. However, I had to see this one because of my obsession with Martin Scorses films, and I am glad Mark Wahlberg had the part he was given. Dignam was my favorite good cop/bad cop and he was hard to hate at all! Matt Damon played Colin soo well, I had to watch Bourne Ultimatum later, just to like him again! And Leo! There is not much to say about Leo because he is close to perfect playing each character he picks up! He's been in his prime since Growing Pains, and I don't think he'll be decendibng any time soon. At least I really hope not. Billy Costigan was entertaining to follow and understanding the story from his POV was nail biter! I really loved his situation! The cast was absolutlely unforgettable! If any cast member had not been there the movie wouldn't have been as good.

The screenplay by William Monahan was a handful of entertaining characters and a mob that is soo close to touching Godfather standards.

And the ending, the ending is to die for!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-07-05","","RT","831303954"
4.0,"I still have lots of love for this cool, cool movie - but it ain't the masterpiece I originally thought it was.  Truth is that while it's a rich, complicated and exciting tale, it's also a bit of a mess and Jack Nicholson often robs it of its credibility with his OTT, often improv'ed, scenery chewing performance.
Still, I don't want to take too much away from it because as I said before; this is a rich, exiting movie and it has some fantastic performances in it.  DiCaprio and Damon are as charasmatic as ever but it's all about Wahlberg and the oldest of the Baldwin brothers.  They steel every scene they're in.
Top notch stuff, but if we're holding it up to the Scorsese Masterpiece Collection then it just doesn't measure up.","e8ac7166-3271-4f40-b9b5-8d30b25eed8c",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2008-07-05","","RT","831531802"
