4.0,"It's been a while since I've seen Infernal Affairs. Can't say which one is better, [b]The Departed[/b] or the original. The Departed was good; very entertaining. The ending maybe dragged on too long, but I don't know if it was me or the film. I was out of steam by then anyhow. Worthy remake of a worthy film.
 
--
 
[b]Juno[/b] was a watchable teen girl movie. Sympathetic in the sense that it was careful not to be unpleasant towards anybody, but boring because it was cronically inable to transcend beyond looking and sounding like an extended pilot episode to an average big budget tv-series. Perhaps an HBO series, if you want to think on the positive side of things, but that's all. A harmless, well-meaning production with a formula it stuck tightly to. Nothing wrong with that. However, do I feel I like I got anything for my time? No. If I wanted to watch sarcastic tv-kids I could have just watched the tv. Still, it was alright with me. Honest, made with upright diligence, entertaining enough.
 
--
 
[b]The Elephant Man[/b]. A true story. Nightmare. Fairy-tale. David Lynch. Good performances. Interesting. The carneval sequences reminded me of The Cabinet of Dr. Caligari. A nice, good movie.
 
--
 
[b]Mildred Pierce[/b]. A melodrama dressed in a thin noirish outfit. Directed by Michael Curtiz. I don't see why Joan Crawford is so praised for this; Jack Carson as slippery businessman Wally is the real attraction in every scene he's in. The film strangely fails and succeeds at the same time. Somehow all the dialogue between the mother and the daughter is ridiculously bad. Veda's whole character is pieced together in a manner way too shallow for it's importance, and her relationship with her mother couldn't be much stiffer. So that's a huge problem, but if you can neglect that, then it's a good movie.
 
--
 
[b]Grand Hotel[/b] isn't a recent viewing. It just sprung to mind from thinking of Joan Crawford. The film is excellent and deserves a rating, so here it be rated. An all-star cast. I can't recall having seen any talking pictures that were made up to that time, that could best Grand Hotel.
 
--","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2008-07-30","","RT","900750525"
