3.5,"Good, but not Best Picture worthy.  Not when it's competing with films like 'Pan's Labyrinth' and 'The Queen' and 'Casino Royale'.  Leonardo DiCaprio and Matt Damon head the film as contrasting rats, and its clear the film wants to distinctly seperate between the two.  Jack Nicholson and Martin Sheen are the gray-haired omnipotent counterpart employers of the two, additionally contrasting.  Sheen's character is constantly seeming paniced and desperate.  Nicholson is calm yet somewhat crazy.  Vera Farmiga is conflicted love interest of both DiCaprio and Damon.  The only reasonably memorable character is Mark Wahlberg as a crass street-smart police sergeant. B-","2c52aaed-66a3-4a5e-8a03-8f2af3eb0f05",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2008-07-30","","RT","807859753"
