3.0,"I was expecting good things from this film, and the story is great, but the screenplay translation from Infernal Affairs didn't live up to the original. What was missing was the understated brilliance of IA. There was needless detail and gore that I actually think drew us away from the story and not into it. Performances were good and original aspects good, but needed to be shorter and snappier - especially in the opening act.","",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2008-07-31","","RT","811494339"
4.5,"[img]http://www.moviecritic.com.au/userimages/user624_1161316622a.jpg[/img]
  
  Even with a flawed script, the immensely talented Scorsese has shown he can make anything artistic and entertaining. Of course, it also helps to have an A-list cast. 
  
  [img]http://z.about.com/d/movies/1/0/u/S/N/departedfallpreview.jpg[/img]
  
  DiCaprio is giving Oscar-worthy performance after Oscar-worthy performance. His portrayal of fear and paranoia is captivating. Nicholson is very good, but its his same kind of shtick from any other crazy movie. Damon is also very good as the deceiving half of the film, though almost everyone in this movie has something to hide. There are a couple of nit-picks, however. The script is somewhat amateurish, especially with unnecessary love triangles and unnecessarily moral attempts at compensation for immoral triumphs toward the end. And for a flick with such a talented director and wonderful actors, is it too much to ask for a good producer and a decent cinematographer?! Even so, this remake is a highly skilled exercise in the genre that rightfully belongs to Scorsese, who has created a brilliant, if flawed, dissection of moral identities.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2008-07-31","","RT","901067595"
