5.0,"I think this is Martin Scorseses best film. Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, Jack Nicholson and Mark Wahlberg were all fantastic - oscar worthy performances. I think the story is brilliant because it is a complicating story but once you get the film going it gets easier to understand. It is a bit like L.A. Confidential but it is better. As far as the characters are concerned this film is like American Gangster because Frank Lucas is like Frank Costello (a crook who does drug deals and steals them) and Billy Costigan is like Detective Richie Roberts (they both want to bring the crook of the city down into prison) but there is one difference: Billy Costigan went undercover. I thought when I watched this for the first time: How can Costello and Mr. French not notice that Billy Costigan is a cop not a criminal?! Leonardo DiCaprio is perfect for the character because he is young, attractive yet arrogant in some places and the character is imagined to look like Leonardo DiCaprio. Jack Nicholson is perfect for Costello too because he is a real bad crook and a real ladies man, even though he is in his 70s at least. In most Jack Nicholson films, you can always tell that he has a very swerve way with women. He would have done better than Robert De Niro. He was Martin Scorseses first choice but rejected because he wanted to direct a film of his own called The Good Shepherd. Ray Winstone and Martin Sheen are excellent in this film aswell. But Vera Farmiga who plays the state police psychiatrist isnt very good at all I dont think.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-08-12","","RT","835701244"
