5.0,"I love the way the story is so deep and intricate that you can keep watching it over and over and find something new each time. This is another film that creates a good number of strong, well-drawn characters, each of which you wouldn't blink twice about seeing an entire film about (I'd love a film about the psychiatrist, but I know I'm the only person that thinks the father of her baby is someone else). This is a masterpiece, a modern mobster-crime drama that doesn't feel like a film the same way other heralded organized-crime pieces have, using quick cuts and a style that feels like an action-cop-drama kind of film instead. Leonardo DiCaprio is great, Matt Damon's performance doesn't leave me using the Team America voice, Jack Nicholson, Martin Sheen, and Mark Wahlberg all add to the dynamic ensemble cast, and Vera Farmiga is a character that offers as much to the thinking audience as she does prescription drugs to her patients. The highest-rated Best Picture winner on my favorite films list, it's the rare super-movie that's both movie and film, but watchable and analyzable.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-08-18","","RT","782019573"
