4.0,"Not as excellent as the original  but still great.

This is the American version of Infernal Affairs which is directed by Martin Scorsese. This means this movie is more realistic, fast paced, less emotional and more violent. Does that make it a bad movie? No. It just makes it a different one.

The casts were great. Leonardo DiCaprio, now already away from his cute Jack Dawson image, gives another brilliant performance. The thirty something actor convinces the audience that he is a troubled and unhappy twenty something year old. Jack Nicholson is Jack Nicholson, doing what Jack Nicholson does. Mark Wahlberg is Mark Wahlberg and plays his typical bad ass character. Matt Damon gives an ok performance, which is not good enough.

The only complaint I have to this movie is Matt Damon's character. Unlike Infernal Affairs' version, you can't sympathise him. In this version, he is just a complete prick. You just want him to die. With that out of the way however, this is a Martin Scorsese classic.","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2008-08-26","","RT","836737352"
