5.0,"I can call it a masterpiece!

It widely deserved the oscars it wons. And Leonardo could've had his 1st Oscar for it.

This movie is 1 million times better than the chinese film (infernal Affairs) a remake of which it is.

A sometimes very violent (psychologically and physically) dive inside the organized crime. 

Jack Nicholson is good, in the role of the leader of the organized crime.
Leonardo DiCaprio too, in the role of the infiltrated cop.
The supporting roles are also well played by Mark Wahlberg, Martin Sheen, Anthony Anderson, Alec Baldwin and the girl, Very Farmiga.
Even Matt Damon that I don't really like is pretty interesting in his criminal infiltrated in the police role.

Sad that so many of the main characters die at the end (even if it's not that sad for 1-2 of them).
The chinese movie has had 2 sequels, so, considering that The Departed is so better, I'd like to see a sequel, but it's hard, considering almost all the characters died.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-08-30","","RT","836901822"
