4.0,"CONSENSUS: Grittier and more violent than the original INFERNAL AFFAIRS, Scorcese is once again in top form. Damon, DiCaprio, and Nicholson all give stellar performances and the trademark wit is ever present in the street-smart dialogue. The inability to become attached to any character is a consistent flaw in Scorcese films (due largely to the fickle nature of morality present in all of them) and this is no exception. However, the characters are nonetheless captivating to watch (with the exception of the distracting love interest). The plot outline is faithful to its predecessor and is therefore intriguing to the end (which is slightly altered from the original, making it less impacting). By far Scorcese's best film since GOODFELLAS. MY GRADE: A-","",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2008-08-30","","RT","827617516"
