3.5,"After nearly a year of people scoffing at me for not having seen this, I finally rented it. Scorsese's Oscar was certainly a charity award - he's made better films - but the entire way through it, you feel you are in exceptionally good hands, and there is something to be said for that. We see everything we are supposed to see, when we are supposed to see it - and nothing we aren't. We enjoy great performances from everyone involved. A good script that might have been made into an average movie by a lesser director becomes instead an entertaining, engaging film with twists and turns in all the right places. You'll forget the movie a week later, but you won't forget you had a good time watching it.","",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2008-09-01","","RT","835988095"
