2.5,"No.  No.  No a thousand times no!!!  This is not the way it was supposed to happen.  He wasn't supposed to finally get his Oscar this way.  Remaking a Hong Kong actioner with Jack Nicholson not just chewing the scenery, but unhinging his jaw and swallowing it whole.  Mark Walhberg as the crusty and hardly benign cop who wouldn't know how to pronounce a word if it didn't have four letters in it.  Plot holes big enough to drive four eighteen wheelers through.  Leonardo Dicaprio doing his earnest sensitive best to stay one step ahead of the crooks and crooked cops that apparently are his Southie destiny.  And the last shot of the movie?  C'mon. WHAT ARE WE KIDS!!!!  Did they say ""Marty if you put that last shot in, the Oscar is yours to lose""?  Did he really have to put me through that?  This movie saddens me when I think that of all the unsung movies Scorsese has made (After Hours, Kundun, The Age of Innocence) this one had to be the one to actually go the distance into the winner's circle.  I hope he's happy not defying gravity.  Not recommneded.","",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2008-10-19","","RT","818940648"
