5.0,"Starting from the year 2000, this is Martin Scorcese's best film to date. He has a command and understanding of human nature and violence that no other director seems to come close to. After years of brilliant yet soft-lit gangster films with too-light tones, he finally does something completely ugly with no apparent smooth flow. You literally feel nervous and disjointed the way people feel when dealing with violence. This is not cathartic in any way, in fact, Scorcese wants you to feel disappointed, and he's saying, ""See? This is what happens when you are involved with this.""","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-12-16","","RT","832704407"
