5.0,"damn this film is good!  doesn't matter how many times i see it it still has the same effect on me.  it's a martin scorsese masterpiece and i've seen more than a few of his films.  it's a mob film in the tradition of good fellas and the godfather only smarter, edgier and more unpredictable.  the plot is riveting and suspenseful.  leonardo di caprio was at his finest, i loved the duality of his character and how he battles between being the cop who only wanted to do things right and the undercover agent who had to pretend to be the bad guy.  i may not have been a leonardo fan before this film but as billy costigan he certainly won me over.  he is certainly one of the best leading men in hollywood right now.  matt damon was perfect as the clean cut, scheming and ambitious sargeant sullivan.  i loved how his character and leo's were played off each other.  they only shared a few scenes together but they blew me away.  jack nicholson was impeccable as always.  he was costello and no other actor could have played that character to such perfection like jack did.  the rest of the cast also did well in their respective roles, namely martin sheen, alec baldwin and mark wahlberg.  the departed truly deserves its oscar and it's only right that scorsese won the oscar best director for his work on this film.  there should be more films like this.","b6277ecf-0509-43fc-969b-e8ae88bbf218",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-12-19","","RT","838338833"
