5.0,"A.k.a the film that finally earned Martin Scorsese that long overdue Best Director Oscar. While The Departed probably won't go down as Scorsese's finest, it is certainly a return to what he does best; the gritty urban gangster film. The Departed has everything you could want from a film. An incredible cast (Nicholson, De Caprio, Damon, Wahlberg, Sheen, Winstone), a superb script from William Monaghan (taking the blueprints of the excellent Infernal Affairs and expanding it into something brilliant), a typically Scorsese-like soundtrack (lots of Rolling Stones) and genius film-making. Nicholson steals the show (as you'd expect), but De Caprio shows how far he's come as an actor while Matt Damon shows why he's probably the finest young actor working today (special mention for Mark Wahlberg too, who does a lot with very little). All the trademarks are there; the sporadic yet heavy violence, the Catholic guilt, some humour and some bravura film-making, all leading to a bloody finale. Scorsese back doing what Scorsese does best, and justly rewarded by the Academy.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2008-12-30","","RT","798751792"
