4.5,"Now I have two major problems with The Departed, the first is that I haven't liked many films that has Matt Damon in since Dogma. Now, many people will say that Matt Damon is a good actor, sure I bet he can out act my ass any day of the week, but I always find him a very shallow, emotionless actor who never fits in to a role.

This however, is not the case with The Departed. I'm very picky about the films I let in to my top ten, and I am very picky about the films I let in to my top five, which brings me on to the second thing that annoyed me about The Departed, I liked it so much that I immediately put it in to my top three.

This may not be a big deal to most people, but the fact that it beat Donnie Darko and Reservoir Dogs is a big thing for me, as both films have had time at the very top of my all time top films, and for a film to reach number three after only watching it once is something that rarely happens in my books.

As some may know, Leo DiCaprio and Martin Scorsese have collaborated in a few films (three in total, Gangs of New York, The Aviator and The Departed) and will soon be collaborating in a fourth film together. I first saw Leo on the big screen when Titanic came out and I didn't think very much of him as an actor, then I saw him in The Beach and everything I thought about him came down (to his credit, I do own The Beach on DVD, and I do like it as a film, I just don't like him). Then a few weeks ago, Film4 was dedicating films to great directors and Martin Scorsese was one of them, they played The Departed and then Gangs of New York the night after, and I was gobsmacked that I have never watched either of these films before, Leo was shown in a new light to me, even Matt Damon seemed great in this role

So, I've given it 4.5/5, and I reccomend that if you get a chance, you should really take the time (and I mean a lot of time) to watch this movie, you won't regret it.

And if some how Leo reads his (lol), please please stay close to Martin Scorsese, he has already done your career wonders, and theres no telling where it can go.","",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2009-03-24","","RT","791198293"
