5.0,"Magnificent. I've never been 100% on Scorsese, enjoying his films becuase intellectually I knew they were good rather than enjoying them on amore visceral level, but this was brilliant. DiCaprio, Damon and Nicholson are all fantastic, playing in the case of the younger men slightly against type and revelling in it. The remainder of the cast is also impeccable. The direction is assured, bouncing between controlled character beats and flashy jarring flourishes, and the dialogure fizzes. As with the best of Scorsese, it is morally ambiguous, but in contrast to his other films, there is less rambling around the plot to create this ambiguity...instead relying on the actors to make their roles sympathetic despite the requirements of the plot. Say it quietly, but I found this more satisfying than Goodfellas.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-04-02","","RT","783053514"
