When I saw this is the cinema a few years back I was so fucking gutted that I had to leave to go to the toilet. It's just such a gripping film that I tried to hold it it as long as I could. First of all the cast is fucking awesome, DiCaprio, Sheen, Damon, Winstone, Baldwin plus Nicholson in one of his finest roles. Plus Marky Mark Wahlberg gives the performance of his otherwise mediocre career in this supporting role. Why can't this translate to his headliner performances? Plus for a film to be this good and it's an American remake look at the poor quality remakes of The Ring, The Eye, The Grudge and Bangcock Dangerous, if I'm honest I've only seen two of these to date but they are basically a simpler recycled version of the first. This movie is obviously very similar to Infernal Affairs but The Departed adds something new and fresh to the story which most remakes lack. The American ending although the happier ending and very American when compared with the original, I actually still prefer because it makes Marky Mark look like the hero. A fantastic re watchable movie that has always stood out as a classic to me, probably even better than Scorese's Goodfellas.","",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-04-04","","RT","820298349"
