4.5,"""She fell funny!"" I know I'm most certainly in the minority when I say this, but ""The Depated"" is, hands down, Scorsese's BEST crime film. Bringing back the same great stylings of ""Goodfellas"" and ""Casino,"" ""The Departed"" trumps these past dramas by utilizing truly flawed characters that blur the lines between ""good"" and ""evil"" within this Cain & Abel-like tale of desperation and deceipt. Jack Nicholson's performance is tremendous as are supporting cast members' Martin Sheen and Alex Baldwin. Wahlberg and Damon are both out of their ""nice guy with an attitude"" shells and breathe new life into familiar ""cop roles."" The true star is DiCaprio and his performance is 100% genuine and captivating. Chock full of all our favorite ""Scorseseisms"" (great soundtrack, hilarous one-liners, relentless pacing, etc.), ""The Departed"" delivers the goods on ALL fronts!","5fa3088d-4de6-4940-8a6c-61d7e5fdc9a8",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2009-05-27","","RT","856365851"
