4.0,"wow the resenblance is UNCANNY. just kidding. after having watched infernal affairs like 10 times, i recently just watched this. i must say there are lots of pros and cons i saw. warning this is a spoiler.

leonardo dicaprio and jack nicholson bring a different dimension than tony leung and eric Tsang. defintely nicholson does a better job but tsang was a bit more sympathetic of a character so you actually felt a little bad when he was killed. 

i actually liked andy lau's character better than matt damon. andy just has that flair about him that makes you WANT to believe that he really wanted to be a good cop. damon's character seems to change too rapidly near the end. 

wahlberg's character brings a new dimension, but he really does kind of confuse the ending a bit and he was basically unneccesary. 

the one thing i like about infernal affairs better than departed is that IA makes the scenes a lot more dramatic. you really dont see a lot of the scenes coming, but in the departed it seems kind of obvious wahts going to happen next. well maybe cuz i knew what happened next. but IA was a lot more unexpected, i guess thats HK cinema for you. the gangsters in the chinese version were better as well... like i dont understand why that irish dude who told dicaprio the wrong address didn't say anything to rat on him. that part was kinda dumb.

welll of course im scrutinizing all this in the eye of infernal affairs. since i watched it first, its hard cuz i loved the movie so much. but if u've never watched it, then this movie stands alone as a really good movie. u'll have to watch it twice though, to get the story line.","3d61fad6-c071-4ab0-87c3-ea4cad5661ec",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2009-05-27","","RT","812301325"
