5.0,"Martin Scorsese is the greatest director who ever lived. He makes the best gangster movies and the most compelling crime thrillers. Leonardo DiCaprio is spectacular like he always has been. Jack Nicholson is sensational, Matt Damon is phenomenal, and Mark Wahlberg is superb. Martin Sheen and Alec Baldwin are also great in this film. The Departed is a masterpiece. Scorsese is a cinematic legend and his films are simply extraordinary. The Departed is one of the greatest films ever made.","23bdb20a-0948-4825-8101-ab6905071b58",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-06-01","","RT","868786854"
3.5,"Departed is a modern cops and criminal tail that at times takes itself way to seriously.  Seeing the twists of undercover cop and undercover criminal, their rather messed up idols and sad love affairs, paints their world in unusually bleak colors.  Based on the Hong Kong movie trilogy ""Infernal Affairs"" it does many things better such as emphasizing the common thread of deceit and puppeteering.  It fails miserably though when it comes to the love triangle (which if I remember correctly is not in the Hong Kong version?) and you also get the feeling that there was a reason the Infernal Affairs was in three parts.
The dept of the characters that could be explored here is so great, the twists and the turns endless.  Watching a movie where one even get confused with the likable undercover criminal, and rather unlikeable cop.  Who are you rooting for?  We get it all in, arguably rather long, single movie.  You almost feel like it you watch the trailer of an epic story.  
The acting was unusually good for most of the actors.  Jack overdid it a bit, but that is his style and he can be forgiven.  Martin simply didn't get anything to do.  Matt and Leonardo both turned in one of their top performances in their career.  And Mark, who I usually hate, was awesome and by far the most memorable character.  The only weak link, as stated before was the love affair, the girl being played by Vera Farmiga.  We never really get to understand her, and her whole inclusion in the story lines seems to be for some end plots to play out.  
I might be a bit harsh, giving this great film only 3,5 stars, but my reasoning is such:  The story is taken from Hong Kong, with such an original story that the set up itself just has to make for an interesting film.  The director is one of the best, collecting her cast of many of the greatest actors of our times.  Therefore I simply demand that a film made with all this talent in combination with fantastic story, should leave me breathless and definitively in AWE.
The Departed does neither, but is rather just a fun trip to the movies or a late Saturday DVD rental.","cb0df0b9-8acb-467c-bec8-195d9b74d07c",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2009-06-01","","RT","789044563"
