3.0,"I find it difficult that a remake won best picture. If the underlying story was <i>that</i> good then the original version would have been good enough to bring state side. I guess not. What I fail to see with this movie is what's so fucking epic about it. Where is it soooo great? Nowhere. It doesn't excell in plot, acting, pacing, nothing. It's simply an adequate movie that struggles to get its point across. I was having trouble caring about any of the characters, and in a movie like this that's crucial. Hell, they don't even use Alec Baldwin and he was the best of the bunch. I suppose this is technical film making at its finest, though. Cinematography is where it's at, but does not a good movie make. Scorsese is going to have to reach deeper into his little bag of tricks.","433f7e0e-cf25-46eb-a6df-5fdbc36575fc",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2009-06-11","","RT","786964687"
