5.0,"Laden with brilliant twists and turns, Scorsese has created what some would, and justifiably so, call his best picture yet. Carried by an absolute star-studded cast, this perfectly constructed crime epic will enthrall you from start to finish, leaving you in awe at its shocking climax.","fef2270f-3051-4427-93db-79d92a846f2a",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-06-14","","RT","848487346"
4.5,"The Departed by Eric Harper

This gritty crime drama from Oscar Winner Martin Scorsese, takes us into the lives of two cops. Colin Sullivan (Matt Damon) is a smart, ambitious, and appears to be on a fast track up the police force in the Massachusetts State Police Department Investigation Squad. As a boy he was granted a job working for a Irish mob boss who just so happens to be the  prime target in his new investigation, Frank Costello (Jack Nicholson). 

Billy Costigan (Leonardo DiCaprio) is a street smart, violent tempered young undercover investigator who comes from a broken family. Costigan goes under Costellos wing as a young recruit. Costiganknows no one in the force other than his two superiors Queenan ( Martin Sheen) and Dignam (Mark Wahlberg). For extra guidance Billy goes to a young gorgeous therapist named Madolyn (Vera Farmiga) who turns out to be Sullivans new girlfriend.

When chief Ellerby (Alec Baldwin) discovers theres a rat in his unit he assigns Sullivan and his team to find out who it is. While Costigans doing the exact same but from the inside.

 But neither Sullivan or Costigan are what they seem. Ones a cop and ones only pretending to be a cop but for these two is there any difference? As they work at different sections of the department, they are plunged into a dangerous game of cat and mouse in which the stakes are there lives. 

The Departed  is driven by fantastic performances which isnt strange for a Scorsese movie. DiCaprio gives off the perfect amount of desperation, and Damon radiates as a pompous ace cadet rising through the ranks. As if it is no surprise Jack Nicholson gives another Oscar worthy performance as he steals every single scene he is in.","a3037f17-7324-4e29-a4e6-0116e05d1cea",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2009-06-14","","RT","901209336"
