4.5,"So I watched Pride And Glory a few months ago and it was clearly the best film i'd seen in a very long time and nothing had really come along which I thought was better than it until I watched The Departed. I haven't really seen a lot of Martin Scorsese movies but I obviously knew who he was and the hype did not disappoint. From the moment this movie starts you are totally griped into it. Jack Nicholson plays a great character, its like Jack from The Shining when he is just starting to go insane which we know Jack Nicholson plays so well. Plus his character is a bit of an enigma, for example he just walks into a room and has his hands covered in blood and the film gives no reason for this, but he acts like everything is fine. But what I think really makes this film great is the chase. Which rat will be discovered first? and hats off to Matt Damon and Leo Di Caprio, they are amazing. The best moment for me in the film is when Damon phone Leo and he picks up, neither person say anything but its an incredible piece of cinema. You'll know what I mean if you've seen. Also Mark Wahlberg's character is brilliant. He brings a great dynamic to the film which runs right up until the end. There is also small roles for Alec Baldwin who is maybe the comic relief in this film but I don't really see the point in him being in it.  Plus Martin Sheen pops up to an untimely death. This film is absolutely incredible and I couldn't recommend it more.","754f658b-6093-472a-af0a-547f4cee25f8",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2009-06-28","","RT","901272669"
