4.5,"Undoubtedly my favorite crime drama of all time for so many reasons. An amazing number of stars at their very best (DiCaprio, Nicholson, Wahlburg, Damon...the list goes on) under the direction of THE premier crime drama master (Scorcese). How could you go wrong? Well apparently...you couldn'. Despite its hefty run time, it never fails to enthrall you scene after scene after scene. The director could have resorted to cookie cutter cops and criminals, but instead he infuses the subtle shades of gray into each of them. And b the time it all comes together and the ""$h!t finally hits the fan"" , it's tough to know who to trust anymore. If that isn't the mark of a good crime drama then I don't know what it is. Crime is always rooted in the subtle grays, and Scorcese brings them in spades, as seems to be par for the course for the man (GoodFellas anybody?). I can't recommend this one enough, but be prepared to become temporarily numb to the unrelentingly foul mobster language that is (often times distractingly) prevalent throughout.","0156bfdf-0b5c-44d8-b5cc-31ddf62ed056",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2009-07-03","","RT","901282791"
