4.5,"By the time this movie came out, I had been waiting a LONG time for a new gangster movie to really blow me away.  After numerous disappointments, too many to mention, Martin Scorsese decided to remake a Chinese movie called Infernal Affairs and in 2006 unleashed The Departed.

Taking place in South Boston the film stars Leonardo DiCaprio (who gets better with every movie) as an undercover cop investigating a gangster based on Whitey Bulger (Jack Nicholson).  Matt Damon plays a gangster who becomes a member of the Boston Police Department.  The movie is great for showcasing two men leading double lives on both sides of the law.  Its fascinating to watch both these guys lead double lives and your remain interested to see if one slips up and blows their cover for one side.

The all-star cast which also features Mark Wahlberg, Alec Baldwin & Martin Sheen and all performances are top notch.  Nicholson is basically Nicholson and doesn't do anything mindblowing; but that's like watching a Yankees game and complaining that Babe Ruth went 3 for 5, 2 RBIs,  but no home runs.

This movie also ended a career long drought at the Academy Awards for Scorsese who in his 7th nomination for Best Director finally took home the Oscar.  The film itself won 4 Academy Awards that year including Best Picture.

Is The Departed the best film of Scorsese's career?  I don't think so.  Its hard to pick one film out of his body of work that is ""his best"".  Like so many Hollywood heavyweights, no one remembers what movie you won the Oscar for...just as long as you win.","6afbf55d-88c3-4e4e-bdd3-5a6de7c5e8cf",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2009-07-08","","RT","862923470"
5.0,"The departed is the masterful work of none other than Hollywood legend Martin Scorsese back where he belongs making films about crime. In this film Scorsese shows the violent story of two rats, on ewithin the Bostan police force and the other inside the Bostan Irish mob led by Mob boss Costello (Jack Nicholson). This is an amazing film and one of Scorsese's best for a long time. Definately worth your money!","22636b11-643d-4e41-8984-5625bbd555cd",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-07-08","","RT","875222817"
