3.5,"The inner conflict of the DiCaprio character is what made this film for me. He had an honorable, strong-willed father and that really meant a lot to him. It meant a lot to bring honor to his father's name and that's something that people have definitely lost in modern times. Being forced to walk in muddy water on the side of the law because his extended family were all crooks just eats him inside and out, and I could see myself in the character, as every action that he took that wasn't true to himself made him feel guilt-ridden and subhuman. So many people are like the Matt Damon character sadly, wanting to appear good so no one can see their flaws and lies, while not seeing those lies as character flaws, and that's a significant detriment to the society of today. The movie's script is thrilling and the cast makes this film a winner.","fe740ccb-2ed4-40d2-9cd0-271b9a2dfb0e",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2009-07-17","","RT","795344791"
