5.0,"First movie since Gilbert Grape in which DiCaptrio plays a character I can both believe and like.  The rest of the fine ensemble no doubt helped, including relative newcomer, Vera Farmiga, a compelling corner of the love triangle involving DiCaprio and Damon's characters.  It's an intricate crime and cop story, with DiCaprio as the undercover agent, and Damon as the bad detective, each racing to uncover the identity of the other.  Scorcese's storytelling and direction are so efficient that somehow within a half an hour the viewer has gotten the biographies of the main characters, background on organized crime in Boston, and the structure of crime-fighting.  It's a bit of a whirlwind, with vivid characters (Wahlberg is incredible, the copside mirror to Nicholson's evil mob boss), with innumerable plot twists that lead to a body count that might make Hamlet jealous.  And it's one of Scorcese's darkest takes on the human condition--truth may out now and then, a kind of justice may win, but only after tremendous human cost.","27873aa1-f3d0-49bf-a4ce-2ec46c4c5665",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-07-25","","RT","806318590"
