5.0,"This movie definitely makes my top 5. I have watched this movie many times and it is as enjoyable as the first time. The casting is ridiculously good. Martin Sheen and Jack Nicholson are amazing. Plus you have Leonardo DiCaprio who normally I don't enjoy, but he is really good in this movie. Matt Damon also does a fine job (surprised Ben Affleck didn't have a cameo). Vera Farmiga certainly doesn't take anything away from this movie, and Alec Baldwin is pretty entertaining. Finally and probably my favorite character is Sgt. Dignam played by Mark Wahlberg is the coolest character in this movie. Along with Nicholson, very quotable and has some of the best lines of the film.

This film really brought me back to GoodFellas, which is a very, very good thing. It is rough around the edges and definitely doesn't shy away from anything. This is a great piece of film and has one of my all time favorite soundtracks of any movie. It has an amazing lineup of classic rock as well as some instrumental which is also very good. Aside from featuring The Rolling Stones, it has an amazing cover of Comfortably Numb (by Pink Floyd) performed by I believe it is Van Morrison (that could be wrong).

If you haven't already watch this film.","dbbbf4c4-3d0f-4aa9-ab76-ea7a126ea757",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-08-03","","RT","901259372"
