5.0,"Leave it to Martin Scorsese to deliever one of the best movies of the decade. Seriously, this is a a great film full of all the elements one enjoys in a movie. Theres story, character, violence, great music, and some serious drama. This movie is a dazzingly example of a cinematic masterpiece from one of the greatest directors in film history.

The Departed is a remake of the 2002 Hong Kong crime thriller Infernal Affairs. Except that it is done the way a remake should be done. Instead of just ripping off the movie it is based on, it expands upon it's story. It's essentially Martin's Scorsese's Infernal Affairs. Thanks to Mr. Scorsese working from a brillant script by Willaim Monahan. 

I'm not saying that Infernal Affairs is a bad movie, in fact it is great, but The Departed has Martin Scorsese behind the camera calling the shots. Any fan of Scorsese knows what to expect from one of his gangster movies, and this is no different. It is every single bit as good as Goodfellas. Scorsese is just a master of balance, and juggles all the elements of the film perfectly. Now that I've given Scorsese credit for his stellar direction, I need to talk about the other absolutely brillant aspect of this movie.The performances. 

I can without a doubt say that there is not a bad perfomance from any memeber of the cast. Leonardo DiCaprio gives a riveting performance as Billy Costigan, a cop that is undercover and completely alone. DiCaprio should've won an Oscar for this performance. He completey sells the character's difficulty as he becomes deeply consumed by his double life.

Matt Damon is also quite good as Colin Sullivan, a mole whose star is shining so brightly no one notices his betrayel. Damon does great with what he is given, but it is clear that Costigan is the meatier part of the two. 

Jack Nicholson gives one of the best performances of his career as Frank Costello, a mob boss losing his mind. I think it's odd that Nicholson was overlooked for an Oscar for this film, as it was a stronger performance than Mark Wahlberg's as Dignam. 

Wahlberg gives a sterotypical performance that is almost too comedic. Still he is great and is really only bound by the script that doesn't give his character much to do but be extremely profane. There is a touching side to his relationship with Captain Queenan, and perhaps this is why he is so hostile towards Costigan. These are two characters who view this man as their father figure, and maybe Dignam doesn't like the idea of not having him completely to himself. 

Martin Sheen gives a performance that deserves more credit than it is given in the biliing. If Robert DeNiro had played the role it would've been a struggle to decide between him and Nicholson for who gets higher billing. Queenan is such a pivotal role to the story. The Departed seems to overlook the character's overall importance in comparison to Infernal Affairs. It isn't in a negative way, it's just that the importance of his character isn't depicted as outright in this film.

Alec Baldwin shines in his limited role as Ellerby. Every scene that he is in is gold. Baldwin has really come into his own as a comedic actor, and a good portion of the comedy in The Departed comes from him. 

This seems like a long critque of the acting, but Ray Winstone must also be credited as Mr. French. Costello wouldn't have worked as well without French...guarnateed. Winstone just needs the right role to completely break out. 

It'd be a crime not to at least mention Vera Farmiga's fantastic performacne. She is great as a Pshychiatrist that is torn between two people she loves that couldn't be any more different. Does she stick to society's rules and stay with the man of worth or does she go with the guy that she finds the most fasicnating. 

Scorsese knows people and their behaviors and that makes him such a brillant voice. The romance aspect is something completely added to The Departed. Unlike some movies, doesn't hinder the story but merly adds to it. 

I want people to see this movie with as clean as slate as possible. You simply owe it to yourself. Watch this movie if you love movies. It is a movie that deserves to be seen. Please watch this...I beg of you.","9cf01240-e39d-4987-afc8-66015500ebe8",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-09-26","","RT","901314177"
