3.0,"This is the film that finally won Martin Scorsese an Oscar for Best Director. How ironic then, that it can't hold a candle to some of his earlier work. The plot is intriguing enough, a deadly game of cat and mouse between the Boston mafia and the cops, who each discover that an undercover agent has infiltrated their organisation. Yet the film is let down by some dubious casting. Jack Nicholson is not best suited to this genre and turns his mob boss into little more than a pantomime villain. Matt Damon and Mark Wahlberg are notable mainly for over-using the f-word. And try as he might, it is virtually impossible for Leonardo DiCaprio to convince as a tough guy. There are flashes of the old magic and the ending packs a punch, but overall this is underwhelming filmmaking from a director capable of so much more.","a906923b-8376-4020-8d2f-fdb50eab5662",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2009-09-28","","RT","791188951"
