3.0,"Another good Scorsese film that seems to suffer from his usual disturbing interest in mobsters and murder. Honestly he's a good director but he has a habit of leaving a bad taste in my mouth. I don't want to invest not only my time but emotionally in characters for them to be blown away in the most unappealing manner before the end credits. 

Yes you could say that's gritty, yes you could say that's realistic and yes dammit you can applaud him for once again going against the Hollywood grain and yes I would say all those things BUT it's doesn't remove the fact that I was enjoying this film, it's web of intrigue, the tightly wound  tension, the Boston politics and of course Jack's sterling performance. Right up until the last twenty minutes or so of the film when I was left feeling like I was in a time warp having watched the best of 70's movie making but felt, as one of Scorcese's mobsters may have put it, why the FUCK have I watched piece of rat bastard SHIT! 

The answer is, it's a Scorcese flick and if you know that, then you know enough to decide if you think it's worth watching. If your a Scorcese fan it's good, if you don't like his work it's horrendous and if like me you're impressed with him technically but find his subject matter unsavoury then you may just find it middling. It's good, certainly not great or Oscar worthy, but it's not bad or ugly either. Worth watching at least the once.","14cc6e19-16b4-49d4-90b2-50ec208bce0a",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2009-10-05","","RT","800177135"
