4.0,"A twisted and tortous film from the very beginning. This has got to be one of the best films I have ever seen. I do not usually watch a lot of DiCaprio films but I have to say this one blows ""Catch Me if You Can"" out of the water, one of his best roles yet! Also Jack Nicholson played yet another sociopath, but with a twist, a sociopath who is also a drug dealer and a crime lord. Sort of like the Joker without the makeup and costume. The plot was extremely intresting and suspensful at the same time. I never got bored. So many twists and turns around every corner. I really like the good guy, bad guy contrast this movie gave and aroung 10 minutes till the end I thought I knew what was going to happen, and then BAM! The unexpected! You will never be able to guess the ending of this movie. I wished that the movie had a different ending but there really isn't much to complain about. But I did think that it was overkill when Sullivan got shot in the very end. Also the whole scene with the rat running across the windowsill was sort of a stupid pun. After Costigan was killed I was dying to see what was in the envelope he gave the therapist, but it was never shown! This was overall an excellant movie but I would no recommend it for children at all. Costello is a crime lord involved in nothing else but crime! All crime! He does drugs, had his women, kills anyone who gets in his way and is still protected by the government. The F word is used every other word and makes the Inside Man look like nothing. This movie contains 226 F words and at least six nice little hand gestures.","709f8be2-770d-441d-9d04-66e83756a4e7",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2009-10-10","","RT","791423277"
