5.0,"Wow this is one fantastic movie. It is a bloody, violent affair about deception, trust and how far one will go to protect their own self. Director Martin Scorsese assembled an all-star cast for this one. Some of the members include: Jack Nicholson, Matt Damon, Leonardo DiCaprio, Mark Wahlberg, Martin Sheen and Anthony Anderson. All of the supporters here do an incredible. 

Leonardo DiCaprio plays Billy Costigan, criminal turned cop as Dignam (Wahlberg) and Queenan (Sheen) get him to go undercover to bring down mob boss Frank Costello. The police have a rat inside Costello's outfit. Matt Damon plays Collin Sullivan who is a fast rising, hard-working and trustworthy cop with a perfect record. No suspects that he is Fank Costello's rat inside SIU. The stakes in this movie keep getting high and higher as an exciting game of cat adn mouse is played out on screen. 

There are a number of surprising scenes in this movie. It takes a number of shocking twist and turns and just when you think it is going to play out one way, it does a back-flip and goes the other. While I won't spoil the ending, let's just say you will have mixed emotions about it. If you have not seen this movie, you may or may not have heard about the infamous elevator scene. It will leave you angry at first, then somewhat satisfied. 

As I mentioned before, this movie is very violent. There are a good number of deaths in this movie, many of them big characters. So if you hate violence, stay away form this movie. This is an edge-of-your-seat thriller that grabs you by the throat at the beginning and doesn't let go until the credits. It is also the kind of movie that will grow on you. What I mean is: the more the watch of it, the more you will pick up and the better it gets. This may be one of the best crime movies of all time and at the very least, of this decade. It more than deserved the awards it got.","9a36de47-3afe-4952-834e-bd52b33142b9",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-10-29","","RT","788218120"
3.5,"Intense. Violent. Lotta F-bombs flying around. Can't say I liked the ending. Definitely could not call this one ""good clean fun,"" but I LIKED Nicholson and Sheen. Thought Leonardo did a great job, but I just had major trouble believing his character would do what he did. Matt Damon was so understated he was almost catatonic. I wouldn't recommend watching it with the kids.","64838ae9-f134-4a1f-a15e-cd89e2fca3b5",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2009-10-29","","RT","783622888"
