2.5,"Boondocks revisited.

Bostonians are far from flattered or thankful of the kiddie exposure that comes with having their culture haphazardly mocked by Hollywood pansies. Although a touch better than ""The Perfect Storm"", no consultant in the world can seem to to train powder-assed, egomaniacal actors into the eastern Massachusetts role and dialectânot even those actors who are allegedly from the area (Wahlberg).

As usual, DiCaprio comes off as a contrived, whiny punk; buffoon Baldwin as his industry-licensed real-life abusive racist womanizing self; and Nicholson as a coke-addled, arrogant, bat shit lunatic who is pitifully more mortal and fallible than it is clear that he believes. (He also turned in the most ridiculously over-emphasized performance this time around, as it were: I've never heard of any fellow Bostonian burying a man in ""tha maaaaash"".)

However, count on Apocalypse veteran Martin Sheen, area Good Will Hunting's Damon and relative unknowns Vera Farmiga and Ray Winstone to provide ample ballast in making this a watchable, if not remorselessly over-stated, ugly pissy cop whodunnit guinea mick ""fack you!"" bang-bang fest. If that's your thing.","e4d4a65a-99c2-48d0-8d6b-25184b5edf22",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2009-11-10","","RT","806257501"
4.0,"a very brilliant remake of a fantastically superb chinese movie trilogy..its like how RAam Gopal Varma combined elements of Godfather 2 n 3 to give a story for Sarkar Raj..Scorcese combined the Infernal Affairs trilogy..takin elements from all movies to give a very good film..the feel of the movie is raw and gritty..very well adapted into the boston environment..bravo!!","b6184ac5-ce38-40c5-bb77-889b12e5e720",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2009-11-10","","RT","890391497"
5.0,"The Departed is is Martin Scorsese's best film since Goodfellas. It won for Best Picture at the Oscars in 2007. I will say the first time I saw The Departed, I was not amazed. I didn't think it was as good as everybody said it was. I thought that maybe I wasn't paying good enough attention to the film and decided to watch it again. It was much better the second time. Each performance is just great, I felt that Mark Wahlberg gave the best performance. I just love that kind of role he played. The accents seemed kind of fake but that didn't matter because the brilliance of this film just overshawdowed it. The plot was amazing, the writting was amazing, and the direction was of course amazing. As you can probably tell, it seems Leonardo Dicaprio is Scorsese's latest prodidgy (the last being Robert Deniro). I am very much looking foreward to his next film Shutter Island. I thought that the twist ending in the film was great. Also just as a side note... Jack Nicholson is a badass. This film had one of the best casts ever. Each actor delivered. An amazing story with great actors and Martin Scorsese as director, you couldn't get anything better. TEN STARS!","6e9e9628-b324-4d84-89f6-9844af939884",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-11-10","","RT","901309501"
