I hope Shutter Island will keep that stigma going.","f5c64e75-1d8b-4ce0-8711-2fa9ce2fb203",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-11-18","","RT","893446912"
5.0,"The Departed...oh what a masterpiece! It is such a well-made film by Scorsese that very few other gangster films can really compare (besides the other ones that he has made). DiCaprio, Damon, and Nicholson are cast as the three main characters, and they each do a phenomenal job. The screenplay is based on another film from Hong Kong called Infernal Affairs, but somehow, it manages to capture the brutal harshness of gang wars with the authorities whilst still keeping emotion and grit between the characters. It is intellectual and real, but also gives a great ending that no one can really see coming. Add to that the scene that basically defines the ""cat-and-mouse chase"" and you get an amazing display of tense emotions of people trying to reveal opposing identities whilst trying to remain secret at the same time. A great screenplay and excellent direction as well as a very desolate backdrop of Boston give this film a great combination, creating a modern classic masterpiece.","3e1542e2-c7ad-4cfd-8831-f3a250bcfa4c",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-11-18","","RT","901311916"
5.0,"A great cast and amazing return to the crime genre for Martin Scorsese. It has some of the best performances from Matt Damon and Jack Nicholson in years and Mark Wahlberg's best. Not to mention another flawless performance from Leonardo DiCaprio. The story is suspenseful and well developed, giving you the best possible connection to the characters. I think it's one of the most visually different films that Scorsese has ever shot, it seemed like a completely different director shot some of the scenes. I think it's just even more evident that Scorsese is always building upon his work and trying new things.","4f93e2d1-ffa6-49c8-9490-4075d8631a0f",False,True,False,False,5.0,"2009-11-19","","RT","893475750"
