4.5,"so well made, acted, written, and directed, the departed is a flat out great movie with a few good laughs, shocking moments and scenes, this movie holds and doesnt let go until the last scene is over","bfb9c3e8-87f6-4ac6-88d0-fdc86d710263",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2009-11-24","","RT","901233877"
4.0,"Martin Scorcese is a defiant filmmaker. With his stories of deep conflict and a eye for suspense, Martin is genuinely unique. Mainly dominating in the crime/thriller genre,  Scorcese is masterful in films such as Taxi Driver, Gangs of New York, and Casino. Now, with his new film, The Departed, Scorcese provides a new and thrilling crime drama based in the heart of Boston.

Following two undercover snitches for the two sides of good and evil, The Departed is a story of underground crime. The two ""snitches"" are played by Leonardo DiCaprio and Matt Damon. The two characters represent to sides of society. One of which stands for the guy who has done nothing wrong with his life, but ends up with the crap job for the Boston Police Department. The other is the ""unfair"" aspect in which the rotten one gets the best slice of life. This guy gets a high position with the BPD, but is also a snitch for the largest crime lord, Mr. Costello (Jack Nicholson). 

Jack Nicholson plays the all-too-creepy link between the two snitches as the mastermind behind the crime. 

Scorcese's film is masterfully put together as a story of suspense and internal conflict. As well with it's deep reflection of the lifestyle and dialect in Boston.

Though the movie presents an excellent story and ambiance, the film has an awkward pace. With the film being nearly three hours long, and editing that seems a tad choppy, the viewing can seem uncomfortable.

But, when things add up, Scorcese's film of crime and drama turns to be a wonderful thrill ride. With awesome performances, and a superb story, The Departed is crime classic that will go down for years.","239d4c10-ba69-43d1-a13e-6cc565f6c9c7",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2009-11-24","","RT","901111129"
