4.5,"This is the best gangster film i have seen in years. I haven't seen many Scorcese films including his critically acclaimed ""Goodfellas"" till now. I just knew about the climax of the movie and it just made me curious to watch the full movie when it was aired on HBO. To my surprise i was glued to the screen for the 2 and 1/2 hours without thinking anything other than what's gonna happen next in the movie. Such an impact it created and the prolific cat-and-mouse chase was brilliant throughout. It bettered the original Infernal Affairs by heaps as the original never kept me this interested.

The plot in one-line is simple. A mole in both the good men and bad men camp and how both these men take desperate measures to find the ""Black Sheep"" before its too late for both of them. The turning point is that the mole in good men searching for the mole in bad men who is working for the good men and mole in bad men searching for the mole in good men who is working for the bad men. I can't provide anything more.   

The Stupendous cast with Jack Nicholson, Leonardo Di Caprio, Matt Damon, Martin Sheen, Mark Wahlberg, Alec Baldwin, Vera Ferminga and Ray Winstone all doing commendable performances. The tear-jerkers and one-liners are always a specialty of Mr.Nicholson and he did nothing less in this movie. I was so excited and shocked to see Matt Damon in a negative role after raving so much about him as my favorite hero after watching ""The Bourne Supremacy"" and ""The Bourne Identity"". He easily fitted the role very well as he has did that kind of a role before in ""The Talented Mr.Ripley"". 

This is a quality entertainment movie for all those gangster-film lovers out there which is worth the oscar it bagged. I recommend it to all. Watch it! You won't be disappointed!","7b27c0fa-98b1-4589-be57-e21651abc5fc",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2009-11-30","","RT","901338090"
