3.0,"You always know what's coming when you go to a Martin Scorsese film.  So it's no surprise that The Departed delivers plenty of violence, intrigue, and suspense.  With all the bangs it delivers in the first two hours, it's just too bad it ends with a just a very loud whimper.

The story is another one about the age-old battle between the cops and the crooks, but it throws in just enough twists to make it a fresh and engaging tale.  The performances are outstanding, particularly Leonardo DiCaprio as the undercover good cop and Matt Damon as the corrupt detective.  Martin Sheen, Mark Wahlberg, and Jack Nicholson are, as usual, strong cast members, but the real kudos goes to Ray Winstone as the ominous Mr. French and the captivating Vera Farmiga as the police psychologist.

It's a long movie that gets confusing at times, as it relies on cell phone displays and an array of various thugs with thick Boston accents to tell the story.  You won't be disappointed if you have a liking for Scorsese's style and accompanying violence, and the plot is better than most.  The only problem I had with this film is its slow death of an ending.  You'll enjoy the movie, but you might feel just a little bit cheated when all is said and done.","b03580a9-e4f2-43d3-85e6-57162a045bcd",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2009-12-28","","RT","901353561"
5.0,"Love this movie! An brilliant & violent crime epic. It about  2 cops, 1 is a under cover. while the other one was a normal one. 1 cop work for the cop while the other one really work for the mobs so he can help them get away with things.","2df80e88-fead-4adf-a052-fc7d37e023d6",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2009-12-29","","RT","806281840"
5.0,"I've been a fan of The Departed since it first came out four years ago. I bought it watched it a bunch of times, put it on the shelf, and completely forgot about it. I watched it again recently, and I gotta say. This is one of the best films I have ever seen. I always knew it was excellent, but I never really took the time to reflect on just how great it really is. Martin Scorsese is one hell of a Director. His masterpieces are definitely his gangster films.

I need to do some research because I would swear that Martin Scorses is a gangster himself. He crafts such perfect gangster movies that it is hard not to think he has personal experience. I guess some guys are just that good of a storyteller. And his cast coudn't be better. Well if Samuel L. Jackson was in it, then it would be better, but even without him it's perfect. It's pretty obvious why Scorsese has Leonardo DiCaprio in alot of his pictures. The guy is fantastic.

Jack Nicholson is pure genious. His mannerisms are unbelievable, and he delivers lines with a beauty that we don't see very often on screen. Matt Damon, Alec Baldwin, Martin Sheen, Ray Winstone and the sexy Vera Farmiga round out the all-star cast. My personal favorite perfomance, after Jack Nicholson, is Mark Wahlberg. His character made me crack a smile almost everytime he spoke, and started a fight. There were great performances all around.

I always pay attention to the music, and Howard Shore's (LOTR trilogy) score is excellent. I won't summarize the story because I doubt that anyone has not seen this movie. But if by some chance you haven't, you really need to, as soon as possible. All I will say about it, is that the last twenty minutes are some of the best film that American Cinema has to offer. Actually the entire movie is. It's a definite must-see.","bee931e5-cce9-4e01-b538-a86b72f95a0b",False,True,False,False,5.0,"2009-12-29","","RT","901316707"
