4.0,"My 77th favorite movie all time (and by the way, a one I could see moving up a great deal, for I have only seen it once)

Martin Scorsese finally got his Academy Award for 2006's The Departed. Although it's not his best movie, it is excellent.

The premise is outstanding, to begin with. Frank Costello (Jack Nicholson) is the dominant crime lord in Boston. He has a rat on the police force in Matt Damon, but the police also have a rat with Costello in Leonardo DiCaprio.

DiCaprio's performance here is really outstanding. You feel his suffering and understand the hardships he has to go through. His identity has been taken away and only Mark Wahlberg and Martin Sheen know he's a cop. And on top of that, he has to commit crime in order to keep his credibility as Costello's man.

The suspense of this movie builds and builds and gets almost unbearable at the end. Damon is desperately trying to find the rat with Costello and DiCaprio is desperately trying to find the rat in the police. The best scene of the movie is when the two of them pick up their cell phones and know that who they want is on the other end. I can't describe the ingenuity of that scene, but it's a testament to Martin Scorsese's brilliance.","b8a5d42a-e30f-47e5-8ddd-24c82a9da327",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2010-01-03","","RT","901049002"
