4.0,"Olipas vain aika pakkaus kylla. Voisi jopa sanoa, etta hammentavan alun jalkeen ku paasi juonesta kiini niin elokuva oli todella mielenkiintoinen. Nayttelijasuoritukset olivat erittain onnistuneita, varsinkin itse Jack Nicholsonilla joka oli Costellon roolissa mahtava. Muutenkin Scorsese onnistuu pitamaan elokuvan juonikuviot taitavasti hyppysissaan. Silti elokuva ei aivan onnistu herattamaan mitaan taydellisyyden ylistyksia, mutta 2,5h pituus ei kuitenkaan tunnu raskaalta.
Mita talle nyt sitten antaa... 4tahtea vai 3,5...... no 4 vaikka Nicholsonin kunniaksi.","4ad820c8-966c-4577-905c-b00bf05021ae",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2010-01-03","","RT","892338720"
4.0,"Before he directed the incredibly fâ¦ed up Shutter Island, Martin Scorsese delivers us of a crime film that could possibly be one of his best movie of his career and of the decade: The Departed

It revolved on two young men who worked in the Masachusetts State police and their story: Billy (Leonardo Dicaprio) is a trooper and is working undercover with Sgts. Dignam (Wahlberg) and Queenan (Sheen) to take out Irish mob boss Frank Costello. At the same time, Colin (Matt Damon) is working undercover for Costello to get info from the offices of the police force. Both guys need to gain trust from Costello to take both rats out.

Trust me, the story was amazing in how corruption can start disturbingly at childhood and how depressing and frustrating it can be to live in a life of crime. A foreign remake on the Hong Kong drama Infernal Affairs, Scorsese makes this into a bloody epic runned up to two and a half hours. This movie shows a symbol of corruption and is well written with no flaws or difference.

Both performances with Leo and Damon are brilliant deivering fine performances. Jack Nicholson who plays Costello bringing in development with characters especially the scene where he is sitting with Billy at a bar to open up his suspicions on a rat in his syndicate and so does Vera Famiga who plays the girlfriend of both Billy and Colin.    

The problem I have with the characters is that they are so pissed-off. Billy gets so angry all the time and you might get killed if you triggered the boy a reaction especially if it isn't affected to him. Mark Walhberg can say the F word whenever he wanted to and has a heavy use of sarcasm and, boy, you don't want to see the ending. Other characters like the Collin's crew of cops were so desperate to be part of the movie overly said the F word a lot. 

A very sad story with The Departed that doesn't have the sentiments against people who can bring down power.

Verdict: Never mind the F word, here's the best movie Martin Scorsese made in years","beae7d66-bd31-46a2-8bf3-0574a23df4ec",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2010-01-04","","RT","896539807"
5.0,"This is one of my favorite movies of all time.  The Overall actig is superb by pretty much all of the actors. There really isn't a weak link to this movie. The cinematography is incredible on all acounts, Martin Scorcese's talent with directing is highly evident. The music to this movie complements every twis and turn of the plot and is just right, as it isn't too overwhelming and distracting but it isn't completely absent from the movie. The only downside of the music is that the composition that was made for the movie is a single guitar, which works well for this type of movie, but it is the same thing over and over again. This is compensated for by well selected peices of modern rock music. But, although all of these things were amazing, the best part of the whole movie was the plot. The storyline to this movie was INCREDIBLE and kept the moviegoer engaged and actively thinking. You can never guess what is going to happen next. Especially in the end. The ending is  completely unexpected and leaves you thinking and in complete wonderment. The only downside of the whole thing is the cussing. There is an excess amount of cussing in the movie and if you don't like that then you can watch it on FX channel because all of the cussing is cut out of it. This is a movie for everyone. An instant classic","3491c644-59b4-4c60-9673-3966bc5ef7a7",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-01-04","","RT","796773501"
