5.0,"This Scorsese crime drama film is superb for so many reasons. From the intense story telling and character developments to the rather humorous dialogue exchanges and scenarios between some the the characters at times, Scorsese made this movie flow very well together. Scorsese brilliantly pulls off the juxtaposing of contrasting moods (ie -paranoia, deceit, humor and bloodshed) very impressively in this drama and has the dialogue overflowing with edgy wit and acidulous arias of imprecation from start to finish. 

Plus the top notch acting by a top notch cast which featured a very loathsome yet lovable villain played by Jack Nicholas didn't hurt this movie either. Leonardo Di Caprio and Mark Wahlberg also added terrific performances which kept the movie intriguing and enjoyable throughout. Set in the mean streets of gritty downtown Boston also added a cultural and flavorful vibe to the whole story telling atmosphere of the film.

To sum it up, The Departed honestly had me at the edge of my seat wondering what would happen next from start to finish, which I can't say many movies I have watched in my lifetime had ever made me do. For this and the myriad of other reasons above I give this movie a perfect 10.","2da55ed5-283a-45d6-9033-e598940bd891",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-01-22","","RT","901362081"
