4.5,"Martin Scorsese really packs a punch with this one.  The story is excellent, and the acting is even better!  I believe not many roles are made for Jack Nicholson (for better or for worse), but this film is different.  I'm a real critic when it comes to Nicholson, but this film really softened me up to him.  Above all, Nicholson was the man who shined here.  Nevertheless, props to Leonardo Dicaprio, who always pleases.  Yet the one thing that stuck in my mind the most about this film was the powerful ending, nay, the whole last-fifteen minute wrap-up, if you will.  It doesn't get better than Scorsese's way of letting you know it's time to un-stick your ass-cheeks from your seat in the theater.","1a57f0aa-4cd9-4c4d-b0a3-2abbbac8816f",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2010-01-24","","RT","901367459"
4.5,"This movie should rate as an all-time classic. Great story (albeit borrowed), great cast. There's not a weak performance to be found. Mark Wahlberg is delightfully foul. Leo DiCaprio is good, but Matt Damon is better.","52f3c4a3-dc85-41e3-badf-a3d53015fe38",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2010-01-24","","RT","818448407"
5.0,"Martin Scorsese's complex, powerfully stylishly crime epic which concerns a notoriously ruthless Irish crime boss named Frank Costello, played to perfection by Jack Nicholson in a vibrant performance who raises and nurtures Colin Sullivan, played by Matt Damon in a superlative turn; a young street-smart neighborhood kid who Costello successfully plants as his mole inside the Boston State Police, Sullivan now has been assigned to capture his mentor Costello. Leonardo DiCaprio delivers a magnificent performance as Billy Costigan who is trying live down his shaky family history by making a name for himself by joining the State Police undercover unit, he also has been sent to work undercover to capture Costello by his superiors Captain Queenan, played superbly by Martin Sheen and Sergeant Dignam, played brilliantly by Mark Wahlberg in an Oscar nominated performance. The tension really mounts as a game of cat and mouse ensues between Damon and DiCaprio's characters as they both try to discover each other's identity. Dynamite Oscar winning direction by Martin Scorsese with rich characterizations by a sterling cast that includes compelling performances by Alec Baldwin, Vera Farmiga, Anthony Anderson, James Badge Dale and Mark Roiston, special kudos must go to Ray Winstone for his marvelous performance as Costello's  number one enforcer the murderous Mr. French. Extraordinary cinematography by Michael Ballhaus, razor-sharp editing by Thelma Schoonmaker and an excellent score by Howard Shore. One of the best crime dramas of the decade. Winner of  4 Academy Awards including Best Picture, Best Director: Martin Scorsese, Best Editing: Thelma Schoonmaker, Best Adapted Screenplay: William Monahan.  Highly Recommended.","abb9728b-7934-455d-810c-51419587eb97",False,True,False,False,5.0,"2010-01-24","","RT","884505555"
