5.0,"This film gives a perfect representation of the phrase ""Trust no one"" as The Departed keeps you on the edge of your seat racing back and forth between this characters wondering who is playing who and whether anyone in this brilliantly executed drama is worthy of redemption. Perhaps the most pivotal and entertaining piece of Scorsese's epic film is DiCaprio's William Costigan, who finds himself caught in a tail spin of lies and deceit as he tries to gain the trust of Nicholson's Frank Costello while trying, also, to bring him and his criminal empire tumbling down. Riveting story, brilliant acting, and a dynamic cast, Scorsese has dome it again.","d1f7b5c6-e59e-4f3b-b2b9-0cf354646f1b",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-02-12","","RT","901246051"
5.0,"Probably one of the best mobster movie of this generation.  Scorsese finally got the attention he deserved as a great director.  Great acting by the entire cast...yes even Mark Walhberg, probably the last time I can say that about him.  For those who see it the first time the ending is just insane in the membrane and for those who rewatch it they feel the seconds tick away knowing what is coming.  Well deserved winner for the Best Picture award!","80fe4c14-41f4-4fd7-9263-7d5b62e04abe",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-02-12","","RT","897545897"
3.0,"(First full viewing - 3/7/2011)","108d10db-d1e1-4122-8123-0ce1de501344",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2010-02-12","","RT","898375055"
4.5,"Scorsese's best since good fellas.

Jack Nicholson performed a flawless and age defying performance for his character the mob boss Costello (which was a perfect addition to the film) and, while its difficult to match such a brilliant performance both Leonardo Di Caprio and Matt Damon did just that.  Or at least they came close.  At times it seemed a bit strange for Leonardo Dicaprio to play a ""tough guy"" but he still pulled it off very well.
The group of actors to back up his leads was somewhat beyond belief.  Marc Walberg (awesome), Alec Baldwin (awesome), and Ray Winstone (awesome).

Now as awe inspiring as the acting was i think the real reason that this movie was as good as it was was because of the sheer level of energy Scorsese can use to make the film feel vibrantly alive.  Few people can get an audience hooked as quickly and completely as Scorsese has in ""The Departed"".
As and extra kick of goodness Scorsese has once again created a perfectly fitting and compelling soundtrack for the movie.  Few Directors can be recognized merely by their soundtracks as Scorsese is.

Scorsese has done all this and still he maintains a remake that is fairly true to the original but still obviously his own.

Simply put this was a movie with a great storyline, great acting, a great soundtrack, and great direction.
Those among you who have not seen this movie should and those that have seen it should see it again.

I loved this movie.  Great job Martin Scorsese.","77ff62a0-6aaa-4a5b-b929-912cac2ef946",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2010-02-12","","RT","901345205"
