5.0,"Zack Thomas

I had a lot of expectations coming into this movie, seeing the combination of a instant home run cast and a director who had proven himself time and time again. However, even my high expecations were shattered by The Departed. 

How anyone can look at this plot and see any fault in it is beyond me. Scorcese spins a web of deception, corruption, and hatred that kept me guessing at every turn. Every character in the plot evoked strong emotions not only in myself, but in the crowd around me. Every scene flows seemlessly into one another, and the different types of camera shots and lighting will impress even the most savvy of film enthusiasts. This film is a must see.","78c394da-fd4c-4ce4-a48d-f534643100a5",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-02-17","","RT","901379293"
4.0,"Wonderfully made movie. Well acted. Well shot. Well written. Never dull. yet it all feels like Scorsese is really going through the motions with this. I mean how many crime oriented films has he done already? Still it has a great central role for Leonardo DiCaprio. And a surprisingly funny performance by Mark Walhberg. My real complaint is that Martin Scorsese finally won his oscar over for this movie. Yet he has directed so many better movies. And Jack Nicholson really seems to be going through the motions as well. but it all comes to a nail biting halt in the last 40 minutes. That makes up for the overrated nature of the movie every time I watch it.","70c6f640-b70c-49a5-b3a7-a543deb60311",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2010-02-17","","RT","860285368"
