3.5,"It was good, but it wasn't the masterpiece I thought it might be. Although I don't have a whole lot of experience with Scorsese films, this felt somewhat underwhelming. I think that while the acting was pretty damn good, Jack Nicholson being one of the best villain-actors ever committed to celluloid, the script fell short, and the characters, with the exception of Costello (again, Jack Nicholson FTW), didn't exactly leave a lasting impression. It felt as though they were depending much more heavily on star power than good screenwriting and compelling characterization. A valiant effort though.","95ec5929-6a76-496b-9c70-5f64e0560e64",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2010-03-03","","RT","886815289"
