4.5,"Martin Scorsese has been making consistently good films since the 70's and this is the one he finally got his long overdue Oscar award for and his best film since Goodfellas.
He's back to what he does best, in dealing with organised crime and corruption and brings a top notch cast with him. DiCaprio is brilliantly on edge as an undercover cop infiltrating the gang of crime lord Frank Costello, played once again with danger and unpredictability by the excellent, one and only Jack Nicholson. Meanwhile, Matt Damon, is working for Nicholson and trying to expose the mole in the gang while working for the police. The film is a cat and mouse race against time in who will be exposed first and Scorsese keeps the tension running easily over a couple of hours. A brilliant supporting cast also in, Alec Baldwin, Martin Sheen, Ray Winstone and Mark Whalberg. The only reason I don't give it 5 stars is because it's not an original idea, but a remake of the Japanese film ""Infernal Affairs"". Nonetheless, its still a cracking film. ****1/2. Mark.","5d3491b7-b158-4ead-9ac0-059eee62a6c0",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2010-03-18","","RT","889275587"
