4.5,"Directors come in many different shapes and sizes and Scorsese ,though small (bless him) makes up for his height in some of the most critically acclaimed movies since that of Hitchcock. With THE DEPARTED Scorsese returns back to his roots of creating gangster crime epics and The Departed in a sense is the GOODFELLAS of the 20000's (except this wasn't robbed at the Oscars) it is that good and Scorsese adds to this present by throwing in big stars Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon and Jack ""the animal"" Nicholson. The story is one of the most tense and gripping I have witnessed in a long time and though based on foreign film INFERNAL AFFAIRS the writers have managed to adapt the story to shape and fit US life in Bostan. The Departed is famous for winning a tone of Academy awards in 2006 but I have to say that it is an outrage that Jack Nicholson was snubbed for best supporting actor. He is what the entire film relies on, a dark, foul old man with the crudest sense of humour sinse a group of rebelious teenage boys how could you not nominate good old Jack? All the performances in this movie are superb however I do feel that Leo's Billy Costigan was somewhat outshone by all of the other great names in the movie that we lose focus on the main character. Still, there's little fault in it. Overall THE DEPARTED should be added onto the list of Scorsese classics like RAGING BULL, GOODFELLAS, THE KING OF COMEDY, MEAN STREETS, TAXI DRIVER, THE LAST TEMPTATION OF CHRIST, GANGS OF NEW YORK.....................the list is endless.","75acf598-1c2d-44d1-b3d4-33a67a3d5de5",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2010-03-21","","RT","901393806"
