5.0,"So if you haven't noticed, I don't do a synopsis when reviewing the movies I talk about. The reason for this is there is a perfectly good one posted right above where you read this on Flixster's site so it would be redundant, I just get to why I do or don't like a movie. Hokay, so. Martin Scorsese has the gangster genre on lockdown, I just want to put that out there. The Departed is without a doubt one of the finest gangster movies I've seen since....well, Gangs of New York maybe? I know Gangs isn't technically a ""gangster"" movie but if I don't qualify it, I'm going back to Goodfellas. Noticing a trend here? Yeah, every movie I've listed is a Scorsese movie, that's how amazing this man is at making gangster movies. Now, all of the TOP NOTCH casting aside, the film is masterfully shot and written and even though you know the angles of all of the main characters right off the bat for the most part, the film still keeps you engaged and in suspense the entire time. For a long time, I did not like Leonardo DiCaprio. I think it was because when I was growing up, he was my generation's teen idol and all the girls left puddles behind after sitting in on a movie he made. My opinion of him has softened quite a bit now, he was amazing in What's Eating Gilbert Grape, Gangs of New York and this movie. Matt Damon, as usual turns out a great performance as a long time gang boss underling turned not-so-honest cop, and Jack Nicholson plays himself and steals his scenes, as he is wont to do. I can't really find a flaw with this film other than not seeing more of Vera Farmiga as Damon's girlfriend, DiCaprio's shrink/lover, sweet Jesus she was smokin hot in this movie...but I guess that's just me. Anyway, see this if you haven't, if you don't like it I may think less of you as a person.","02e35b48-c2f2-4ace-b743-58f9f5f76bf7",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-04-22","","RT","817569367"
5.0,"I gotta be honest, I'm not the hugest Martin Scorcese fan--some of his films are not my favorites. But I think him and Leo D. make an awesome team...judging from their track record together, especially this one and Shutter Island. All of that aside, I have to say The Shawshank Redemption is my absolutely favorite movie of all time--and this is second. I think I watch this movie at least once a month. you really feel tension in the air, the feeling of dread that not everyone bad will be taken down and not everyone good will come out on top. you want to punch Matt Damon in the face for being a rat and screwing Costigan in the end, and you can feel Leo DiCaprio's frustration that he is stuck in the middle...trying to help the cops, and trying not to let the mob he is infiltrating come down. this movie is absolutely, above all else, about loyalty. the elevator scene was a shocker--dissapointing, but it was somehow done justice with the very last scene in the movie. I don't feel sympathy for the woman who the two main characters fell for--but she made up for it in the end. I have never seen ""Infernal Affairs"" but this is enough for me. AWESOME","078cc108-a9a4-4e53-a761-9aed2ee42880",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-04-22","","RT","901312632"
