4.5,"Another great movie from Martin Scorsese. This movie took me two viewings to understand the structure of the movie, because what we see is a mix between a spy movie and a gangster movie.

The movie is set in Boston and it follows the war between the Massachusetts State Police and the Irish mob. Each of the camps decides to send an informant to spy the other. The police's informant is Billy Costigan, played by Leonardo DiCaprio. The mob's informant is Collin Sullivan, played by Matt Damon. The boss of the Irish mob is played by Jack Nicholson, and in the police department we have Martin Sheen, Mark Wahlberg, Alec Baldwin and Vera Farmiga.

Every actor in this movie delivers a great performance. Leonardo DiCaprio and Matt Damon ""the pretty faces"" aren't here to stay around, smile and wink at the camera, they're acting and they give really strong performances. Jack Nicholson, who's always been good, gives his second craziest performance after the Joker in Batman. Mark Wahlberg is excellent, his character has one the pottiest mouth in movie history.

Martin Scorsese's a master at telling stories like this. He knows how to make them compelling by focusing on the characters, building up a climax and create a real sense of tension. He also knows how to deal with many characters, by giving everyone enough screen time so that you can know who is who, what's his mission etc.

The soundtrack is fantastic, the cinematography is beautiful, this movie is in my opinion Scorsese's latest masterpiece, he earned his Oscar for more than two decades and know he finally got it. Congratulations Marty.

The Departed is one the best movies of the past decade, see it now.","3dba9f8b-5766-433d-a5df-0693ef5ea06c",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2010-04-29","","RT","904358620"
