4.0,"Excellent execution of a modern gangster film. Scorsese effectively uses the actors and settings available to him with a great sense of timing. Overall, the movie still lacks consistent suspense or plot development forming a masterpiece to fans of the genre but just another drama to all others. This style is probably not an accident, it is Scorsese after all, but it leaves the average film connoisseur questioning. Although, a great piece, The Departed fails to excite in the typical manner.","2ed4ace6-a6b8-47a5-ab9e-f232bb2cee48",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2010-05-05","","RT","901388034"
4.5,"well, I'm coming down to the end of it. only 3 Best Picture winners left to review after this one. you know, I rather liked Scorsese's The Departed the second remake to win Best Picture. I'm really glad that he finally got his due and the Academy finally handed him an Oscar. (I mean look at his career, Raging Bull, Taxi Driver and Goodfellas just to name a few). now onto the movie itself. I really liked it. there are very few actors who deliver an amazing performance every time. well, Jack Nicholson just happens to be one of those actors. he really did a great job as the mob boss Frank Costello. I feel that this film was littered with amazing performances: Matt Damon, Leonardo DeCaprio (he's normal Scorsese now isn't he?), Mark Whalberg, Martin Sheen, Vera Farmiga, Jack Nicholson, Ray Winstone, and Alec Bladwin all give fantastic performances. notice how long that list was?  Scorsese proves with this one that he can do whatever kind of movie he wants and make it fantastic. I loved the plot. I loved the screenplay. I loved most things about this movie. it wasn't perfect. but few films are. Final Verdict: Right on. I fell that Scorsese should have won LONG before this but I'm glad he won now. despite heavy competition from Little Miss Sunshine, The Queen, and Letters From Iwo Jima, I fell that this film deserved the win.

TRIVIA TIME: 1. A possible reason why Leonardo DiCaprio did not receive an Oscar nomination for his performance in this movie was because the Warner Bros. Studios initially did not want to favor DiCaprio over his co-stars and place him in the leading actor category. The studio favored DiCaprio's leading performance in Blood Diamond (2006) (which eventually got him a nomination). DiCaprio himself refused to campaign against his male co-stars in the supporting actor category, so Warner bought no supporting actor ads for DiCaprio, and he did not receive a nomination. 

2. The only remake of a foreign film to win an Academy Award for Best Picture.","f02f5471-2a3c-43f2-88ff-84829c8b78aa",False,True,False,False,4.5,"2010-05-06","","RT","901242064"
4.5,"Excellent movie with solid acting all-around, nobody in particular standing out above the rest because they all do equally and that's what makes most of the film. What makes the rest is the incessant suspense, even after I watched this movie twice on my third viewing I was still on the edge of my seat. Nonetheless, once you've seen it first you'll know the ending--and oh how it ranks up there with the top 3 best endings of all time. IMO at least. Anyhow, Scorsese directs impeccably, though I could've done without the shared love interest. But whatever. All I can do now is anticipate the sequel, which has been confirmed, which Mark Wahlberg has stated his avidity to be involved in. Kudos.","91aa23ca-d053-4994-8ecc-fd5fd58f5040",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2010-05-06","","RT","808319215"
5.0,"This is one of Martin Scorsese's best motion pictures since his all-round and all-time gangster classic ""Goodfellas"", with a sucker-punch performances of an all-star cast that inlcudes Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, Jack Nicholson, Martin Sheen, Vera Farmiga, Ray Winstone, Alec Baldwin, Anthony Anderson and (nominated for a 2006 Oscar for his Sucker-Punch Performance of his Career *Make Fanfare music*) Mark Wahlberg.  The movie takes place in South Boston, where the state police force is waging war on organized crime, young undercover cop Billy Costigan is assigned to infiltrate the mob syndicate run by gangland chief Costello. While Billy is quickly gaining Costello's confidence, Colin Sullivan, a hardened young criminal who has infiltrated the police department as an informer for the syndicate, is rising to a position of power in the Special Investigation Unit. Each man becomes deeply consumed by his double life, gathering information about the plans and counter-plans of the operations he has penetrated. But when it becomes clear to both the gangsters and the police that there's a mole in their midst, Billy and Colin are suddenly in danger of being caught and exposed to the enemy--and each must race to uncover the identity of the other man in time to save himself.","9d3416f5-e3e6-495f-bea3-6cbc70caec39",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-05-06","","RT","889269132"
