5.0,"From the first time I saw this, I was about 13. I didn't completely grasp it, the jokes, the humor, or the story all together. All I knew is that someone (Leonardo De Caprio) was a good guy pretending to be a bad guy and someone else (Matt Damon) was a bad guy pretending to be a good guy. By the time the movie reached its end, I was absolutely blown away. It's kind of like the first time you see Star Wars. The plot is the last thing that you can remember, all that matters is that what you just saw was amazing and incredible to cinema. Eventually, I re-watched this movie when it came out on DVD. That night, I remembered why this was such a great movie, and I ended up watching the very next night again. Not once was I bored and annoyed with it. This entire movie is perfection, an epic crime classic. Their is a balance between violence, gripping plot twists, character development, and a sense of humor. All of the actors do incredibly well. Matt Damon, Mark Wahlberg, Leonardo De Caprio, Ray Winstone, Jack Nicholson, Martin Sheen, Alec Baldwin, and Vera Farmiga are all at the top of their game. They make the characters very believable. All the way through the movie you will be gripped by the 2 hours and 30 minutes of crime and punishment. The entire movie is a game of cat and mouse with an ending for the books that will literally leave you speechless.","c4785478-a5e9-450a-b445-bed11c24ef10",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-05-21","","RT","901394376"
