5.0,"The Departed still proves that director Martin Scorsese makes a landmark film every decade since the 1970s. It finally got him his well-deserved Best Director Oscar (ABOUT TIME!!!),too. The Departed is a remake of the film Infernal Affairs and it's assembled by an amazing ensemble cast including Leonardo Dicaprio,Matt Damon,Jack Nicholson,Mark Wahlberg,Martin Sheen,Alec Baldwin,and Ray Winstone. The film is set in Boston where mob boss Frank Costello (Jack Nicholson) has put one of his own men Colin Sullivan (Matt Damon),into the police department as a mole. However,young rookie cop Billy Costigan (Leonardo Dicaprio) has been ordered by the department to infiltrate the mob in undercover fashion. Soon,things start to take a turn and the two officers both suspect a ""rat"" in the department for Costello's mob. 

One of the best things about The Departed has to be the exceptional acting given by the whole cast. Everyone just turns in great performances no matter how small or big their role is. The three leads are probably the best in the performances but if there was a standout,it would be Mark Wahlberg. He doesn't have a lot of screen time compared to most of the other actors,but his character grabs you from the first scene he's in and just leaves you in awe at the end. I still believe that Leonardo Dicaprio should have gotten a second Best Actor nomination (other was for Blood Diamond) for the Oscars three years ago because he has definitely shown that he can turn in a rich and powerful performance in nearly every movie he's starred in. Matt Damon is just pure slime as Colin Sullivan and he really intrigued me as the secondary villain of the film. Jack Nicholson does fantastic as Costello as he plays an EVIL mob boss. In addition,his character is so great because Nicholson improvised nearly all of his lines.

The action is pure Scorsese style violence as blood spurts big time when someone is shot or beaten. It's edited brilliantly by Thelma Schoonmaker and it keeps you on the edge of your seat until the credits start to roll.

The Departed is without a doubt Scorsese's best masterpiece since Goodfellas. Like all of his other films,The Departed grabs you from the very beginning and takes you on a journey that never lets go until the end. A true masterpiece of this decade,go see The Departed right now!!!","bfab1916-6dbd-47fd-b4f4-8ebbcf6721a8",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-05-25","","RT","901324010"
