5.0,"Another masterpiece from director Martin Scorsese.  It's one more American crime classic to add to his legedary resume.  The Departed is a spectacular and sensational crime epic that is up to par with Goodfellas and State Of Grace.  The best film of 2006 by far, it's violent, gritty, raw, hardcore and funny as hell.  A crime thriller cannot get any better, from the acting to the story, it's completely flawless.  Scorsese is the king of manufacturing gangster and mafia based films, from Mean Streets to Goodfellas and Casino, he can't miss.  The Departed is no different, it's a raw and tense look at mafia life on the streets of Boston.  
         The Boston Police Department and the Massachusetts state police have waged an all out war on organized crime in the city.  From undercover officers to rats in both the department and the outfit, both sides play a cat and mouse catch me if you can game with one another.  
         The cast is truly star studded, this cast couldn't get any better.  It features masterful performances by all involved, Jack Nicholson, Matt Damon, and Leonardo DiCaprio are show stoppers in this film, they shine.  Also featuring appearances by Martin Sheen, Mark Wahlberg, Ray Winstone, Vera Farmiga, and Alec Baldwin.  This movie is a breathtaking epic that engages and grabs with a wicked punch of tense and action packed entertainment.  From the shootouts to the clever and snappy dialogue, The Departed shouldn't be missed.  An instant Classic.","5b6c5b5f-633b-42d2-8f31-2a2e1fdfde1e",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-08-08","","RT","901889122"
