2.5,"It is still baffling why this film won Best Picture Oscar in its year and Best Director for Martin Scorsese.

This is a remake of the much better executed and better written Hong Kong thriller, ""Infernal Affairs"".  At times, Hollywood runs out of original ideas.  They will take a little known foreign film, load it with big name stars and a well-known director then repackage it.  Itâs happened before with ""Vanilla Sky"", which is a remake of ""Abre Los Ojos"".  Both films have Penelope Cruz playing the same character but adding Tom Cruise as the draw for the remake.  It didnât work then and sadly, the same mistake is made here.

Iâll bet that Academy members who voted for this have never even seen the original.  They awarded Martin Scorsese not because this is a great motion picture but rather for his body of work and failing to do so in 1981 for ""Raging Bull"" when he should have won instead of Robert Redford for ""Ordinary People"".

As I sat through ""The Departed"", I was shaking my head the entire time and asking, why?  Hong Kong usually makes knock offs of first rate products.  But the tables have turned.  ""The Departed"" plays second rate to the original it was based on.  It is a well-financed knock off as knock offs go only this time it is Hollywood doing the deed.  This remake does not do the original justice since there is no need for it to begin with.  Go see ""Infernal Affairs"" instead.  It is a much more satisfying film.","7aa8c3b1-ce6c-4e05-a743-9a1e8388779c",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2010-08-10","","RT","893365577"
