3.0,"Pretty much a shambles of a film and it's crazy that Scorsese won his Oscar for this but it's enjoyable in patches as long as you don't think too much.  DiCaprio is the stand-out by a country mile playing the only character with any semblance of depth, and the only one without a truly ridiculous accent - for this film has the worst attempts at accents I've ever heard in a move.  Ray Winstone thankfully doesn't speak beyond about the half-way point.  The mass of heavyweight names gives the film a pedigree that it doesn't come close to living up to and makes it even more disappointing that the film is so very average.  Take out everyone bar DiCaprio and Sheen, fill the other roles with lesser names, remove most of the dreadful dialogue and it would have been a very fine crime caper.  Instead it's an fun bit of silliness but incredibly over-rated.","8d26af3c-de01-4787-905a-8ab592590f27",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2010-08-13","","RT","792588664"
