4.5,"A very impressive film that takes the audience on a twisting, weaving rollarcoaster of an experience guided by the capable hands of either Matt Damon or Leo DiCaprio. The two are both undercover, one a criminal in the police force, the other a cop in the underworld and the plot slips and slides its way towards them revealing the extent of their deception. Scorsese has done a fantastic job of creating a genuine thriller, I was on the edge of my seat for most of this film and completely immersed and engaged in the ever more complex plot. The two leads are very strong performers in their own right and though not sharing a great deal of screen time keep the action flowing brilliantly with Leo demonstrating why he is one of the best actors of his generation- Jack Nicholson (one of the best actors of his generation) plays the main mafia bad guy with relish, clearly enjoying himself and having a great deal of fun with the character. This film continues to twist and twirl all the way to the end before the film ties itself up nice and neatly with the dramatic equivalent of concrete shoes. Don't expect much in the way of humour, romance or musical numbers - but if you like Scorsese and his dark gangster thrillers - this might just be your cup of tea.","b12c93f3-f2a2-4879-af02-9598f6ab9ad4",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2010-09-14","","RT","783805763"
