5.0,"A symphony of flawless acting, gritty writing and direction of a master.  The Departed is about two cops in Massachusetts (Leonardo DiCaprio and Matt Damon), one working deep undercover for a crime boss (Jack Nicholson), but still with his loyalties with the police, and the other the opposite, with his loyalties to the same crime boss, but he has infiltrated the precinct by being a very respectable police officer.  When it comes out that both parties have a rat in the house, both try to discover the identity of the other.  I love the duality of this movie, with the only difference between the two cops being a few life decisions.  Jack Nicholson sets it up perfectly in the beginning, too, by saying, âwhen you're facing a loaded gun, what's the difference?â This is a movie that has balls.  It is such an intricate story and it never shies away from showing a blow to the ribs or a haymaker to the face.  I still havenât seen the original Chinese movie it is based on, Infernal Affairs, but it is pretty safe to say that this is one of the best remakes of all time.  Every performance is memorizing; Nicholson, Damon and Mark Wahlberg all give performances that are nothing short of amazing, but Leonardo DiCaprio, oh MAN, is he good here.  I loved him in Titanic, but this is the movie that made me really start taking him seriously as an actor.  This is a crime masterpiece of epic proportions that should be seen by all.","5bfb6923-e850-4f9d-bbcb-f48ba70f0e57",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-09-20","","RT","782214838"
