5.0,"THE DEPARTED This is the kind of movie you go into knowing Jack Nicholson can act, and coming out realising, that you had no idea how well he actually could. For a long time Mr Nicholson has seemed to be content in doing an impersonation of what we think he is, only in a couple of other instances( As Good As It Gets, About Schmidt) has he been able to break out of the mold. Here he doesn't break out as much as he chews his way out. It's the story of two cops( Dicapio, Damon) from south Phillidelphia one who is a mole for the police working in Crime Kingpin Frank Costella ( Jack ) The other an employee of Costella who has worked his way into a trusted position in the FBI. Both sides find out there is a leak in their outfits and it's a race to find the other guy first. I gushed over Nicholson earlier and it really is his film, but honestly everyoe including Scorsese has stepped up there game for this movie. I don't know if this will end up being the best film of the year, but I can see it being in my top 5. ( A + )","8b1075b6-a463-47f0-88d4-a278ab288ad2",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-09-22","","RT","867343050"
5.0,"A brilliant and violent Crime Drama with Terrific performances by Matt Damon, Leonardo DiCaprio, Mark Wahlberg, and Jack Nicholson.","41d5a5dc-3b60-4638-bea0-7e4ab72fedc3",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2010-09-23","","RT","896455313"
4.5,"""All due respect Mr. Costello, school is out.""

To take down South Boston's Irish Mafia, the police send in one of their own to infiltrate the underworld, not realizing the syndicate has got a mole of their own within the police force.

Though i'v not seen the original Hong Kong picture, Infernal Affairs, this english remake from legendary director Martin Scorsese leaves nothing to be desired. You name an aspect of filmmaking and there isn't a one that The Departed doesn't deliver (beside maybe digital effects, which is a good thing). The acting is fantastic, the cinematography is sublime, Martin Scorsese brought his A game, the script is hilarious and very witty, it is simply the best gangster film since Goodfellas.

As I viewed the film I gradually started feeling like i was dwelling deeper and deeper into some kind of rabbit hole from wonderland (except here it's gangland), as the two moles get closer and closer to the upper hierarchy of the establishments they are infiltrating.  The constant intertwining of characters from both sides of the law ( and i don't mean just the moles either) make for one hell of a finale.

Martin Scorsese has crafted a new kind of gangster picture, one that makes me desperately want to view the Hong Kong original, not because The departed failed to deliver on it's potential, but because it did so in spades.","d19c9e9c-e458-46e7-a665-7ed0f9461d3c",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2010-09-23","","RT","905385592"
