3.0,"I'm being harsh on this one because the original Infernal Affairs is just so much better.  Jack Nicholson was great, but was just the wrong character for this movie.  Also, I've never been the biggest fan of Scorsese.  He's always so gratuitous, and here too he falls back on his standard way of ending a movie.  He doesn't really know where to go with it, so he just kills everybody and that pretty much ends a story now doesn't it?  The suspense cat & mouse game of the original film just isn't here as much, and the entire quandry we're left with as viewers is obliterated because Scorsese just KILLS EVERYONE OFF!  The whole POINT of this story is to leave us with the question of whether Matt Damon's character has really become a righteous policeman or not.  But then WHO CARES now after he, like everyone else in this movie, gets shot in the face and has their brains splattered over everything. :/","af6f6f11-27bc-4a2f-b5c8-6867d9988e63",False,False,False,False,3.0,"2010-10-25","","RT","786444882"
