4.5,"Scorsese soars with this gangster epic, receiving a well deserved Oscar which many considered to be a life-time achievement award. A film that adapted the tale of the Hong Kong thriller Infernal Affairs which I have not seen and hence I shall not compare. A straightforward story of moles in both the police department and gang, this gangster epic shines for a few reasons. Firstly Cinematography and editing: As I watched this, I always felt that the urgency of the actors can be seen. This is only because of whizzing camera work as well as the fast cuts. Secondly, Dialogue: There is not a moment where one feels that the dialogue is corny or derivative which makes it really realistic and actually funny. Finally the cast: Here is a movie where there is not one bad actor.Obviously the shining star is Leonardo Dicaprio, but the others compliment his performance and he returns the favour, making you feel the gritty realism of the Irish mob.","f034e1f8-16e1-41fd-9f91-e4a8a1b348a9",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2010-10-29","","RT","875859044"
