4.0,"Though the film is undeniably great, it is just not worth it's hype. On the negatives are performances of Matt Damon and Leonardo DiCaprio. DiCaprio's young boyish face betrays him completely and we are left with only his fist punching and his constant use of 'fucks' to show some tension. Jack Nicholson is brilliant in some parts, but in the others his useless grinning and unwanted smiling makes him look like a joker rather than a mobster. On the plus is Wahlberg, and his performance lights up film. The tight script and some stylish dialogue delivery courtesy Mr.Nicholson are also among the highlights.The constant use 'fucks' in the most unprofessional manner is yet another problem. Reservoir fuckin' Dogs this is not. So this does not even come close to Scorsese's best or say even Casino is better than this.","3516e816-74ce-4524-80cd-744100bad298",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2010-11-01","Adwait K","RT","4d6bdf5e-a38a-4849-aac3-a0885482308c"
