4.5,"Director Martin Scorsese really outdoes himself in this gangster-themed crime film. The film boasts an all-star cast with lead roles like Jack Nicholson, Matt Damon, Leonardo DiCaprio, and Mark Wahlberg. Damon and DiCaprio play paralleling roles, Damon playing Colin Sullivan, a mole inside the Massachusetts State Police mentored by Irish mobster Frank Costello (Nicholson), and DiCaprio taking a role as agent Billy Costigan, who goes undercover and is taken under Costello's wing. The bulk of the film takes place with Costigan and Sullivan slowly learning of each other's position, their paths crossing along the way, which includes sharing a similar love interest in the form of psychiatrist Madolyn Maddon, who is played by Vera Farmiga. As events unfold and the two meet, the story comes to a climactic end filled with unexpected twists.
	The film utilizes Boston as its setting, which seems accurate and depicted well. The cast is also top-notch, but it would have been nice to see some of the supporting characters fleshed out a little more. There are few who will not be able to appreciate this film because even if the theme is not your cup of tea, it is hard to ignore each actor's commitment to their role. If there is one thing The Departed can offer is a rich and interesting story, that will have you intrigued and entertained every step of the way.","812f80e4-3d44-4075-8578-bfcb6ca9f873",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2010-11-01","","RT","905853130"
