2.5,"If you don't know where this movie went wrong, then I'm guessing you're a die-hard Scorsese apologist and/or you never saw Infernal Affairs, which is a much better film even though it was directed by a man who was previously known as a hack (the HK equivalent of Michael Bay). A cat and mouse thriller lacking in tension is a big problem. Just watch the warehouse drug deal scene in IA and compare it to this one. Infernal Affairs also had flaws, but instead of correcting them, Scorsese made most of them worse (2 weak female characters become one weak female character coincidentally involved with both men). Maybe Marty SHOULD have watched the original film instead of depending on William Monahan's flawed screenplay. Jack Nicholson's clownish performance didn't help things and the lame Hollywood ending is just too easy and tidy and the exact opposite of the point of the original film. It's sad that THIS ends up being the film Scorsese gets the Oscar for instead of something more well-made like Goodfellas.","cf984f99-ef45-4a99-8b0b-ab386bee129a",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2010-11-12","","RT","905898584"
