4.0,"The Departed is renowned for being the film that finally gained Martin Scorsese his more than deserved Best Director Oscar. Personally, I think the Departed is far from Scorsese's best, but a good film nonetheless. I've not seen Infernal Affairs... well not yet at least. What I liked about the Departed most was the casting. Each actor in the film, from DiCaprio and Damon to Nicholson and Wahlberg and even Farmiga is fantastic. I greatly enjoyed the concept, and the film was never boring. What I disliked, and held the film back mostly for me was a lack of depth for the characters. Damon plays a Criminal undercover as an FBI agent, and DiCaprio the other way around. Each character is nothing more than the basic statement I've just provided them, and this doesn't change until the end of the film. I've heard people discuss their disappointment with the ending. I for one liked the ending. Good film, just a tad over-rated.","0394982e-406f-42aa-9f83-2d4587fcc989",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2010-11-13","","RT","901295181"
