3.0,"A lot of people have called ""The Departed"" a masterpiece, and potentially on par with his greatest work, the 1990 film ""Goodfellas"". It's not the home run ""Goodfellas"", but I'll call it a solid ground-rule double. The movie follows the cat-and-mouse game engineered by two moles (DiCaprio and Damon); the former infiltrating the notorious Irish mob in Boston (sporting a menacing Jack Nicholson as their leader) and the latter placed in the Boston police department by the aforementioned mob. This is actually an Americanized version of the 2002 Hong Kong film ""Infernal Affairs"" and exemplifies a case where the original foreign picture gets the better of the remake. How? In a sentence, Scorsese overdoes it here. The dialogue, while not totally boring, still seems as if it's been pieced together from unused portions from his previous efforts. As a consequence, some of the line readings come off as hokey, but that's not a shot at the actors - in fact, the cast is uniformly strong from top to bottom, as is usually the case with a Scorsese release. Moreover, the pace builds in an anti-climactic fashion; the final act drags noticeably when it should be at its most energetic. However, perhaps this is all a product of Scorsese's reputation  - once you've tasted near-perfection, as an audience, you might not be willing to accept much less. Therefore, I'll stick with my ground-rule double analogy: it's a solid base hit of entertainment, but somehow manages to skip over the wall based on the past triumphs of its director and not on its own merits.","e2c14ab2-7f87-4c4b-9771-6eca91a310de",False,True,False,False,3.0,"2011-04-03","","RT","812968865"
5.0,"Leo is this generations Marlon Brando and this was his Godfather. It will never reach the iconic status of the classic but the nuances of his performance are bested in this genre perhaps only by Brando and Pacino in what were perhaps the best performances in cinema history.","ee123679-b99b-4b17-bd9b-3d19df88553b",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2011-04-04","robbie n","RT","cb8a3ac5-8049-4129-9174-68829f51a9c6"
