5.0,"One of the greatest crime thrillers of all time, and possibly the best one of the decade, The Departed is truly an interesting one. In Boston, the Boston Police Department has planted a mole ( spy ) inside of notorious mobster Frank Costello's (Jack Nicholson) mob to get info on him so he can be arrested. At the same time, Costello has planted a mole inside of the police department so can easily avoid arrest. The Police's mole, Billy Costigan (Leonardo DiCaprio) is a young man who just wants to have a fresh start, and Colin Sullivan (Matt Damon) is a young man who was corrupted at a young age by Costello. Now, with The Departed, it has an odd but amazing technique in which you feel great suspense without any really intense action going on at the time. The complexity of this film makes it sometimes hard to follow, but if you really pay attention, the complexity all comes together. With fantastic performances from Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, Jack Nicholson, and for at the time newcomer Mark Wahlberg, The Departed is truly one of Martin Scorsese's best films since Goodfellas, Taxi Driver, and Raging Bull. Definitely see this movie. 5/5 Stars","2afe9a55-dbde-4b69-9fa6-66f33a37994c",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2011-04-19","","RT","906747392"
