5.0,"Classified: Perfectly Fresh

Defining Moment: So many ... But for me the ending scene between Mark Wahlberg and Matt Damon, it just brings so much closure. 

Highs: 
Great story that has been told by a master, brilliant believable acting, brutal themes told with an emotional attachment. This is one of Jack Nicholson's best performances in a long time and Leonardo Dicaprio is just amazing, but with that said it is an amazing ensemble of actors but you don't come away thinking one out-shined the other you feel that all worked together to create this amazing story. 

Lows:
I personally can't find fault with this film, I tried to find things that were annoying, overbearing or poorly done but the reality is I couldn't. Would love to hear of some peoples opinions if they differ. 

H&L Conclusion:
One of my favourite movies of all time! Martin Scorsese is amazing. This interweaving story leaves us the audience questioning all the characters motives and feeling left empty as their are no winners in this film.

