4.0,"To rate The Departed good or bad by comparing to Infernal Affairs would be stupid. A film is not automatically bad if its not as good as a great film and vice versa. 

The complaint of The Departed copied too much from the original shouldn't be an issue. Why fix something if it isn't broken? The whole point of the remake was to push the story to a wider audience. So if something was good in the original, keep it and show it to the new audience.

All that being said, The Departed is a good solid film. Personally (and I emphasise the word) I do feel its slightly weaker than the original. The minor differences and changes in The Departed has its good and bad point. Sadly the bad just out weights the good by a little bit. The biggest of the few was the ending and the character portrayed by Sheen and Damon, as they were a bit flat. It was also less tense and gripping as it was a little stretched at some scenes. However there were good points., I liked Wahlberg and Baldwin's character, although it was superfluous. DIcaprio was great as usual. Nicholson did a job that was so much better than the head boss of Infernal Affairs. 

To wrap things up I feel it was worthy of it's praise and viewers just need to relax and enjoy it.","fdc1c34a-44a7-4e48-b323-4d434d92cbae",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2011-05-11","","RT","151694325"
