5.0,"Featuring powerhouse performances from Leonardo Dicaprio and Mark Wahlberg (giving argubly the strongest performances of their careers) and equally great performances from Jack Nicholson, Matt Damon and Ray Winstone. Martin Scorsese pumps tension and energy throughout the whole film with the perfect pace and great amount of style. A brilliant, twisty, turny screenplay with fully realised themes and character. The Departed is a crime thriller masterpiece and one of the masters of cinema Martin Scorsese's very best films.","1811ac6a-20e8-488c-b93c-d119b0482ebe",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2011-06-23","","RT","906578448"
5.0,"Rookie cop Billy Costigan (Leonardo DiCaprio) grew up in crime. That makes him the perfect mole, the man on the inside of the mob run by boss Frank Costello (Jack Nicholson). It's his job to win Costello's trust and help his detective handlers (Mark Wahlberg and Martin Sheen) bring Costello down. Meanwhile, SIU officer Colin Sullivan (Matt Damon) has everyone's trust. No one suspects he's Costello's mole. See how these covert lives cross and collide at the ferocious core of the widely acclaimed The Departed. Martin Scorcese directs, guiding a cast for the ages in a visceral tale of crime and consequences. This is searing, can't-look-away filmmaking: like the eyes of a con - or a cop - with a gun.

There is no other word for this than amazing. Once again, Scorcese has delivered me a brilliant piece of cinema that deserves every single bit of good credit that it gets. The cast is absolutely brilliant with plenty of modern acting legends such as Damon, DiCapio and Wahlberg as well as one of the oldest legends left: Jack Nicholson himself. As you can guess from such a great cast, the acting in the film was as top notch as you can get. The direction, as with all of Scorsese's films I have yet seen, is pretty much perfect down to the last bit of scenery. It is hardly surprising such a great film won Best Picture, Best Director and various other awards from various award ceremonies.

The story itself is fashioned as a remake of Infernal Affairs but after this masterpiece; I don't see a reason to watch that. The story is not totally unique, because moles and police corruption is done all the time in the film industry but it is the best damn one of its type of seen. I cannot think of a single reason to not like this film. I was on the edge of my seat all the way through, wondering what would happen and who would die. The ending was crafted really well, leaving me with so many emotions that I wish every film could leave me with.

Overall, this is a film hard to criticise. The only regret I have is not having seen this pure awesomeness before now because it truly is just so good. The plot is long but flashes before your eyes like any good film. When the story is over, it leaves you wishing it wasn't. It's the kind of story you would like to keep going on and on and on and on until the day you die. A perfect cast, perfect direction and perfect story has made this easily one of the best films that ever came out in the noughties decade.","e3f5f173-f839-4bcd-ae5f-ef4e6c0c36d7",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2011-06-23","","RT","908108290"
