4.5,"So, having finally seen this movie in its entirety, I am extremely impressed. First off, the acting was phenomenal. Leonardo Di Caprio puts forth a very emotional performance, Matt Damon breathes life into his character, Jack Nicholson is just fantastic, and Mark Wahlberg stole the show in all of his scenes. The story was very well-written and intense all the way through, showing great elements of suspense among other things. The ending is crazy good, mainly just because it really doesn't hold back and has no mercy, which I love to see in a movie. Now, one complaint I have (not the only one, just a significant one) was the music. Many of the prominent musical choices were honestly, a bit loud and annoying (that Dropkick Murphys song is just obnoxious, I'm sorry). But beyond this, there are few things holding this film back from being a masterpiece. In my opinion, it isn't the greatest film of all time by any means. However, it is an extremely interesting, deep, and entertaining piece of work. I loved it.
