2.5,"The movie ""Face Off"" is a perfect example to demonstrate what you get and what you don't get from watching this movie. The huge difference between Face Off and The Departed is that Face Off had a point in the movie (at the end) when there was actually -a face off. You didn't know how it was going to end but you knew that whatever ride it took you through, it was going to be well worth it and something to talk about afterwards. 

The Departed, however, lacks this crucial point. After going through a whirl wind of suspense, deception, and deceit, you are left with an ending that leaves question of whether the movie was actually good. And the more you try to substitute the end with how good the rest of the movie was, the end inevitably keeps over powering your thoughts and leaves you feeling..wellâ?¦..robbed. It doesn't make since for a movie like that to not have an explosive end. The thing that really makes you upset (you realize I'm saying ""you"" instead of ""me"") is that, when you're watching the movie, you KNOW the ending is going to be good. You can hardly bear the weight. But that's just it. 

You're left thinking:
What was the point? 
What the heck was that movie about anyway!? 
I don't want to remember.

**********

Epic Fantasy Books
www.epicfantasybooks.com","0caf9d07-2c87-4dce-b037-fbe95d496710",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2011-09-01","","RT","893082996"
