5.0,"Anyone who doesn't see the depth of this movie is a film neophyte. The story goes far deeper than simple gangstering and crime drama. At its core it deals with themes of distrust in modern America, the achievement of the American Dream (and what that achievement can do to a person), and the moral ambiguity inherent in the real world. One only need consider the masterful blurring of archetypal characters (the hero/anti-hero, villain/anti-villain ones, in particular) to realize the genius of the story. One of the best contemporary films ever made.","55ac3944-cb76-4718-b5ed-f92e50bfc8da",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2011-11-07","","RT","901828394"
