5.0,"This is one of the best gangster movies ever made and it definitely is the best one of this century and decade. It also completes Scorsese's 4 decades of dominance with movies (70's being Taxi Driver, 80's being Raging Bull, 90's being Goodfellas and 00's being The Departed). Whether its gangster or any genre you know Scorsese will deliver, and this will leave fans chomping at the bit for another famous Scorsese gangster movie which could possibly be a sequel or prequel to this. His Oscar and golden globe wins are much deserved. A good movie movie keeps you thinking. But a excellent, perfect, or great movie like this makes the dopamine receptors in your head go insane (in a good way). It is impossible to hate this movie. This is the second Scorsese film that shows Leonardo DiCaprio as a more mature great actor. Dicaprio's golden globe nomination is much deserved. Then theres Matt Damon who again shows a sign of growing up much from his earlier films and he actually plays an antagonist for once which is actually tough to see but he does an amazing job. Jack Nicholson delivers as always, playing the main gangster and villain which any Nicholson fan can expect. His awards and nominations are much deserved as usual. Alec Baldwin and Martin Sheen both play great supporting roles and Mark Wahlberg deserved his wins and nominations. This is Wahlberg's best film and the one that got his career back on track. The Boston Irish type setting was pretty cool and Matt Damon plays that perfectly considering he is a real life Boston resident. Then the newcomers like Anthony Anderson (Transformers),  James Badge Dale (24, The Pacific, and Vera Farmiga (Up in the air, Source Code) all do a great job. The movie is about two recent trainees in the Massachusetts state police (Damon and DiCaprio). Sergeant Sullivan (Damon) grew up with and was raised by criminal gangster Frank Costello (Nicholson) and he now is Costello's mole in the state police. But as Costello's rise to power becomes greater the police send their own mole into Costello's gang, with William Costigan (Dicaprio). The scences towards the end are crazy and mind-twisting, with the ending being the best of all.","41719317-6549-4eec-a609-d1886e113749",False,True,False,False,5.0,"2011-11-24","","RT","906583143"
