5.0,"The Departed is my second favorite Martin Scorsese film (after Goodfellas) and is a fantastic crime film and one of the greatest  films of its time.  Whenever I see this work of art its hard to stop watching, I mean Scorsese has a passion with his films that truly make him original and great.  He gives a story that reels us into a web of crime, betrayals, and rats.  I love telling people th premise of this film, I mean its just one of those movies that is easy to explain to people and they get excited because it just sounds so great.  A film like this never comes out in theaters, I mean Scorsese's last real crime film was Casino (an incredible film) and so people were excited to see what he had cooked up next, and it ends up being one of the greatest crine films ever made.  This film explores both the modern day police and mobsters, and its shows both ends of the world of crime.  Leonardo DiCaprio is phenomenal in his role, I mean anyone who found his performance dull is just ridiculous.  DiCaorio is my favorite actor, and his films with Martin Scorsese are all fantastic if you ask me, just like his collaborations with Robert DeNiro.  Jack Nicholson plays one of the finest roles of his career, and that is saying a lot since he is one of the best actors of all time.  He is intenae and drags us into his life with so much anger and danger, I loved him.  Matt Damon is great as well, and watching him play two different people blows me away completely.  Mark Wahlberg really turned his career around here, I mean he hadn't given such a mighty performance since Boogie Nights, and he is just so great in this film.  What I really just love about this film is that they pull us in so much that it almost gets hard to stop watching, and the characters just let the walls close in on them tighter as the film goes on.  Martin Scorsese is the lord of crime films, I mean Francis Ford Coppola could've been too if he had not ruined his career in the 90's, but Scorsese has created many violent films like this and they all are masterpieces in my eyes.  He directs his films with so much passion with each character and with each scene filmed, and its what makes him my second or third favorite director.  The Departed is a genius and thrilling crime film with a perfect screenplay, perfect cast, and is just a perfect film that ends up being one of my favorite films of all-time.","c82424a7-2c14-4964-9af4-60e5d08be318",False,True,False,False,5.0,"2011-12-02","","RT","898931506"
5.0,"Martin Scorsese once again gave us another American classic.","9456418e-14ac-4d8b-8f47-e8a79f4a29ab",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2011-12-02","","RT","825904485"
