5.0,"I AM VERY IMPRESSED! I know I am way late in watching this movie but I wasn't watching much movies back in 2006. I think the acting was superb but DiCaprio stole the spotlight in my book. His character was so complex and he displayed all of the characters' sides to perfection! The end was surprising and sad. I was sad to see such great characters go and it seemed like DiCaprio's character only wanted to get out of his ""crime driven"" family only to be condemned to that corrupt life by association...but it definitely made the ""big picture"" very evident as far as Irish crime lords go. If DiCaprio, Damon and Nicholson's characters were just pawns, makes the ""king"" on the chessboard that much impressive and unattainable. The last image in the movie of the Massachusetts State House with a rat running on the ledge was perfect.","a0feadfd-682c-4686-9c8b-df731ba333a1",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2011-12-04","","RT","822070534"
