4.5,"Perhaps the best movie of this decade; some might think it is too much like GoodFellas, but the storyline is more riveting and it is much bloodier. Sure, it was in step with Infernal Affairs, the great Hong Kong film, but I loved how Scorsese tied the story of the Winter Hill Gang and James ""Whitey"" Bulger (Frank Costello) and his dealings with former FBI agent John Connelly (Colin Sullivan) into the film. This along with Mystic River and The Town showcased Boston really well. Excellent acting by Mark Wahlberg as the foul mouthed Sgt. Sean Dignam, an aspect which also separated the Departed from Infernal Affairs. Great music to boot and good win for Scorsese finally.","0e797d62-5a32-4b2b-bd6e-f6e3045060c6",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2012-02-12","","RT","836409280"
2.5,"I do like the film but it's nowhere near Scorcese at his best, indeed for much of the film you just feel he's retreading old territory.  Heavy on the Stones? - check, punch-ups in delicattesens - check...it all feels a bit 'Goodfellas' lite, then there's Winstone's accent...WOW.  Anyway, perhaps it's because I was such a fan of the Chinese original (and it really isn't a patch on that), but I just never really connect with it.  Nicholson feels like he's doing a bad De Niro impression and there are so many plot holes that when we get to the everyone gets shot conclusion it just feels messy.  Don't get me wrong it's a fun film in parts and worth a watch, but nothing more...and the Oscar was clearly just because it was time Marty got one.","de6964c9-05eb-42a7-bad4-0db7214e0208",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2012-02-12","","RT","785959210"
