3.5,"Another great film by Martin Scorsese, and his only best picture winner. But I'm pretty sure he will have more best picture winners in the near future. Although this won, I don't think it's his best. There where many ways I could think of that would have made this better. Some examples include the editing. It could have been even more slow paced like Scorsese's past films. But on every other level this film shines. Scorsese said that this is his first film with a plot. I don't know what he was referring to. But I do have an idea. First off, story is different then plot. A story is something that is told. Plot is the structure of events. All films have story but not all have plot. If a film had no story then the screen would be black the whole time. But a film can get away with not having a plot. The order of plot goes as fallows, introduction, rising action, climax, falling action, and resolution. Not all films fallow this plot structure. As to the other Scorsese films not having plot I have no idea. As for the actual film it was good. The acting was one of the best parts along with the terrific cast. The directing was okay. Yes, I said it. This is not his best. The best part of the film was that it was hard to fallow. But all you have to do is pay attention and your good. That last scene was badass. Good job on the decision on how much blood to use. If you like badass gangster films then this is for you.","056d2b88-6fd9-4bc8-a310-14ff30c744c2",False,True,False,False,3.5,"2012-03-14","","RT","916915362"
