2.5,"There was certainly no shortage on acting or polish for this movie, but I do have one large problem with it that I cannot get past, and that is how bad of a job the writers did of ending it. The resolution that exists is hardly resolution at all. I understand that maybe this was an intentional choice to underscore the gritty nature of organized crime and police corruption, but even so, after two hours of building tension, the 30 minutes they spent tying up loose ends left me feeling worse than I did when it was unresolved. I get that not all movies should have a fairy tale ending, and I'm not really asking for that. This ending felt like a contrived attempt to be shocking, yet still be somewhat satisfying. If the filmmakers are going to give it a negative resolution, then give it a negative resolution. Don't straddle the fence. Only doing a halfway negative resolution makes for a resolution that doesn't know how it is supposed to make the audience feel, and that makes for a bad ending for a movie. Really though, it's ending is the only bad part of it. It is definitely thrilling and kept me intrigued the entire way through. However, as far as storytelling goes, which, in my opinion, is far more important that how good of a movie it is, it is lacking quite a lot.","b52ff80f-e531-4c2a-91df-ab384ee7c43c",False,False,False,False,2.5,"2012-07-09","","RT","783120643"
