4.0,"The Departed

	In 2006, it had been a while since Martin Scorsese had done a mob movie. Then he burst back onto the scene with this explosive, violent, and extremely well written film based not in his go to New York City, but taking us and introducing us to the hardcore gangsters of Boston, Massachusetts. With its all star cast including Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, Jack Nicholson, Alec Baldwin, Martin Sheen, Mark Wahlberg, and new comer Vera Farmiga, its great writing and bloody tale of loyalty and corruption, The Departed never slows down for a minute and is engaging literally from the first frame to the last.
	Leo and Matt play Boston cops. Leo behind a few years in the academy and when he graduates, he is asked not to just be a cop, but due to his family's background, to be an informant. Meanwhile, Matt has been raised to be a rat and was paid to go to the police academy by local big time boss Frank Costello, played by the crazy Jack Nicholson. As Leo goes into his gang, with Matt on the other side, they try to find each other and as one tries to protect Frank and the other tries to sell him out. It's not that difficult, but I feel like I didn't word it right, I don't know. Anyways what ensues is a violent tale from beneath the underbelly of Boston.
	What makes the film so good, with its somewhat complicated story, is the writing and directing. With its swooping camera shots, its use of slow-motion, hell the film even puts a small circle over one of the characters with the rest of the screen black and then pulls back to reveal the rest of the screen in the beginning of the film, the film is just so visually entrancing. And the writing is some of the best ever. It uses somewhat of a montage approach  to it where there are maybe two scenes that are interlocking with each other, which for the most part are happening at the same time, which makes you get a bigger sense of what's going on. And, along with the complicated story that it tells, the writing also features great dialogue from its characters, particularly that of the characters Jack Nicholson, Alec Baldwin and Mark Wahlberg play, almost every time they are on screen, either together or on their own, they say the most outrageous and hilarious thing, truly some of the best lines from the movie come from them. It's a great way to break up the seriousness of the rest of the film.
	So, if you couldn't tell, this movie is so good, better than good, freaking great, rightly winning multiple Oscars in 2007 for its writing, directing, first for legendary director Martin Scorsese, editing, like I said with its interlocking multiple scenes at the same time, and for best picture.  I haven't seen the original Honk Kong film that it's based on, but if it's as good as this I definitely want to check it out. Overall this is another reason and example of why Martin Scorsese is one of the best directors of all time, especially with his mob movies. And if you don't like it, well as multiple characters say in the film ""You can go fuck yourself."" 

4/4, A","57dfc385-a5f1-4dcd-8951-2ceab7e0ee35",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2012-07-12","","RT","906302110"
5.0,"If you have not seen this movie, then you should drop everything you are doing and watch it right now. This movie was absolutely fantastic. Jack Nicholson plays the character of Frank Costello so well that you just can't help but hate him. You are forced to choose sides whether you would be on Matt Damon's or Leo's. This movie just blew me away. There are just so many twists and turns that you can not take your eyes off of the screen. THE ENDING. It was probably the most unexpected ending you would find in some movies. I enjoy twist endings like say Usual Suspects or maybe Sixth Sense. If you have watched those movies and enjoyed the ending, well then you should definitely watch this movie. The characters were amazing. You can't help but be on Leo's side and just hope for the best for him. Mark Wahlberg played a light but significant role. Everything about this movie was great. It was well written and just.....Martin Scorsese is just amazing. Thank you Mr. Scorsese for bringing this movie and adding it to one of my favorite movies of all time. So much happens in the end that you are just left at the end with a....Well Damn! I would definitely recommend you watch this movie. If you don't, well you are missing out.","a18e93ba-6355-42b3-84b5-9d4eb77e0015",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2012-07-13","","RT","905376468"
