3.5,"Apart from the constant stream of authentic Bostonian profanity spewing from the mouths of everyone onscreen, The Departed manages to suck the viewer into the criminal underworld that envelop the lives of the characters.  This film is an acting tour de force with DiCaprio, Damon, Sheen, and Wahlberg all at their absolute best.  Not to mention Jack Nicholson, who is the very embodiment of pure evil.  The editing is crisp and nearly perfect, and the length of the movie doesn't deter from its ability to keep one's attention.  In typical Scorsese fashion, the violence is detestable and at times all too real, but it serves a purpose, and it's hard not to admit that those characters who meet their demise deserve what was coming to them.  I may not feel as strongly about this film as most (it won best picture after all), but I freely admit that it is a powerhouse of a movie.","aa6a7934-b745-4f4c-86e7-39287202fa35",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2012-07-30","","RT","910209267"
5.0,"""The Departed"" is a fantastic film. The performances are great, the storyline and screenplay are strong and funny, and the pacing is great. Also, the direction from Scorsese is very good. A must see. ""The Departed"" gets 95/100.","add1d582-b40f-4294-ad94-795fa364f5f9",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2012-07-30","","RT","906463764"
