5.0,"A modern crime masterpiece!

This film is extremely powerful in it's delivery with the help of marvelous character progression, brutal actuality, and some of the best acting in recent memory. Martin Scorsese is undoubtedly the best filmmaker of the 21st century, and just the fact that he can turn a remake into something more compelling and more engrossing than the original ever dreamt of being is a strong testament to his  directing ability. Although the cinematography is simple it still is beautiful and reflective of the very same innovative tactics used in his past films. This film and 'GoodFellas' are the only works by Scorsese that are even comparable to 'Taxi Driver'.

Leonardo DiCaprio shines like never before; compelling and dramatic. Matt Damon is impressive, not as impressive as his performance in 'Good Will Hunting' but still very good. Surprisingly enough I was actually very impressed with Mark Wahlberg, he is crass, profane, and brutally honest. All the makings of a perfect tough-as-nails on-screen cop. But none were more impressive than Jack Nicholson. I had seen him in some great roles since 'The Shining' such as 'As Good As It Gets' but nothing much that was too terribly impressive until this amazing tour-de-force, one of the most impressive performances in years!

A vivid and realistic crime drama that pushes countless cinematic boundaries. One of my all time favorite films!","24f16b52-88af-4151-b2f5-97f61e14164e",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2012-09-12","","RT","935899721"
