4.5,"A rousing return to form for Martin Scorsese, who has never been able to repeat the success of his early career (and maybe never will again). Flashy camerawork, taut pace, boiling tension, and career-making performances. Still, there's something missing and I can't quite put my finger on it.","bd2e6eb3-5fde-4c5a-9969-b7b6a3ea66be",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2013-01-15","","RT","880141813"
4.5,"If you're looking to a watch a movie directed by one of the best contributors to film of all time and an A-list cast then 'The Departed' is for you. Scorsese is amazing! His efforts in this film remind me a lot like 'Mean Streets' and 'Goodfellas' His actions with the camera never cease to amaze me and his editing with Schoonmaker is epic as always. This film consists of an incredible ensemble of actors. DiCaprio, Nicholson, Damon, Wahlberg, Sheen and the list goes on. It's easily the best film of 2006 and one of the all time greats!","8f93423c-c3ac-49fa-9630-912c103ddf4d",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2013-01-15","","RT","943604903"
5.0,"Leonardo DiCaprio. Matt Damon. Jack Nicholson. Mark Wahlberg. Alec Baldwin. All directed by Martin Scorsese. How can this not be good? However, when I sat down to watch The Departed, I was skeptical because Martin Scorsese has made such excellent crime dramas in the past that I was almost positive that this could never live up to expectation. Thankfully, it did! I now watch this film every other month along with Goodfellas. 

The film centers on two main characters, each a protagonist, but each an antagonist to the other. These are William Costigan (Leonardo DiCaprio) and Colin Sullivan (Matt Damon). Costigan is a cop undercover in the Irish mafia of Boston, while Sullivan is the opposite: an informant for the mob, undercover in the police department. They both race to uncover the other's identity before they are caught themselves. 

The acting in this film is superb on all levels. DiCaprio and Damon are both very good. Jack Nicholson fails to dissapoint (as always) in his role as the mob boss. Mark Wahlberg and Martin Sheen play excellent foils as crime unit detectives because Wahlberg is a mean douchebag while Sheen is a sympathetic older gentleman. 

Although there already is a good handfull of household names in the film's cast, Martin Scorsese is the star of the film. He takes the classic mafia story, and twists it to include the police, and the Irish mob instead of Italian. His wonderful directing and camera movements are, once again, perfect. There are too many good camera shots to mention, so I just won't mention any so none will be left out. One of the joys of this film is the spectacular surprise ending! Shocking!

Anybody that has enjoyed the other three masterpieces by Scorsese (Taxi Driver, Raging Bull, and Goodfellas) will definitely enjoy this one as well. Put down everything and watch this film now.","f7d8b958-a300-4658-92f3-151a84bcb2ad",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2013-01-16","","RT","940732056"
4.5,"One of the best movies I've seen in a long time. It had a killer cast, a great plot, and so much deception it's insane, but you love it. It also has a great ending. An epic film eveyone needs to see.","f4b73397-bb14-4169-863e-4bb683a7270d",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2013-01-16","","RT","790366409"
5.0,"A very original vision of an unoriginal plot. While films about infiltrated police forces and gangs have been done before, Scorsese offers an intelligent, well thought-out story which captivates viewers and keeps them thinking. The casting for this film was outstanding, with impressive performances from Jack Nicholson, Leo DiCaprio, Matt Damon and Mark Wahlberg. The ending was spectacular and very characteristic of Scorsese; especially with the series of unexpected deaths. A must watch!","76ddeb52-feba-44f1-a0ec-f07c58135d79",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2013-01-17","","RT","944157626"
4.5,"Scorsese delivers a thrilling, taut film that packs an emotional punch to the gut. With a cast that's second-to-none, it's not surprising The Departed brought the legendary director his first and only Oscar for Best Director. It isn't Scorsese's best film (see Goodfellas), but the Boston setting, complex noirish story, and outstanding performances leave you thrilled. The Shakespearean ending seems a bit rushed, but this is otherwise a magnificent piece of gritty, violent art from the master of capturing street life in America.","d9f48fb5-c034-4a57-8667-b88649881191",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2013-01-18","","RT","943995338"
