4.0,"Frank Costello (Nicholson): When you decide to be something, you can be it. That's what
they don't tell you in the church. When I was your age they would say we can become cops,
criminals. Today, what I'm saying to you is this: when you're facing a loaded gun, 
what's the difference? 

Not my typical genre of choice, but I have to admit, I liked it a lot. This film has a great ensemble but Jack (not surprising) was the star of the show, being his charismatic, devious self as always. This was an interesting game of cat-and-mouse, with the ending for Billy Costigan (DiCaprio's character) being the only real surprise for me; but honestly, the film's overall outcome was pretty predictable (I called it as soon as I saw that character), but it was still all very entertaining to watch unfold.","e58b954b-3d0d-426a-983b-a0743012b1e1",False,False,False,False,4.0,"2013-03-04","","RT","833753143"
