5.0,"A darkly gripping, utterly absorbing piece of brilliance from Martin Scorsese, The Departed succeeds on virtually all levels, with an incredible cast (Nicholson, DiCaprio, Damon, Wahlberg, Sheen, Baldwin, Winstone etc.), clever direction and an intense tone. It's reminiscent of Scorsese's gangster classic, but with a modern twist. The moody lighting and abrasive plot are helped by Scorsese's genius behind the camera to make this remarkable feature such a joy to behold.","dbbe0128-9615-42d4-a3f2-adf2ad99c97e",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2013-03-15","","RT","900177986"
5.0,"This is Scorcese at his most confident. Dicaprio, Nicholson, Damon, and Wahlberg give career-best performances. The soundtrack is pitch perfect (Will I ever tire of hearing ""Gimme Shelter"" in a Scorcese flick? I answer thee nay). Ultimately, the real genius lies in impeccable editing and increasingly rising stakes that build to a perfect climax. This is one of the most purely entertaining, visceral experiences of cinema of the last 10 years, and one of increasing relevance in the modern age. The final 20 minutes is jaw-dropping. This is the work of a master at the top of his game.","8fb61d8c-b45c-48bd-adae-2f7f4a51746e",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2013-03-16","","RT","910711026"
