4.5,"The second gangster movie spectacular from Martin Scorsese (for which he won both Best Picture and Best Director) is this time set in inner city Boston where Jack Nicholson is a mob boss and Matt Damon and Leonardo DiCaprio are informers in the gang and the police force who go undercover in the other's establishment where they try to take each other down. Getting strength from powerhouse acting from the three leads in addition to a solid supporting cats that includes Mark Wahlberg as the profane, provocative, and outrageous staff sergeant of the police and Alec Baldwin as the equally charged and amusing police captain who heads the group of cops going after Nicholson's character. Music is put to good use as usual in a Scorsese film, including a new rendition of Comfortably Numb, along with the customary Rolling Stones. Yes, it's surprising to see his big win come from a crime story set in Boston rather than his home turf in New York, but this one supplies plenty of thrills, double-crosses, and clever dialogue to make for an excellent edge-of-your seat drama from a master director at work.","94c8add3-fa68-45ea-9719-b9548f1ccfe8",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2013-03-26","","RT","935936767"
5.0,"Every time I watch this movie I am reminded how good it is. It is tense, dark, funny, and always keeps you guessing. In my opinion this is Martin Scorsese's masterpiece. It has great shots, amazing acting, an outstanding cast, great plot, dialogue, and special effects. I can recommend this movie to anyone there is something for everyone to enjoy in this film. Check it out if you haven't yet it is well worth your time!
-Spencer Mlekoday","1c233ec7-8d06-4130-b7ec-ca7c5e446965",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2013-03-27","","RT","945674743"
