4.5,"The Departed was outstanding, with one of the best casts in a movie that i have ever seen. Jack Nicholson, Leonardo DiCaprio, Mark Wahlburg and Matt Damon are what keep you watching even after the dull first 20-30 minutes of the film, but you know what they say, ""the best films always start off slow"". Martin Scorsese's best film in my opinion but would have to be pretty hard to screw up a movie with the cast that was within it. The tracks were done by Howard Shore who also did the tracks for all three Lord Of The Rings films, and is pretty well known within the industry. Howard Shore how ever did not impress me with his work in this film and at times had me wondering why certain tracks were placed where they were. Never the less, the film was great and the ending had you glad you spent 2 hours and a half in front of a television.","65002bbf-5f8f-4577-94f1-eff7c373f0cb",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2013-06-25","","RT","797840572"
5.0,"What else can I say? This was amazing! Every bit of this movie was just incredible from the directing, acting, writing, and editing! The storytelling was just so complex and brilliant that you can feel so much irony throughout this movie for both the lead characters who are both double agents on different sides. Leonardo Dicaprio and Matt Damon were incredible in this movie playing these super complex roles. Jack Nicolson is also incredible in this movie as well the rest of the cast ( Alec Baldwin, Mark Walberg, Martin Sheen, etc. ). The script is brilliant taking all these characters and throwing all these crazy twists with them and they places they have to go just to keep a secret to where their true loyalties are. Lastly, the directing was remarkable! I loved how well put together the whole movie was and how dark and gritty his mob world was.  I'm now a huge fan of Martin Scorcesse ( truthfully the only other movie I've seen of his is Hugo ). Overall incredible movie!!!
10/10","dfbd134b-2f2d-4d75-9759-d6be2a53110f",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2013-06-27","","RT","919606937"
