4.5,"The premise is classic cinema, but the script and the pacing are slightly off - too many plot holes, too repetitive - basically this would've worked better as a TV series, it is so densely layered and rich with potential. Yet a TV series never could've captured the talent  here. Despite some odd cross-scene editing decisions, Scorsese is in exceptional technical and thematic form, and there is nothing wrong with his outstanding artistic sensibility being focused on possibly the most traditional and least provocative script he's ever worked on. 

The best thing about the script is the salty cock-comparing dialogue, particularly as envisaged by Nicholson (a slightly-less cartoony but no-less entertaining version of the Joker)), Winstone, Baldwin and (I can't believe I'm writing this) Wahlberg. 

The story itself might bring little surprises, but there is ample tension and thrills (and laughs) in many individuals scenes. Overall, nowhere near as kinetic or hypnotic as Goodfellas, but Marty's Oscar for this validates his epic career.","640ab30b-01d5-4db8-9336-6813dc107dc9",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2013-06-29","","RT","790842734"
