4.5,"This isn't just a film. Scorsese authored a masterful work of art. The Departed is the perfect exemplification of what John Truby describes as an ""organic story"", a living, breathing, and captivating narrative told with brilliant precision, brought to life by the most raw, believable performances I've seen in years. We're not watching Leo DiCaprio and Matt Damon act on screen. We're being pulled into this story by Billy Costigan and Colin Sullivan. The premise is simple and gripping, the characters real and genuine. This would be the perfect movie, if it weren't for the many twists and turns the film boasts at the end. Despite them, Scorsese's masterpiece is truly a cornerstone in modern American cinema, and should be revered and studied for decades to come. But what else should we expect from the renowned filmmaker?","a6f235b0-ab95-4632-97a7-925763af6b8b",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2013-09-15","","RT","899054391"
