5.0,"The Departed is unlike any other movie directed by Scorsese.With a really well rounded cast and a plot which is filled with one twist after another,this movie is an all time favorite and even though its run time is longer when compared to average movies,the movie feels slickly edited-every moment is full of energy and is important to the movie in some way or the other.
 Leonardo DiCaprio plays the role of Billy Costigan.His family has a rough past as they were connected with organized crime and this turns out to be a problem when Costigan enlists himself to become a cop.Instead,he is asked by Queenan(Sheen) and Dignam(an over the top and highly amusing and cursing Walhberg)to go undercover.
 On the other hand,Collin Sullivan(played by Damon) is from a seemingly good family.But that does not stop him from getting introduced to organized crime by the fearful Frank Costello played by the ever so dependent Nicholson.Costello trains him  to become a mole inside the State Police.It is more or less understood that these characters will certainly cross paths with some really jaw-dropping results.To say more would only lead to spoiling the movie.
 The twists in the movie are well thought out and believable, albeit a bit over the top.The actors are all in top form-from Damon to Wahlberg.Even DiCaprio cannot overshadow any performance here.This movie is directed perfectly and it is hard to believe that it is a Scorsese movie-his other movies are more so about money,power and the main focus is on a single title character but here there are multiple characters and the movie is in no ways connected to the themes of money and power.
 The Departed is a solid thriller and crime drama with some really solid performances,great direction and editing,and a really fresh plot.The movie is done well and has also won multiple oscars,including Best Picture,Editing and Director.There are no flaws which this movie could possibly have and hence it is a must watch.","79bf7d71-9d67-443c-8e10-636d7da53122",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2014-01-05","","RT","951965424"
