4.5,"I love movies with rich characters, where nothing is as simple as it seems, you never know what exactly is happening, or who can be trusted. This is one of those movies. Martin Scorsese fully emeses you in the world of Boston's brutal mobsters and corrupt law enforcement. Leonardo DiCaprio and Matt Damon deliver strong performances, as they portray two spies from similar backgrounds working for opposing sides. One is an undercover cop infiltrating a criminal organization, while the other is a gangster informant in good standing with the police force. The movie operates as two related storylines following each of the spies. These two stories develop details in parallel but do weave together; they even unknowingly share cross-relationships. This makes the plot rich and satisfyingly complex. The big names in the cast do not disappoint DiCaprio and Damon are great as the leads, and Jack Nicholson, Mark Wahlberg, Martin Sheen, and Alec Baldwin round out an excellent cast that is full of swagger. Such high-quality direction and acting reinforce an outstanding story with quality characters and atmosphere. Alas, it is not perfect; the unfulfilling finish lacks meaning and leaves things feeling unsettled.","b1d3c2d7-86e1-4b68-a490-540dc83516cc",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2014-01-27","","RT","783507988"
5.0,"I don't even like crime thrillers and I can honestly say this movie is absolutely exquisite. From start to finish, the film pulls you into this realistic world and catches you and holds on tight from start to finish. This edge-of-your-seat thriller is a record and career high for every single cast member in it, along with it's director. Not only does it have one of the greatest ensembles ever on film but every single one of them pulls it off brilliantly. Leonardo is superb, Damon is perfect, Nicholson is captivating, Wahlberg is stunning, along with Sheen and Baldwin. The story is incredibly told and each character depicted is excellent, this is truly one of the best movies I have ever seen in my entire life.","d51c2c94-4bdb-4d42-ab23-c6a3922c2438",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2014-01-28","","RT","940888130"
5.0,"This movie hands down deserves a 5 out of 5. Leonardo DiCaprio brings the action into this movie, just like he always does. Matt Damon brings the sex, and Mark Wahlberg  delivers the package of packages if you know what I mean. Legendary Director Martin Scorsese did a phenomenal job on the mechanics and the construction of this movie. Although the movie did seem to feel like a long watch, the amount of time that was spent into The Departed made up for it. The funny thing about this movie was the fact that the f-bomb was dropped almost literally 100 times! Even more than 100 I imagine!! The elevator scene near the end was my favorite course (my favorite scene of all time), and the ending where Matt Damon gets his delivery is my 2nd favorite part to this movie. It is good to see these 3 phenomenal actors work together to create the greatest movie of all time. Not only does Scorsese here brings true grit of an action-packed thriller, but the actors as well. I can go on like this forever if may be. I want to see Scorsese do what he does best on every movie he does, by making the movie flow with many themes, scenes, and sex. Leonardo DiCaprio did a fantastic job on keeping the themes flow perfectly and fluidly. Matt Damon did a fantastic job on keeping the sex alive and going, and Mark Wahlberg did a fantastic job on keeping the scenes of this movie functional and fun to watch.","c967b1df-d578-401b-84c3-36c3fc4f2354",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2014-01-31","","RT","962831328"
