4.5,"Like all of Scorcese's films, The Departed is unflinchingly violent, as if to give audiences a wake up jolt throughout it's 2.5 hour run time. It's also, to my knowledge, his only adaptation of another film, which I can't imagine did this tale any more justice (ha!). Another hallmark of a Scorcese film is that the plotting itself seems rote, rife with what might be, in a lesser filmmaker's hands, cliche. The Departed manages to transcend those cliches by being intricately plotted, deliberately shot, and perfectly fleshed out.","4e70b2e2-a67b-4da9-a77f-99afa8cab40c",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2014-06-30","","RT","907023216"
