5.0,"Kept me engaged and on the edge of my seat. The script was an explosion of entertainment that had me laughing, although sometimes tacky but I'm watched this 12 years after its release. I'm a fan of Death Note since 2006 and seen infernal affairs, yet it didn't dampen my love for this movie. 

Scorsese once again showed why he is well-respected. There is a substance to his craft that critics will never grasp. He's able to brings out the best in the actors. 

Leonardo deserved an Oscar for this performance, heck he deserved one for Gilbert Grape, heck even Shutter Island, people must have something against him. Art-wise this was phenomenal!! Matt Damon showed so much Versatility in this, he embodied RAT in every way and that was challenging. Mark Wahlberg is my favorite actor since I was 12 back in 2000! Seeing him with Matt Damon, finally, and in a movie that's perfect through and through was just a GIFT. AMAZING.","b363f4f7-fb65-4c10-8262-0666eff927cb",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2017-10-13","","RT","976758550"
