4.5,"Extremely well made film in so many aspects. For one the acting was done so well to the point where I felt bad for DiCaprio's character and started to loathe Matt Damon's. Each major character was described in depth in one way or another to the point where you understood which each character stood for, even if some of those descriptions were plot twists you did not see coming. Not to mention the cinematography was done very well and the only setting that did not look very realistic and easy to tell it was green screened was when (no spoilers) Leonardo DiCaprio's character and Martin Sheen's met on the top of a building, but it looked real enough to gloss over. There were many parts of this film I glossed over which came back at the end to surprise me. Overall, the simple idea of DiCaprio's character serving with a good intent but on the outside it appears he is doing it for the opposite reason and Matt Damon's character vice versa works very well in another well crafted film from Martin Scorsese.","5f709bbe-a80b-48bc-bf87-74a28df10453",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2018-07-03","","RT","976978410"
