3.5,"A film with many great acting talent. The acting is the films strengths from Jack Nicholson, Matt Damon, Mark Wahlberg and Leonardo Dicaprio. They play off each really well. A film where a rat is in the police but also into a mob. We see both trying to not get caught as they delve deeper into their surrounding. Both Dicaprio and Damon are impressive in their roles. The film does feel very macho, plenty of guns, plenty of swearing and plenty of violence. Mark Wahlberg got an best supporting actor Oscar nomination for basically being foul mouthed, others i felt deserved it more. Martin Scorcese finally won a best director Oscar, but even he would have to admit he has done much better work. But that does not mean the film is bad by any means, with a cast like that and a great director the film will always have qualities. There are moments that are very tense as Dicaprio is close to being caught. The final shootout is well staged with much crashing off cars and gun fire. I like how the film started as Jack Nicholson mop boss wanders the street with power and links up  with a young Matt Damon, its sets the film nicely for what is to follow. For me the many deaths at the end was off putting to story that was going on. Plus some of the characters were doing things out of character. The film strength is in the acting talent and their scenes bouncing off each other.","f04f33a2-5af6-450b-a190-9e605e15e96a",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2020-06-23","","RT","978664196"
