5.0,"This is easily Scorsese's best work since Goodfellas, and he and DiCaprio finally click to make a nearly perfect movie. The characters are amazing, and Scorsese finally grabs that Oscar.","c86aef5a-58c0-4394-9637-92a7f1e05dd7",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2020-09-01","","RT","978830610"
5.0,"The Departed may be one of the best films ever made. I said it at the beginning of this article but amassing a cast this talented was a masterstroke but to bring a story together you can't just have great actors you also have to have someone leading them and Scorsese is the perfect choice. He loves a gangster flick and he brings this story together incredibly well. Having some of the best actors to ever do it helps also. A lot of these guys are at their absolute best in this film!


Leo is brilliant as Billy. We constantly relate to him and what he's going through. He's in so deep and only has two people in the world he can trust and one of them doesn't like him a great deal. The stakes for him are so high and what he has to go through is horrendous. He's trying his best to not get too drawn into the world he's pretending to be a part of and he is doing his utmost to not lose himself as a person. Obviously with such a complex character you need someone to portray him as excellently as Leo does. I can't forget Damon though. He's such a great actor and this film really showcases his levels. We all know him as the quiet hero in the Bourne franchise but in this film he's the sneaky and slimy rat. Him and Leo obviously are both rats but Leo is doing it for good and you can see his struggle with his role whereas Damon is the opposite and he gets more underhanded and dirty the more the film goes along. We genuinely dislike his character and want him to get his comeuppance. 

Despite both of those excellent performances from our leads the star of the show for me is Nicholson. He's so eccentrically excellent as Costello. He has that perfect combination of wit and lunacy that all great villains need. Whereas Damon is slimy, Nicholson is not he just plays his part to perfection and comes across as an all time great Mob boss leader. It's such a shame he retired from acting but for me this is up there as one of his greatest roles. 


I'm not usually a massive lover of films that win Oscars but The Departed for me is what all Oscar movie winners should be about. It's a great film and thoroughly enjoyable for everyone whereas I find most films that win best picture are usually incredibly acted but don't have the most exciting of stories. The Departed has both and that's why it won the Oscar for best picture in 2007 and also a host of other awards including best director for Scorsese. Leo also won a Golden Globe for his performance as Billy. Wahlberg and Nicholson were nominated for best supporting as well. 

As I've said before this film is really one of the all time greats. The acting and story is superb but for me the reason it stands out so vividly in my mind is the ending. It's shocking and moments from it will always stick with me. I remember being blown away by the twists at the end and just when we feel like we're not going to get a happy of sorts ending we do get what we want and in the most brilliant of ways. I honestly do not know how anyone could not like this film. It twists, turns and most importantly surprises you throughout. You're constantly gripped to the story as our characters get themselves into some seriously sticky situations in which we as an audience and engrossed in finding how they get out of them.  It's got something for everyone and is a film that everybody really has to see! 

Check out my site LifeLowdown.com for more Film & TV news!","9a53e38d-dad0-4199-8308-86967933c4d6",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2020-09-03","","RT","978834159"
