3.5,"If I had a dime every time I could talk about ""The Departed"" and not have someone tell me the original, Hong Kong version was better, I would have a dime.","b2f08a79-d26e-40c9-83bf-b0fd6a1494f8",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2020-10-12","","RT","978873775"
4.5,"Aggressive and entertaining, The Departed is an in your face, fast moving character driven drama that delivers heart in the midst of heat and violence on Boston's gritty streets. Grounded in strong performances by Dicaprio, Damon and Nicholson (as well as the other famous and civilian faces that pop up) it's easy to be carried on the parallel and intersecting journies of Costigan and Sullivan. The script (adapted from Mou gaan dou) is tight in plot and dialogue, and also delivers on the emotional front. In tandem with wildly fast paced editing and an ever moving camera, the story and image move! The action drives forward like a freight train and while there are moments that settle -- Costigan's nearly incessant dark emotional soup, rightly slows the journey -- they are surrounded by explosions of action and chatter. I'd say one of the most impressive parts of the film is how thoroughly laced with comedic dialogue it is -- a throw back to the quick witted films of the 30s and 40s -- Sturgess and Wilder would be honored. Even the theme music has a stylish quick moving Spanish guitar, and while there may be no explicit context for the choice, it fits right in to the boisterous explosive energy of the moving frame. When Scorcese says he wanted to make a great B movie, it's understandable. The roots here are meant to grow a genre film (a near copy cat of a Hong Kong cop film) and ""that film"" would these days go straight to streaming starring only Wahlberg. But what Scorcese (and Schoonmaker) are able to pack in, elevates the story to an electric dance of epic proportions. Is it his greatest and deepest film, maybe not. But it may just be the most entertaining.","0e0be890-6243-4001-8fa3-8d7a5e28c679",False,False,False,True,4.5,"2020-10-18","Craig N","RT","253e073a-4392-4d1c-9f8a-99d12e8e7a85"
