5.0,"One of the best crime movies I have ever seen. It's narrative is winding in a way no other movie in the genre can replicate. The Departed nails it down to the most minute detail, but what is most striking is how well the cast embodies their characters. Each character could justify their own review and each would be showered in praise. Just when you think you know what is going to happen, the film takes a quick turn and keeps your head on a swivel. Absolutely thrilling.","90b634d4-15b5-4667-a625-b07f66e49aec",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2021-03-03","","RT","8810399b-b1fc-4e7d-9735-f97e1b2edeaf"
4.5,"In The Departed, Martin Scorsese weaves a complex tale of deception and loyalty set in the world of organized crime and law enforcement.  Leonardo DiCaprio and Matt Damon play moles, one infiltrating the Boston mob while the other infiltrates the state police force.  Both Damon and DiCaprio are fantastic in their respective roles in Scorsese's predictably stylish film, but Jack Nicholson is electric as mob boss Frank Costello, maniacally chewing up scenes as only Nicholson can.  The tension is palpable throughout the film and builds steadily to the explosive conclusion.  While it may not be on par with Raging Bull, Taxi Driver, or Good Fellas, it's not far behind on the list of Scorsese's best work.","33644640-1682-417d-8b81-8545594940b9",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2021-03-10","dave s","RT","2a1643d2-6913-4dea-9582-8d51686059df"
3.0,"It's a pity to say, but the film just grew old badly: the action and plot development seem to be a bit artificial, and the pacing makes you feel like you never left the intro part of the film.
