3.5,"The Departed is the story of a mob boss and his two sons (neither of whom know that they're half-brothers or that the boss - Jack Nicholson - is their father). The sons (Matt Damon & Leonardo DiCaprio) both graduate from the State Police academy. Damon acts as a mole in the State Police for Nicholson & DiCaprio is assigned by the State Police to be a mole in Nichoson's outfit.

To the world, Damon *appears* to be the Golden Boy with a bright future, whilst DiCaprio seems but a crook. In actual fact, of course, this is the opposite to the truth.

This is further complicated by Nicholson being an FBI asset.

Vera Farmiga lives with Damon, but loves DiCaprio. No one knows who is responsible for Fariga's pregnancy.

She finds out the truth but DiCaprio is killed. Damon kills Nicholson and is in turn killed by a State Police officer (Mark Wahlberg).

Nothing is sorted out.

Some great performaces here.

My main criticism of the film is that the timeframe is supposed to cover several years, but there is absolutely no sensation that any time has passed.","83b82e07-9f84-4031-ae07-f6ecee586d31",False,False,False,False,3.5,"2022-10-13","diana d","RT","003e1f8e-818a-4f3b-8c32-ab041c3a225c"
5.0,"This is one of the greatest movies I have ever seen. I first saw it in 2012, and I have seen it countless times since. 

The Departed made me a fan of Martin Scorsese, Leo, and Jack Nicholson. Matt Damon, Alec Baldwin and Mark Wahlberg are all also on top of their games. 

In my opinion, this is one of the greatest movies ever made and a must-see if you're a fan of the genre. Martin Scorsese deserved an Academy Award for Goodfellas, but I'm so glad he finally won it for this!","fa762520-204e-4bc0-afac-87b40ee5b284",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2022-11-03","Adithya S","RT","7cf4daba-005a-4df8-aef7-2db653421cfe"
