5.0,"An undercover agent and a spy constantly try to counter-attack each other in order to save themselves from being exposed in front of the authorities. Meanwhile, both try to infiltrate an Irish gang.

I have watched quite a bit of Scorsese over the years, but I have not watched as much films of his filmography, as I would have liked, so I am going to watch some big gabs that I have not watched, in the coming days. The Departed is probably my favorite Scorsese I have watched so far, maybe the Wolf of Wall Street is on the same level for me personally and maybe it's because I just watched it, but man what a ride this movie was. The Departed keeps you invested from the moment you start the movie, till the end of it all, it's one hell of a ride. Before I say more about the movie, can I just say, why the hell is and was Mark Wahlberg the only one who got nominated for an Oscar, like seriously? Yeah Mark Wahlberg is fine, but even if he was the only one in the movie, I would not have nominated him, he has some scenes here and there, but nothing extraordinary. You have one of Leonardo Di Caprio's best performances, probably Matt Damon's second best performance after Good Will Hunting and you have Jack Nicholson giving one of his best performances of his already impressive career, a decision by the Academy I will never understand. The movie delivers another sharply written script, a perfectly edited movie, a great score and a story that keeps you gripped till the end of the movie. The whole movie is fantastic, but then the 3rd act starts to get going and the movie takes itself to a whole other level. I loved every second of the Departed, I have literally zero notes for it, it's simply just a masterpiece!","e9bc0f93-2361-4c6e-904f-179fc4856dcb",False,False,False,False,5.0,"2023-06-08","casnien v","RT","6b4ff4a3-5534-4214-a7f3-bff8bedecb7f"
4.5,"I was never bored with this movie, although the beginning of the first act of the movie wasn't really clicking with me, it got really good after that. It has great writing and dialogue, plus it is extremely action packed and suspenseful throughout. Great performances all around, great cinematography, and a very energetic and at times noir feel. Overall, this was a really good Martin Scorsese that proved he is one of the all time greatest film makers to ever live.","8b267306-d813-4035-ad3e-070d1da45a39",False,False,False,False,4.5,"2023-06-11","Raymundo A","RT","fc03dbe5-313b-4452-8bcd-8936b2a78970"
